{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals","id":977995,"title":"Black Furies and Transgender Individuals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-28T15:14:38-07:00","id":977995,"title":"Black Furies and Transgender Individuals","content":"So I searched the forums and saw there was a conversation about this awhile back, about a year ago. I didn't want to necro it, but for the sake of reference here's the link: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/574157-black-furies-feminism-and-gender-identiy\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...gender-identiy</a><br /> <br /> I'm making a new thread for it because I think it got a bit derailed at the end, and there's plenty of things I'd like to add to the discussion, and would also like to hear any new points of view that might not have existed on the board at that time.<br /> <br /> My first point of confusion is how the Black Furies and their reverence for the Wyld never seems to come up in these discussions where I find them. This seems pretty important if you're going to have a discussion about how they would feel regarding the issue, especially when it comes to gender variance and individuals who don't feel they belong to one gender or the other, or who seem to alternate in their own minds. Would the Black Furies consider this a win? Would it warrant further inspection? The Black Furies in their Revised Tribebook are painted with a fairly conservative brush (by today's standards) in contrast to their reverence for a force that represents explosive volatile change.<br /> <br /> Another factor that might influence their treatment of children with the condition is the fact that, especially in the World of Darkness, there are tangible culprits to blame. A Black Fury wouldn't really have the traditional TERF response of men simply trying to steal the last sacred bastion of femininity, when you consider things like Endocrine Disruptors. These are chemicals that are put in pharmaceuticals, pesticides, and plastics, or just as byproducts of industry and agriculture. <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Bisphenol A being present in baby bottles would be just another reason for them to hate anything other than traditional breastfeeding, up there with the properties of the formula in the game's setting. Bisphenol A can leech from the plastic and into the milk or formula, thus affecting their bodies and brains at critical points in development, to say nothing of the effect it might have on pregnant women. The whole situation is very 'Pentex' in general, and I imagine that they'd make a habit of confronting that, especially since - in setting - you could make an argument for it drastically affecting women and their unborn children. The question becomes whether or not they'd support these children, or would they insist on testing and the like to see how they 'would have been' without chemical tampering? That strikes me as a pretty Weaver course of action and I can't see them doing it, maybe they'd just have a Ritual? Or they could just take the child's word for it, or possibly all of the above depending on which faction you ask.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to approach this concept from a general standpoint, instead of focusing on things like how they would view transgender 'werewolves'. I feel like the former would greatly influence the later anyway; and besides that, it likely wouldn't concern them that much so long as more werewolves are being made, WTF simplified that approach with one of the least expensive gifts you can get, so I can't imagine it being that much more difficult in WTA. I would imagine any Garou who has carried and birthed a child would carry some respect/status as a woman as far as the general tribe is concerned.<br /> <br /> This being said, it's a pretty controversial issue still, for lots of people, and my own viewpoint may be biased. Before I take the time to run a game for my friends with these themes, I'd like to get as many viewpoints as possible, and would love to see what other people think.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 09-28-2016, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:30:32-07:00","id":978032,"title":"","content":"When you're fighting an apocalyptic war and only accept women into your Tribe, I imagine any woman is welcome. While I'm sure there's an older or more conservative faction with TERF ideology (you see a lot of transohobia in some Wicca communities, for instance), I can't imagine it's more than a minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:46:24-07:00","id":978044,"title":"","content":"I don't think you'll get very far trying to establish any kind of etiology for being trans, as there is no known etiology. Establishing one in game would almost certainly be a matter of driving an agenda, and trans people pre-existed the factors you bring up. The stuff about endocrine disruptors and other similar issues tends to be more of an MRA talking point than one picked up by women, with the concern that it is &quot;emasculating&quot; men and boys. While I can certainly see the Black Furies concerned about such things I don't see them adopting similar stances to MRAs.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:11:30-07:00","id":978052,"title":"","content":"It was discussed in wolves and whiskey, the only woman Developer there was pretty heated on the issue.<br /> <br /> Richt Says he's gotten DEATH THREATS for stating he will do that in the new Werewolf LARP.<br /> <br /> If you want my opinion?<br /> <br /> I think its a little TOO Hellbent on saying &quot;Hey! Look how progressive we are!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> things CAN get too preachy, believe it or not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:26:12-07:00","id":978056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978044#post978044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you'll get very far trying to establish any kind of etiology for being trans, as there is no known etiology. Establishing one in game would almost certainly be a matter of driving an agenda, and trans people pre-existed the factors you bring up. The stuff about endocrine disruptors and other similar issues tends to be more of an MRA talking point than one picked up by women, with the concern that it is &quot;emasculating&quot; men and boys. While I can certainly see the Black Furies concerned about such things I don't see them adopting similar stances to MRAs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are plenty of disciplines that have found reasonable etiologies for the phenomena. It's only an issue when someone tries to find the single prevailing etiology, and I'm not trying to invalidate any ideas or anyone, the example I gave was just that - an example of how, in the setting of Apocalypse, the Wyrm and the Weaver might be involved in promoting dysphoria in human beings.<br /> <br /> I am transgender, and I know that it's something that has <i>always</i> existed, and is as old as dirt. To use a problematic comparison, saying that lead can cause mental disorders is not the same thing as saying that lead is the origin point for mental disorders. There's nothing flawed about being transgender, or on the surface, anything undesirable about it - though I would argue that gender dysphoria, the feeling of disconnect with one's body, can be disabling, speaking from personal experience. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978044#post978044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stuff about endocrine disruptors and other similar issues tends to be more of an MRA talking point than one picked up by women, with the concern that it is &quot;emasculating&quot; men and boys. While I can certainly see the Black Furies concerned about such things I don't see them adopting similar stances to MRAs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting this specifically because it's personally relevant to me and I want to emphasize it, and my answer.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty well aware of the MRA types you specify as well, they're also the types that go around promoting testosterone cream wherever they can. The issue is that endocrine disruptors do exist, and they can have a physical and mental effect on human beings, especially at important developmental stages. Just because an MRA trope is blaming male feminists on a lack of Testosterone is a thing doesn't mean it's not an issue worth exploring.<br /> <br /> I sometimes encounter backlash because my dysphoria was very strong as a child, that made it 'a problem' and a painful thing, regardless of whether or not I would be accepted in my society or not. The acceptance helps, sure, but it's not going to make the constant migraines or tension go away.<br /> <br /> I don't think there's anything wrong with studying the effects of hormones during early human development, and how that affects gender identity or potential dysphoria later in life, as the brain has to deal with a body it simply didn't develop for. I think there's plenty of compelling evidence and it's a complicated subject that shouldn't just be dismissed because MRAs like to complain about emasculated men.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it was my hope to avoid making this too personal on my end, and I think I've pretty much failed on that, at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:28:22-07:00","id":978057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978052#post978052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Richt Says he's gotten DEATH THREATS for stating he will do that in the new Werewolf LARP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm entirely not surprised by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:31:34-07:00","id":978062,"title":"","content":"I got both my W20 Corebook, and W20 Book of the wyrm signed by him and someone else.<br /> <br /> Oh one other thing.<br /> <br /> I asked Richt if Metis or Kinfolk were meant as allegories for racism or Sexism in real life, he said only &quot;you can read whatever you want into it&quot; <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-28-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:37:14-07:00","id":978067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978052#post978052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was discussed in wolves and whiskey, the only woman Developer there was pretty heated on the issue.<br /> <br /> Richt Says he's gotten DEATH THREATS for stating he will do that in the new Werewolf LARP.<br /> <br /> If you want my opinion?<br /> <br /> I think its a little TOO Hellbent on saying &amp;quot;Hey! Look how progressive we are!!!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> things CAN get too preachy, believe it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accepting trans people is preachy now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:41:23-07:00","id":978071,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would have the Black Furies dislike transgender people. Werewolf culture is extremely conservative as well as bigoted. Hating things that fall outside of their world view is one of the central elements of Garou culture and the Black Furies represent this more than most Tribes do. If I were running this in a game, I'd have the BF's consider a transwoman to be an abomination, perhaps Wyrm tainted - a man who thinks that he can use Weaver shenanigans to thwart the will of Gaia and violate the sacred feminine. I feel that making WoD splats overly tolerant may be projecting one's own beliefs onto these fictional groups in contradiction to what would likely be the most thematic and realistic situation.<br /> <br /> Of course, since werewolves are not real, there is no strictly right or wrong answer, but that is how I would run it. As for Tribes that would be tolerant of transgender people, I would imagine that the Children of Gaia would be as well as Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:54:39-07:00","id":978077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978071#post978071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would have the Black Furies dislike transgender people. Werewolf culture is extremely conservative as well as bigoted. Hating things that fall outside of their world view is one of the central elements of Garou culture and the Black Furies represent this more than most Tribes do. If I were running this in a game, I'd have the BF's consider a transwoman to be an abomination, perhaps Wyrm tainted - a man who thinks that he can use Weaver shenanigans to thwart the will of Gaia and violate the sacred feminine. I feel that making WoD splats overly tolerant may be projecting one's own beliefs onto these fictional groups in contradiction to what would likely be the most thematic and realistic situation.<br /> <br /> Of course, since werewolves are not real, there is no strictly right or wrong answer, but that is how I would run it. As for Tribes that would be tolerant of transgender people, I would imagine that the Children of Gaia would be as well as Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, transgender people are real people who live in the real world, unlike Black Furies. Reproducing the same oppressive systems that exist in the real world in what's supposed to be fantasy escapism strikes me as a great way to alienate those real transgender people from the game. This would also make such a decision a terrible decision and maybe a different take would be more appropriate - one that doesn't cut transgender women out of Werewolf's definition of womanhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:56:25-07:00","id":978079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978056#post978056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there are plenty of disciplines that have found reasonable etiologies for the phenomena. It's only an issue when someone tries to find the single prevailing etiology, and I'm not trying to invalidate any ideas or anyone, the example I gave was just that - an example of how, in the setting of Apocalypse, the Wyrm and the Weaver might be involved in promoting dysphoria in human beings.<br /> <br /> I am transgender, and I know that it's something that has <i>always</i> existed, and is as old as dirt. To use a problematic comparison, saying that lead can cause mental disorders is not the same thing as saying that lead is the origin point for mental disorders. There's nothing flawed about being transgender, or on the surface, anything undesirable about it - though I would argue that gender dysphoria, the feeling of disconnect with one's body, can be disabling, speaking from personal experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's a fair point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978056#post978056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quoting this specifically because it's personally relevant to me and I want to emphasize it, and my answer.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty well aware of the MRA types you specify as well, they're also the types that go around promoting testosterone cream wherever they can. The issue is that endocrine disruptors do exist, and they can have a physical and mental effect on human beings, especially at important developmental stages. Just because an MRA trope is blaming male feminists on a lack of Testosterone is a thing doesn't mean it's not an issue worth exploring.<br /> <br /> I sometimes encounter backlash because my dysphoria was very strong as a child, that made it 'a problem' and a painful thing, regardless of whether or not I would be accepted in my society or not. The acceptance helps, sure, but it's not going to make the constant migraines or tension go away.<br /> <br /> I don't think there's anything wrong with studying the effects of hormones during early human development, and how that affects gender identity or potential dysphoria later in life, as the brain has to deal with a body it simply didn't develop for. I think there's plenty of compelling evidence and it's a complicated subject that shouldn't just be dismissed because MRAs like to complain about emasculated men.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it was my hope to avoid making this too personal on my end, and I think I've pretty much failed on that, at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not trying to say it should be dismissed, just that I would hope for a nuanced approach to the topic (which I would say MRAs fail at).<br /> <br /> And I am sorry for pushing you to make this too personal. That wasn't my intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:57:12-07:00","id":978081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978071#post978071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would have the Black Furies dislike transgender people. Werewolf culture is extremely conservative as well as bigoted. Hating things that fall outside of their world view is one of the central elements of Garou culture and the Black Furies represent this more than most Tribes do. If I were running this in a game, I'd have the BF's consider a transwoman to be an abomination, perhaps Wyrm tainted - a man who thinks that he can use Weaver shenanigans to thwart the will of Gaia and violate the sacred feminine. I feel that making WoD splats overly tolerant may be projecting one's own beliefs onto these fictional groups in contradiction to what would likely be the most thematic and realistic situation.<br /> <br /> Of course, since werewolves are not real, there is no strictly right or wrong answer, but that is how I would run it. As for Tribes that would be tolerant of transgender people, I would imagine that the Children of Gaia would be as well as Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine as long as it fits the rest of the story, but often a lot of the bigotry in Apocalypse specifically doesn't make sense. Example? The Get of Fenris White Supremacist model, as well as their own issues with gender. It doesn't make a whole lot of sense for werewolves to base so much of their world view on human institutions when they interact with spirits on a regular basis that prove those human models wrong. The Get of Fenris have Fenris for a tribal totem as well, not Odin. This is something that would horrify modern day Asatru types. There's plenty of reconstructionist teachings that revere the Jotuns, of whom Fenris is allegedly a descendant, and those beings were always far more tolerant of gender variance in general. It seems like that would be a lot more enticing to a human who grew up in a system where his instincts are wrong.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of the fact that there are lupines and metis who are just about as removed from those systems as one can be.<br /> <br /> The mention of using Weaver shenanigans is interesting, since in the regions Black Furies originally came from transgender women would remove their parts with shards of broken pottery and drink pregnant mare urine for the hormone content. That stuff was actually used in medicine up until very recently when we started just making it in a lab.<br /> <br /> So while you could argue that Weaver shenanigans = a lack of support from Black Furies, I'd argue that it would likely have no effect on how they view people who feel that way, and would instead reflect their esteem for those procedures, rather than going out into the woods, cutting things off in ritualistic fashion, and getting the hormones naturally, like from flax seeds and licorice root.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:59:59-07:00","id":978083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978071#post978071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would have the Black Furies dislike transgender people. Werewolf culture is extremely conservative as well as bigoted. Hating things that fall outside of their world view is one of the central elements of Garou culture and the Black Furies represent this more than most Tribes do. If I were running this in a game, I'd have the BF's consider a transwoman to be an abomination, perhaps Wyrm tainted - a man who thinks that he can use Weaver shenanigans to thwart the will of Gaia and violate the sacred feminine. I feel that making WoD splats overly tolerant may be projecting one's own beliefs onto these fictional groups in contradiction to what would likely be the most thematic and realistic situation.<br /> <br /> Of course, since werewolves are not real, there is no strictly right or wrong answer, but that is how I would run it. As for Tribes that would be tolerant of transgender people, I would imagine that the Children of Gaia would be as well as Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a counterpoint, the Greek mythology background of the Black Furies does sometimes suggest that Achilles was raised as a woman, if you're looking for precedent, and Cybele's priesthood consisted almost entirely of self-castrating individuals argued as trans or third-gender. &quot;Conservative&quot; does not have to mean intolerance of subverting the gender binary, as a great deal of non-Western cultures tells you. You're also gonna have a real hard time telling me the staunch young feminists who make up many of the modern Furies aren't going to be the intersectional sort, who are all for transwomen.<br /> <br /> But hey, I guess I'm just projecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-28-2016, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:15:37-07:00","id":978099,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978081#post978081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fine as long as it fits the rest of the story, but often a lot of the bigotry in Apocalypse specifically doesn't make sense. Example? The Get of Fenris White Supremacist model, as well as their own issues with gender. It doesn't make a whole lot of sense for werewolves to base so much of their world view on human institutions when they interact with spirits on a regular basis that prove those human models wrong. The Get of Fenris have Fenris for a tribal totem as well, not Odin. This is something that would horrify modern day Asatru types. There's plenty of reconstructionist teachings that revere the Jotuns, of whom Fenris is allegedly a descendant, and those beings were always far more tolerant of gender variance in general. It seems like that would be a lot more enticing to a human who grew up in a system where his instincts are wrong.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of the fact that there are lupines and metis who are just about as removed from those systems as one can be.<br /> <br /> The mention of using Weaver shenanigans is interesting, since in the regions Black Furies originally came from transgender women would remove their parts with shards of broken pottery and drink pregnant mare urine for the hormone content. That stuff was actually used in medicine up until very recently when we started just making it in a lab.<br /> <br /> So while you could argue that Weaver shenanigans = a lack of support from Black Furies, I'd argue that it would likely have no effect on how they view people who feel that way, and would instead reflect their esteem for those procedures, rather than going out into the woods, cutting things off in ritualistic fashion, and getting the hormones naturally, like from flax seeds and licorice root.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm torn about the racism thing. It seems like werewolves wouldn't really object to racism, but the form depicted as being a part of the GoF does seem like an extremely modern variant that would strike most werewolves as more silly than evil. One issue regarding the Get of Fenris is that they are more anti-Asatru than Asatru really, so it seems like appeals to Norse ancestors may not be appealing to them, since the Norse worshiped the bad guys essentially. <br /> <br /> I do think it would possible to come up with a somewhat reasonable thematic explanation for the BF tolerating transgender people, it's just not the way I would handle it in game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978077#post978077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, transgender people are real people who live in the real world, unlike Black Furies. Reproducing the same oppressive systems that exist in the real world in what's supposed to be fantasy escapism strikes me as a great way to alienate those real transgender people from the game. This would also make such a decision a terrible decision and maybe a different take would be more appropriate - one that doesn't cut transgender women out of Werewolf's definition of womanhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the conclusion you draw here is going to make for a ridiculous game. If that is your logic, then no in-game group should have any problems at all. All groups should be tolerant of everything and the world would be bright and shiny and the game would be about groups holding hands and singing Kumbaya. Werewolf Tribes aren't nice, they aren't tolerant. by most humans' standards, they are evil. I think trying to shoehorn tolerance onto them isn't appropriate. To a large extent, White Wolf games are about being an outsider, about not being tolerant. I would say that is a player wants his or her character to be tolerated by a Tribe, make a character from one of the Tribes which is explicitly supposed to be tolerant - like the Children of Gaia - not one of the least tolerant Tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978083#post978083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a counterpoint, the Greek mythology background of the Black Furies does sometimes suggest that Achilles was raised as a woman, if you're looking for precedent, and Cybele's priesthood consisted almost entirely of self-castrating individuals argued as trans or third-gender. &quot;Conservative&quot; does not have to mean intolerance of subverting the gender binary, as a great deal of non-Western cultures tells you. You're also gonna have a real hard time telling me the staunch young feminists who make up many of the modern Furies aren't going to bthe intersectional sort, who are all for transwomen.<br /> <br /> But hey, I guess I'm just projecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you probably are. I don't discount the possibility of non-binary gender ideas existing among ancient Greeks, but even if that was the case, I don't foresee that being accepted by such a sex/gender obsessed group as the BF. Staunch young feminists, assuming that you mean the kind of feminists that you might find on a college campus, are going to be outsiders, even heretics of sorts, among the BF. Any women with such belief systems as that are likely going to have to heavily readjust their worldview to fit into a group like the BF. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:16:12-07:00","id":978100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978052#post978052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> things CAN get too preachy, believe it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>E.g., what you're doing right here, complaining about this change being &quot;too progressive&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:24:58-07:00","id":978103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978052#post978052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was discussed in wolves and whiskey, the only woman Developer there was pretty heated on the issue.<br /> <br /> Richt Says he's gotten DEATH THREATS for stating he will do that in the new Werewolf LARP.<br /> <br /> If you want my opinion?<br /> <br /> I think its a little TOO Hellbent on saying &quot;Hey! Look how progressive we are!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> things CAN get too preachy, believe it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>This whole post is incredibly vague and seems to be trying to keep the issue at arm's length. What are you referring to with &quot;it&quot;? <i>What</i> has Rich gotten death threats for stating he will do? <i>What</i> is too hellbent on saying &quot;look how progressive we are&quot;? Why not say what you actually mean instead of trying to hide it behind a veil of ambiguity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:25:55-07:00","id":978105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978099#post978099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm torn about the racism thing. It seems like werewolves wouldn't really object to racism, but the form depicted as being a part of the GoF does seem like an extremely modern variant that would strike most werewolves as more silly than evil. One issue regarding the Get of Fenris is that they are more anti-Asatru than Asatru really, so it seems like appeals to Norse ancestors may not be appealing to them, since the Norse worshiped the bad guys essentially. <br /> <br /> I do think it would possible to come up with a somewhat reasonable thematic explanation for the BF tolerating transgender people, it's just not the way I would handle it in game. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think that the conclusion you draw here is going to make for a ridiculous game. If that is your logic, then no in-game group should have any problems at all. All groups should be tolerant of everything and the world would be bright and shiny and the game would be about groups holding hands and singing Kumbaya. Werewolf Tribes aren't nice, they aren't tolerant. by most humans' standards, they are evil. I think trying to shoehorn tolerance onto them isn't appropriate. To a large extent, White Wolf games are about being an outsider, about not being tolerant. I would say that is a player wants his or her character to be tolerated by a Tribe, make a character from one of the Tribes which is explicitly supposed to be tolerant - like the Children of Gaia - not one of the least tolerant Tribes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, you probably are. I don't discount the possibility of non-binary gender ideas existing among ancient Greeks, but even if that was the case, I don't foresee that being accepted by such a sex/gender obsessed group as the BF. Staunch young feminists, assuming that you mean the kind of feminists that you might find on a college campus, are going to be outsiders, even heretics of sorts, among the BF. Any women with such belief systems as that are likely going to have to heavily readjust their worldview to fit into a group like the BF. </div> </div> </div> </div>You're fighting real hard to say that an ancient group would have modern notions of gender, and then freely accuse others of projecting. Just think about that real quick.<br /> <br /> Would Hermaphroditus, child of two of the greatest Greek gods be seen as &quot;Wyrm-tainted&quot; to you? Would the venerable cult of Magna Mater, which spanned Greece and later Rome? Iphis, born a woman but raised as a man? The aforementioned Achilles? I'm real curious how you can say an ancient Greek faction would uphold your very modern, very Western, Christian, conservative viewpoint of gender, even before you factor in decades worth of intersectional feminists joining their ranks.<br /> <br /> If you want to argue that the Red Talons are transphobes, then you might have a chance. But not the Tribe that champions all women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-28-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:30:39-07:00","id":978107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978105#post978105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're fighting real hard to say that an ancient group would have modern notions of gender, and then freely accuse others of projecting. Just think about that real quick.<br /> <br /> Would Hermaphroditus, child of two of the greatest Greek gods be seen as &quot;Wyrm-tainted&quot; to you? Would the venerable cult of Magna Mater, which spanned Greece and later Rome? Iphis, born a woman but raised as a man? The aforementioned Achilles? I'm real curious how you can say an ancient Greek faction would uphold your very modern, very Christian viewpoint of gender, even before you factor in decades worth of intersectional feminists joining their ranks.<br /> <br /> If you want to argue that the Red Talons are transphobes, then you might have a chance. But not the Tribe that champions all women.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not fighting hard, I expressed an opinion of how I would handle the OP's question and people got mad about it. Would it be Wyrm tainted? There is no correct answer to that as the Wyrm is a fictional creature. I am certainly not using the BF, of all the strange Tribes to use, to be my mouthpiece. Nor am I trying to project my own notions of gender (which you have no idea about, by the way) onto ancient Greece, White Wolf's cosmology, or the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that some people have a need for WoD splats to completely reflect their own very modern liberal views about the world 100% and I don't feel like that makes any sense. A modern person should view any werewolf Tribe as highly problematic morally in many regards. It breaks suspension of disbelief to me that the BF should hold exactly the same ideology as a modern gender studies class at a university.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-28-2016, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:33:18-07:00","id":978108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978107#post978107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not fighting hard, I expressed an opinion of how I would handle the OP's question and people got mad about it. Would it be Wyrm tainted? There is no correct answer to that as the Wyrm is a fictional creature. I am certainly not using the BF, of all the strange Tribes to use, to be my mouthpiece. Nor am I trying to project my own notions of gender (which you have no idea about, by the way) onto ancient Greece, White Wolf's cosmology, or the Black Furies.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not using them as a moutpiece, just saying that they hate trans people and would reject &quot;college campus feminists,&quot; whatever the hell that means. Gotcha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:38:47-07:00","id":978110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978108#post978108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not using them as a moutpiece, just saying that they hate trans people and would reject &quot;college campus feminists,&quot; whatever the hell that means. Gotcha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why on earth would I use the Black Furies as a mouthpiece? If, for some bizarre reason, I were trying to express my hatred of trans people why would I choose the feminist Tribe to do it with while attributing tolerance of TG to more reasonable Tribes like the Children of Gaia, Bone Gnawers, or Glass Walkers? Why must you make this discussion of a fictional world about accusations of real life bigotry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:46:00-07:00","id":978113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978105#post978105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're fighting real hard to say that an ancient group would have modern notions of gender, and then freely accuse others of projecting. Just think about that real quick.<br /> <br /> Would Hermaphroditus, child of two of the greatest Greek gods be seen as &quot;Wyrm-tainted&quot; to you? Would the venerable cult of Magna Mater, which spanned Greece and later Rome? Iphis, born a woman but raised as a man? The aforementioned Achilles? I'm real curious how you can say an ancient Greek faction would uphold your very modern, very Western, Christian, conservative viewpoint of gender, even before you factor in decades worth of intersectional feminists joining their ranks.<br /> <br /> If you want to argue that the Red Talons are transphobes, then you might have a chance. But not the Tribe that champions all women.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I personally think Red Talons would be confounded by how much humans talk about gender in general, instead of just behaving in whatever way comes naturally to them. Transgender and homosexual behaviors exist in nature after all, but I doubt they care about it, or give it much thought. Some of the procedures I imagine would alarm them, but the lifespans of wolves are short and brutal enough that I doubt dysphoria really comes up too often.<br /> <br /> A lupus that changes and finds their sapience and increased lifespan turning an inconvenience into a source of real pain might be an interesting character idea, and if they were a Red Talon I imagine the elders would struggle to grapple with it, since so much of the vocabulary is just not part of their world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:46:45-07:00","id":978115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978099#post978099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm torn about the racism thing. It seems like werewolves wouldn't really object to racism, but the form depicted as being a part of the GoF does seem like an extremely modern variant that would strike most werewolves as more silly than evil. One issue regarding the Get of Fenris is that they are more anti-Asatru than Asatru really, so it seems like appeals to Norse ancestors may not be appealing to them, since the Norse worshiped the bad guys essentially.<br /> <br /> I do think it would possible to come up with a somewhat reasonable thematic explanation for the BF tolerating transgender people, it's just not the way I would handle it in game.<br /> <br /> I think that the conclusion you draw here is going to make for a ridiculous game. If that is your logic, then no in-game group should have any problems at all. All groups should be tolerant of everything and the world would be bright and shiny and the game would be about groups holding hands and singing Kumbaya. Werewolf Tribes aren't nice, they aren't tolerant. by most humans' standards, they are evil. I think trying to shoehorn tolerance onto them isn't appropriate. To a large extent, White Wolf games are about being an outsider, about not being tolerant. I would say that is a player wants his or her character to be tolerated by a Tribe, make a character from one of the Tribes which is explicitly supposed to be tolerant - like the Children of Gaia - not one of the least tolerant Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>What they are and aren't tolerant of tends to be very weird to human cultures and based on what kind of spirits they have truck with, not some bizarre and pseudo-archaic standard of &quot;the pre-industrial world was incredibly intolerant because the Victorians made revisionist material that said so&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, you probably are. I don't discount the possibility of non-binary gender ideas existing among ancient Greeks, but even if that was the case, I don't foresee that being accepted by such a sex/gender obsessed group as the BF. Staunch young feminists, assuming that you mean the kind of feminists that you might find on a college campus, are going to be outsiders, even heretics of sorts, among the BF. Any women with such belief systems as that are likely going to have to heavily readjust their worldview to fit into a group like the BF. </div> </div> </div>BF society strongly frowns on establishing &quot;heretic&quot; status. Even if it might seem at odds with the Revised TB, recall that even that book had the Furies express a profound dislike of witch hunt-type activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:47:45-07:00","id":978116,"title":"","content":"Black Furies celebrate the feminine to the exclusion of the masculine, so a male rejecting the masculine in favor of the feminine to the degree of a transwoman would probably be considered to be a good, if unusual, convert to the cause (the inability to reproduce would be a minor issue, but there are always more men who can reproduce with Garou females). They would probably not be as forgiving towards transmen though, as a female rejecting the feminine in favor of the masculine to the degree of transmen would probably be considered to be a traitor to the cause (the inability to reproduce would be a major issues because women capable of bearing Garou without a Garou males are uncommon). Of course, this is a Kinfolk issue because, quite frankly, the regenerative capabilities of the Garou would prevent them from changing their sex without some interesting form of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:48:43-07:00","id":978117,"title":"","content":"This is a controversial issue and there is not going to be a consensus. Discussion on this is simply going to become a discussion on current politics about transgenderism. Different people are going to be vastly different in terms on where they come down. If you want to include this in the game for whatever reason, the discussion you should have is with your gaming group - not people who won't be playing in your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:51:13-07:00","id":978119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978116#post978116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Furies celebrate the feminine to the exclusion of the masculine, so a male rejecting the masculine in favor of the feminine to the degree of a transwoman would probably be considered to be a good, if unusual, convert to the cause (the inability to reproduce would be a minor issue, but there are always more men who can reproduce with Garou females). They would probably not be as forgiving towards transmen though, as a female rejecting the feminine in favor of the masculine to the degree of transmen would probably be considered to be a traitor to the cause (the inability to reproduce would be a major issues because women capable of bearing Garou without a Garou males are uncommon). Of course, this is a Kinfolk issue because, quite frankly, the regenerative capabilities of the Garou would prevent them from changing their sex without some interesting form of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue a sex change would be a fairly simple ritual, and likely one well old in the minds of the Black Furies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:52:16-07:00","id":978120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978107#post978107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not fighting hard, I expressed an opinion of how I would handle the OP's question and people got mad about it. Would it be Wyrm tainted? There is no correct answer to that as the Wyrm is a fictional creature. I am certainly not using the BF, of all the strange Tribes to use, to be my mouthpiece. Nor am I trying to project my own notions of gender (which you have no idea about, by the way) onto ancient Greece, White Wolf's cosmology, or the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that some people have a need for WoD splats to completely reflect their own very modern liberal views about the world 100% and I don't feel like that makes any sense. A modern person should view any werewolf Tribe as highly problematic morally in many regards. It breaks suspension of disbelief to me that the BF should hold exactly the same ideology as a modern gender studies class at a university.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you're probably not referring to me, personally, but I don't really consider accepting of transgender behaviors to be a necessary modern mindset, especially considering their relationship to Pegasus, and their own male metis. A lot of the hangs up 'are' relatively modern when taken in the context of all of human history, which leaves a lot of room for variance. Loki switches sex constantly, and has been a mother at least twice that I can recall off hand. Odin learned woman's magic by dressing as a woman and in a sense, becoming one. Thor had his magical journey with aunt Loki as well. The Greeks have just as many myths and stories where someone crosses that boundary once or twice, Rome had the Cybele worshipers, the being that went down to the underworld to save Ishtar does not fit a binary gender system, and the myth ties how often they are treated poorly by their families and society, and so on. <br /> <br /> My only point of consternation with you so far is you keep saying that word - 'Modern', when it's anything but.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:52:23-07:00","id":978121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978117#post978117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a controversial issue and there is not going to be a consensus. Discussion on this is simply going to become a discussion on current politics about transgenderism. Different people are going to be vastly different in terms on where they come down. If you want to include this in the game for whatever reason, the discussion you should have is with your gaming group - not people who won't be playing in your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can certainly agree with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:54:44-07:00","id":978122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978099#post978099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the conclusion you draw here is going to make for a ridiculous game. If that is your logic, then no in-game group should have any problems at all. All groups should be tolerant of everything and the world would be bright and shiny and the game would be about groups holding hands and singing Kumbaya. Werewolf Tribes aren't nice, they aren't tolerant. by most humans' standards, they are evil. I think trying to shoehorn tolerance onto them isn't appropriate. To a large extent, White Wolf games are about being an outsider, about not being tolerant.I would say that is a player wants his or her character to be tolerated by a Tribe, make a character from one of the Tribes which is explicitly supposed to be tolerant - like the Children of Gaia - not one of the least tolerant Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're drawing a conclusion I never hinted at. I specifically referred to not excluding transgender women from the definition of &quot;woman&quot; in Werewolf, which is specifically being allowed membership in the Black Furies. I explained why I see this as more appropriate than your suggestion to basically use Black Furies to smack trans women down. I didn't say that nothing bad would ever happen or that everyone has to be tolerant of everything. What I specifically said was about providing a welcoming gaming environment, something that people should really be open to if they genuinely want people to play games with them. What you want is the opposite of that, probably not a great loss to you, but it sort of betrays a certain attitude about who should be welcome where.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:56:06-07:00","id":978123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978121#post978121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can certainly agree with this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978117#post978117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a controversial issue and there is not going to be a consensus. Discussion on this is simply going to become a discussion on current politics about transgenderism. Different people are going to be vastly different in terms on where they come down. If you want to include this in the game for whatever reason, the discussion you should have is with your gaming group - not people who won't be playing in your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>An issue is contentious so let's not discuss it? How is that rational or sensible? You basically just said that you're not convinced you will sway anyone with your arguments, so talking about the issue is pointless. That's not really how this works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:56:58-07:00","id":978124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978122#post978122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're drawing a conclusion I never hinted at. I specifically referred to not excluding transgender women from the definition of &amp;quot;woman&amp;quot; in Werewolf, which is specifically being allowed membership in the Black Furies. I explained why I see this as more appropriate than your suggestion to basically use Black Furies to smack trans women down. I didn't say that nothing bad would ever happen or that everyone has to be tolerant of everything. What I specifically said was about providing a welcoming gaming environment, something that people should really be open to if they genuinely want people to play games with them. What you want is the opposite of that, probably not a great loss to you, but it sort of betrays a certain attitude about who should be welcome where.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Trans women only have a place in the &quot;hippie&quot; and cutting edge Tribes&quot; basically says &quot;trans people a a new thing invented by young people,&quot; and barring them from thr Black Furies is to deny the concept of being a trans woman a place in history or tradition... even among the champions of women of all stripes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:58:01-07:00","id":978125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978119#post978119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue a sex change would be a fairly simple ritual, and likely one well old in the minds of the Black Furies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artemis did it to a guy named Sipriotes, so yeah, I doubt drawing on the weight of that myth would be hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:09:25-07:00","id":978129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978124#post978124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Trans women only have a place in the &quot;hippie&quot; and cutting edge Tribes&quot; basically says &quot;trans people a a new thing invented by young people,&quot; and barring them from thr Black Furies is to deny the concept of being a trans woman a place in history or tradition... even among the champions of women of all stripes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem with this is that the Black Furies - like all the Tribes - have a disconnect between their ideology and their actions as presented.<br /> <br /> If I were redoing the game, I would change the way the Furies are written to get rid of their incredibly TERF 1e/2e presentation that Rev./W20 could only do so much to mitigate.<br /> <br /> That doesn't really change how the game was written though. I see a lot of reasons for why the way they were written was problematic and great ideas of material to draw on to make a better version of the Black Furies that's not just &quot;shove modern sensibilities on them,&quot; and is really drawing on a long history of cultural inspirations that the game as written just doesn't do.<br /> <br /> Transwomen having their easiest place in the Children of Gaia, Glass Walkers, and Bone Gnawers is what the state of the Tribes as written leaves us as the logical conclusion. I really wish this wasn't the case (I think it's obvious that we're not alone because the BNS Werewolf book already moved in this direction), but that's how the game is written: the leadership of the Black Furies has traditionally gone to gender essentialists that didn't see protected transwomen as part of their sacred duty because they wouldn't acknowledge them as women.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, fixing it isn't hard. Which perhaps should be the thrust of the thread rather than arguing over how things &quot;should be&quot; when trying to integrate the way the books were written with what we know makes far more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:13:47-07:00","id":978133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978129#post978129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the problem with this is that the Black Furies - like all the Tribes - have a disconnect between their ideology and their actions as presented.<br /> <br /> If I were redoing the game, I would change the way the Furies are written to get rid of their incredibly TERF 1e/2e presentation that Rev./W20 could only do so much to mitigate.<br /> <br /> That doesn't really change how the game was written though. I see a lot of reasons for why the way they were written was problematic and great ideas of material to draw on to make a better version of the Black Furies that's not just &amp;quot;shove modern sensibilities on them,&amp;quot; and is really drawing on a long history of cultural inspirations that the game as written just doesn't do.<br /> <br /> Transwomen having their easiest place in the Children of Gaia, Glass Walkers, and Bone Gnawers is what the state of the Tribes as written leaves us as the logical conclusion. I really wish this wasn't the case (I think it's obvious that we're not alone because the BNS Werewolf book already moved in this direction), but that's how the game is written: the leadership of the Black Furies has traditionally gone to gender essentialists that didn't see protected transwomen as part of their sacred duty because they wouldn't acknowledge them as women.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, fixing it isn't hard. Which perhaps should be the thrust of the thread rather than arguing over how things &amp;quot;should be&amp;quot; when trying to integrate the way the books were written with what we know makes far more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a compelling case to be made that the younger, newer members of the tribe are much more LGBT-friendly, in order to reflect the shifting focus of feminism over the last few decades and as queer identities have (re)gained a lot of legitimacy, and you could pit that against a more essentialist bunch of elders as a pretty solid narrative.<br /> <br /> That they're arguing about who is and isn't a women instead of fighting the Wyrm is also a valid topic, and again makes for interesting material. &quot;You're turning away people willing to fight and die for us because they don't have a vagina? We're a dying breed, and you won't accept new warriors because of something as trite as their organs?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:17:49-07:00","id":978135,"title":"","content":"I would add that while I do not have a problem with the Black Furies as including Transwomen I very well could see them marginalizing them to the point that male Metis are treated better.<br /> <br /> I agree that Children of Gaia, Glasswalkers, and Bone Gnawers would more likely be more welcoming than the Black Furies. I would also add the Uktena and Wendigo tribes to the list that would be more accepting of Trans individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:18:31-07:00","id":978136,"title":"","content":"Just personally, I think some Black Furies accept trans people and some don't. and it has nothing to do with who and what kind of garou/people these transwomen are.<br /> <br /> Black Furies are portrayed often being at schism with each other, the younger generations wanting to be progressive while the older ones being more focused on ancient traditions. And often it can be confusing which side accepts which thing. Generally, I think transwomen are accepted, but sometimes grudgingly by both sides. Ancient traditions support trans people, but there are Crone Furies who see their rites and gifts so sacred that any man seeing them is a crime. Meanwhile, some Maidens are progressive thinkers and some might see changing ones gender as a perversion.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the tribe is in general like that, and I think involving trans people in the game with Furies can lead to good discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:37:44-07:00","id":978147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978135#post978135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add that while I do not have a problem with the Black Furies as including Transwomen I very well could see them marginalizing them to the point that male Metis are treated better.<br /> <br /> I agree that Children of Gaia, Glasswalkers, and Bone Gnawers would more likely be more welcoming than the Black Furies. I would also add the Uktena and Wendigo tribes to the list that would be more accepting of Trans individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Metis are pretty marginalized in general, would you be willing to elucidate as to why they're more marginalized, and in what ways?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978136#post978136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just personally, I think some Black Furies accept trans people and some don't. and it has nothing to do with who and what kind of garou/people these transwomen are.<br /> <br /> Black Furies are portrayed often being at schism with each other, the younger generations wanting to be progressive while the older ones being more focused on ancient traditions. And often it can be confusing which side accepts which thing. Generally, I think transwomen are accepted, but sometimes grudgingly by both sides. Ancient traditions support trans people, but there are Crone Furies who see their rites and gifts so sacred that any man seeing them is a crime. Meanwhile, some Maidens are progressive thinkers and some might see changing ones gender as a perversion.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the tribe is in general like that, and I think involving trans people in the game with Furies can lead to good discussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually glad you mentioned that, because Black Furies do have that vengeful 'no man must see these rites' side to them. It's worth noting that when Artemis was caught in one of her sacred springs, the 'punishment' was being turned into a woman, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":".  Adding a quote instead of double posting. 09-28-2016, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:50:06-07:00","id":978152,"title":"","content":"I think both Sergeant Brother and Atamajakki raise good points. I understand and would agree with his notions on what tribes would accept LGBTQ people. And I think he's right about the Black Furies as a whole.<br /> <br /> At the same time, Atamajakki's ideas about newer BF's being more inclusive is possible, too(though I'd say it with a bit less vitriol as it seems some are taking this way too personal). There's plenty of stories in there for this as well.<br /> <br /> But like Heavy Arms said, nothing wrong with creating and playing your game the way you want to play it. My ST makes changes to the game all the time; most of which he runs by the group to make sure we're okay with them. In the end, this is the World of Darkness. In the end, I want my games to be darker, more crime ridden, more disease filled, more sexist, more racist, and more angrier and hateful than the real world. This is my escapism, and I play it as such.<br /> <br /> Now excuse me, Mario Kart is calling my name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T20:00:11-07:00","id":978156,"title":"","content":"The Black Furies are divided over abortion I can easily see the Black Furies being just as divided over Trans members. For Example: While Pegasus accepts Trans women the crones of the Sept of Pearl Lake hold that only Woman born of Woman are allowed access to the Heart of the Caern and the healing waters that flow from the spring. Metis males are allowed to guard the bawn of the Caern and at certain times even view the Heart of the Caern, but any Trans woman is barred from entry. The Sept of Healing Minds based in an abuse shelter however openly welcomes Trans members and allows Leta to hold the position of Gatekeeper an important position as the Sept focuses on abused women and more than once has sheltered an abused kinfolk in the Caern.<br /> The issue of Trans Members is going to be Sept by Sept and even to a degree pack by pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T20:33:35-07:00","id":978163,"title":"","content":"Hm, how exactly are we getting transwomen among the Garou again? I doubt that hormone replacement and gender reassignment surgery is going to be effective against Garou healing. Any magical transformation would probably be complete genetic transformation, male sex to female sex, and I doubt that any Black Fury would care about the origin of a member if she can give birth to new Garou (and Kinfolk).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T20:39:14-07:00","id":978166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978163#post978163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, how exactly are we getting transwomen among the Garou again? I doubt that hormone replacement and gender reassignment surgery is going to be effective against Garou healing. Any magical transformation would probably be complete genetic transformation, male sex to female sex, and I doubt that any Black Fury would care about the origin of a member if she can give birth to new Garou (and Kinfolk).</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinfolk, and not all garou interaction is between garou. That said, a garou could be transgender without having surgery or hormone therapy (as for how could it be effective, they're hormones... they're functionally identical to what his or her body would be producing if they were the opposite sex. It's not the same thing as intoxicating yourself with alcohol and marijuana, estrogen feminizes the body because they communicate to the body that that is what it needs to do, and anti-androgens block masculinization because they bind to those receptor sites and trick it.So if anything Garou regeneration just means that treatment could theoretically go more smoothly than it does for humans.) <br /> <br /> Also rituals, fetishes, and spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T20:40:48-07:00","id":978168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978163#post978163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, how exactly are we getting transwomen among the Garou again? I doubt that hormone replacement and gender reassignment surgery is going to be effective against Garou healing. Any magical transformation would probably be complete genetic transformation, male sex to female sex, and I doubt that any Black Fury would care about the origin of a member if she can give birth to new Garou (and Kinfolk).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still a transwoman well before you do any of those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:32:00-07:00","id":978219,"title":"","content":"From my understanding Black Furies are not just about gender but also about Sex. They allow Metis in, and only sometimes, because they are sterile and therefore one step removed from masculine energies in that they cannot impregnate. Garou Culture is heavily hammered into the reproduction aspect, to the point were even if you are gay you need to produce as many children as you can.<br /> <br /> I feel it would be welcome if you are a metis and are transgender, but not a homid.<br /> <br /> I believe the metis thing also ties into Tireisias and the Hermaphroditic thing.<br /> <br /> If a Black Fury got a woman pregnant without using some sort of wyld magic... it feels like it would be an abomination to their sensibilities. They are particularly tied to the whole waxing and waning of the Moons and Menstruation thing, as well as giving birth.<br /> <br /> Its a big deal to be sterile in the Garou Nation, they aren't a human culture they don't have to be PC. Get Pegasus to accept you and you are in, but as it is Pegasus seems to have disdain for functional testicles. <br /> <br /> Also ancient forms of Transgender are not the same as modern societies, often they could represent different outlets, for instance when your gender is not chosen by you but instead by others, or for cultures where you had to become one gender for certain rights, similar to how Exalted handles the Lyta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:35:02-07:00","id":978221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978166#post978166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinfolk, and not all garou interaction is between garou. That said, a garou could be transgender without having surgery or hormone therapy (as for how could it be effective, they're hormones... they're functionally identical to what his or her body would be producing if they were the opposite sex. It's not the same thing as intoxicating yourself with alcohol and marijuana, estrogen feminizes the body because they communicate to the body that that is what it needs to do, and anti-androgens block masculinization because they bind to those receptor sites and trick it.So if anything Garou regeneration just means that treatment could theoretically go more smoothly than it does for humans.)<br /> <br /> Also rituals, fetishes, and spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Garou healing counteracts imbalances, your body produces adrenaline, but Garou regen can work to nullify an external shot of it. Hell with gifts like resist Toxin you even ignore bear mace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:40:01-07:00","id":978225,"title":"","content":"It depends on your definition. Transsexual refers to someone who is undergoing hormonal and/or physical transformation (transgender is the term for someone born the wrong sex who may or may not be transsexual). As for the transformation process, I imagine that it would be rejected by the healing factor of the Garou because it is a change from their physical form. Unless they did the surgery with silver tools, it will heal, and I can see no practical way that hormone therapy will not be rejected like any other chemical toxin. <br /> <br /> Of course, the Garou probably can use magic to truly change sexes, so it would be rather silly to call them trans- anything. Yes, they may have been born a male but, after they give birth to their first child, I do not think anyone will really care. I do wonder if they would be willing to use that magic on their Kinfolk? If so, it would make life a lot simpler for transgender Kinfolk because they could truly become their desired sex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:41:42-07:00","id":978226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978135#post978135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add that while I do not have a problem with the Black Furies as including Transwomen I very well could see them marginalizing them to the point that male Metis are treated better.<br /> <br /> I agree that Children of Gaia, Glasswalkers, and Bone Gnawers would more likely be more welcoming than the Black Furies. I would also add the Uktena and Wendigo tribes to the list that would be more accepting of Trans individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would add Stargazers to this list. In fact I would say Children of Gaia, Uktena and Stargazers first, with Glasswalkers, Bone Gnawers and Wendigo 2nd. To the first three it shouldn't matter and their tribal philosophy as a whole reflects that, with the last three the over all tribal philosophy would be accepting, but it would also be accepting of people bigoted against it for whatever reason, what with Gangster sensibilities and breeding emphasis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:45:45-07:00","id":978228,"title":"","content":"Also noting that Vampires of the Bahari, for very similar reason to why the Furies accept Metis, view birth sex as rather moot because they are essentially sexless because they are corpses and thus have nothing but gender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:57:33-07:00","id":978237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978221#post978221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Garou healing counteracts imbalances, your body produces adrenaline, but Garou regen can work to nullify an external shot of it. Hell with gifts like resist Toxin you even ignore bear mace.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware of that, certainly it's not how it works in Werewolf the Forsaken, which I played before approaching this. Thanks for the heads up, though of course it doesn't really address the possibility of awakened drugs, rituals, fetishes, etc. It seems pretty unrealistic to me that a race of consummate shapechangers would be stuck, though that would serve as a source of irony in a story where that has value.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T23:55:49-07:00","id":978248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978133#post978133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a compelling case to be made that the younger, newer members of the tribe are much more LGBT-friendly, in order to reflect the shifting focus of feminism over the last few decades and as queer identities have (re)gained a lot of legitimacy, and you could pit that against a more essentialist bunch of elders as a pretty solid narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. It's the case I made in my first post on the old thread that was linked to in the first post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978221#post978221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou healing counteracts imbalances, your body produces adrenaline, but Garou regen can work to nullify an external shot of it. Hell with gifts like resist Toxin you even ignore bear mace.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually one of the issues with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978226#post978226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add Stargazers to this list. In fact I would say Children of Gaia, Uktena and Stargazers first, with Glasswalkers, Bone Gnawers and Wendigo 2nd. To the first three it shouldn't matter and their tribal philosophy as a whole reflects that, with the last three the over all tribal philosophy would be accepting, but it would also be accepting of people bigoted against it for whatever reason, what with Gangster sensibilities and breeding emphasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gnawers and the Walkers are the two Garou groups least concerned with the &quot;spiritual sacredness&quot; of the body. They're explicitly called out as the two Tribes that don't face Renown issues for using Rites on things all the other Tribes would look down on (such as medical technology).<br /> <br /> One of the reasons the Glass Walkers are put to the front of the line, is because they'd have zero issue using magical means to overcome a Garou's innate resistance to surgery or drugs, as well as have the resources to make it happen. The Glass Walkers have a Camp that's focused on cybernetic implants; hormone therapy and sexual reassignment surgery is nothing compared to grafting an artificial limb onto a stub that's fully functional as a normal limb (if not superior) in all five forms. To an extent this is less, &quot;The Glass Walkers would purposefully recruit trans Garou,&quot; but more, &quot;trans Garou would feel like the Glass Walkers are the only ones that can provide what they really want.&quot;<br /> <br /> This also gets to an issue with adding the Stargazers, Wendigo, and Uktena to the list. The Uktena are sort of on the fence since they're philosophically closer to the Children of Gaia in many ways, but a lot of modern trans people do not identify with various cultural practices that have overlap is trans identity expression. An Uktena cross dressing contrary Ragabash is playing a role, not inherently expressing who they are. There might be some trans Garou that are OK with filling that role being an adequate expression of who they are, but many will not; and a significant portion will not want to be forced into such specific roles (esp. since those roles are very heavily weighted to specific Auspices) at the expense of other parts of their identities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T00:15:12-07:00","id":978249,"title":"","content":"Ok Solana, as someone who wears the hammer here, I strongly urge you to read proper archeology on Norse culture and not to accept the current tumblr understanding on what they considered a cultural norm 1000 years ago.<br /> <br /> Thor dressed as a woman is supposed to be a comedy, it's humiliating for him. Not a norm. Odin learning female magic is a sign of his obsession with knowledge and how far he's willing to go. It's still heavily frowned upon. It's why Loki uses it to insult him in lokesenna. Loki is the only one to actively switch genders and we've seen how the gods view him.<br /> <br /> Tales written about the gods, potentially written by Christians defaming them to make christ look more glorious (iirc this is where bringsamen comes from) must be examined more closely then a social justice issue.<br /> <br /> And I believe ana mizuki has the right of it. This would come down to a generational difference between the tribes. Might even be its own sect to avoid elder scorn. It would also be a homid only deal. I cant imagine a lupus garou being concerned about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 09-29-2016, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T00:34:29-07:00","id":978255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978249#post978249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok Solana, as someone who wears the hammer here, I strongly urge you to read proper archeology on Norse culture and not to accept the current tumblr understanding on what they considered a cultural norm 1000 years ago.<br /> <br /> Thor dressed as a woman is supposed to be a comedy, it's humiliating for him. Not a norm. Odin learning female magic is a sign of his obsession with knowledge and how far he's willing to go. It's still heavily frowned upon. It's why Loki uses it to insult him in lokesenna. Loki is the only one to actively switch genders and we've seen how the gods view him.<br /> <br /> Tales written about the gods, potentially written by Christians defaming them to make christ look more glorious (iirc this is where bringsamen comes from) must be examined more closely then a social justice issue.<br /> <br /> And I believe ana mizuki has the right of it. This would come down to a generational difference between the tribes. Might even be its own sect to avoid elder scorn. It would also be a homid only deal. I cant imagine a lupus garou being concerned about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't appreciate assuming my views on the culture are based on tumblrisms, when you know nothing about me or my web browsing habits. My views are based on the sagas, sure, but the Archeology, as you put it, has several burial sites in the region where bodies with male body types were found buried in dresses, adorned with feminine belongings, so on and so forth. I never suggested that Thor's little adventure wasn't a comedy, that it wasn't embarassing for him, as surely it would be because he is not a transgender figure. As for how the gods viewed Loki - he was Odin's blood brother, and was allowed to dwell in Asgard. Whatever shit he might have gotten from the Aesir that says a great deal about his status. Odin's motives for doing it are immaterial, because the point wasn't that it was encouraged, the point was that in the minds of the people who told those tales, it was a boundary that could be crossed, and the person doing it could still be respected afterward. <br /> <br /> And as you pointed out, nearly all our accounts of the society and culture are from early Christian historians, who were so audacious as to shove Jesus into a poem about sacred healing herbs. If you look closely enough there are plenty of elements of Norse mythology that lend to shamanism, and when you take my statement in context that is far more appropriate for a game of Werewolf than strictly adhering to what Christians said a people they barely understood felt over a thousand years ago. A lot of the gaps when you're crafting an understanding of what they 'might' have been like before the Christians, before the point where many of these people stopped believing in their own legends in the first place if records are true, would be to pull from tribal societies in the same region, like the Saami people further North, <br /> <br /> I also don't think it's appropriate to brand it as me trying to insert Social Justice issues into societies, especially when someone is postulating what a tribal Norse society might have been like, as many of the spirits in this game would be <b>from</b> that time. Issues of gender are commonplace in those societies, almost all of the ones I've read at least, and in most cases if the gods or spirits want you to be a girl or a man, you put on a dress or pants and you do it.<br /> <br /> I apologize if some of them came across as a bit heated, I simply felt that my intentions were misrepresented by your statement, and in this particular instance it's hard to feel like that wasn't intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T01:03:40-07:00","id":978262,"title":"","content":"Saami culture is and was different from the Norse. There may be some overlap at the boundaries, but there's a definite separation. A better examination at true pre-christian Scandinavia would involve a multi disciplinary research of archaeology and historical research, going back several centuries if not millennia. The Saami aren't a good example of their ways, it would be like assuming the finns are Scandinavian. As I understand it they are not. Similar region, different life styles and gods. <br /> <br /> I'm curious to see the sources of the burial sites of men dressed as women. I haven't seen that in any of my research, unless it's a recent find. I've heard of the study saying half of Vikings buried were women, but that study was heavily misrepresented, and consisted of a very small sample size in the Dane law (13 graves I believe, out of a population of thousands), half of those burials may have been women, but there was nothing to say they were Vikings. They used buzzwords to make their research zing and people ran with it.<br /> <br /> And it's exactly that that fires me up about it. I can't read anything about Norse culture without people making wide ranging assumptions and using the old tales out of context. People are viewing it through a 2016 lense and assuming we're of the same mind as our ancestors and thus it all must mean the same thing. It certainly does not. It assumes that human mind sets haven't changed in over 1000 years, and obviously we have. Hell look at the last 10 years. <br /> <br /> Bearing in mind this has nothing to do with the transgender topic at hand and entirely my annoyance at people's lack of cultural understanding. I suppose you'd say I was triggered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" 