Dane law (13 graves I believe, out of a population of thousands), half of those burials may have been women, but there was nothing to say they were Vikings. They used buzzwords to make their research zing and people ran with it.<br /> <br /> And it's exactly that that fires me up about it. I can't read anything about Norse culture without people making wide ranging assumptions and using the old tales out of context. People are viewing it through a 2016 lense and assuming we're of the same mind as our ancestors and thus it all must mean the same thing. It certainly does not. It assumes that human mind sets haven't changed in over 1000 years, and obviously we have. Hell look at the last 10 years. <br /> <br /> Bearing in mind this has nothing to do with the transgender topic at hand and entirely my annoyance at people's lack of cultural understanding. I suppose you'd say I was triggered.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make all these valid points and then throw it out the window by shitting on trigger warnings for no reason. Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T02:38:31-07:00","id":978289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978262#post978262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saami culture is and was different from the Norse. There may be some overlap at the boundaries, but there's a definite separation. A better examination at true pre-christian Scandinavia would involve a multi disciplinary research of archaeology and historical research, going back several centuries if not millennia. The Saami aren't a good example of their ways, it would be like assuming the finns are Scandinavian. As I understand it they are not. Similar region, different life styles and gods.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see the sources of the burial sites of men dressed as women. I haven't seen that in any of my research, unless it's a recent find. I've heard of the study saying half of Vikings buried were women, but that study was heavily misrepresented, and consisted of a very small sample size in the Dane law (13 graves I believe, out of a population of thousands), half of those burials may have been women, but there was nothing to say they were Vikings. They used buzzwords to make their research zing and people ran with it.<br /> <br /> And it's exactly that that fires me up about it. I can't read anything about Norse culture without people making wide ranging assumptions and using the old tales out of context. People are viewing it through a 2016 lense and assuming we're of the same mind as our ancestors and thus it all must mean the same thing. It certainly does not. It assumes that human mind sets haven't changed in over 1000 years, and obviously we have. Hell look at the last 10 years.<br /> <br /> Bearing in mind this has nothing to do with the transgender topic at hand and entirely my annoyance at people's lack of cultural understanding. I suppose you'd say I was triggered.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't that hard to find references to the sources on burial sites. I mean I found it pretty easily googling the other day.<br /> <br /> I mean I'd share some links myself but I don't want to &quot;trigger&quot; you (and atamajakki is right to call you out on that comment).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T03:15:14-07:00","id":978297,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms touched on it slightly, but just a reminder... when the game was first written (by authors who probably didn't have degrees in the historical groups the tribes were mimicking, and 15 years before anyone could just look it all up on their phone) most of the Garou were the BAD GUYS. I can't stress that enough... a major plot point of the game was that the Garou were mostly to blame for everything being as bad as it was, but they're the only ones still around to fix it (also their fault).... and they weren't about to get their act together any time soon. Supernatural Rage left most Garou presented as super-charged racists, bigots and abusers... with the PCs as perhaps the sole beacons of hope along with a select few NPCs. The World of Darkness, and especially Garou, were a caricature of everything an angst-ridden Nine-Inch-Nails fan from the 90s would say was wrong with America (because the game was written from a pretty American perspective, as well).<br /> <br /> So, in a game world designed to highlight the frustration of beating your head against stubborn ignorance and unapologetic ego, the question of how a Tribe would react to anything would have been pretty clear: whatever the worse answer is. (And for the most part, this is still the answer I choose)<br /> <br /> Of course there have been rewrites, retcons, new authors, more research, and even new discoveries in the cultures and mythologies involved. If you know more about a culture than the authors (which you well could... they're RPG authors, not gods) then you might want to adjust your game setting to make more sense in that capacity. If you want a more progressive game where Garou are sensible, thinking people rather than the biggest obstacles to their own success... go for it.<br /> <br /> Just keep in mind that there have been very stark changes in a lot of elements over the course of 4 editions and 24 years. Any forum-goer's opinions of what makes sense for Garou was probably forged by the first book they picked up, not the most recent one they own. I probably own every WtA book ever written, but I can say for certain I haven't reread the fluff chapters end-to-end four times, nor has all the new stuff effectively overwritten the old in my mind.<br /> <br /> A lot of the game we play today is layers of band aids wrapped around nostalgia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:05:57-07:00","id":978408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978249#post978249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok Solana, as someone who wears the hammer here, I strongly urge you to read proper archeology on Norse culture and not to accept the current tumblr understanding on what they considered a cultural norm 1000 years ago.<br /> <br /> Thor dressed as a woman is supposed to be a comedy, it's humiliating for him. Not a norm. Odin learning female magic is a sign of his obsession with knowledge and how far he's willing to go. It's still heavily frowned upon. It's why Loki uses it to insult him in lokesenna. Loki is the only one to actively switch genders and we've seen how the gods view him.</div> </div> </div> </div>In which case it still works out, because the Get hate the Aesir and want to kill them (if they haven't already put that to bed in ages past), being descended from the being that the pagan cultures in the region saw as the worst thing ever and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T09:35:50-07:00","id":978448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978262#post978262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saami culture is and was different from the Norse. There may be some overlap at the boundaries, but there's a definite separation. A better examination at true pre-christian Scandinavia would involve a multi disciplinary research of archaeology and historical research, going back several centuries if not millennia. The Saami aren't a good example of their ways, it would be like assuming the finns are Scandinavian. As I understand it they are not. Similar region, different life styles and gods.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see the sources of the burial sites of men dressed as women. I haven't seen that in any of my research, unless it's a recent find. I've heard of the study saying half of Vikings buried were women, but that study was heavily misrepresented, and consisted of a very small sample size in the Dane law (13 graves I believe, out of a population of thousands), half of those burials may have been women, but there was nothing to say they were Vikings. They used buzzwords to make their research zing and people ran with it.<br /> <br /> And it's exactly that that fires me up about it. I can't read anything about Norse culture without people making wide ranging assumptions and using the old tales out of context. People are viewing it through a 2016 lense and assuming we're of the same mind as our ancestors and thus it all must mean the same thing. It certainly does not. It assumes that human mind sets haven't changed in over 1000 years, and obviously we have. Hell look at the last 10 years.<br /> <br /> Bearing in mind this has nothing to do with the transgender topic at hand and entirely my annoyance at people's lack of cultural understanding. I suppose you'd say I was triggered.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's alright, it's an interesting enough tangent, and relevant, based on some of my <i>claims</i> earlier. <br /> <br /> I cannot personally find where I've read about the burial sites I mentioned, and don't really have time to provide evidence for it that would satisfy me, because I'm not going to just post a wikipedia or news article at you. I've got some urgent stuff to deal with later and it would derail the thread a bit further, but here are some book links? <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">https://goo.gl/Vb3daE</span></span><br /> <br /> There's also: <b>In Pursuit of Gender: Worldwide Archaeological Approaches</b><br /><br />Which unfortunately doesn't have any of the relevant information on Google Books (you'd have to buy it/check it out).<br /> <br /> As for the Saami people, they occupied/occupy parts of Northern Scandinavia, Norway, etc, the sorts of places where worshipers of Skadi likely existed. Understand that when I'm doing this, or proposing this in a forum set in a fictionalized universe parallel to our own that I'm not trying to detract from academics or people who make this subject their job. Even using inter-disciplinaryism there is going to be a lot of gaps when you're trying to reconstruct a tribal society for a game about tribal shapeshifters. The Saami people are conveniently more or less present still, which helps. In the context of Werewolf (The Forsaken, so far, I'm still grappling with learning Apocalypse's Cosmology and how to portray it, that's partially why this thread exists) I do borrow from those things, and also go with the assumption that Jotuns represent Hunter-Gather gods, the Vanir became the norm when agriculture took off, and the Aesir supplanted them (literally, in the sagas) when cities and war became more commonplace. <br /> <br /> Which considering the nature of werewolves and the fact that their tribal totem is Fenris, means I try to go with a tribal reconstructionist view toward Get of Fenris, instead of making them Supremacists, or Asatru.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I wasn't explicit and if my assertions made you feel like I was reinforcing lazy thinking.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:12:49-07:00","id":978466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978297#post978297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the game we play today is layers of band aids wrapped around nostalgia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god, I love this so much. I would ask if I could sig this quote, but I worry it would come off the wrong way coming from me, as someone who prefers Chronicles. Still, what a wonderfully succinct and apt description of World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:21:48-07:00","id":978473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978219#post978219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a big deal to be sterile in the Garou Nation, they aren't a human culture they don't have to be PC. Get Pegasus to accept you and you are in, but as it is Pegasus seems to have disdain for functional testicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor do they have to be modern conceptions of PI. Apart from anything else, I find it hard to picture <i>werewolves</i> being particularly strict about being bound to the body you started off with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:34:12-07:00","id":978479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978225#post978225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on your definition. Transsexual refers to someone who is undergoing hormonal and/or physical transformation (transgender is the term for someone born the wrong sex who may or may not be transsexual).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Born the wrong sex&quot; is a very limiting definition for transgender, and does not apply to a lot of transgender peoples' experiences. I, for example, would have come to terms with my identity much earlier in life if I hadn't been fed that narrative, and might not have to live my professional life in the closet if that had been the case. The most widely accepted definition among transgender people, is someone who's gender does not match the gender they were assigned at birth. It does not have to relate to sex at all, which admittedly complicates the way the Black Furies would relate to transgender people, as from what I understand, their concept of womanhood is very wrapped up in biological factors like sex and reproduction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978225#post978225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the transformation process, I imagine that it would be rejected by the healing factor of the Garou because it is a change from their physical form. Unless they did the surgery with silver tools, it will heal, and I can see no practical way that hormone therapy will not be rejected like any other chemical toxin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, though, a person can be transgender without undergoing any surgery or hormonal treatment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978225#post978225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the Garou probably can use magic to truly change sexes, so it would be rather silly to call them trans- anything. Yes, they may have been born a male but, after they give birth to their first child, I do not think anyone will really care. I do wonder if they would be willing to use that magic on their Kinfolk? If so, it would make life a lot simpler for transgender Kinfolk because they could truly become their desired sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, &quot;born as a male&quot; doesn't really track to the idea of gender as a social construct. Second of all, having one's sex changed, whether by medical or supernatural means, doesn't make a person stop being trans, and suggesting it would belies an outlook that doesn't view trans women as &quot;real women&quot; on the basis of inability to bear children. Which, granted, some people do hold, some of whom may be Black Furies in the world of Apocalypse. But it is a transmysoginistic way of thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-29-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:46:05-07:00","id":978481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978479#post978479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Born the wrong sex&quot; is a very limiting definition for transgender, and does not apply to a lot of transgender peoples' experiences. I, for example, would have come to terms with my identity much earlier in life if I hadn't been fed that narrative, and might not have to live my professional life in the closet if that had been the case. The most widely accepted definition among transgender people, is someone who's gender does not match the gender they were assigned at birth. It does not have to relate to sex at all, which admittedly complicates the way the Black Furies would relate to transgender people, as from what I understand, their concept of womanhood is very wrapped up in biological factors like sex and reproduction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, though, a person can be transgender without undergoing any surgery or hormonal treatment.<br /> <br /> <br /> First of all, &quot;born as a male&quot; doesn't really track to the idea of gender as a social construct. Second of all, having one's sex changed, whether by medical or supernatural means, doesn't make a person stop being trans, and suggesting it would belies an outlook that doesn't view trans women as &quot;real women&quot; on the basis of inability to bear children. Which, granted, some people do hold, some of whom may be Black Furies in the world of Apocalypse. But it is a transmysoginistic way of thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Controversial though it might be, I think the Black Furies would have a very hard time accepting someone who identifies as a woman but also doesn't want to &quot;correct&quot; their body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:52:54-07:00","id":978482,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the Black Furies would be fairly split on accepting transgender women into their group. Some would be fine with it, some would view it as a betrayal of Pegasus' beliefs.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, who is a Black Fury and who isn't is more a spiritual matter than anything else, and if Pegasus decides that someone is suitably female to join her brood, that's what matters. Still, I suspect that more conservative Black Furies would treat transgender members like &quot;second class&quot; Black Furies and, those transgender BF's would often face discrimination and be forced to prove themselves more than biological females.<br /> <br /> I also suspect that transgender Black Furies would be encouraged to undergo rites or engage in spirit quests for the purpose of changing their physical sexual characteristics so that they can become female in both body and soul.<br /> <br /> The thing is though, not all transgender people <i>want</i> to change their physical bodies, something that more conservative Black Furies might simply not understand. They may feel, for example, that allowing transgender women to join the Black Furies is acceptable, with the unstated assumption that those Black Furies would be seeking out ways to become female in body. When confronted those transgender BF's who insist on keeping their male body parts, those conservative Black Furies might view this as a betrayal of the conditions that they were allowed into the Black Furies in the first place by.<br /> <br /> I think it's generally better if transgender BF's face some kind of discrimination (not intense, but something that might come up now and again) rather than simply be accepted without anyone batting an eye, if only because this is the World of Darkness we're dealing with, the game is more interesting when characters face challenges, and including issues of transgender discrimination is a good way to get players to learn about and to explore the topic.<br /> <br /> Most other tribes won't really care, but that's because no other tribe is based around physical sex and gender in the way the Black Furies are. So the Black Furies would probably be a better tribe to tackle this issue with than most any of the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:00:36-07:00","id":978486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978481#post978481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Controversial though it might be, I think the Black Furies would have a very hard time accepting someone who identifies as a woman but also doesn't want to &amp;quot;correct&amp;quot; their body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the vibe I get from them as well. I do agree with Atamajakki that there's a strong case to be made for the younger generation of Black Furies trying to change that. Whether or not they'be gained any traction is, I think, something for the ST to consider and decide for their own games, but it seems unlikely to me that in 2016 there wouldn't be a significant number of third wave feminists in the Furies <i>as well as</i> a significant number of trans-exclusionary radical feminists, and those groups wouldn't clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:35:43-07:00","id":978507,"title":"","content":"I think a better question would be why you would bother including a gender-obsessed group like the Black Furies in your game in the first place. Gender, even more so than race, is a dumb thing for werewolves to fight over when there is the war with the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:40:20-07:00","id":978510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978507#post978507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a better question would be why you would bother including a gender-obsessed group like the Black Furies in your game in the first place. Gender, even more so than race, is a dumb thing for werewolves to fight over when there is the war with the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're a part of the setting and sometimes a story needs more to it beyond raging against impossible odds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:01:39-07:00","id":978521,"title":"","content":"As well, the idea of the Black Furies makes a good deal of sense in the history of the setting (though it was written for that in mind). Fighting the Wyrm isn't just killing banes and BSDs. The frequently violent oppression of women by societies is something that feeds the Wyrm too, and fighting to protect women is part of the fight against the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:08:45-07:00","id":978525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978510#post978510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they're a part of the setting and sometimes a story needs more to it beyond raging against impossible odds.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of things that are part of the setting that are weak/poorly thought out and therefore (by me) de-emphasized. Black Furies and Kung-Fu werewolves are prime examples.<br /> <br /> Fighting with a bunch of gender-biased zealots about who they get to let into their dumb exclusionary tribe-cult seems silly.<br /> <br /> Edit for Heavy Arms- good point.Slavery was much the same way, I suppose, in how it fostered the Wyrm. Women do get treated horribly, not saying otherwise- I guess the Furies just feel a little too stilted and reactionary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 09-29-2016, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:33:55-07:00","id":978537,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between gender (a social expression) and sex (a genetic and physical expression). While sex is a genetic and physical spectrum, 90% of human beings are reproductively male or female, 99% are functionally sexually male or female, and 99.9% are genetically and physically male or female (genetic disorders like CAIS and PAIS make up the majority of the remaining 0.1%). <br /> <br /> Once again, it depends on definitions. The dozen or so transwomen I have known have sought to physically become women and, if given a genetic option, would have jumped on it in an instant (I discussed that scenario with them specifically from a scientific point of view). While I am sure that there are transgender women who would not want to be genetically and physically female, I would imagine that the majority of transsexual women would welcome the opportunity to do so because they truly want to be women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:47:25-07:00","id":978542,"title":"","content":"Alright. Pray for me. I'm going to open worms and wyrms and worms from drums, not cans. Please read what I write with an open mind, because some of you aren't going to like it. World of darkness attracts a lot of people with gender nonconformity, and while I don't know how much, i'm certain it's not proportionate to the wider population.<br /> <br /> The garou are an extremely tiny minority of the world's population. Transgenderism in variable extents, in a 2012 survey, was found in 1% of the surveyed population. Now 1 out 100 isn't too bad, even if it doesn't represent the players, there's going to be some Transgender garou, right?<br /> Coming out is extremely difficult for transgender people. Especially in homids. But it'll come with issues, especially if the person has had to keep them bottled up. A person born male with who idenifies as female might, say, decide to not put on muscle, because they don't want to look more masculine. For a female wanting to be male, well, other than overcompensation (potentially lethal), there isn't a big problem. Now these two problems are problems in their own right, but they're unfortunately further compounded.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm just going to throw something subjective in here, and you can all verify or deny this here: but people who are 'the norm' think and speak a lot less about their gender, race, nationality and whatnot, and people who aren't, let's say a gender minority or a racial minority,half the time treat the thing that causes them to stand out as a very important issue.<br /> Being straight doesn't occur to me unless I find myself in a gaybar, but one of my gay friends has modeled his life around fitting the stereotype, and another gay/trans person who I play with regularly won't play a character that is ugly or masculine<br /> It's not everyone that does that, but it's undeniable that there are people like that. Anyway. How does this become relevant to the question?<br /> <br /> Firstly, Garou society is harsh, conservative, and highly critical.<br /> You don't want to upset elders. Acting out against their oppression will cost glory, honour and wisdom. Causing tribal divides is worse.<br /> Focusing on the problems most relevant to you, rather than most relevant to gaia, will loose you glory, honour and wisdom. (yep. Totally aware that this is probably how seperate tribes formed)<br /> Having less glory, honour and wisdom means less ranks, and less ranks mean you've got weaker gifts and are more likely to die.<br /> You are probably going to feel pressure to move into your family's tribe. There's three that are modern enough to happily embrace a trans member. They're noted for being the least glorious. Would you really dishonour your ancestors that much?<br /> Black fury specific: The cycle of a woman: Maiden, Mother, Crone, Is sacred. A reassignment could easily be seen as a mockery of that. The father isn't mentioned, but it's no doubt an important roll in this metaphysical trinity. Black Furies have kinfolk husbands. Changing yourself and trying to get into the tribe could easily be seen as an insult.<br /> <br /> Secondly. Gaia chooses you and luna gives you an auspice.<br /> Now, this was really a matter I argued with a friend about, who suggested that gaia/luna is stupid, (or maybe uses random selection, but he said stupid) whilst I believe at least luna makes you predisposed to having tallents relevant to your auspice. Anyhow, if we assume random selection isn't how gaia does garou; why would gaia pick someone likely to have the above issues? I mean, this isn't something that's entirely based on gender identity, but rather the problems that gender identity can cause- an uktena who's culture is accepting isn't going to have the same issues as a fianna who's family would never accept him should he come out of the closet and put on a dress. All things considered: We're looking at less than that 1% for transgender garou<br /> <br /> A physcial note:<br /> Garou regenerate. Physical gender reassignment has gotta be the most hardcore and brutal shit ever devised, unless you had a really late first change.<br /> <br /> <br /> And lastly, all these reasons have been more related to the social effects of being transgender. Now one that isn't: Spirits don't register gender in the same way you do. To some, unimportant, but to others, you're a deceiver or your misguided and some spirits might take this as an offense.<br /> Maybe it's some kind of wyrm taint or the wyld's accident, with the weaver jumping in to try and 'fix' it. I wouldn't be surprised if someone blamed gender dysphoria on something in the food or meds or radiowaves and it's all the fault of pentex.<br /> <br /> To black furies, you've scorned motherhood or have usurped the possition of the woman.<br /> Children of Gaia, Bone gnawers and Glass walkers will be happy to have you, but as said before, they're not the most respected tribes. Remember: the Rokea are in the self-beating betweener war because some wyrm thing tricked them into thinking weresharks that went to land were responsible for all the evil of the sea. Garou are the closest breed to rokea in terms of brains. I recall there being an annecdote about black furies getting really mad about males appearing in their tribal homelands. Many black furies calling for a purge of those men. Rage affects reason, remember. Pegasus can never accept a man with working genitals, and there can never be a perfect tribe. If one tribe fixed it's issues, then the whole setting is undermined.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is all default setting. If you wanna ignore everything I just said for the sake of escaping reality, that's fine, but remember that world of darkness default is set in a dark and shitty reality. You can get your way if you want, the golden rule is always there. But you are going to be going against the spirit of the book with ideas like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 09-29-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:48:41-07:00","id":978544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978537#post978537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, it depends on definitions. The dozen or so transwomen I have known have sought to physically become women and, if given a genetic option, would have jumped on it in an instant (I discussed that scenario with them specifically from a scientific point of view). While I am sure that there are transgender women who would not want to be genetically and physically female, I would imagine that the majority of transsexual women would welcome the opportunity to do so because they truly want to be women.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just keep in mind that not all transgendered people also have gender dysphoria. There are people who want to live &quot;cross gender&quot; but who would have no interest whatsoever in undergoing sexual reassignment surgery, even if it was offered to them for free.<br /> <br /> Admittedly like you said about definitions, part of that is the way that the term &quot;transgendered&quot; has become something of a catch-all umbrella term for people with issues about the way society commonly classifies sex and gender. Still, it's useful to keep in mind that there are transgender people out there who don't want to change their primary (or possibly even secondary) sexual characteristics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:00:11-07:00","id":978550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978537#post978537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference between gender (a social expression) and sex (a genetic and physical expression). While sex is a genetic and physical spectrum, 90% of human beings are reproductively male or female, 99% are functionally sexually male or female, and 99.9% are genetically and physically male or female (genetic disorders like CAIS and PAIS make up the majority of the remaining 0.1%).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure how this relates to the discussion at hand, but yeah, that's our current best estimate based on the available data.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978537#post978537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, it depends on definitions. The dozen or so transwomen I have known have sought to physically become women and, if given a genetic option, would have jumped on it in an instant (I discussed that scenario with them specifically from a scientific point of view).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhmm. Though there's that verbiage &quot;physically female&quot;, which doesn't track to your earlier (accurate) statement about gender and sex being different things. Female is a gender, and gender is not physical. But yeah, your point is accurate, a large number of trans people do desire to sexually tramsition in some way, and would take the option for a complete and functional biological transition if such a thing was possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978537#post978537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I am sure that there are transgender women who would not want to be genetically and physically female, I would imagine that the majority of transsexual women would welcome the opportunity to do so because they truly want to be women.</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrasing &quot;truly want to be women&quot; is where I take issue with this, as the implication is that trans women who <i>don't</i> want to transition either don't &quot;truly&quot; want to be women or that what we want to be is not &quot;truly&quot; women. Either way, it is disrespectful of our identities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-29-2016, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:17:57-07:00","id":978565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978544#post978544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">part of that is the way that the term &quot;transgendered&quot; has become something of a catch-all umbrella term for people with issues about the way society commonly classifies sex and gender.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd probably be better off just saying trans. A lot of people are very uncomfortable with transgendered because it makes it sound like a thing that was done to them instead of just being who they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:23:30-07:00","id":978573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978565#post978565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd probably be better off just saying trans. A lot of people are very uncomfortable with transgendered because it makes it sound like a thing that was done to them instead of just being who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the term is transgender. The ed at the end is not really grammatically correct anyway. But yeah, trans works too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:35:56-07:00","id":978590,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting Garou put emphasis on birth and spirit, after all Metis can't just change their deformity and be accepted as cool by the Fianna. And body and spirit are the tied for werewolves because they are half spirit and half flesh. It really seems like even if garou with male genitalia became furies they would be treat as 2nd class garou like Metis males.they are kind of Compromise candidates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:47:55-07:00","id":978682,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The garou are an extremely tiny minority of the world's population. Transgenderism in variable extents, in a 2012 survey, was found in 1% of the surveyed population. Now 1 out 100 isn't too bad, even if it doesn't represent the players, there's going to be some Transgender garou, right?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two things about this - another study on the subject has been done suggesting that the numbers are quite a bit more common. Add to this that the original survey from 2012 is a compilation on information from the 80s and 90s, before the internet was mainstream in households, before people were educated or able to educate themselves on the subject. I know that growing up in the 90s I didn\u2019t get a computer or internet until the mid-00s, and the number of books my library had on the subject was nil. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This correction comes up a lot because a lot of conservatives will misappropriate it to suit a narrative where there aren\u2019t enough trans people to warrant changing rules, I know that\u2019s not what you\u2019re trying to do, but that number is arguably much lower than the reality.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming out is extremely difficult for transgender people. Especially in homids. But it'll come with issues, especially if the person has had to keep them bottled up. A person born male with who idenifies as female might, say, decide to not put on muscle, because they don't want to look more masculine. For a female wanting to be male, well, other than overcompensation (potentially lethal), there isn't a big problem. Now these two problems are problems in their own right, but they're unfortunately further compounded.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You\u2019re referring to after they become Garou? Rituals fetishes etc have been brought up, and as far as I\u2019m aware there is little difference between female and male Garou in terms of strength or stamina, at least in Crinos/Wolf Form. Put simply, why would a hypothetical transwoman Garou who cares about the things you stipulated, desire to be any different than the other female Garou around them? And, this being the case, how does this pose a problem that those women don\u2019t also face without being trans?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just going to throw something subjective in here, and you can all verify or deny this here: but people who are 'the norm' think and speak a lot less about their gender, race, nationality and whatnot, and people who aren't, let's say a gender minority or a racial minority,half the time treat the thing that causes them to stand out as a very important issue.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All of this is true until you mention race and nationality, which people, at least in England and America, won\u2019t shut up about. I can only assume you\u2019re not paying attention to the political climate? As for the gender thing, yes. It\u2019s the squeaky wheel that gets the grease. And it is an important issue, for some trans people it\u2019s a source of constant pain, bitterness, and resentment, especially if the society around them is stacked against them, which presently it is.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being straight doesn't occur to me unless I find myself in a gaybar, but one of my gay friends has modeled his life around fitting the stereotype, and another gay/trans person who I play with regularly won't play a character that is ugly or masculine</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It's not everyone that does that, but it's undeniable that there are people like that. Anyway. How does this become relevant to the question?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">99% of my friends who aren\u2019t straight, and I include myself in this because I am Bi, don\u2019t make a big deal out of it ever and don\u2019t want to be associated with flamboyant behaviors, and some people do because it helps them connect to other people who are like them and that community benefits them. Personally I\u2019d argue that as a straight person you\u2019re surrounded by trans and homosexual people and you have no idea because they\u2019re not doing exactly what you\u2019re saying here.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, Garou society is harsh, conservative, and highly critical.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yes, they are conservative because they place great emphasis on the traditions of the Garou nation, they\u2019re not conservative human being, conservative human values in the setting tend to serve either the Weaver or the Wyrm, that\u2019s not to say you can\u2019t make an argument for or against that, but it\u2019s the reality of the current setting. It\u2019s unrealistic to expect Garou people to conservatively cling to human mindsets over the past hundred or so years, as opposed to ancient tribalistic mindsets dating back thousands of years, with the help of their dedicated oral tradition and the spirits themselves. Also magic.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't want to upset elders. Acting out against their oppression will cost glory, honour and wisdom. Causing tribal divides is worse.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That depends on how the tribal divide ends up. It could also </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>lead</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> to great renown if you change garou society for the better.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Focusing on the problems most relevant to you, rather than most relevant to gaia, will loose you glory, honour and wisdom. (yep. Totally aware that this is probably how separate tribes formed)</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transgender individuals are 40% more likely to attempt suicide, many succeed, many are murdered in grizzly fashion. How does the despair and oppression this produces not feed the Wyrm? How is preventing that no in Gaia\u2019s best interests?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having less glory, honour and wisdom means less ranks, and less ranks mean you've got weaker gifts and are more likely to die.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yes, in a very narrow situation where you are flamboyant, refuse to carve a place for yourself in garou society, and constantly deny the elders and spirits, you will be at a disadvantage. Having lower rank also means you\u2019re less likely to be sent into situations where you are going to die. Garou life is valuable, even if it\u2019s Garou life you find obnoxious. Bone Gnawers are a thing that exists. You\u2019re ignoring the fact that a garou who behaves this way is almost certainly going to become a Ragabash anyway.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are probably going to feel pressure to move into your family's tribe. There's three that are modern enough to happily embrace a trans member. They're noted for being the least glorious. Would you really dishonour your ancestors that much?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Black Furies:</b> Subject of this thread, honestly, arguments for both sides are in the thread already.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Bone Gnawers:</b> One of the modern tribes you mentioned, except they\u2019re also one of the least consistent, one on hand impoverished transgender people are often prostitutes, and are much derided especially in minority communities. I\u2019ve read books on cultural diffusion with the spanish and oppressed peoples as a culprit, but I\u2019m not going to turn the thread into a Gender Studies thread unless the discussion really calls for it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That said, the Bone Gnawers aren\u2019t necessarily \u2018all\u2019 impoverished humans, their tribal totem and their overall aesthetic seems to make them pretty accepting of anyone - as long as you have what it takes to survive, and if you\u2019re one of their human kinfolk who is trans, and you haven\u2019t died from drugs, suicide, homidice, or what have you, you are a survivor. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Children of Gaia:</b> Pretty cut and dry wouldn\u2019t have a problem with it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fianna:</b> Probably have a problem with it more than most, I\u2019m putting them tied with Red Talons.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Get of Fenris:</b> As written where they\u2019re basically not-Asatru, not on board with it unless you\u2019re a Theurge or Ragabash. If you go with a reconstructionist approach where they respect the Jotuns more than the Aesir and human Aesir worship, then they should have no problem with it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Glasswalkers:</b> Are counter-culture enough to support it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Red Talons:</b> Lack a proper vocabulary or framework for the problem. They\u2019re also the tribe who will care the most about not leaving your ancestors for another tribe. Unless the Lupus can find a ritual that can change their sex (assuming that\u2019s a thing they want) they\u2019re probably going to be in for a bad time.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Shadow Lords:</b> Implying these guys don\u2019t switch sex when a politically advantageous marriage could be had. The culture they\u2019re rooted on, going back far enough, has a place for transgender individuals as well.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Silent Striders:</b> Are basically nomads and vagabonds at this point, weirdness is to be expected, when someone threatens one of their own, you circle the wagons, to say nothing of their feelings on reincarnation, the nature of the soul, and so on. The middle east is also a region where surgery and treatment is covered by the state in Iran because \u2018At least you\u2019re not a gay man.\u2019</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Silver Fangs:</b> On the one hand Russia is one of the most homophobic areas in the world, on the other the indigenous populations, some of which still exist, have a lot of gender variance in their lore and cultures, particularly the shamanic traditions which are the most applicable since shaman are likely to be Silver Fang Kinfolk, and are informed by the same spirits the Silver Fangs regularly deal with.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Uktena:</b> I have not read their tribebook yet.I know they\u2019re Native American and have implications of wyrm taint, but that\u2019s about it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Wendigo:</b> I don\u2019t see them supporting modern notions of gender dysphoria, but that\u2019s not really an uncommon problem for new members already. They\u2019re a very hostile hidebound group, and the two spirit mold is one that a lot of modern transgender people can\u2019t or don\u2019t like being fit into.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black fury specific: The cycle of a woman: Maiden, Mother, Crone, Is sacred. A reassignment could easily be seen as a mockery of that. The father isn't mentioned, but it's no doubt an important roll in this metaphysical trinity. Black Furies have kinfolk husbands. Changing yourself and trying to get into the tribe could easily be seen as an insult.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Except the reassignment is very similar to what Pegasus, their tribal totem, has gone through. To consider those people in that light they would have to consider their own totem a perversion rather than a force against oppression. The father is in fact, not even relevant to that trinity, per the tribebook, and you\u2019re not gonna find an abundance of Black Furies with Pure Breed above 3. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly. Gaia chooses you and luna gives you an auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Actually, Gaia is asleep, and the triad she put in place to manage things is broken. The Wyld is dwindling, the Weaver is obsessed, and the wyrm is mad. No Garou is going to argue that Gaia made you the way you are unless they are a Homid who just first changed awhile back, and is used to a heavily Christian view of the world. The truth of the entire Garou plight is that the world is \u2018not\u2019 in balance, so why should they expect everyone to be born \u2018the right way\u2019?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, this was really a matter I argued with a friend about, who suggested that gaia/luna is stupid, (or maybe uses random selection, but he said stupid) whilst I believe at least luna makes you predisposed to having tallents relevant to your auspice. Anyhow, if we assume random selection isn't how gaia does garou; why would gaia pick someone likely to have the above issues? I mean, this isn't something that's entirely based on gender identity, but rather the problems that gender identity can cause- an uktena who's culture is accepting isn't going to have the same issues as a fianna who's family would never accept him should he come out of the closet and put on a dress. All things considered: We're looking at less than that 1% for transgender garou</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Luna, specifically, is the one who decides if you change, and Luna is quite literally a </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>lunatic.</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> As for your friend saying your argument is stupid, I wouldn\u2019t say that. I feel it\u2019s a bit short-sighted but I don\u2019t think you\u2019re stupid, and I don\u2019t think your argument is.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A physcial note:</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Garou regenerate. Physical gender reassignment has gotta be the most hardcore and brutal shit ever devised, unless you had a really late first change.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unless you use a ritual, spirit quests, sacred sites, fetishes, etc etc. Honestly I have a hard time believing transgender people would seek mundane treatment when you are literally magic.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lastly, all these reasons have been more related to the social effects of being transgender. Now one that isn't: Spirits don't register gender in the same way you do. To some, unimportant, but to others, you're a deceiver or your misguided and some spirits might take this as an offense.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maybe it's some kind of wyrm taint or the wyld's accident, with the weaver jumping in to try and 'fix' it. I wouldn't be surprised if someone blamed gender dysphoria on something in the food or meds or radiowaves and it's all the fault of pentex.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If you\u2019re going to base spirits on actual animistic cultures in mythology and history, then no. No spirit is going to consider you a deceiver, no spirit is going to take offense, unless it\u2019s some Ancestor spirit with a personal issue against it. Spirits in history and mythology are overwhelmingly the source of these issues in the first place, either because they decided you need to be their spouse or because they need to remake you in order to be a vessel for their power.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To black furies, you've scorned motherhood or have usurped the possition of the woman.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Which would be the TERF response, but arguments for and against this have been made, just asserting that they will do this without explanation isn\u2019t really helpful to the discussion.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Children of Gaia, Bone gnawers and Glass walkers will be happy to have you, but as said before, they're not the most respected tribes. Remember: the Rokea are in the self-beating betweener war because some wyrm thing tricked them into thinking weresharks that went to land were responsible for all the evil of the sea. Garou are the closest breed to rokea in terms of brains. I recall there being an annecdote about black furies getting really mad about males appearing in their tribal homelands. Many black furies calling for a purge of those men. Rage affects reason, remember. Pegasus can never accept a man with working genitals, and there can never be a perfect tribe. If one tribe fixed it's issues, then the whole setting is undermined.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You just said pegasus can\u2019t accept a man with working genitalia but claimed earlier that he also wouldn\u2019t accept those who are, like him \u2018gelded\u2019. The Black Furies wanted to purge those men not because they have Rage, but because the mythology they are inspired by has those beliefs and practices already. All female mystery cults are a thing that existed in Ancient Greece, the women would revel, and if they came upon a man they would rip him to shreds. The book Lavinia depicts something similar and is a very good read in general.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978542#post978542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, this is all default setting. If you wanna ignore everything I just said for the sake of escaping reality, that's fine, but remember that world of darkness default is set in a dark and shitty reality. You can get your way if you want, the golden rule is always there. But you are going to be going against the spirit of the book with ideas like this.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And this is why my response to you has been more heated than it has been to other people. You got quite a bit of setting elements wrong and then have the audacity to say \u201cFeel free to disagree with me, but if you do you\u2019re wrong and aren\u2019t cleaving to the spirit of the \u2018real\u2019 game.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And with all do respect, saying \u2018With all do respect\u2019 or something along those lines at the beginning of your argument doesn\u2019t excuse that.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 09-29-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:56:48-07:00","id":978688,"title":"","content":"I love the argument that spirits would view a trans person as a deceiver instead of perceiving their true gender. The meat body you're in matters so little to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:57:31-07:00","id":978689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978550#post978550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure how this relates to the discussion at hand, but yeah, that's our current best estimate based on the available data.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mhmm. Though there's that verbiage &quot;physically female&quot;, which doesn't track to your earlier (accurate) statement about gender and sex being different things. Female is a gender, and gender is not physical. But yeah, your point is accurate, a large number of trans people do desire to sexually tramsition in some way, and would take the option for a complete and functional biological transition if such a thing was possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> The phrasing &quot;truly want to be women&quot; is where I take issue with this, as the implication is that trans women who <i>don't</i> want to transition either don't &quot;truly&quot; want to be women or that what we want to be is not &quot;truly&quot; women. Either way, it is disrespectful of our identities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always take a bit of issue with the claim that female is exclusively a gender and that gender is not physical. If my brain were not wired in a way similar to a 'female' brain is, I would not suffer constant dysphoria over having a non-traditional body, because the brain wouldn't be wired to accept that. I have no feelings whatsoever regarding female gender norms in society (I don't hate dresses, I just don't feel strongly about what sorts of clothes I wear, how society sees me, etc.) My issue is solely with the fact that my physical body causes me discomfort, and that after a childhood of constant therapists, hormones was the only thing that helped ease some of the tension, there there is still quite a bit of dysphoria present because getting other services besides hormones is difficult after being banished from your family with no college education.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:08:34-07:00","id":978726,"title":"","content":"They would probably see the 'inner' person and, in some cases, would 'help' them become their 'inner' person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:16:27-07:00","id":978732,"title":"","content":"Probably the best counterargument I've ever recieved. I admit, I'm not so well read in werewolf as I am in vampire. <br /> <br /> Spirits in world of darkness aren't soley based on the animistic of history and mythology. History and mythology cover very few things in the spirit world. Spirits come in such innumerable counts and vareities that there is surely both spirits that would be outwardly amazed and overjoyed by someone's gender change, just as there are others who mock it, loath it, or even consider it a bane. A school's spirit of education might hate that a transgender person transgresses what is taught at a school and violates uniform standards. a spirit of comedy might want to use the person as a comedic focus. Weaver spirits might consider it a logistical error and offer to 'fix' it. <br /> <br /> Firstly, Yes, Male and female garou are all equally prone to be physically olympian. Even if you wanna be <i>that </i>guy, I'm sure glabro to lupus the difference is mute. Eventually Men are muscle bound monsters, women are muscle bound monsters. (Though I've noted that maybe the amount of damage-boosting gifts the furys have might be to compensate for a perceived lack of physical strength) However, the issue with disphoria is, well, even if all the women have masculine muscles, maybe you wont want to. Maybe you want to be a girly girl, and muscles are a terrible way to undermine that. Your thought process says you need to look more like a girl to compensate for that fact that you were born with a penis; Those muscly female Garou are fine- They've got the right thing between their legs and have a feminine look to them even with the musculature. Alternatively, as said, Being super-man will probably get you killed early. You could no doubt have it fixed it with magical means: but consider that you're probably underdeveloped for a great spirit quest, and such a great quest would detract from the garou cause (those resources would be much better spent fighting the wyrm directly or fighting a cause that affects the majority rather than minority. Like Poverty or Obesity) and no sane garou would trust a mage who could provide a quick fix. . <br /> <br /> <br /> also<br /> Red talons probably don't give a fuck about transgender, In the good way. &quot;It's nature, It happens, ignore the humans over-complicating it.&quot; Probably. <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I kinda imagine all garou as really masculine. Even ragabash and theurges. Even children of gaia. Come Adren you should have 3 in all physicals at least, then you've got rage, then auspice. I guess this doesn't happen all the time as in group games, you've got players who specialise and limited XP. But for a warrior standpoint, you should all get into shape because your physical stamina helps you stop bullets. A woman-turn-man is easy to imagine. A man-turn-woman is a more difficult fit. Honestly, Even in black furies I imagine that underneath all that girl-power is an underlying machismo. Being soft and feminine is almost fundamentally un-garou. That's not to say that girls don't do girly things, but the ones who play with dolls are the same ones who'll rip a formori in half and try and get the bloodsplatter to form an artwork. Essentially: Women wear trousers. They don't go on shopping sprees or wear perfume, because we all know that stuff is wyrm tainted. For other changing breeds? It'll depend on the breed. Subtle breeds like corax,Nuwisha, Ananasi, Kitsune, some kinds of bastet? A lot less testosterone fueled. Much more room to try the transgender theme. Garou though? There's less gender dimorphism; you're all noble savages. You're all warriors, and you can all transform into terrifying war machines.<br /> <br /> Anyway: I don't think it's the right medium to rollplay your accepted transgender Reason 1? Rage. Normal humans are going to think you're a dangerous wierdo regardless of what flags you wave. Reason 2? Garou society. Yes, you might win big if you change something big, but that's going to be a horrific uphill battle, and you're probably going to have a serious falling out with the storyteller unless they give you an easymode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:49:14-07:00","id":978741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978732#post978732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits in world of darkness aren't soley based on the animistic of history and mythology. History and mythology cover very few things in the spirit world. Spirits come in such innumerable counts and vareities that there is surely both spirits that would be outwardly amazed and overjoyed by someone's gender change, just as there are others who mock it, loath it, or even consider it a bane. A school's spirit of education might hate that a transgender person transgresses what is taught at a school and violates uniform standards. a spirit of comedy might want to use the person as a comedic focus. Weaver spirits might consider it a logistical error and offer to 'fix' it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The interaction between humans and spirits are based on tribal and animistic societies, that's the point. Your point about the spirits of education or patriarchy or whatever else taking umbrage is a good one, except werewolves are more likely to either not deal with those spirits in favor of more nature based entities, or else they're Glasswalkers, in which case being told what to do with their own bodies is a good way to get laughed at. As far as I'm aware the Triad does not have spirits 'in the traditional sense' and no one but the Glasswalkers are going to care what the Weaver wants anyway, it already drove the Wyrm insane and is threatening to stagnate existence. A spirit of comedy who is antagonizing you is going to do that regardless depending on what Rank you are.<br /> <br /> Mage is the game where you are much more likely to run into spirits that disagree with you, and it's also a game where you're just as likely to enslave those spirits to your own ends anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978732#post978732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, Yes, Male and female garou are all equally prone to be physically olympian. Even if you wanna be <i>that </i>guy, I'm sure glabro to lupus the difference is mute. Eventually Men are muscle bound monsters, women are muscle bound monsters. (Though I've noted that maybe the amount of damage-boosting gifts the furys have might be to compensate for a perceived lack of physical strength) However, the issue with disphoria is, well, even if all the women have masculine muscles, maybe you wont want to. Maybe you want to be a girly girl, and muscles are a terrible way to undermine that. Your thought process says you need to look more like a girl to compensate for that fact that you were born with a penis; Those muscly female Garou are fine- They've got the right thing between their legs and have a feminine look to them even with the musculature. Alternatively, as said, Being super-man will probably get you killed early. You could no doubt have it fixed it with magical means: but consider that you're probably underdeveloped for a great spirit quest, and such a great quest would detract from the garou cause (those resources would be much better spent fighting the wyrm directly or fighting a cause that affects the majority rather than minority. Like Poverty or Obesity) and no sane garou would trust a mage who could provide a quick fix. .</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to focus more on Social/Appearance traits as a werewolf there are gifts for that as well, but again this has no actual bearing on transgender complications because it's a complication any 'girly girl' is going to face after she first changes. I'm noticing your biggest hurdle is the reality that garou are not human, they are conservative in ways aliens to humans, and it's unlikely a girly girl is going to remain that way for much longer in the face of her rage, her drive to hunt, that becomes more important than not breaking a nail.<br /> <br /> And the Black Furies have gifts that enhance their ability to inflict <i>pain</i> because that's considered part of being a woman in their spiritual identity. Women suffer what men cannot, and they employ gifts to inflict that suffering on those who justly deserve it. It's where their name comes from. The Greek Furies were vengeful women who traveled in packs and ripped offenders to literal pieces. There's no 'compensation', those gifts don't put them on par with a male werewolf of any other tribe, it makes them 'better at that' then those tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978732#post978732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also Red talons probably don't give a fuck about transgender, In the good way. &quot;It's nature, It happens, ignore the humans over-complicating it.&quot; Probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned earlier in this thread, I expect wolf lives are short and their emotional complexity limited enough that any gender dysphoria they do suffer is limited, once they change, though, they'll be immersed in a tribe of very very angry individuals who don't have the vocabulary to have a discussion on the subject, and don't have the patience to often empathize.<br /> <br /> Though if you're lucky enough to be a transwoman, I'm sure they wouldn't mind more female wolves, since strictly speaking women are more valuable for breeding purposes than men are, and the Red Talons face extinction more than most.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978732#post978732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I kinda imagine all garou as really masculine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really depends on where you set the goal posts, generally speaking, you're wrong, read any of the tribe novels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978732#post978732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even ragabash and theurges. Even children of gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing could be further from the truth. Again, you're just kind of asserting this is true without any evidence. The only evidence I can really provide is - read any of the tribe novels, read the Children of Gaia book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978732#post978732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come Adren you should have 3 in all physicals at least, then you've got rage, then auspice. I guess this doesn't happen all the time as in group games, you've got players who specialise and limited XP. But for a warrior standpoint, you should all get into shape because your physical stamina helps you stop bullets. A woman-turn-man is easy to imagine. A man-turn-woman is a more difficult fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not even listening, and you try to be subtle about how sexist you're being but every so often you slip with statements like this. A transwoman Garou would not suffer any behavioral issues that a Cis-Woman would not also face in Garou society, because women don't generally suffer complications in garou society, being a woman is not at odds with the lifestyle. A woman in physical shape is not the same thing as being Zarya. Super models have to box and lift weights in order to get their figures, which means that female werewolves could look like super models and still kick ass when they need to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978732#post978732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Even in black furies I imagine that underneath all that girl-power is an underlying machismo. Being soft and feminine is almost fundamentally un-garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the issue is that you're being incredibly sexist with little understanding of how the 'other sex' lives. Being soft and feminine is fine for Black Furies 'when they are maidens', but even then they are wolves, they hunt, they kill. Their entire spiritual identity is based on greek myths which at this rate I very much doubt you've read, since the assumption seems to be that all women either are or want to be a Kardashian, and anyone who doesn't is being 'masculine'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978732#post978732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not to say that girls don't do girly things, but the ones who play with dolls are the same ones who'll rip a formori in half and try and get the bloodsplatter to form an artwork. Essentially: Women wear trousers. They don't go on shopping sprees or wear perfume, because we all know that stuff is wyrm tainted. For other changing breeds? It'll depend on the breed. Subtle breeds like corax,Nuwisha, Ananasi, Kitsune, some kinds of bastet? A lot less testosterone fueled. Much more room to try the transgender theme. Garou though? There's less gender dimorphism; you're all noble savages. You're all warriors, and you can all transform into terrifying war machines.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a woman wears in werewolf depends on the woman, plenty of strong women in the shadow lords and silver fangs are going to dress in pencil skirts, dresses, whatever. If you don't want your perfume to be 'of the wyrm' then don't buy from JC Penny, you could get hand crafted scented oils from places like Black Phoenix Alchemy Labs easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway: I don't think it's the right medium to rollplay your accepted transgender Reason 1? Rage. Normal humans are going to think you're a dangerous wierdo regardless of what flags you wave. Reason 2? Garou society. Yes, you might win big if you change something big, but that's going to be a horrific uphill battle, and you're probably going to have a serious falling out with the storyteller unless they give you an easymode. </div> </div> </div>Rage is not going to present a hurdle to transgender people that is not already posed to cis-gendered people. You haven't even provided an excuse as to why it would except men are STR0NG and Women are frivilous, which is demonstrably wrong. Your second reason didn't even have an argument packaged with it, you're simply ignoring what I said and reasserting your initial perspective that for some reason Garou society feels the way you do about it.<br /> <br /> As for your final reason, that the storyteller is going have a falling out with me if I press the issue? I am the storyteller, most of the people in my social circle also wouldn't have a problem with it, and from what I've read of the upcoming LARP treatment, the designers for the game have rejiggered it to suit these ideas.<br /> <br /> In other words, your argument that &quot;You can do whatever you want, but it's not in the spirit of the game&quot; has no ground to stand on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":".  Removed the top line because it was a broken quote and I didn't actually have a response to them praising me on having a decent argument. 09-29-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:35:28-07:00","id":978764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978682#post978682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Uktena:</b> I have not read their tribebook yet.I know they\u2019re Native American and have implications of wyrm taint, but that\u2019s about it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Wendigo:</b> I don\u2019t see them supporting modern notions of gender dysphoria, but that\u2019s not really an uncommon problem for new members already. They\u2019re a very hostile hidebound group, and the two spirit mold is one that a lot of modern transgender people can\u2019t or don\u2019t like being fit into.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>So one thing I wanted to point out, because it was slightly brought up. Just as transgender people can't/don't like being fit into molds such as the two spirit, also remember that not all Native peoples have the same views on gender. While the Lakota (Wendigo) have the Two Spirit (which from my research doesn't include transmen), the Navajo (Uktena) had 5 genders before Christianity made its impact, there are other Native peoples who had binary systems like the Haudenosaunee (Croatan and Wendigo, then later Uktena and Wendigo, and who's culture I'm used to since my family is both Mohawk and Seneca). <br /> <br /> *not saying that trans people didn't exist in cultures with binary systems, so much as I have a thing against people painting all of the First Nations with the same cultural brush<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:37:29-07:00","id":978766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978764#post978764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So one thing I wanted to point out, because it was slightly brought up. Just as transgender people can't/don't like being fit into molds such as the two spirit, also remember that not all Native peoples have the same views on gender. While the Lakota (Wendigo) have the Two Spirit (which from my research doesn't include transmen), the Navajo (Uktena) had 5 genders before Christianity made its impact, there are other Native peoples who had binary systems like the Haudenosaunee (Croatan and Wendigo, then later Uktena and Wendigo, and who's culture I'm used to since my family is both Mohawk and Seneca).<br /> <br /> *not saying that trans people didn't exist in cultures with binary systems, so much as I have a thing against people painting all of the First Nations with the same cultural brush</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> **In my opinion Wendigo and Uktena would probably be more case by case basis of the individuals, and if the tribes themselves had an official cultural view on it I think it'd have more to do with the Garou tribe then the kin they hail from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:43:45-07:00","id":978772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978764#post978764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So one thing I wanted to point out, because it was slightly brought up. Just as transgender people can't/don't like being fit into molds such as the two spirit, also remember that not all Native peoples have the same views on gender. While the Lakota (Wendigo) have the Two Spirit (which from my research doesn't include transmen), the Navajo (Uktena) had 5 genders before Christianity made its impact, there are other Native peoples who had binary systems like the Haudenosaunee (Croatan and Wendigo, then later Uktena and Wendigo, and who's culture I'm used to since my family is both Mohawk and Seneca).<br /> <br /> *not saying that trans people didn't exist in cultures with binary systems, so much as I have a thing against people painting all of the First Nations with the same cultural brush</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so well versed on all the variances between Native American tribes, doing that is literally a full time job, though if there are any beliefs or practices that stand out as relevant for a game of werewolf I'd love to hear them.<br /> <br /> I know that in Mexico/Central America there are reports that the native peoples there would actually just raise their children without giving them any clothes at all, and part of their rite of passage was picking what clothes they'd wear, and what role they'd have in society. I hesitate mentioning it when it comes to things like the Bastet because the book was incredibly old, like back in the 50s old. It does apparently tie into how some nahautl and hispanic groups have such a complicated relationship with gender variance, after the Spanish came in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:10:29-07:00","id":978809,"title":"","content":"Alright. Sorry. My definitions of 'masculine' and 'feminine' may cause confusion <br /> <br /> Garou<br /> Get big muscles<br /> Like fights. <br /> Live by strict rules. <br /> Draw strength from magic anger, and a rejection of the material world. <br /> Settle issues with contests<br /> Believe murder to be a common and effective solution. <br /> Live under a strict hierarchy. <br /> Respect great blood, Ancestors, and oversized weapons. <br /> Believe their life duty is to fight the Wyrm and it's minions, A bunch of really ugly monsters fit for the cover of a metal album. <br /> Are werewolves. Werewolf myths often contain sexual symbolism, largely that of a male wolf taking the young female. <br /> Live in tribes, war with tribes unless an evil comes along<br /> Shapeshift and murder things for food with their own teeth<br /> Intimidate passers by with the presence of their sheer anger. <br /> Are prone to violent rages.<br /> <br /> Now. I think it's fair to say that most of these lead us to a western interpretation of masculine, maybe even hyper-masculine. Now, The Ajaba have their females more &quot;warrior&quot; than their males and most of this stuff applies to them, but the point is that they're still a 'macho' society, even if their gender ideas have been flipped (or ours have been flipped, or whatever). Liking 'girly' things isn't an issue. Becoming 'feminine' in behaviour is. To be more like a girl, you've got to throw away a lot of things that both garou nature and garou society give you. <br /> <br /> Now, if you wanna play the man-turn-woman, and be feminine, you're doomed.<br /> If you wanna play the man-turn woman, and be at an acceptable level of feminine whilst still being appropriately masculine, what's the point? <br /> <br /> The wonder of garou society is that men and women are equal (unless you're BF or a certain kind of GF) but the problem here lies that, to the average joe, you're considerably more 'masculine'. A Garou child can walk into a den of monsterous child molesters and act as if she didn't have a single fear. You never need to cross the road to avoid shady guys. You can have anyone you want in your bed with the eye-rape power. If a guy wolf-whistles you, you challenge him to a formal duel and run him through with your klaive. You're not going to threat too much over dresses beyond how much they hide, because you've probably got a really nasty scar visible somewhere Garou psychology favours the masculine,Or the one in power. Everyone's a warrior, but you have nothing to fear from normal people, who likely cower before you, and you are empowered through that. You can be somewhat nuetral about this, resentful of it, or you can lord it over others. You can be 'that well-adjusted soldier in a war film' level of manly or you can be an action hero of the man's masculine ideal. But you're a warrior of Gaia, so, you're always going to be predisposed towards a certain mentality. <br /> <br /> The only difference between men and women is how they have children in a garou society. Really. That's it. (other than the BF thing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T21:17:33-07:00","id":978837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. Sorry. My definitions of 'masculine' and 'feminine' may cause confusion</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because they're antiquated and nonsensical, but I'll bite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Garou</u><br /> Get big muscles</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for when they don't, see Mephi Faster than Death, and countless other NPCs given art that wasn't contributed by Ron Spencer. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for when they don't, see Children of Gaia, examples exist in other tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Live by strict rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this Machismo? What makes this trait masculine? Matriarchal societies, when and where they exist, are just as strict as male societies. See the all female mystery cults in Greece and Egypt. If you want to get into classical concepts of gender, Capricorn, Virgo, and Scorpio are three of the most strict signs in Astrology, they are associated with earth, earth, and water, both of which are feminine elements in contrast to Air and Fire, which were the &quot;masculine&quot; elements. Stories of goddesses will nearly 'always' have them reacting more strictly to transgressions than males ever do. See Hera, Sekhmet, Yemaya, Skadi (the jotun who claimed a place in Asgard by virtue of bloodline, is responsible for hanging the serpent over Loki in his bondage, and whose earliest sacrifices were men tried to a specific tree and offered as spouses to her, before being castrated to make sure they'd never sleep with another woman), Artemis, Aphrodite, Athena, the expression 'Hell Hath No Fury Like a Woman Scorned'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Draw strength from magic anger, and a rejection of the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Women are often considered more magic to compensate for physical strength, and are general depicted as more other worldly, being emotional instead of cool and rational is also a stereotypical 'feminine' trait, using your own rules. <br /> <br /> Also, werewolves are animistic, so they don't reject the material world, they embrace it, because the material world is part of the 'natural world'. Mages reject the material world because they are gnostic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Settle issues with contests</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, because the &quot;Stereotypical Woman&quot; doesn't do that at all, ever. It couldn't possibly be that humans crave competition just in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Believe murder to be a common and effective solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Murder&quot; is not something garou aspire for, that's why the hunt, that's why glorious battle. There is nothing glorious about murdering someone outside of those two categories. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Live under a strict hierarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>'cause rank and posturing isn't the bread and butter of the stereotypical teenage girl's life? I thought 'men' were supposed to be distant, aloof, and self sufficient, not beholden to any law except their own, so which is it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Respect great blood, Ancestors, and oversized weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>In any society that respects bloodlines the women care about it just as much as the men if not more so. Evolution wise, that's why females would breed with the best survivors. Males however are portrayed as far less concerned about who they're having sex with. <br /> <br /> What does over-sized weapons have to do with bloodlines? You lumped them together for no reason. Also many werewolves do not use weapons at all, and those that do often have weapons that are perfectly suited for their size - see Mephi Faster-than-death, or the Margrave. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Believe their life duty is to fight the Wyrm and it's minions, A bunch of really ugly monsters fit for the cover of a metal album.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually they existed before the Wyrm went out of wack, and their job is to keep balance between flesh and spirit, and preserve harmony/environmental homeostasis, right now, that means fighting the Wyrm because the Wyrm is believed to be the greatest threat. Though some like the Black Furies and the Red Talons argue they'd be better served focusing on The Weaver. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are werewolves. Werewolf myths often contain sexual symbolism, largely that of a male wolf taking the young female.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of which the game specifically chooses to ignore, you're also considering a very narrow selection of werewolf myths, those from a specific point in time in Europe, as opposed to transformation myths throughout human history, to add to your issue of a myopic viewpoint. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Live in tribes, war with tribes unless an evil comes along</div> </div> </div> </div>What matriarchal societies that have existed or still exist today have been tribal societies. These tribes sometimes went to war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshift and murder things for food with their own teeth</div> </div> </div> </div>Savagery is not a masculine trait, it's an 'inhuman' trait.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Flower,Innocent;n978809]Intimidate passers by with the presence of their sheer anger./quote]<br /> <br /> Women are more renowned for this in history than men are, see Rudyard Kipling's 'The Female of the Species'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are prone to violent rages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Men don't experience PMS. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now. I think it's fair to say that most of these lead us to a western interpretation of masculine, maybe even hyper-masculine.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, it doesn't. The western interpretation of masculine has changed a lot in the west, aside from a few outliers. Second, who cares? So what? The game in question rejects human society and interpretations of what is and isn't acceptable behavior. What you are really and truly arguing is that women should not enjoy werewolf because it's a purely masculine game with nothing for them, except they do enjoy it, and find reasons to play it, mostly because your interpretation of the setting is like Peleps Deled navigating a ball house while blind folded and drugged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, The Ajaba have their females more &quot;warrior&quot; than their males and most of this stuff applies to them, but the point is that they're still a 'macho' society, even if their gender ideas have been flipped (or ours have been flipped, or whatever).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Even if the gender roles are flipped they're 'actually' still behaving like men!&quot; Excuse me, what? Do you even know what macho/machismo means? I have to assume you do because you're consistently using it in the proper context, but your argument makes no sense. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liking 'girly' things isn't an issue. Becoming 'feminine' in behaviour is. To be more like a girl, you've got to throw away a lot of things that both garou nature and garou society give you.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Excuse me, but that's bullshit. As I mentioned earlier a trans woman does not have to do anything, or put up with anything, to be a 'practicing female' that any cis-woman doesn't also have to do/put up with. For some transwoman, the transition means taking some pills, developing the appropriate secondary sexual characteristics, and having surgery to correct the primary characteristics, that's it. Statistically you have interacted with a transwoman who you simply accepted as a ciswoman purely because you did not have an inside look into their private lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if you wanna play the man-turn-woman, and be feminine, you're doomed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Way to misunderstand what transgender individuals are, or what people going through gender dysphoria require as treatment. This is only true if you believe that the only way for a transwoman to be a woman is to be a hyper feminized doll, and even <i>that</i> has a place in Werewolf and would lead to a lot of personal drama as she constantly gets kicked into the dirt by her elders, her instincts, and her nature as a savage predator. It turns into a tragic story of whether or not she'll change or break.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanna play the man-turn woman, and be at an acceptable level of feminine whilst still being appropriately masculine, what's the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>This logic makes no goddamn sense, by this same argument no one should play female characters in Werewolf, period. Why play a female character if you're 'actually' just playing a guy? Do you even read or listen to the thoughts you put out there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wonder of garou society is that men and women are equal (unless you're BF or a certain kind of GF) but the problem here lies that, to the average joe, you're considerably more 'masculine'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not hardly, there is plenty to distinguish a man and a woman beyond just being STR0NG or behaving like a predator. If you can't think of any examples for yourself then it illustrates a lacking in your soul, I strongly encourage you to make some female friends and learn the fine art of empathy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Garou child can walk into a den of monsterous child molesters and act as if she didn't have a single fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>... What? Uh... Sure I guess? If he or she is a metis? Any homid won't have changed as a child, any Lupus lives for about a year or three before changing and being a full adult, so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You never need to cross the road to avoid shady guys. You can have anyone you want in your bed with the eye-rape power. If a guy wolf-whistles you, you challenge him to a formal duel and run him through with your klaive.</div> </div> </div> </div>No reason why this might serve as a source of empowerment to women - or a population that is constantly being murdered for what they are. Nope, not at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not going to threat too much over dresses beyond how much they hide, because you've probably got a really nasty scar visible somewhere</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll assume you meant to type 'fret'. You're still 'assuming' that a transwoman cares anymore about dresses than a ciswoman does. Also, yes, they do, read the Shadow Lord tribe novel, read the Glasswalker tribe novel, read the tribe anything for any tribe that regularly deals with humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou psychology favours the masculine,Or the one in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure in your next post you're going to say something truly outrageous, like: &quot;WOMEN WERE BORN TO BLEED IN THE BIRTHING BED, MEN WERE BORN TO BLEED ON THE BATTLEFIELD, THAT IS THE NATURE OF THE SPECIES MAN.&quot;<br /> <br /> Garou psychology favors your own compartmentalized notion of what masculinity is, which seems to be prepackaged with the assumption that women are meek lost and alone children, who care more about dresses and looking good than they do about social hierarchies or rank.<br /> <br /> You're wrong, by the way, according to every discipline of science that bothers to look into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone's a warrior, but you have nothing to fear from normal people, who likely cower before you, and you are empowered through that. You can be somewhat nuetral about this, resentful of it, or you can lord it over others. You can be 'that well-adjusted soldier in a war film' level of manly or you can be an action hero of the man's masculine ideal. But you're a warrior of Gaia, so, you're always going to be predisposed towards a certain mentality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you can be the protagonist of the Tamir Trilogy, or you could be akin to the furies of greek myth, or the amazons, or a mother wolf who will give <i>anything</i> to protect her cubs, especially her life, like Raksha in the Jungle Book. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978809#post978809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only difference between men and women is how they have children in a garou society. Really. That's it. (other than the BF thing)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why you're so adamant about the veracity of your position when you've already confessed to not knowing the setting. Again, read any of the tribe novels, for this specific statement - especially Shadow Lords and Get of Fenris. You're demonstrably wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T21:33:35-07:00","id":978843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978837#post978837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...snip...</div> </div> </div> </div>Realizing this doesn't add much to the discussion, but I would Like this post more than once if I could. Most of the points I thought of to chime in with people have already covered.<br /> <br /> Also, going into this thread, I was pretty sure it would end up horribly offensive and get shut down by Mods. Kudos to you guys for having a civil discussion that is (mostly?) somewhat non-offensive.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T00:03:28-07:00","id":978895,"title":"","content":"Alright. Let's make it really simple so we don't battle it out with lists that continually disprove of what the other person said. <br /> The garou represent this 'warrior ideal' mixed with the 'beast ideal'. Powerful and primal. In their animal, they are like humans.In their human, they are like the beasts. <br /> A great beast is a great beast, and if you're hunting or being hunted by some legendary beast, the only difference is between 'he' and 'she' is what you call it. It doesn't matter if it's the white whale, the Kraken, the red dragon, whatever. Except for the few bestial rapists, your gender and their gender matters little to each-other. The question isn't &quot;will it love me?&quot; but rather &quot;will it eat me?&quot;. The point being: Garou in their homid form are still &quot;of the wolf&quot;. They still have their lupus half of them hidden away. There's not a massive difference between wolf genders. So any massive difference that could be there on the homid side will be dampened by the lesser difference of the wolf side. All that really matters in wolf gender is their roll in family life. And deviating in that is likely totally permissible. You add the 'war' bit to the garou. The rage and Gaia's pain and whatnot. You get someone who ultimately isn't defined by their gender (but maybe by their rage). <br /> With that in mind, I'm not really sure if a non-cis character would or should have the impact some people think it would. If a character was really vocal, the party whip would tell them to focus on the wider issues, and they did not, they'd be punished. Garou probably don't trust blue-for-boys pink-for-girls mentality, but they'd not promote transgender any more than any other issue. You're a warrior, focus on fighting the wyrm. Don't create internal conflict. Conform to the cultural identity and rules of your tribe Etc. <br /> I can easily see someone giving the line 'you wouldn't reject your auspice, so why would you reject your gender?' (even though some do reject auspice. I'm sure there's a connection there) <br /> <br /> <br /> I still find it weird that I'm the 'Gender no longer matters' guy and I'm considered the sexist. Maybe I'm a heartless iron man with issues like this because I have no problems beyond an empty bank account. No psychological issues or even physical ones (baring a probable stroke at 40) I'm a cold fish. But I think/hope that my only agenda is getting WoD close to the slightly shittier reality it's promised to be, and I'm not biassed by strong pro/anti transgender views. Sometimes it's better to show something clearly unjust than it is to have it favour you, if you want to make a point. <br /> <br /> I don't read the novels. Part of me dreads the prospect, because I know how inconsistent white wolf can be. I've Read most of the revised era tribebooks, some revised umbra stuff, some black dog stuff and all the w20 stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T00:35:42-07:00","id":978902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978895#post978895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not a massive difference between wolf genders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there isn't really such a thing as proper &quot;gender&quot; in wolves. Gender is the social construct, not the sex of the animal. Roles enforced by biology and instinct aren't the same as a socially constructed gender. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So any massive difference that could be there on the homid side will be dampened by the lesser difference of the wolf side. </div> </div> </div>I don't think this really fits the way the books construct the characters. Garou are not dual-personality characters. A homid isn't like a vampire with &quot;the man,&quot; and &quot;the beast&quot; struggling for control. A homid is a single entity with a set of instincts and drives that are different from humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still find it weird that I'm the 'Gender no longer matters' guy and I'm considered the sexist </div> </div> </div>The issue is that your attempt to construct Garou society as an inherently masculine society and/or would be interpreted by outsiders as more masculine is essentially a sexist argument when sex doesn't actually impact a Garou's ability to contribute to their warrior society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:08:51-07:00","id":978911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978895#post978895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The garou represent this 'warrior ideal' mixed with the 'beast ideal'. Powerful and primal. In their animal, they are like humans.In their human, they are like the beasts. A great beast is a great beast, and if you're hunting or being hunted by some legendary beast, the only difference is between 'he' and 'she' is what you call it. It doesn't matter if it's the white whale, the Kraken, the red dragon, whatever. Except for the few bestial rapists, your gender and their gender matters little to each-other.</div> </div> </div> </div>This paragraph (and it is a paragraph, try formatting sometime) is only <i>barely</i> coherent. The only difference between 'he' and 'she' is a lot when it comes to wilderness survival with animals. A female bear with cubs is going to be far more aggressive than a male bear, a female black widow is far more aggressive than the male, and so on. You even mention whales, which is ironic, because many pods of whales are matriarchal, with males kept on the periphery. Many big cats also do this. You can't have the argument that a concept is invalid because werewolves are too masculine but also oops they're just animals and animals don't have gender, so the idea has no value. It makes the motivations behind your argument fairly transparent.<br /> <br /> And also, wolves 'do' have gender, speaking as someone who studied them quite a bit, and as I mentioned, a hunter or survivalist 'will' tell the difference between they're experienced and trained to notice those differences, you, not being either of those things, likely won't notice the difference. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978895#post978895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question isn't &quot;will it love me?&quot; but rather &quot;will it eat me?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... your first thought on seeing a human woman is whether or not she'll 'love' you in any sense of the word? That's not... creepy, at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978895#post978895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point being: Garou in their homid form are still &quot;of the wolf&quot;. They still have their lupus half of them hidden away. There's not a massive difference between wolf genders. So any massive difference that could be there on the homid side will be dampened by the lesser difference of the wolf side.</div> </div> </div> </div>The inherent difference between genders in humans is also not that massive, aside from the the social foibles foisted on them by a society that spent thousands of years limiting their freedoms, choices, and treating them like property. Even the Red Talons are far more human than they care to admit, to degrees that frighten them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978895#post978895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that really matters in wolf gender is their roll in family life. And deviating in that is likely totally permissible. You add the 'war' bit to the garou. The rage and Gaia's pain and whatnot. You get someone who ultimately isn't defined by their gender (but maybe by their rage)</div> </div> </div> </div>A wolf is a sentient animal, a human is a sapient animal. A werewolf is also a sapient animal. Werewolves have rage, they have predatory instincts. You even go so far as to mention 'Gaia's Pain', which really is just a testament to how much empathy garou have with the world, a trait normal wolves do not have. Garou are defined by anything and everything a human would be defined by, yes, including the Lupus, whether the Red Talons are comfortable with that or not. .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978895#post978895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind, I'm not really sure if a non-cis character would or should have the impact some people think it would. If a character was really vocal, the party whip would tell them to focus on the wider issues, and they did not, they'd be punished. Garou probably don't trust blue-for-boys pink-for-girls mentality, but they'd not promote transgender any more than any other issue. You're a warrior, focus on fighting the wyrm. Don't create internal conflict. Conform to the cultural identity and rules of your tribe Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>So which is it? Are Garou war-crazed animals with nothing on their mind but bloodlust, or are they highly complex social creatures, just like humans, with nuanced political systems that include a governing nation, offices, political seats, and 'house whips'? You don't get to have both. At the end of the day this point is also <i>demonstrably wrong</i>, because the Black Furies care about protecting women, children, and the oppressed, the Silent Striders fight to get their home back, the Children of Gaia work to create peaceful relations. The Get of Fenris care about their bloodlines, the Shadow Lords care about political <b>power</b>, the Glasswalkers care about augmenting the self. The Fianna care about art and song. The war effort is a part of life, but it's not the only facet of a werewolf's existence, if it were, Apocalypse would be a dull uninteresting story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978895#post978895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can easily see someone giving the line 'you wouldn't reject your auspice, so why would you reject your gender?' (even though some do reject auspice. I'm sure there's a connection there)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, there are plenty of Garou who also happen to pose non sequitors. It's cute that you refute your own point in the same sentence, though. Yes, Garou do reject their auspice, there is a rite and procedures in place for doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978895#post978895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find it weird that I'm the 'Gender no longer matters' guy and I'm considered the sexist. Maybe I'm a heartless iron man with issues like this because I have no problems beyond an empty bank account. No psychological issues or even physical ones (baring a probable stroke at 40) I'm a cold fish. But I think/hope that my only agenda is getting WoD close to the slightly shittier reality it's promised to be, and I'm not biassed by strong pro/anti transgender views. Sometimes it's better to show something clearly unjust than it is to have it favour you, if you want to make a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't get to say racist things and then say &quot;I'm the only one here who is colorblind and yet somehow I'm still racist.&quot; You're sexist because all you've done in this thread is spout sexist ideas in an attempt to explain why transcharacters have no place in werewolf, whilst sniping femininity in general in the crossfire. You're sexist because you claim warrior outlooks are a necessarily male concept. Also, gender is a thing that exists, in humans and animals, and it is important or we wouldn't have Gender Studies, it just doesn't work the way you seem to think it does. So please stop with the nonsensical claims that you <i>think</i> progressive people want to hear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't read the novels. Part of me dreads the prospect, because I know how inconsistent white wolf can be. I've Read most of the revised era tribebooks, some revised umbra stuff, some black dog stuff and all the w20 stuff. </div> </div> </div>You mean you have no interest in seeing any of the themes in practice because it would be contrary to the assumptions you've foisted on the settings and the people who took the time to create them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:14:56-07:00","id":978915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978902#post978902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because there isn't really such a thing as proper &quot;gender&quot; in wolves. Gender is the social construct, not the sex of the animal. Roles enforced by biology and instinct aren't the same as a socially constructed gender.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think this really fits the way the books construct the characters. Garou are not dual-personality characters. A homid isn't like a vampire with &quot;the man,&quot; and &quot;the beast&quot; struggling for control. A homid is a single entity with a set of instincts and drives that are different from humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The issue is that your attempt to construct Garou society as an inherently masculine society and/or would be interpreted by outsiders as more masculine is essentially a sexist argument when sex doesn't actually impact a Garou's ability to contribute to their warrior society.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gender, by my understanding, has many facets, among which is the general behavior in a group of animals. They share similar pronouns to 'sex' because there is typically relation between the two, in other words, lionesses will hunt, female jaguars will raise their young and often chase the male away once they've given birth, etc, etc. The reason why animals have gender, and these are gender behaviors, is because sometimes an animal of the male sex will behave differently, or a female likewise. Animals with complex social behaviors are even more likely to exhibit this, which is why I refer to wolves having gender, because that is what the evidence suggests.<br /> <br /> Certainly they're not gender roles the way Innocent views them, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T02:59:36-07:00","id":978937,"title":"","content":"I appreciate what you saying, but for me it is always important to not anthropomorphize when dealing with non-human animal behavioral studies. We can't ask a lioness about how she feels regarding what biology demands of her and her social role in her pride as it relates to her biological sex.<br /> <br /> When dealing with humans, it is very easy to demonstrate the separate of sex and gender, because we can show how different groups of humans consider a given behavior &quot;masculine,&quot; &quot;feminine,&quot; or, &quot;neutral.&quot; For example there are modern human cultures that consider relatively heavy applications of make-up a &quot;feminine&quot; behavior (ex: most Western mainstream cultures), others that consider it a masculine behavior (ex: some of the Saharan indigenous tribal groups model masculine sexual displays after birds which includes being more colorful via make up), etc.<br /> <br /> When dealing with non-human animals that gets extremely difficult to suss out; if not impossible. There are very few animals on earth where we can observe disparate social groups that have clearly developed their own cultures to even begin to try to look at if they have gender that can vary from social unit to social unit. When we study orca pods - which display some of the widest diversity in social cultures of non-human animals - we just don't see any real evidence of &quot;gender&quot; that can be separated from sex. Even when there's some separation, there are other factors. For example in pods that have more &quot;individual skill&quot; focused cultures (that is, their life strategies tend to focus on each individual hunting and so on for themselves) mothers do far more teaching. In pods that focus more on communal skills, teaching is... more communal. But all orcas seem to actually treat those teach methods the same way, with the time spent on each being more important than any sort of gender role that varies from pod to pod.<br /> <br /> We can't really say that &quot;males and females behaving differently,&quot; establishes gender in non-human animals, because that abandons the idea of socially constructed genders: lots of non-social animals have sex based differences in behaviors. How can they establish genders if they don't form social units?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T04:41:02-07:00","id":978949,"title":"","content":"Relevant: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8fhpXrrLBsI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8fhpXrrLBsI</a><br /> <br /> This video is the White Wolf Q&amp;A from Grand Masquerade 2016. The relevant bit is fairly brief, but starts at around 10 minutes, and specifically reference to including transgender Black Furies referenced at 10:40. It's brief, but to the point.<br /> <br /> The following bit by Marcus is interesting, but listen to all of it before reaching for any conclusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 09-30-2016, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:04:36-07:00","id":978953,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that a tribe that honours Artemis would follow the example of Artemis and view transformation of gender as entirely possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:54:30-07:00","id":978969,"title":"","content":"Mildly annoyed that, even when I backpedaled, you went for it. You make a big deal out of animal gender being so important despite saying that my comments of masculinity and femininity are outdated? Listen man, You can pick and choose, but just because something didn't work for you doesn't mean that they're suddenly invalid for everyone. And I really dislike how much you're inflating what I'm saying to give yourself an argument. Guess I was wrong 'bout initial assumptions.<br /> <br /> Gender identity in animals is a simple thing, probably synonymous with gender rolls. It's about who hunts and who looks out for children and how territory works and a few other things.<br /> Gender Identity in humans; We could say it's a bit more complicated. We could also say that it's simple, and the majority of the problems are from cultural stigmas rather than problems.<br /> <br /> A garou is not just a human. It's material and spirit, man and beast. Fill it with rage and call it a monster. Regardless, to NORMAL HUMANS, who get freaked the fuck out by rage, they are going to feel like you're a predator. Go into a nightclub and you'll give off predator vibes and everyone's instinct will tell them that you're a weirdo. You're unsettling them because of the animal, because rage isn't just magic anger. but if you go lupus for a bit, the problem is the human in your rage. Or maybe this is entirely just you? Now, the usual prelude to the first change is a dysphoria on it's own. As a homid, You feel a disconnect between society. It's not just rage, it's the wolf (and lupus feel the intellegence of the man seperating them from the pack)<br /> <br /> As a homid, you're going to be a bit wolf. As a Lupus, you're a bit like man. If we look at art for every other changing breed, there's some truth to this. Ghural for instance look more like bears in homid. Ratkin look ratlike.<br /> So, if you're a bit more wolf, and let's say you got unlucky enough to have gender dysphoria, chances are it'll be lessened in effect by the fact that there's some wolf in you, who suffer less, and the fact that you'll be distancing yourself from human society/culture as you are slowly taught that everything's poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:02:49-07:00","id":979023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978937#post978937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate what you saying, but for me it is always important to not anthropomorphize when dealing with non-human animal behavioral studies. We can't ask a lioness about how she feels regarding what biology demands of her and her social role in her pride as it relates to her biological sex.<br /> <br /> When dealing with humans, it is very easy to demonstrate the separate of sex and gender, because we can show how different groups of humans consider a given behavior &quot;masculine,&quot; &quot;feminine,&quot; or, &quot;neutral.&quot; For example there are modern human cultures that consider relatively heavy applications of make-up a &quot;feminine&quot; behavior (ex: most Western mainstream cultures), others that consider it a masculine behavior (ex: some of the Saharan indigenous tribal groups model masculine sexual displays after birds which includes being more colorful via make up), etc.<br /> <br /> When dealing with non-human animals that gets extremely difficult to suss out; if not impossible. There are very few animals on earth where we can observe disparate social groups that have clearly developed their own cultures to even begin to try to look at if they have gender that can vary from social unit to social unit. When we study orca pods - which display some of the widest diversity in social cultures of non-human animals - we just don't see any real evidence of &quot;gender&quot; that can be separated from sex. Even when there's some separation, there are other factors. For example in pods that have more &quot;individual skill&quot; focused cultures (that is, their life strategies tend to focus on each individual hunting and so on for themselves) mothers do far more teaching. In pods that focus more on communal skills, teaching is... more communal. But all orcas seem to actually treat those teach methods the same way, with the time spent on each being more important than any sort of gender role that varies from pod to pod.<br /> <br /> We can't really say that &quot;males and females behaving differently,&quot; establishes gender in non-human animals, because that abandons the idea of socially constructed genders: lots of non-social animals have sex based differences in behaviors. How can they establish genders if they don't form social units?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, but that raises the problem of an inconsistent definition. There are, for example, individuals in the transgender community who have no interest in dresses, or female typical gender displays, and only seek treatment due to mental and emotional tension regarding their body, but we don't call these people 'Transsexual' until after they've received hormones or in many cases, received surgery, but no one is going to deny that they're transgender. There are a lot of people in feminism who are adamantly against the notion that gender can be <b>anything</b> but social construct, my own anecdotal experience suggests that, unless we're going to start redefining what sex and gender actually mean, then there are parts of gender that are inborn, gender being a spectrum, though, it's difficult to nail these things because there is unlimited possibility for variance.<br /> <br /> And I don't so much consider it 'anthropomorphizing animals' as it is shrinking the britches of humanity, which in general really likes to set itself again or apart from the rest of the animal kingdom. In my own research the context has been that gender refers to behavior and personality, any behavior and personality, sex refers purely to the biological and physical characteristics of the person place or thing in question. <br /> <br /> But I majored in Psychology, not Gender Studies, so I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:26:50-07:00","id":979039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978969#post978969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mildly annoyed that, even when I backpedaled, you went for it. You make a big deal out of animal gender being so important despite saying that my comments of masculinity and femininity are outdated? Listen man, You can pick and choose, but just because something didn't work for you doesn't mean that they're suddenly invalid for everyone. And I really dislike how much you're inflating what I'm saying to give yourself an argument. Guess I was wrong 'bout initial assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arrogantly stating that it's your way or the reject everything the game and book stands for way is not back pedaling. No, not even after you complete invalidate both of your arguments when you haphazardly throw shit at the wall to see what will stick. Gender is important or we wouldn't study it. It's important to a lot of people, the issue is when you come in and assert that werewolf is a masculine game for masculine people and masculine themes, only. It's when you come into a thread that was mostly civil and then present your case like Peleps Deled, where the first mistake anyone else makes is having an interpretation of the gameline at all. It comes from your stubborn refusal to accept that there is more than one way to be a woman in this world for the sake of excluding broad groups 'in general'. Let's be clear, the brunt of your argument is that transwomen have no place in Werewolf the Apocalypse, period. Not in the Children of Gaia, not in the Glasswalkers. If you wanted to come into this thread and make a case against them being in the Black Furies, that would have been fine, that's the question this thread is meant to answer. You didn't, you came in with some very heavy handed generalizations that, if you follow to their conclusion, means that it's pointless to explore <i>any </i>non-male characters in werewolf. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978969#post978969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gender identity in animals is a simple thing, probably synonymous with gender rolls. It's about who hunts and who looks out for children and how territory works and a few other things.<br /> Gender Identity in humans; We could say it's a bit more complicated. We could also say that it's simple, and the majority of the problems are from cultural stigmas rather than problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything with the number of contributing factors gender has is not going to be simple, is my argument. Non-Human animals have simple 'displays' of gender because they are simple-minded, and almost without except, non-sapient. This doesn't mean anything for werewolf, any Lupus is going to be borderline sapient right from the beginning, he or she will be considered an oddity by the rest of the pack, it will make them uncomfortable, and he or she <b>will</b> be foisted out. Expressing a more complex gender would be one source of tension between themselves and normal wolves. This is another reason why looking at gender as purely a social construct imposed on you by other people is not necessarily helpful, because we also create gender for ourselves, and this is likely something a Lupus would do, it's something that would set them apart, and when they do change, and their mind expands further, the stakes will only become sharper in contrast. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978969#post978969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A garou is not just a human. It's material and spirit, man and beast. Fill it with rage and call it a monster. Regardless, to NORMAL HUMANS, who get freaked the fuck out by rage, they are going to feel like you're a predator. Go into a nightclub and you'll give off predator vibes and everyone's instinct will tell them that you're a weirdo. You're unsettling them because of the animal, because rage isn't just magic anger. but if you go lupus for a bit, the problem is the human in your rage. Or maybe this is entirely just you? Now, the usual prelude to the first change is a dysphoria on it's own. As a homid, You feel a disconnect between society. It's not just rage, it's the wolf (and lupus feel the intellegence of the man seperating them from the pack)</div> </div> </div> </div>The human part is often what is most relevant in the context of werewolf because that's where your drama is coming from. The Red Talon desire to assault the Wyrm, to protect their kinfolk, etc - these are not the sorts of things wolves could conceptualize or pursue, it's on a scale that is beyond them for all that they are highly social animals capable of planning hunts days, weeks, or even seasons in advance. And yes, Garou who have yet to change do experience Dysphoria, so do Kinfolk, arguably, who may never change at all. There's plenty there for a transgender person to relate to and identify with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978969#post978969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a homid, you're going to be a bit wolf. As a Lupus, you're a bit like man. If we look at art for every other changing breed, there's some truth to this. Ghural for instance look more like bears in homid. Ratkin look ratlike.<br /> So, if you're a bit more wolf, and let's say you got unlucky enough to have gender dysphoria, chances are it'll be lessened in effect by the fact that there's some wolf in you, who suffer less, and the fact that you'll be distancing yourself from human society/culture as you are slowly taught that everything's poison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except there are plenty of transgender people who would be trans if they existed in a vacuum and had to define themselves from nothing. because their physical brain, that thing what is responsible for consciousness at all, is at odds with its body, and that body's chemistry. <br /> <br /> Yes, you are part wolf, but as previously mentioned being a wolf does not make you 'simple' it does not detract from your sapience, all it means is that you are a sapient wolf, and if wolves were sapient they'd care a lot more than they already do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:25:08-07:00","id":979343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978688#post978688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the argument that spirits would view a trans person as a deceiver instead of perceiving their true gender. The meat body you're in matters so little to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, as written I think spirits in WtA are kind of overly literal. In a sense, I think the conservativeness of the Garou (like Breed and Auspice roles) is probably in no small part enforced or even forced by the spirits, who are (up until a certain power level) incapable of divergent or open-minded thought. Spirits, who are themselves the spiritual manifestations of concepts or ideas, are extremely narrow-sighted in just about everything based on the concept they represent. I doubt they would perceive or tolerate duality or conflict between physicality and nature. Just like a War-spirit wants to be in a weapon, and a healing spirit in medicine.<br /> <br /> If we're to say Gender is a social construct, it would be fair to say that it's one that doesn't- or barely- exists outside of human society. Only sex exists in raw nature, and trying to explain anything beyond that to an animal or a spirit would probably be met with irritation at best, frustration and anger at worst.<br /> <br /> Again, I stress, I'm talking about spirits AS WRITTEN IN THIS FICTITIOUS GAME BOOK. This is clearly a sensitive issue in which many have personal stakes. I'm attempting as best I can to weigh in as an unbiased outsider, looking only at game concepts as they relate to the topic as written. I'm not trying to advocate what's better, fair, right, what should-be, or even what makes the most sense for the setting. This is my take on the answer from the fictional reality we read about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:47:08-07:00","id":979362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979039#post979039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except there are plenty of transgender people who would be trans if they existed in a vacuum and had to define themselves from nothing. because their physical brain, that thing what is responsible for consciousness at all, is at odds with its body, and that body's chemistry.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a bio-chemist, this is the statement I've kind of avoided up until now (despite passionately agreeing with), because it begs a question... Do Garou wear glasses at the same rate as humans? Do they have impacted wisdom teeth, or heterochromia (a very groovy mutation), or dwarfism, or huntington's, asperger's, down syndrome, polydactyly, or anything else that deviates genetically from some convoluted, uncomplicated &quot;ideal&quot; (which the vast majority of us don't meet) at the same rates as regular humans?<br /> <br /> Because I've generally assumed not.<br /> <br /> And while all of these things are completely normal and natural parts of the human experience, I don't legitimately know if they're part of the Garou experience. The majority of people need or wear glasses, yet it's often a flaw for PCs in the WoD as though it weren't technically &quot;the norm&quot;. Between the already relatively low numbers of trans people, combined with the incredibly low number of Garou... and add in the assumption that Garou enjoy at least some level of genetic favoritism toward specific slices of the bell curves, and there may only be an extremely small number of Garou who this entire question addresses.<br /> <br /> There may be no good answer... because the PC might be unique, or a member of such an exclusive number that they might as well be unique. Would the tribes have an official stance on trans Garou if you could count on your fingers how many were born to each?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:51:56-07:00","id":979365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979343#post979343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, as written I think spirits in WtA are kind of overly literal. In a sense, I think the conservativeness of the Garou (like Breed and Auspice roles) is probably in no small part enforced or even forced by the spirits, who are (up until a certain power level) incapable of divergent or open-minded thought. Spirits, who are themselves the spiritual manifestations of concepts or ideas, are extremely narrow-sighted in just about everything based on the concept they represent. I doubt they would perceive or tolerate duality or conflict between physicality and nature. Just like a War-spirit wants to be in a weapon, and a healing spirit in medicine.<br /> <br /> If we're to say Gender is a social construct, it would be fair to say that it's one that doesn't- or barely- exists outside of human society. Only sex exists in raw nature, and trying to explain anything beyond that to an animal or a spirit would probably be met with irritation at best, frustration and anger at worst.<br /> <br /> Again, I stress, I'm talking about spirits AS WRITTEN IN THIS FICTITIOUS GAME BOOK. This is clearly a sensitive issue in which many have personal stakes. I'm attempting as best I can to weigh in as an unbiased outsider, looking only at game concepts as they relate to the topic as written. I'm not trying to advocate what's better, fair, right, what should-be, or even what makes the most sense for the setting. This is my take on the answer from the fictional reality we read about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry that we've reached the point where you feel you need to walk on eggshells to offer your thoughts, it's not the kind of tone I wanted for the thread, but it's the one that's come to dominate it in the last couple of pages.<br /> <br /> I personally don't interpret Garou society to be any form of spirit-led police state, if anything that would be contrary to their role as assigned by Gaia. If you're a kinfolk then that's a bird of a different feather, and would depend on a lot of factors. You're right that lower level spirits aren't as open-minded but that's not because they are necessarily conservative, it's because they are simple-minded, low level spirits are effectively wearing blinders, and I don't imagine they're going to care or have opinions on transgender individuals unless they are specifically a spirit of a relevant concept. If you go into a church the spirits probably aren't going to like it. If you go into a place where counter culture is rife and freedom of expression is encouraged, then a spirit might take someone who is otherwise content with their identity and give them a little push outside of their comfort zone.<br /> <br /> It's really situational, and a subject like that could probably warrant its own thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:55:47-07:00","id":979371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979362#post979362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a bio-chemist, this is the statement I've kind of avoided up until now (despite passionately agreeing with), because it begs a question... Do Garou wear glasses at the same rate as humans? Do they have impacted wisdom teeth, or heterochromia (a very groovy mutation), or dwarfism, or huntington's, asperger's, down syndrome, polydactyly, or anything else that deviates genetically from some convoluted, uncomplicated &quot;ideal&quot; (which the vast majority of us don't meet) at the same rates as regular humans?<br /> <br /> Because I've generally assumed not.<br /> <br /> And while all of these things are completely normal and natural parts of the human experience, I don't legitimately know if they're part of the Garou experience. The majority of people need or wear glasses, yet it's often a flaw for PCs in the WoD as though it weren't technically &quot;the norm&quot;. Between the already relatively low numbers of trans people, combined with the incredibly low number of Garou... and add in the assumption that Garou enjoy at least some level of genetic favoritism toward specific slices of the bell curves, and there may only be an extremely small number of Garou who this entire question addresses.<br /> <br /> There may be no good answer... because the PC might be unique, or a member of such an exclusive number that they might as well be unique. Would the tribes have an official stance on trans Garou if you could count on your fingers how many were born to each?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a really good question, my thoughts are that if it does come up, it's probably very spiritually significant. Heterochromia for example has been evidence in cultures that a child is 'special' and marked by the spirits, transgender behaviors have been too. With werewolves a good rule of thumb is that nothing pertaining to them is purely biological. Crippling gender dysphoria could conceivably be a valid Metis flaw, in my mind. It's problematic, but Metis in general are problematic in that they are spiritually being punished for the actions of their parents.<br /> <br /> Also the first half of that movie was the grooviest thing, I felt it was kind of downhill once it started being about the xmen, though : \\","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T18:30:42-07:00","id":979391,"title":"","content":"Not that its important but had to say it<br /> &lt;-----Heterochrome here...I tell all my students I'm my own twin brother!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T18:38:26-07:00","id":979399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979391#post979391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that its important but had to say it<br /> &lt;-----Heterochrome here...I tell all my students I'm my own twin brother!</div> </div> </div> </div>can you sacrifice yourself to yourself for more power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T18:45:15-07:00","id":979403,"title":"","content":"not sure....I've never tried...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T18:46:23-07:00","id":979404,"title":"","content":"Writers have a choice when writing things that bump up against transphobia and the serious real life issues surrounding it. They can either write groups that are divided by gender as accepting of trans membership or they can write them as not, but accept that doing so will alienate many people who otherwise might be interested in exploring their game because it's <i>transphobic as fuck</i> and that it's a step back from their stated policies of acceptance.<br /> <br /> You don't get to leave great heaping turds of transphobia in your book and then claim that you're respecting the source material and get a free pass any more.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T19:16:31-07:00","id":979420,"title":"","content":"Personally, as I stated before in this thread, I do think it is important that there is a discussion in the setting about Black Furies and trans people.<br /> <br /> Mainly, because Black Furies do in fact nicely how a tribe based on ideals of equality and rights can end up fighting itself over what defines their focus.<br /> <br /> Especially, like the Children of Gaia, Black Furies have this divide between them the new blood and the older generations. With the new blood being active in protests and issues, while the old guard usually are more spiritually focused. And especially in Furies, that old guard tend to be very alien to the new blood. Many Crones embrace being witches, and they even have a rite meant to curse entire bloodlines, among other things.<br /> <br /> So having Black Furies be divided on the matter of trans people makes sense. Of course, the setting -itself- should not be against them, only just the npcs. Still, having the tribe fight over this, even as a background event, can add to the game by showing that aspect of the tribe well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T19:34:02-07:00","id":979430,"title":"","content":"I am actually surprised that people consider anger and aggression to be an 'inhuman' emotion rather than a perfectly human emotion. In fact, in my own family, we have a centuries long history, dating back to the 6th century AD, where both the men and women of my family experienced levels of aggression and anger equal to that of the fictional Garou. I do not see the Rage of the Garou as an 'inhuman' curse, I see it as a family trait, just as I see their issues of controlling their Rage as identical to my own family's issues with controlling their anger.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there are no 'male' or 'female' social traits in humans. While there are reproductive roles for each sex, anything beyond that is 'gender', which is desinged by society as a way to assign job roles. In the developed world, they are anachronisms that rarely have a relevant role in society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T19:50:58-07:00","id":979436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978297#post978297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy Arms touched on it slightly, but just a reminder... when the game was first written (by authors who probably didn't have degrees in the historical groups the tribes were mimicking, and 15 years before anyone could just look it all up on their phone) most of the Garou were the BAD GUYS. I can't stress that enough... a major plot point of the game was that the Garou were mostly to blame for everything being as bad as it was, but they're the only ones still around to fix it (also their fault).... and they weren't about to get their act together any time soon. Supernatural Rage left most Garou presented as super-charged racists, bigots and abusers... with the PCs as perhaps the sole beacons of hope along with a select few NPCs. The World of Darkness, and especially Garou, were a caricature of everything an angst-ridden Nine-Inch-Nails fan from the 90s would say was wrong with America (because the game was written from a pretty American perspective, as well).<br /> <br /> So, in a game world designed to highlight the frustration of beating your head against stubborn ignorance and unapologetic ego, the question of how a Tribe would react to anything would have been pretty clear: whatever the worse answer is. (And for the most part, this is still the answer I choose)<br /> <br /> Of course there have been rewrites, retcons, new authors, more research, and even new discoveries in the cultures and mythologies involved. If you know more about a culture than the authors (which you well could... they're RPG authors, not gods) then you might want to adjust your game setting to make more sense in that capacity. If you want a more progressive game where Garou are sensible, thinking people rather than the biggest obstacles to their own success... go for it.<br /> <br /> Just keep in mind that there have been very stark changes in a lot of elements over the course of 4 editions and 24 years. Any forum-goer's opinions of what makes sense for Garou was probably forged by the first book they picked up, not the most recent one they own. I probably own every WtA book ever written, but I can say for certain I haven't reread the fluff chapters end-to-end four times, nor has all the new stuff effectively overwritten the old in my mind.<br /> <br /> A lot of the game we play today is layers of band aids wrapped around nostalgia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have often thought that. I would go far far as to say if there is a question about whether or not the Garou tolerate something, the default answer should be a resounding &quot;no&quot; unless there is some strong reason to suspect that they would. An exception would be Children of Gaia or other groups written as explicitly tolerant. The Black Furies are not that. They are zealots consumed by the bigotry and hatred. They have a history of killing male children and occasionally still do, it is hard to imagine what kind of mindset that could lead to such actions. Did those Black Furies who murdered their male infants ask the babies if they actually identified as females before they murdered them? I suspect not. <br /> <br /> This is a bit of a tangent, but it reminds me of an essay I read about Werewolf years ago, I don't recall where. The gist of it was that W:tA isn't a game about playing heroes. It is a game about playing religious fanatics. It is a game about being the Nazis. Why the Nazis? Because you are playing violent fanatics who hate and kill anything that falls outside of their narrow worldview. It was exactly this violence and hate which created many of the Garou's problems and still plagues them. Furthermore, the Garou have a worldview that they accept without the slightest bit of doubt, one where they are fighting absolute evil personified and where any horrific action can be justified for this supposed greater good. Murder a group of innocent children? They were going to grow up to be polluters anyway. Your buddy rapes kinfolk and likes to torture humans for fun - well, such foibles can be forgiven because he is fighting the Wyrm after all. A group kills their own male children for <i>reasons</i> - well, they serve Gaia and fight the Wyrm so those reasons must be alright. We can see how this sort of attitude could be used to justify virtually any evil and indeed has for the Garou, including the War of Rage and the Impergium. <br /> <br /> But, people didn't understand Garou as a game about getting into the mindset of villains, they thought that it actually was about heroes and so the game has become a mishmash of heroism and villainy. <br /> <br /> Of course, this is a controversial take on W:tA, but I think in many ways this vision of the game appeals to me more than &quot;Garou good, Wyrm bad, pass the wheelbarrow full of d10's&quot;<br /> <br /> In any case, I don't think you have to go quite as far as my post to be alright with a fictional organization within a fictional setting believing something that you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T19:51:17-07:00","id":979437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979430#post979430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am actually surprised that people consider anger and aggression to be an 'inhuman' emotion rather than a perfectly human emotion. In fact, in my own family, we have a centuries long history, dating back to the 6th century AD, where both the men and women of my family experienced levels of aggression and anger equal to that of the fictional Garou. I do not see the Rage of the Garou as an 'inhuman' curse, I see it as a family trait, just as I see their issues of controlling their Rage as identical to my own family's issues with controlling their anger.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there are no 'male' or 'female' social traits in humans. While there are reproductive roles for each sex, anything beyond that is 'gender', which is desinged by society as a way to assign job roles. In the developed world, they are anachronisms that rarely have a relevant role in society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anger is a human thing for sure, and it might be the human in them that allows the wyrm to give the garou their rage. That said, the rage garou have is phenominally on a bigger scale then that of the humans. Instead of getting mad, punching a wall and maybe stabbing someone its a supernatural death rage that leads to half a city being killed, with the werewolf likely not giving two shits beyond &quot;how am i going to cover this up.&quot; I feel like the disconnect here is from the much softer tone world of darkness has had lately. If you read the older material its very much evident that shit is not good. Reading some of this new stuff and the things on the forums, you'd think werewolves were super friendly types. They aint.<br /> <br /> I agree with you on gender roles. Modern civ has killed the human team spirit with the constant technology and ease of life (the irony of me using a computer while saying that isn't lost on me.). We've all lost something of the wilderness in our species and it only gets worse with each new development. One day, potentially soon we shall have no roles with which to fill but to be the slaves of our own equipment, more so then we are now. Maybe it is time onyx path wrote that book about the weaver ending the world instead of the wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T19:54:54-07:00","id":979438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979430#post979430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am actually surprised that people consider anger and aggression to be an 'inhuman' emotion rather than a perfectly human emotion. In fact, in my own family, we have a centuries long history, dating back to the 6th century AD, where both the men and women of my family experienced levels of aggression and anger equal to that of the fictional Garou. I do not see the Rage of the Garou as an 'inhuman' curse, I see it as a family trait, just as I see their issues of controlling their Rage as identical to my own family's issues with controlling their anger.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there are no 'male' or 'female' social traits in humans. While there are reproductive roles for each sex, anything beyond that is 'gender', which is desinged by society as a way to assign job roles. In the developed world, they are anachronisms that rarely have a relevant role in society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage is a supernatural force that transcends anger or aggression. This is specifically the nature of it in the game, and it's not well conveyed at times, which is one reason why I like Werewolf the Forsaken more, they make less of a to-do about it.<br /> <br /> When I personally referred to the Garou as inhuman, I'm referring specifically to their bestial predatory instincts, and those 'are' inhuman, even if humans exhibit them, because humans are animals. <br /> <br /> That said, claiming you or anyone in your family 'experiences anger or aggression to the extent the fictional garou do' puts you at <b>incredible</b> risk of sounding like a person trying to be edgy. The fact is, your family line still exists without shapeshifting super powers, so it can't be nearly that extreme or you all would have been put down by human society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:20:42-07:00","id":979449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979438#post979438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rage is a supernatural force that transcends anger or aggression. This is specifically the nature of it in the game, and it's not well conveyed at times, which is one reason why I like Werewolf the Forsaken more, they make less of a to-do about it.<br /> <br /> When I personally referred to the Garou as inhuman, I'm referring specifically to their bestial predatory instincts, and those 'are' inhuman, even if humans exhibit them, because humans are animals. <br /> <br /> That said, claiming you or anyone in your family 'experiences anger or aggression to the extent the fictional garou do' puts you at <b>incredible</b> risk of sounding like a person trying to be edgy. The fact is, your family line still exists without shapeshifting super powers, so it can't be nearly that extreme or you all would have been put down by human society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so. Scottish and Germanic bloodlines can be known for the blood rage and tempers still flair to this day. For those of us prone to incredible levels of anger the garou rage may seem very close to it. Still isn't, but I get where they're coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:36:50-07:00","id":979456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979436#post979436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit of a tangent, but it reminds me of an essay I read about Werewolf years ago, I don't recall where. The gist of it was that W:tA isn't a game about playing heroes. It is a game about playing religious fanatics. It is a game about being the Nazis. Why the Nazis? Because you are playing violent fanatics who hate and kill anything that falls outside of their narrow worldview. It was exactly this violence and hate which created many of the Garou's problems and still plagues them. Furthermore, the Garou have a worldview that they accept without the slightest bit of doubt, one where they are fighting absolute evil personified and where any horrific action can be justified for this supposed greater good. Murder a group of innocent children? They were going to grow up to be polluters anyway. Your buddy rapes kinfolk and likes to torture humans for fun - well, such foibles can be forgiven because he is fighting the Wyrm after all. A group kills their own male children for <i>reasons</i> - well, they serve Gaia and fight the Wyrm so those reasons must be alright. We can see how this sort of attitude could be used to justify virtually any evil and indeed has for the Garou, including the War of Rage and the Impergium.</div> </div> </div> </div>To follow this tangent a little, first editions of any WoD thing in general were more simplistic. And I think out of all the games, I think WtA really benefitted from having revised and W20 editions.<br /> <br /> But not because it made the garou heroes as such, more because actual research was done on the cultures each tribe came from and so a more nunanced setting could be built from that.<br /> <br /> I admit I started with revised, so I never really got into the 1st ed or 2nd ed mentality. To me garou were always heroes. However, they were never these pure heroes of goody good. Rather, their heroism was often shadowed by the world and their own culture.<br /> <br /> I generally take a more &quot;people are people&quot; approach to garou, so in my view of WtA setting, some Black Furies kill males for their rituals while others fight tooth and nail to keep a shelter for battered women funded. Some Glass Walkers are goofy technomancers who spend all day hacking, while others deal in drug trade and vivisection. Some Children of Gaia want to heal the world, while others want to convert all garou and fera to their One True Way. As with humans, garou are many kinds, even in the same tribe.<br /> <br /> Also, with seeing garou as unapologetic villains, I think a lot of good nuance that makes WtA for me, is lost. For example, the topic of this thread. Stuff like this is very much discussed outside gaming, and it is important that the bad stuff is mentioned as well. But more importantly, metis are such a great way to portray what it is like to have disabilities and how to deal with being seen as wrong. At least for me, playing metis has helped me deal with a lot of trauma I had from being bullied.<br /> <br /> Plus, WtA's canon deals with things like homelessness, native american rights and their situation, what IS feminism, nature and conservation and so on. Each one of these can be easily made into a very deep game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:59:59-07:00","id":979468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979456#post979456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To follow this tangent a little, first editions of any WoD thing in general were more simplistic. And I think out of all the games, I think WtA really benefitted from having revised and W20 editions.<br /> <br /> But not because it made the garou heroes as such, more because actual research was done on the cultures each tribe came from and so a more nunanced setting could be built from that.<br /> <br /> I admit I started with revised, so I never really got into the 1st ed or 2nd ed mentality. To me garou were always heroes. However, they were never these pure heroes of goody good. Rather, their heroism was often shadowed by the world and their own culture.<br /> <br /> I generally take a more &quot;people are people&quot; approach to garou, so in my view of WtA setting, some Black Furies kill males for their rituals while others fight tooth and nail to keep a shelter for battered women funded. Some Glass Walkers are goofy technomancers who spend all day hacking, while others deal in drug trade and vivisection. Some Children of Gaia want to heal the world, while others want to convert all garou and fera to their One True Way. As with humans, garou are many kinds, even in the same tribe.<br /> <br /> Also, with seeing garou as unapologetic villains, I think a lot of good nuance that makes WtA for me, is lost. For example, the topic of this thread. Stuff like this is very much discussed outside gaming, and it is important that the bad stuff is mentioned as well. But more importantly, metis are such a great way to portray what it is like to have disabilities and how to deal with being seen as wrong. At least for me, playing metis has helped me deal with a lot of trauma I had from being bullied.<br /> <br /> Plus, WtA's canon deals with things like homelessness, native american rights and their situation, what IS feminism, nature and conservation and so on. Each one of these can be easily made into a very deep game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't endorse the idea that Garou should be totally villainous. Though I like seeing such a different take on things. I rather prefer the idea that such ideas as &quot;heroes&quot; or &quot;villains&quot; is somewhat flawed and that who is truly good and evil can be somewhat ambiguous. Not just that different factions have the good and bad members, but that individual have their good and bad components. From one perspective, a werewolf can truly be a hero and from another truly an evil villain. I think that goes along with the history of mankind. All of these wars and conflicts, each group believing themselves to be the heroes and the enemies to be villains - both being right in a way. Because seeing yourself as completely good and your enemies as completely evil is an idea that so often sows the seeds of some of the worst evils. I think that of all the messages someone could take away from a morally ambiguous game, that might be the best one. A question I love to see in werewolf game is a character (or even player) coming to wonder if fighting monsters has transformed them into monsters.<br /> <br /> So as for Garou society, I think that it should have many elements that a modern person should have major moral issues with. I would go so far as to say that if the Tribes and Garou culture becomes something that is generally agreeable to the average WW player, then the game has lost part of what gave not only W:tA but all of the WoD games their character. That doesn't mean that they are villains exactly, but rather that they are alien cultures that are harsher than our own and in playing a member of that culture, we can try to expand our way of thinking somewhat. I would apply the same reasoning to playing a game in a historical setting that didn't have all of the values of the time and place whitewashed away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:15:22-07:00","id":979474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979449#post979449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so. Scottish and Germanic bloodlines can be known for the blood rage and tempers still flair to this day. For those of us prone to incredible levels of anger the garou rage may seem very close to it. Still isn't, but I get where they're coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. The Red Rage and the Black Rage are both part of the human experience. Before firearms, it was an evolutionary benefit because one person could save their extended family with their sacrifice. After firearms, well, there is a reason why my paternal ancestor who came to the Americas was the last surviving member of his branch of the Clan. You either learn to control it or it controls you and, nowadays, it controlling you ends up with you dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:30:34-07:00","id":979485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979430#post979430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am actually surprised that people consider anger and aggression to be an 'inhuman' emotion rather than a perfectly human emotion. In fact, in my own family, we have a centuries long history, dating back to the 6th century AD, where both the men and women of my family experienced levels of aggression and anger equal to that of the fictional Garou. I do not see the Rage of the Garou as an 'inhuman' curse, I see it as a family trait, just as I see their issues of controlling their Rage as identical to my own family's issues with controlling their anger.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there are no 'male' or 'female' social traits in humans. While there are reproductive roles for each sex, anything beyond that is 'gender', which is desinged by society as a way to assign job roles. In the developed world, they are anachronisms that rarely have a relevant role in society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see the documentation of this fourteen-century history of berserkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:52:10-07:00","id":979497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979449#post979449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so. Scottish and Germanic bloodlines can be known for the blood rage and tempers still flair to this day. For those of us prone to incredible levels of anger the garou rage may seem very close to it. Still isn't, but I get where they're coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pffft, buwahahaha!<br /> <br /> Oh my god you're serious. Yeah, I'd like to see some actual proof of this, edgelord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:54:53-07:00","id":979500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979449#post979449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so. Scottish and Germanic bloodlines can be known for the blood rage and tempers still flair to this day. For those of us prone to incredible levels of anger the garou rage may seem very close to it. Still isn't, but I get where they're coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Axiomatically impossible given the definition of Rage. If an actual human in real life can feel it, it's not intense enough!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So as for Garou society, I think that it should have many elements that a modern person should have major moral issues with. I would go so far as to say that if the Tribes and Garou culture becomes something that is generally agreeable to the average WW player, then the game has lost part of what gave not only W:tA but all of the WoD games their character. That doesn't mean that they are villains exactly, but rather that they are alien cultures that are harsher than our own and in playing a member of that culture, we can try to expand our way of thinking somewhat. I would apply the same reasoning to playing a game in a historical setting that didn't have all of the values of the time and place whitewashed away.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> While you could interpret that to mean that Garou are not friendly to minorities, I typically see it a different way...<br /> <br /> Trans Garou: I'm with this tribe, right?<br /> <br /> Cis Garou: The totem accepted you as you are. Everything should be fine.<br /> <br /> Other Cis Garou: Hey guys, check out this Pokemon Go app!<br /> <br /> Cis Garou: URRAH! DO NOT STAIN THIS DEN WITH YOUR WEAVER-FILTH WIFI! YOU WILL LABOR UNDER THE VOICE OF THE JACKAL FOR THE NEXT MOON FOR THIS TRANSGRESSION!</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-01-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:01:06-07:00","id":979501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979468#post979468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as for Garou society, I think that it should have many elements that a modern person should have major moral issues with. I would go so far as to say that if the Tribes and Garou culture becomes something that is generally agreeable to the average WW player, then the game has lost part of what gave not only W:tA but all of the WoD games their character. That doesn't mean that they are villains exactly, but rather that they are alien cultures that are harsher than our own and in playing a member of that culture, we can try to expand our way of thinking somewhat. I would apply the same reasoning to playing a game in a historical setting that didn't have all of the values of the time and place whitewashed away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a thing, though. Are they really all -that- alien? After all, everything the garou have done, people have done with even less justification than the garou have. And continue to do. And I think that is actually such an interesting part of WtA. Garou are extreme, but what they do does reflect to things that we do. Not always positively, of course.<br /> <br /> For example, to use your example of history being whitewashed, marriages in the middle ages were not typically made when the girl was in early teens despite popular belief of such. Instead, people married usually in their mid-20s. Even the nobility, who did marry much earlier, only did so due to land and family ties. The girl did not have to consummate the marriage until she was mature enough to safely bear a child, and I bet very early consummation was highly frowned upon like it would be today. This is just one example of portraying before from times before ours as backwards or alien. Yes, values WERE very different then, but these were still people like us. To not see it is to not see that people today are as capable of similar horrid acts as people were then. And even for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> Same with the garou. The treatment of metis can be horrid, but hardly all that fantastical in the end. Many disabled children even today face abuse and isolation by their parents or community. But many also get support from their community, despite their disability. Red Talons' mentality is both a reflection of dwindling spaces for predators causing them to attack humans AND of extremists who will die for their cause no matter how lost or illogical it seems. Children of Gaia are the white middle class person who forwards links and likes facebook posts, thinking it will help with problems that need far more than just support. And, any horrid thing a Black Spiral Dancer does is outshone by actual serial killers or wannabe satanists.<br /> <br /> I'd say the garou serve as good horror by being -very- human in the end.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:08:11-07:00","id":979503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979497#post979497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pffft, buwahahaha!<br /> <br /> Oh my god you're serious. Yeah, I'd like to see some actual proof of this, edgelord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Op look we have ourselves an internet warrior here throwing out terms like edge Lord. Dunno if you've got an explosive temper or have ever been in a fight, but believe or not there are some people who do have murderous anger. <br /> <br /> I know the internet tells you all of humanities teeth are blunted but there's still violent individuals around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:15:04-07:00","id":979504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979500#post979500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While you could interpret that to mean that Garou are not friendly to minorities, I typically see it a different way...<br /> <br /> Trans Garou: I'm with this tribe, right?<br /> <br /> Cis Garou: The totem accepted you as you are. Everything should be fine.<br /> <br /> Other Cis Garou: Hey guys, check out this Pokemon Go app!<br /> <br /> Cis Garou: URRAH! DO NOT STAIN THIS DEN WITH YOUR WEAVER-FILTH WIFI! YOU WILL LABOR UNDER THE VOICE OF THE JACKAL FOR THE NEXT MOON FOR THIS TRANSGRESSION![/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, it may be the case that if we realistically looked at Garou, the most jarring aspects of their culture wouldn't be where they come down on real world contentious issues, but when they completely disapprove of things that are completely accepted by humans or vice versa.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979501#post979501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's a thing, though. Are they really all -that- alien? After all, everything the garou have done, people have done with even less justification than the garou have. And continue to do. And I think that is actually such an interesting part of WtA. Garou are extreme, but what they do does reflect to things that we do. Not always positively, of course.<br /> <br /> For example, to use your example of history being whitewashed, marriages in the middle ages were not typically made when the girl was in early teens despite popular belief of such. Instead, people married usually in their mid-20s. Even the nobility, who did marry much earlier, only did so due to land and family ties. The girl did not have to consummate the marriage until she was mature enough to safely bear a child, and I bet very early consummation was highly frowned upon like it would be today. This is just one example of portraying before from times before ours as backwards or alien. Yes, values WERE very different then, but these were still people like us. To not see it is to not see that people today are as capable of similar horrid acts as people were then. And even for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> Same with the garou. The treatment of metis can be horrid, but hardly all that fantastical in the end. Many disabled children even today face abuse and isolation by their parents or community. But many also get support from their community, despite their disability. Red Talons' mentality is both a reflection of dwindling spaces for predators causing them to attack humans AND of extremists who will die for their cause no matter how lost or illogical it seems. Children of Gaia are the white middle class person who forwards links and likes facebook posts, thinking it will help with problems that need far more than just support. And, any horrid thing a Black Spiral Dancer does is outshone by actual serial killers or wannabe satanists.<br /> <br /> I'd say the garou serve as good horror by being -very- human in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>By alien I don't mean something inhuman so much as a different sort of culture. That is why I compared it the human cultures of the past. I think you're expressing the same idea that I was trying to. That things which are alien and perceived as evil are both very human. <br /> <br /> I guess the truly alien stuff is growing up as a literal wolf or going into the spirit world. Hatred, bigotry, fanaticism, conflict, and the struggle to morally justify it all are all very human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:18:27-07:00","id":979505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979503#post979503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Op look we have ourselves an internet warrior here throwing out terms like edge Lord. Dunno if you've got an explosive temper or have ever been in a fight, but believe or not there are some people who do have murderous anger.<br /> <br /> I know the internet tells you all of humanities teeth are blunted but there's still violent individuals around.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://pics.onsizzle.com/on-well-okay-2805130.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:21:57-07:00","id":979507,"title":"","content":"Yes, I have seen humans bite people hard enough to break bone. Human teeth are blunt, but humans can be frighteningly strong when they are enraged. Fists and fees are even more effective then teeth, and anything you can swing is even more effective than that.<br /> <br /> People with murderous tempers exist, but they are not quite what I am talking about. The Red Rage is an uncontrollable berserk rage where you are aware of your actions while the Black Rage is an uncontrollable berserk rage where you are unaware of anything. In every case though, the Black Rage is much more impressive than the Red Rage, as all of the governors of the brain are turned off, and everything amps up to '11'. It is also a beautiful thing, as you experience an unbelievable euphoria when you come back from the Black Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:24:51-07:00","id":979508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979503#post979503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Op look we have ourselves an internet warrior here throwing out terms like edge Lord. Dunno if you've got an explosive temper or have ever been in a fight, but believe or not there are some people who do have murderous anger.<br /> <br /> I know the internet tells you all of humanities teeth are blunted but there's still violent individuals around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that humans don't zwee around at super speed like in anime because they fly off the handle. Garou and Fera, on the other hand, do. So there you go - unless your anger makes you flicker in the air and gets you to shunpo, you don't have Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:27:46-07:00","id":979509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979508#post979508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that humans don't zwee around at super speed like in anime because they fly off the handle. Garou and Fera, on the other hand, do. So there you go - unless your anger makes you flicker in the air and gets you to shunpo, you don't have Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're ignoring the part where I said human rage was nothing like what you would see in a game like apocalypse. <br /> <br /> I might also argue that Bruce Lee was Goku made flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:28:59-07:00","id":979510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979507#post979507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I have seen humans bite people hard enough to break bone. Human teeth are blunt, but humans can be frighteningly strong when they are enraged. Fists and fees are even more effective then teeth, and anything you can swing is even more effective than that.<br /> <br /> People with murderous tempers exist, but they are not quite what I am talking about. The Red Rage is an uncontrollable berserk rage where you are aware of your actions while the Black Rage is an uncontrollable berserk rage where you are unaware of anything. In every case though, the Black Rage is much more impressive than the Red Rage, as all of the governors of the brain are turned off, and everything amps up to '11'. It is also a beautiful thing, as you experience an unbelievable euphoria when you come back from the Black Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why don't you provide us a single reputable source agreeing that the red rage and the black rage are actual psychological phenomena? And no - viking berserks don't count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:30:35-07:00","id":979511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979507#post979507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I have seen humans bite people hard enough to break bone. Human teeth are blunt, but humans can be frighteningly strong when they are enraged. Fists and fees are even more effective then teeth, and anything you can swing is even more effective than that.<br /> <br /> People with murderous tempers exist, but they are not quite what I am talking about. The Red Rage is an uncontrollable berserk rage where you are aware of your actions while the Black Rage is an uncontrollable berserk rage where you are unaware of anything. In every case though, the Black Rage is much more impressive than the Red Rage, as all of the governors of the brain are turned off, and everything amps up to '11'. It is also a beautiful thing, as you experience an unbelievable euphoria when you come back from the Black Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any human who manages to crack the bone of another with their teeth, assuming it's one of the larger, stronger ones, is going to have gums in pretty bad shape afterward, and possibly snapped muscle fibers, much like the ones who move cars or other heavy weights during episodes of extreme stress and danger. Blunt teeth aren't the issue; the human body is fragile and neotenous compared to other apes, so spitting on your hands and hoisting the black flag tends to be a medically bad idea. The ST system, of course, does not model this well at all.<br /> <br /> (You aren't going up to 11. It's going to be somewhere over 4 and under 10, and approaching 10 means that you end up like Motoko Kusanagi's body in the first GitS movie when she pries the hatch off the cybertank. Even in your state of stress, your pain response will stop and/or kill you before you &quot;redline&quot; things up like this.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:32:08-07:00","id":979513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979497#post979497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pffft, buwahahaha!<br /> <br /> Oh my god you're serious. Yeah, I'd like to see some actual proof of this, edgelord.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may not be a perfect example of level-headed discourse in this thread, but I did try to make sure I confronted every point my nemesis made with an argument and some degree of reason. If possible I would like to try and keep comments out of this thread that are purely antagonistic, like laughing at them without actually contributing anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-01-2016, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:37:44-07:00","id":979516,"title":"","content":"I think my &quot;Are werewolves villains?&quot; tangent is way better than the &quot;Do real humans have Rage and can they fight with their teeth?&quot; one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:30:13-07:00","id":979541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979404#post979404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Writers have a choice when writing things that bump up against transphobia and the serious real life issues surrounding it. They can either write groups that are divided by gender as accepting of trans membership or they can write them as not, but accept that doing so will alienate many people who otherwise might be interested in exploring their game because it's <i>transphobic as fuck</i> and that it's a step back from their stated policies of acceptance.<br /> <br /> You don't get to leave great heaping turds of transphobia in your book and then claim that you're respecting the source material and get a free pass any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The World of Darkness was always willing to look humanity dead in the eye and include things in it that many other games were afraid to portray. There are, absolutely, real life organizations based around gender that don't get or understand transgender individuals. I mean, just look up stories about trans women trying to get into battered women's shelters. These days they usually can, but many transgender women ran into literally life life-threatening problems with being accepted by and treated equally by biological women. Transgender women, being rejected by and kicked out of battered women's shelters by biological women is, to be clear, something that is &quot;transphobic as fuck&quot; but it's something that happens today nevertheless. <br /> <br /> It's certainly not hard to imagine that <i>some</i> members of the Furies might react in similar ways when they encounter transgender werewolves. In fact, it's kind of easy to imagine some kind of fairly militant transphobic group of Furies that might spring up in certain parts of the world (I mean there's little werewolf groups that pop up over everything, right?). That said, such individuals should ideally be the exception to the Furies rather than the norm. <br /> <br /> I think in the end, the gameline is better off if this is an issue for the Furies, one difficult issue that they're struggling to death with. Dealing with progressive issues, tackling prejudice and trying to change minds has always been a core theme of Werewolf. And, I mean, this is the World of Darkness so issues like prejudice and transphobia are worse there than they are here in our world. If there's a place in the gameline for dealing with the issues that transgender people face, I can't think of many places more suitable to it than the Furies. It's certainly better than som Pentex-led conversion therapy cult (those just come off as so hamfisted).<br /> <br /> Of course, if the authors introduce the idea that transgender women don't find immediate and overwhelming acceptance with the Furies (and sometimes face issues and problems) I suspect some people would find that transphobic and decide to not bother with the game. But in the end I feel that sidestepping the issue because it makes people uncomfortable just hurts the setting's authenticity and does a disservice for the audience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:52:47-07:00","id":979546,"title":"","content":"Again, I don't see why they wouldn't just go 'well, if Artemis is down, so are we'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:16:06-07:00","id":979600,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Because Garou are not sensible beings. For the most part, despite what they claim, they try to impose their will on the spirits rather than the other way around. We're talking about the race that got together, practically on a whim, to commit multiple attempted genocides of their own allies.... and then again of OTHER GAROU.<br /> <br /> The question of &quot;Why wouldn't they just (smart thing)?&quot; is something we ask ourselves in frustration toward our own race daily... be it peace between Israel and Palestine, American election reform, dealing with Syrian refugees, or global warming or world hunger or any of these issues that the majority of us can at least all agree on a few good first steps.... yet the situations continue to get worse, not better.<br /> <br /> Now add on top of the incredible ego of &quot;the chosen&quot; of the universe, and a rage so powerful that they literally have an issue with accidentally murdering their entire families because they stubbed their toe (and, by the way, have yet to make any widespread fetish or talen to prevent this... because I guess inconveniencing gafflings is a bigger deal than blacking out, murdering, and possibly eating your own kinfolk.)<br /> <br /> What actually disturbs me is how accurate Sergeant Brother's description of the Garou beliefs (as framed as villainous) are... because while Nazi's may have become a tired system of measure these days, that description also sure as hell has a lot in common with ISIL/Al-Qaeda/The Taliban. And I think a lot of the reason the Western world has struggled so much in dealing with the modern religious terrorists has a lot to do with the fact that we simply can't grok the mindset of a zealot suicide bomber blowing up a school bus for their beliefs, or the culture and society that puts such things on a pedestal. But the Garou might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:23:57-07:00","id":979605,"title":"","content":"I would imagine any servant of the Wyrm who saw a cross dressing Werewolf in action would die laughing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, on the topic of human strength, I'm going to have to call BS on the crunching bone bites. There are dogs with a bite strength roughly 20 times stronger than humans who can't crush bones like that. And you're missing the vital information that this strength is NOT SUSTAINABLE!<br /> <br /> Humans are weak because our bodies make us weak. If we went around at full power all day every day, we would tear ourselves to pieces from the force of our own strength. And, unlike Werewolves, we don't regenerate after a few seconds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> And any Black Fury who doesn't reproduce <i>asexually</i> needs to be smacked for killing their newborn son.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Also Edit:</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979500#post979500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Axiomatically impossible given the definition of Rage. If an actual human in real life can feel it, it's not intense enough!<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q8SWMAQYQf0\" data-code=\"q8SWMAQYQf0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/q8SWMAQYQf0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Human rage.... not intense enough! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-01-2016, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:13:52-07:00","id":979617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979600#post979600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Because Garou are not sensible beings. For the most part, despite what they claim, they try to impose their will on the spirits rather than the other way around. We're talking about the race that got together, practically on a whim, to commit multiple attempted genocides of their own allies.... and then again of OTHER GAROU.<br /> <br /> The question of &quot;Why wouldn't they just (smart thing)?&quot; is something we ask ourselves in frustration toward our own race daily... be it peace between Israel and Palestine, American election reform, dealing with Syrian refugees, or global warming or world hunger or any of these issues that the majority of us can at least all agree on a few good first steps.... yet the situations continue to get worse, not better.<br /> <br /> Now add on top of the incredible ego of &quot;the chosen&quot; of the universe, and a rage so powerful that they literally have an issue with accidentally murdering their entire families because they stubbed their toe (and, by the way, have yet to make any widespread fetish or talen to prevent this... because I guess inconveniencing gafflings is a bigger deal than blacking out, murdering, and possibly eating your own kinfolk.)<br /> <br /> What actually disturbs me is how accurate Sergeant Brother's description of the Garou beliefs (as framed as villainous) are... because while Nazi's may have become a tired system of measure these days, that description also sure as hell has a lot in common with ISIL/Al-Qaeda/The Taliban. And I think a lot of the reason the Western world has struggled so much in dealing with the modern religious terrorists has a lot to do with the fact that we simply can't grok the mindset of a zealot suicide bomber blowing up a school bus for their beliefs, or the culture and society that puts such things on a pedestal. But the Garou might.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your argument for why Black Furies wouldn't emulate one of their most revered entities is... Garou are stupid. I'm not exactly convinced that it follows that because Garou can be prideful idiots the Furies won't follow the example of Luna in her aspect of Artemis in this matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:16:01-07:00","id":979619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979600#post979600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Because Garou are not sensible beings. For the most part, despite what they claim, they try to impose their will on the spirits rather than the other way around. We're talking about the race that got together, practically on a whim, to commit multiple attempted genocides of their own allies.... and then again of OTHER GAROU.<br /> <br /> The question of &amp;quot;Why wouldn't they just (smart thing)?&amp;quot; is something we ask ourselves in frustration toward our own race daily... be it peace between Israel and Palestine, American election reform, dealing with Syrian refugees, or global warming or world hunger or any of these issues that the majority of us can at least all agree on a few good first steps.... yet the situations continue to get worse, not better.<br /> <br /> Now add on top of the incredible ego of &amp;quot;the chosen&amp;quot; of the universe, and a rage so powerful that they literally have an issue with accidentally murdering their entire families because they stubbed their toe (and, by the way, have yet to make any widespread fetish or talen to prevent this... because I guess inconveniencing gafflings is a bigger deal than blacking out, murdering, and possibly eating your own kinfolk.)<br /> <br /> What actually disturbs me is how accurate Sergeant Brother's description of the Garou beliefs (as framed as villainous) are... because while Nazi's may have become a tired system of measure these days, that description also sure as hell has a lot in common with ISIL/Al-Qaeda/The Taliban. And I think a lot of the reason the Western world has struggled so much in dealing with the modern religious terrorists has a lot to do with the fact that we simply can't grok the mindset of a zealot suicide bomber blowing up a school bus for their beliefs, or the culture and society that puts such things on a pedestal. But the Garou might.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Nazis may not be the best example, they are overused, don't entirely fit, and Godwin's Law. I used them because I think the essay I read did and because they are nearly universally viewed as villains. I think that ISIS may be a better comparison, though since they didn't exist when I had read that essay, I didn't want to use them as an example. <br /> <br /> Though the belief that one's enemies are completely evil as a justification for one's own evil is hardly unique to ISIS or Nazis. In fact, people can indeed commit terrible acts in opposing ISIS or Nazis. I guess the message in my mind is not to see things in too black and white a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:44:16-07:00","id":979626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979617#post979617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So your argument for why Black Furies wouldn't emulate one of their most revered entities is... Garou are stupid. I'm not exactly convinced that it follows that because Garou can be prideful idiots the Furies won't follow the example of Luna in her aspect of Artemis in this matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, if they literally kill their entire family for <i>stubbing their toe</i>, I don't think they can boast about their higher learning capacity. They sound like the kind of people who flex and scowl if they hear even one sentence that goes against their beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:59:19-07:00","id":979629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979626#post979626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, if they literally kill their entire family for <i>stubbing their toe</i>, I don't think they can boast about their higher learning capacity. They sound like the kind of people who flex and scowl if they hear even one sentence that goes against their beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's the thing. It doesn't actually go against their beliefs. It goes against what is being <i>imputed</i> into their beliefs based on little more than 'they're the feminist tribe, some feminists don't like transpeople, therefore they don't like transpeople' and 'they value fertility'. We don't have any statement as to their actual, factual view of transwomen. What we <i>do</i> have is the knowledge that their totem is Pegasus, a geldling who demands mercy for male metis (thus indicating, along with their revered roles for old women, that fertility is not the be all and end all of their matriarchy), and that they worship Luna-as-Artemis, who turned a man into a woman, while coming from a region in which transgender, third gender, and agendered priesthoods all existed in antiquity, some associated with Artemis herself. It is in fact going <i>less</i> against their known beliefs to hold that they view transformation of gender as possible.<br /> <br /> So again. Why wouldn't the tribe of Artemis follow the way of Artemis in this matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:36:24-07:00","id":979648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979629#post979629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's the thing. It doesn't actually go against their beliefs. It goes against what is being <i>imputed</i> into their beliefs based on little more than 'they're the feminist tribe, some feminists don't like transpeople, therefore they don't like transpeople' and 'they value fertility'. We don't have any statement as to their actual, factual view of transwomen. What we <i>do</i> have is the knowledge that their totem is Pegasus, a geldling who demands mercy for male metis (thus indicating, along with their revered roles for old women, that fertility is not the be all and end all of their matriarchy), and that they worship Luna-as-Artemis, who turned a man into a woman, while coming from a region in which transgender, third gender, and agendered priesthoods all existed in antiquity, some associated with Artemis herself. It is in fact going <i>less</i> against their known beliefs to hold that they view transformation of gender as possible.<br /> <br /> So again. Why wouldn't the tribe of Artemis follow the way of Artemis in this matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably the fact that Artemis was a goddess and transformed the man into a biological woman via divine intervention, where as transgenders either perceive themselves as the opposite gender, or use surgical procedures to become one. Both versions could be interpreted as Wyrm taint from a Werewolf's point of view. Remember, Werewolves are fanatics, driven by supernatural Rage and a perpetual hatred for modern society. What humanity calls progressive, they call unnatural, and anything unnatural must be destroyed.<br /> <br /> And Pegasus demanding mercy for male offspring is not the same thing as giving them a thumbs up to join their ranks. At most, he's allowing them to be handed off to a different tribe so their talents may be fostered elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-01-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:50:01-07:00","id":979653,"title":"","content":"Why should they view it as different? If the Garou are born according to Luna's artifice - itself a constantly changing, evolving thing - and Artemis has seen fit to consider gender non-fixed, why should they view it as unnatural? For that matter, why should they view surgery or hormone treatment (neither of which is needed to transition between genders) as wyrm-tainted? Do they view all surgery as wyrm-tainted? All medicine?<br /> <br /> Pegasus demanded not only mercy for male offspring, but a thumbs up to join the ranks in the form of the male metis. Between Pegasus and Artemis, we see a tribe who follow - even if they don't like it sometimes - the dictates of their totem quite carefully, who hold dearest an aspect of Luna who saw fit to visit her divine changing nature upon a mere mortal, and who already make allowances for persons who don't fit the strict reading of 'ladies only'.<br /> <br /> So again. Why should the tribe of Artemis not follow the way of Artemis in this matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:50:03-07:00","id":979654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979648#post979648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Probably the fact that Artemis was a goddess and transformed the man into a biological woman via divine intervention, where as transgenders either perceive themselves as the opposite gender, or use surgical procedures to become one. Both versions could be interpreted as Wyrm taint from a Werewolf's point of view. Remember, Werewolves are fanatics, driven by supernatural Rage and a perpetual hatred for modern society. What humanity calls progressive, they call unnatural, and anything unnatural must be destroyed.<br /> <br /> And Pegasus demanding mercy for male offspring is not the same thing as giving them a thumbs up to join their ranks. At most, he's allowing them to be handed off to a different tribe so their talents may be fostered elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transgender people aren't new to the world. Garou would have lived with them for millennia before humans developed written historical records, and while they wouldn't have what would be considered a &quot;progressive&quot; modern acceptance of them, they would probably have acceptance for them based in an ancient context and spiritual correspondences. Trans Garou being uneasy about spirits reading into their identity and offering chiminage based upon it should be the contention (being treated like your condition is magical is probably not something that most people would take well), not the bizarre want to make Garou into ideological followers of Rush Limbaugh and macho primitivists with a very modern idea of what &quot;the good old days&quot; were like based on their fad &quot;paleo&quot; diets. Which, given how flora and fauna have changed over the past few tens of thousands of years, are not properly paleo (and throw in a conflicting side order of TERF). You want Throwback fomori for those types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-01-2016, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:05:33-07:00","id":979661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979654#post979654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Transgender people aren't new to the world. Garou would have lived with them for millennia before humans developed written historical records, and while they wouldn't have what would be considered a &quot;progressive&quot; modern acceptance of them, they would probably have acceptance for them based in an ancient context and spiritual correspondences. Trans Garou being uneasy about spirits reading into their identity and offering chiminage based upon it should be the contention (being treated like your condition is magical is probably not something that most people would take well), not the bizarre want to make Garou into ideological followers of Rush Limbaugh and macho primitivists with a very modern idea of what &quot;the good old days&quot; were like based on their fad &quot;paleo&quot; diets. Which, given how flora and fauna have changed over the past few tens of thousands of years, are not properly paleo (and throw in a conflicting side order of TERF). You want Throwback fomori for those types.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And the lore of Apocalypse makes it a point that humanity is a creation of the Wyrm, and thus tainted by default. Remember, Wolf Good, Wyrm Bad.<br /> <br /> If Artemis was willing to change a man into a woman before, then it's a simple process of asking her to do so again. Just use some rite to channel her (or a similarly powerful totem) and request to become the gender you wish. Then, the man-turned-woman can join the Black Furies without issue. Instead, they attempt to use the tools of civilization (read Wyrm) to defile their natural bodies so that they can emulate female anatomy.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly rational for the Black Furies to perceive such actions as abominable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:08:54-07:00","id":979663,"title":"","content":"And why then should the Furies not accept those who would supplicate Artemis for that assistance?<br /> <br /> Also, again. Is every form of medicine tainted by the wyrm? Is all surgery?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Also? Gaia created mankind, not the Wyrm. Try again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:16:38-07:00","id":979670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979661#post979661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> And the lore of Apocalypse makes it a point that humanity is a creation of the Wyrm, and thus tainted by default. Remember, Wolf Good, Wyrm Bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the lore says that they're easily led astray because they don't know shit. It also says that the Garou shot themselves in the foot by assuming something closer to what you just mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Artemis was willing to change a man into a woman before, then it's a simple process of asking her to do so again. Just use some rite to channel her (or a similarly powerful totem) and request to become the gender you wish. Then, the man-turned-woman can join the Black Furies without issue. Instead, they attempt to use the tools of civilization (read Wyrm) to defile their natural bodies so that they can emulate female anatomy.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly rational for the Black Furies to perceive such actions as abominable. </div> </div> </div>That's concentrating on a very modernist view of history. Again, all Garou would have lived with the spectrum of human sexuality and gender identities for as long as humans have existed. Their judgments are not going to be the same as modern transphobic folk, or even the people of the ancient world, so there's no particular reason for them to hew to what modern humans regard as &quot;non-progressive&quot; or &quot;conservative&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:27:36-07:00","id":979676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979663#post979663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why then should the Furies not accept those who would supplicate Artemis for that assistance?<br /> <br /> Also, again. Is every form of medicine tainted by the wyrm? Is all surgery?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Also? Gaia created mankind, not the Wyrm. Try again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 - You seem to have misunderstood. I was suggesting that the Furies be the one to conduct such a ritual for the applicant. If Artemis is willing to accept them, then great. If she doesn't, the Furies tell them to piss off.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - From the wolf's point of view, I would have to say yes on the process of surgery. On the topic of medicine, however, that's a bit half and half. Even wild animals have figured out how to feed on certain herbs in order to ease medical problems. But surgery could be taken as an affront to the process of natural selection. A broken bone, a failing organ, a mangled limb, all plausible signs of weakness that must be cut from the herd in order for it to remain strong.<br /> <br /> And besides, Werewolves have highly efficient regenerative powers, which means the only time they would need surgery is for the process of removing silver from the body, or treating supernatural wounds. And even then, there's the possibility that spiritual mysticism could cleanse such wounds<br /> <br /> <br /> 3 - I thought I read somewhere that they were a creation of the Wyrm? Or maybe it just corrupted them over time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:35:58-07:00","id":979680,"title":"","content":"1. Then the Furies would, by definition, be accepting some transwomen - which is exactly what you've been arguing against.<br /> 2. Why is it wyrm-tainted? Is any interference whatsoever with natural processes 'of the wyrm'?<br /> 3. They are creations of Gaia, who all three forces of the Triat have an interest in and who embody all three in various forms and capacities. The Wyrm and the Weaver have grown stronger in their influence on humanity, though this is in large part due to the Garou's own arrogance throwing the triat out of whack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:44:38-07:00","id":979684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979680#post979680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Then the Furies would, by definition, be accepting some transwomen - which is exactly what you've been arguing against.<br /> 2. Why is it wyrm-tainted? Is any interference whatsoever with natural processes 'of the wyrm'?<br /> 3. They are creations of Gaia, who all three forces of the Triat have an interest in and who embody all three in various forms and capacities. The Wyrm and the Weaver have grown stronger in their influence on humanity, though this is in large part due to the Garou's own arrogance throwing the triat out of whack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 - No, I'm not arguing that they wouldn't accept transwomen, I'm saying they wouldn't accept <i>non-biological</i> women. If Artemis or some other spirit changed a man biologically into a woman, then sure, the Furies may be willing to accept them. On the other hand, if they're only trying to emulate women by 'mutilating' their bodies, that's where they would be offended. They're not actual women, they're just mocking their form. Or at least's that's how the Furies would perceive it.<br /> <br /> 2 - I was lead to believe that is the case, yes. Werewolves, Gaia, and the Fera work to defend nature. The Wyrm works to despoil nature. Anything that defies nature, would thus be part of the Wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3 - Ah, so I misinterpreted the lore on that. Thank you for the clarification.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:47:34-07:00","id":979686,"title":"","content":"1. And why would they perceive it this way? Further than that, is there more utility created for the setting, the game, the playerbase, and the stories those three things create for the Furies to be extremely transphobic than there is to apply the course of logic that states that there is no actual canonical basis for that stance?<br /> <br /> 2. Is it then wyrm-tainted to preserve a tree from dying in a drought, to prevent a naturally-sparked wildfire from incinerating a sacred grove, or to prevent a mother from dying in childbirth? To plant a tree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:00:10-07:00","id":979694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979676#post979676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - From the wolf's point of view, I would have to say yes on the process of surgery. On the topic of medicine, however, that's a bit half and half. Even wild animals have figured out how to feed on certain herbs in order to ease medical problems.<b> But surgery could be taken as an affront to the process of natural selection.</b> A broken bone, a failing organ, a mangled limb, all plausible signs of weakness that must be cut from the herd in order for it to remain strong.<br /> <br /> And besides, Werewolves have highly efficient regenerative powers, which means the only time they would need surgery is for the process of removing silver from the body, or treating supernatural wounds. And even then, there's the possibility that spiritual mysticism could cleanse such wounds</div> </div> </div> </div>A process not detailed until the 19th century. That's some kickin' Backwards Mnesis that their Mokole friend must have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:01:19-07:00","id":979695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979546#post979546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I don't see why they wouldn't just go 'well, if Artemis is down, so are we'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Black Furies, like every other werewolf are human, and if humans have proven one thing it's that even if they believe a deific being says or does one thing in a very clear way, they still often manage to find ways to do the opposite. They will jump though all sorts of legalistic hoops in order to interpret those words or actions in the ways that go along with what they already wanted to do. I mean, just at some of the things Jesus said about money, and misers and then stop to consider how there are so many priests out there with fancy cars and huge houses.<br /> <br /> People are great at interpreting laws or rules or ideals in ways that let them do whatever they wanted to do in the first place.<br /> <br /> You're inevitably going to have Fury factions who have different interpretations and ideas on what Artemis' words actually mean, and they will do their best to interpret those words in a way to justify their own personal prejudices. Humans do that <i>all the time</i> - hell, Werewolves in the setting have chosen to interpret spiritual rules in the most self-serving way possible. It just seems a bit odd to think that Furies would somehow be an exception to that.<br /> <br /> And to be clear, that doesn't make the Furies <i>stupid</i> if some of them continue to act in prejudicial ways against transgender members in spite of the example of Artemis, that just makes them <i>human</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:04:13-07:00","id":979697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979686#post979686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. And why would they perceive it this way? Further than that, is there more utility created for the setting, the game, the playerbase, and the stories those three things create for the Furies to be extremely transphobic than there is to apply the course of logic that states that there is no actual canonical basis for that stance?<br /> <br /> 2. Is it then wyrm-tainted to preserve a tree from dying in a drought, to prevent a naturally-sparked wildfire from incinerating a sacred grove, or to prevent a mother from dying in childbirth? To plant a tree?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 - Because they are <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>fanatics!</b> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">I thought we established this a few pages ago? They hate men, they want to kill men, a man walking up to them dressed like Chris Crocker and chanting about &quot;girl power&quot; is likely to piss them off, more than anything else.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - If that stuff was caused by unnatural phenomenon, then no. If, however, it was caused by the natural environment then it is simply nature taking its course. The forest burns down, but forests have burned down before and recovered naturally over time. A woman (or any female) dying in childbirth is a sign they weren't strong enough for proper breeding. A simple lack of endurance is not a sign of Wyrm taint. And as for planting a tree, I encourage you to look up how plants spread their seeds around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>By the way, I want to make it very clear, I'm trying to portray my argument from the point of view of Werewolves as I understand them in Apocalypse.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:06:17-07:00","id":979698,"title":"","content":"Yes. And that's where we once again get into the question of overall utility to the game. Is there more utility in having the Furies be transphobic than not, especially when there is no canonical reason to believe they are? (And if there were, would there be more utility in holding to that reason over changing it?) When there is a plausible narrative already in play that presents a reasonable and non-phobic option for an issue that is deeply personal, deeply important to quite a lot of gamers, why should we not adopt that narrative over the contrary one, which is imputed purely based on analogy to our real world?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979697#post979697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - Because they are <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>fanatics!</b> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">I thought we established this a few pages ago? They hate men, they want to kill men, a man walking up to them dressed like Chris Crocker and chanting about &quot;girl power&quot; is likely to piss them off, more than anything else.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - If that stuff was caused by unnatural phenomenon, then no. If, however, it was caused by the natural environment then it is simply nature taking its course. The forest burns down, but forests have burned down before and recovered naturally over time. A woman (or any female) dying in childbirth is a sign they weren't strong enough for proper breeding. A simple lack of endurance is not a sign of Wyrm taint. And as for planting a tree, I encourage you to look up how plants spread their seeds around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>By the way, I want to make it very clear, I'm trying to portray my argument from the point of view of Werewolves as I understand them in Apocalypse.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1. Except that a transwoman is not a man dressed like a woman. A transwoman is a woman. Nor do the Black Furies as a whole desire to kill all men.<br /> <br /> 2. Then much of what the Furies do carries with it Wyrm-taint. They do all the things I asked about, even when it would be nature's course. Why then should they oppose medicine and surgery in this particular matter?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 10-01-2016, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:20:05-07:00","id":979710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979698#post979698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. And that's where we once again get into the question of overall utility to the game. Is there more utility in having the Furies be transphobic than not, especially when there is no canonical reason to believe they are? (And if there were, would there be more utility in holding to that reason over changing it?) When there is a plausible narrative already in play that presents a reasonable and non-phobic option for an issue that is deeply personal, deeply important to quite a lot of gamers, why should we not adopt that narrative over the contrary one, which is imputed purely based on analogy to our real world?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Except that a transwoman is not a man dressed like a woman. A transwoman is a woman. Nor do the Black Furies as a whole desire to kill all men.<br /> <br /> 2. Then much of what the Furies do carries with it Wyrm-taint. They do all the things I asked about, even when it would be nature's course. Why then should they oppose medicine and surgery in this particular matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 - Wait, I'm confused. Is a transwoman a woman who became a man, or a man who became a woman? <br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - Except we've established that Werewolves do some pretty evil shit (from a human perspective) for the purpose of fighting the Wyrm. That's how they justify their actions, by saying it's for the greater good. But when it comes to letting outsiders into their ranks, I think that crosses a line. Even among human cultures, we've seen signs of xenophobia, jealously guarding their secrets because &quot;outsiders wouldn't understand.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I might be willing to accept that in some packs, the Furies would tolerate their presence, but they would never accept them as a true woman. Oh, sure, they might put on airs for them in public, but all it takes is one bad mood for them to snap and take their pent up aggression out on the scapegoat. I imagine<b> &quot;What would you know!? You're not even a real woman!&quot;</b> to be a very common quote among such packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:24:38-07:00","id":979713,"title":"","content":"1. A transwoman is a person who was designated as male at birth, and who then transitions to living as a woman. It is the conventional term for such women when specificity is needed and just 'women' won't suffice.<br /> <br /> 2. You haven't answered the actual question. What makes this source of wyrm-taint (a position I do not, incidentally, accept) different from that created by preserving the life of someone who should have died in childbirth, planting a fruit tree where it would not naturally arise, or preventing a natural fire from burning down a sacred space? If, as your argument requires, all these things create taint, why is the taint associated with surgery and medicine worse than other categories?<br /> <br /> 3. What canonical basis do you offer for this suggested stance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:26:32-07:00","id":979716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979697#post979697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Because they are <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>fanatics!</b> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">I thought we established this a few pages ago? They hate men, they want to kill men, <b>a man walking up to them dressed like Chris Crocker and chanting about &quot;girl power&quot;</b> is likely to piss them off, more than anything else.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <br /> So that bolded bit sort of belies your claims that you're trying to portray your argument from the point of view of werewolves as you or anyone else understands them. This isn't the first time in this thread that you've tried to describe trans women as absurd (this line, for example: &quot;I would imagine any servant of the Wyrm who saw a cross dressing Werewolf in action would die laughing.&quot;)<br /> <br /> It might help your argument a lot if you were to stop making snide comments about trans women. I mean, it won't make anyone agree with you if they don't already, but at least you wouldn't be tainting your argument by association with such nonsense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979697#post979697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - If that stuff was caused by unnatural phenomenon, then no. If, however, it was caused by the natural environment then it is simply nature taking its course. The forest burns down, but forests have burned down before and recovered naturally over time. A woman (or any female) dying in childbirth is a sign they weren't strong enough for proper breeding. A simple lack of endurance is not a sign of Wyrm taint. And as for planting a tree, I encourage you to look up how plants spread their seeds around.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has no relationship to how werewolves view anything. There's nothing anywhere in the game to indicate that they hold these kinds of views about, say, death in childbirth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>EDIT: </b>By the way, I want to make it very clear, I'm trying to portray my argument from the point of view of Werewolves as I understand them in Apocalypse. </div> </div> </div></span></span>As noted above it looks like you are portraying a perspective you hold with your comments about Chris Crocker and crossdressers, and maybe you should back off from that and find a different - more respectful - way to express your views.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding another post: Transgender isn't a noun, so you wouldn't talk about &quot;Transgenders.&quot; You might talk about trans women, trans people, trans men, etc. Or transgender women, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:31:52-07:00","id":979721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979713#post979713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. A transwoman is a person who was designated as male at birth, and who then transitions to living as a woman. It is the conventional term for such women when specificity is needed and just 'women' won't suffice.<br /> <br /> 2. You haven't answered the actual question. What makes this source of wyrm-taint (a position I do not, incidentally, accept) different from that created by preserving the life of someone who should have died in childbirth, planting a fruit tree where it would not naturally arise, or preventing a natural fire from burning down a sacred space? If, as your argument requires, all these things create taint, why is the taint associated with surgery and medicine worse than other categories?<br /> <br /> 3. What canonical basis do you offer for this suggested stance?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 - thanks for the clarification<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - I have tried to explain this as delicately as I could without coming across blatantly offensive. If you haven't seen my point by now, then I don't know how to explain it to you without a shit ton of backlash directed at me.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3 - Same explanation as 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:37:05-07:00","id":979724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979710#post979710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Wait, I'm confused. Is a transwoman a woman who became a man, or a man who became a woman?</div> </div> </div> </div>The language you're using here is not generally accepted within trans communities. A trans woman is a woman. To say that she &quot;was a man&quot; who &quot;became a woman&quot; implies that she was not a woman until she transitioned, which is not how gender works. Instead, we say that a trans woman is a woman who was assigned male at birth - her parents said &quot;this baby has a penis, so we will use he/him/his pronouns to refer to him and give him a masculine name.&quot; If that baby grows up and finds that those designations are at odds with their identity, they are trans. Alternatively, if that baby grew up feeling those designations suited their identity just fine, they are cis (which is Latin and literally means &quot;not trans&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:37:14-07:00","id":979725,"title":"","content":"On a side note, one of the greatest weapons of the Wyrm is emotional pain - especially despair, self-loathing, and hatred. Condemning those who seek to lessen their own suffering at the hands of gender dysphoria is, in fact, playing into the Wyrm's hands, so from the 'point of view of Werewolves' it in fact should be avoided. No one is harmed by working to assist transwomen, and in fact, the ability of the wyrm to utilize the emotional pain created by gender dysphoria is reduced or eradicated by that assistance.<br /> <br /> It is also interesting to me that in discussions of spirits, it is assumed the perception by spirits of a transwoman is that of a man 'pretending'. Why should it not be the opposite - that a transwoman's spiritual identity is what we would consider a female one (insofar as one can consider any spiritual entity to meaningfully possess gender, at least) while their physical form is male-bodied? Certainly, we have examples of spiritual entities within the setting taking bodies of both gender, including from all three sides of the Triat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979721#post979721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - thanks for the clarification<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - I have tried to explain this as delicately as I could without coming across blatantly offensive. If you haven't seen my point by now, then I don't know how to explain it to you without a shit ton of backlash directed at me.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3 - Same explanation as 2.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you cannot adequately answer why there should be a perceived difference between the two by either logic or by express canon, you should abandon your argument. It has no basis other than kneejerk 'but they're not real women' sentiment, which is both blatantly offensive and essentially baseless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 10-01-2016, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:49:04-07:00","id":979733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979725#post979725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side note, one of the greatest weapons of the Wyrm is emotional pain - especially despair, self-loathing, and hatred. Condemning those who seek to lessen their own suffering at the hands of gender dysphoria is, in fact, playing into the Wyrm's hands, so from the 'point of view of Werewolves' it in fact should be avoided. No one is harmed by working to assist transwomen, and in fact, the ability of the wyrm to utilize the emotional pain created by gender dysphoria is reduced or eradicated by that assistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently - according to some - cis Garou love the idea of pushing trans Garou into harano.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979725#post979725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is also interesting to me that in discussions of spirits, it is assumed the perception by spirits of a transwoman is that of a man 'pretending'. Why should it not be the opposite - that a transwoman's spiritual identity is what we would consider a female one (insofar as one can consider any spiritual entity to meaningfully possess gender, at least) while their physical form is male-bodied? Certainly, we have examples of spiritual entities within the setting taking bodies of both gender, including from all three sides of the Triat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hesitate to describe trans women as &quot;male-bodied,&quot; simply because that plays into certain kinds of narratives about trans bodies (like the idea that a trans woman is a &quot;man who becomes a woman.&quot; Not saying you're doing that) That said I would tend to think that spirits would recognize someone's actual gender rather than view them as being deceitful for not being the sex they were assigned at birth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you cannot adequately answer why there should be a perceived difference between the two by either logic or by express canon, you should abandon your argument. It has no basis other than kneejerk 'but they're not real women' sentiment, which is both blatantly offensive and essentially baseless. </div> </div> </div>I'm not the expert or anything, and I've only probably read about 80% of the Werewolf supplements over the years but I don't remember ever seeing anything that would indicate Garou follow such an extreme &quot;survival of the fittest&quot; ideology that they'd let women die in childbirth if it could be prevented (and assuming the Garou weren't Red Talons or something).<br /> <br /> That's such a stark perspective, and totally untenable as well. I won't say Garou never do badly by their kinfolk, but just letting people die of preventable causes seems beyond the pale. Esp bringing this up in a discussion about Black Furies, who would be very pro-surviving childbirth if at all possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:50:56-07:00","id":979736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979733#post979733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd hesitate to describe trans women as &quot;male-bodied,&quot; simply because that plays into certain kinds of narratives about trans bodies (like the idea that a trans woman is a &quot;man who becomes a woman.&quot; Not saying you're doing that) That said I would tend to think that spirits would recognize someone's actual gender rather than view them as being deceitful for not being the sex they were assigned at birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, and mea culpa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:40:10-07:00","id":979749,"title":"","content":"Well, like life, it is more complicated than that. Some transwomen are born with a male physiology and male genetics, some transwomen are born with an intersex physiology and either male genetics or female genetics, and some transwomen are born with a female physiology and male genetics (such as people born with CAIS or PAIS). In all case, hormones and surgery are used to 'normalize' individuals with their view of themselves.<br /> <br /> And Black Furies do not hate men or the male sex, they hate male privilege. While they will not accept a fertile male into their tribe (because of Pegasus), they are not going to commit genocide against men. In fact, most Black Furies have healthy relationships (as much as can be expected with any Garou) with men who do not try to use their male privilege against the women in their lives. After all, they have to reproduce, they are practically obligated to reproduce, and they do not usually kill the men after sex.<br /> <br /> And Garou are not necessarily religious fanatics, they are trying to save the world from the stupidity of the humans and the corruption of the Weaver and the Wyrm. Yes, some of them are evil, but the majority of the tribes stomp down hard on anyone who commits evil behavior because it is a sign of the Weaver or the Wyrm. Of course, the Get of Fenris and the Glass Walkers tend to backslide on wife-beaters, but that is why the Black Furies tend to pick up the slack and 'eliminate' wife-beaters from the Garou nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:59:09-07:00","id":979758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979749#post979749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, like life, it is more complicated than that. Some transwomen are born with a male physiology and male genetics, some transwomen are born with an intersex physiology and either male genetics or female genetics, and some transwomen are born with a female physiology and male genetics (such as people born with CAIS or PAIS). In all case, hormones and surgery are used to 'normalize' individuals with their view of themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problematic terminology aside (&quot;male/female genetics/physiology&quot; implies that certain physiological and genetic traits are necessary qualities of certain genders,) it's more complicated even than that. In many cases, hormones and surgery are <i>not</i> used to &quot;normalize&quot; <i>anything</i>, because many trans people are perfectly comfortable with the physiologies and genetics they were born with, but still do not conform to the genders they were assigned at birth. Or are not comfortable but are unwilling or unable able to transition surgically or hormonally for any of a tremendous number of reasons.<br /> <br /> I am a woman. This is my body. Therefore, it is a woman's body, with or without any surgical or hormonal changes. To call my physiology or my genetics &quot;male&quot; is to invalidate my womanhood, whether intentionally or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-01-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:20:07-07:00","id":979760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979605#post979605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine any servant of the Wyrm who saw a cross dressing Werewolf in action would die laughing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You may be confusing transgender people for transvestites, or I may be reading too deep into it. Either way, I'm sure the Wyrm has plenty of embittered disenfranchised transpeople who have gone full Nightmare and would strap down people and force the wrong hormones on them if presented the opportunity. I don't really for see the Wyrm having anything but apathy toward it unless they're consciously trying to tease someone into snapping and joining the dark side.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979605#post979605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>EDIT:</b> And any Black Fury who doesn't reproduce <i>asexually</i> needs to be smacked for killing their newborn son.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is someone willing to explain this to me? I have no idea what they're talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979617#post979617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your argument for why Black Furies wouldn't emulate one of their most revered entities is... Garou are stupid. I'm not exactly convinced that it follows that because Garou can be prideful idiots the Furies won't follow the example of Luna in her aspect of Artemis in this matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rereading the Tribebook last night and this morning, I really don't see why Pegasus wouldn't be in full support of transwomen. She specifically charges the Furies with helping the helpless (but not the weak) which is apparently a distinction the Get have trouble making. A transgender person who risks ostracism from the family, work, friends, etc, as well violence for the sake of being who they feel they are is by definition 'not weak' in Pegasus's eyes if you take it in the context of what the tribebook says about weakness and helplessness. If anything Pegasus would have nothing but disdain for a transperson who refuses to be true about themselves, and who won't act on their feelings for fear of violence and public shaming. Which would be similar to the book's definition of weak, which is people who refuse to fight back or act even before the shackles of oppression are placed.<br /> <br /> And I tend to think that you reject the views and values of your tribal totem at your own peril. Arguing with Pegasus about how she should or shouldn't feel also seems like a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979626#post979626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, if they literally kill their entire family for <i>stubbing their toe</i>, I don't think they can boast about their higher learning capacity. They sound like the kind of people who flex and scowl if they hear even one sentence that goes against their beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've never seen a werewolf 'literally' do anything close to the sort. It would at least require getting stabbed, or taking a gunshot. Stubbing your toe is like... not even damage, in game terms.<br /> <br /> Also as has been consistently pointed out in this thread, not following your elders is a very unwise decision in Garou society. So even if Garou are prideful and prone to genocide, and there's no indication they are any more so than humans are based on our own human history (we've wiped out just as many of our own as they have, if not more), I'm noticing that people are either going to go with &quot;werewolves will listen to the spirits and their elders when it lets them be abusive people&quot; or, &quot;werewolves will ignore their spirits and elders if it lets them be abusive people.&quot;<br /> <br /> That doesn't seem to be the thing you can have both ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979648#post979648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably the fact that Artemis was a goddess and transformed the man into a biological woman via divine intervention, where as transgenders either perceive themselves as the opposite gender, or use surgical procedures to become one. Both versions could be interpreted as Wyrm taint from a Werewolf's point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, it's grammatically incorrect to use 'transgenders', and also it's a bit of a slur at this point based on how it's been used in the past, not trying to give you shit about it, just letting you know that some people take issue with it.<br /> <br /> Second, those are both good arguments why a Black Fury mother would seek some form of ritual that draws on the Wyld rather than letting their daughter be enslaved by pharmaceuticals and surgery that will make sure they have to dilate and get doctor visits for the rest of their lives, whilst also not always providing full sexual and reproductive capabilities. But I don't think a typical Black Fury would view the condition as 'Wyrm Tainted' just the modern solutions available to humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979648#post979648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, Werewolves are fanatics, driven by supernatural Rage and a perpetual hatred for modern society. What humanity calls progressive, they call unnatural, and anything unnatural must be destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty big strawman you're building there, is it that soon to walpurgisnacht or something? Glasswalkers don't hate modern society, or progressivism, Bonegnawers also don't. Children of Gaia don't. Black Furies demonstrably do not hate progressivism since it's bundled in with feminism and not fucking up the environment, as well as regulation on corporations like Pentex. Shadow Lords don't hate modern society, they use those tools all the time. Silver Fangs seem at best indifferent and at worst more concerned with hiding out in the tundra, Silent Striders just want to go home and don't seem to think there is anything wrong with modern society except that it is crawling with vampires, which has always been the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979648#post979648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Pegasus demanding mercy for male offspring is not the same thing as giving them a thumbs up to join their ranks. At most, he's allowing them to be handed off to a different tribe so their talents may be fostered elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pegasus goes by female pronouns, which means she would be a bit of a hypocrite if she 'didn't' accept transgender garou who have taken steps to transition (by rite or fetish, presumably).<br /> <br /> Not that spirits can't be hypocrites, but she doesn't have a problem with the male metis for specifically that reason, and most refer to them as 'she' and 'sister' too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979653#post979653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, why should they view surgery or hormone treatment (neither of which is needed to transition between genders) as wyrm-tainted? Do they view all surgery as wyrm-tainted? All medicine?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned above, Black Furies would probably consider pharmaceuticals to be Wyrm Tainted because in the ye Olden World of Darkness, corporations are corrupt and tainted by the wyrm. To be fair, the pharmaceutical industry in the real world is already incredibly corrupt and absent regulations that are arguably needed. In the World of Darkness, this is even more exacerbated. Keep in mind, the Black Furies have a sidebar on how baby formulae is evil, and pharmaceutical companies (who own the baby formula companies) will do whatever it takes to brain wash women into using it instead of their own natural abilities.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979661#post979661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, they attempt to use the tools of civilization (read Wyrm) to defile their natural bodies so that they can emulate female anatomy.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly rational for the Black Furies to perceive such actions as abominable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tools of civilization are the Weaver, actually. It's just that most pharmaceutical companies are corrupted heart and soul by the Wyrm at this point. It's a fine distinction, but a necessary one. Of course, the Black Furies aren't going to appreciate the Weaver any more than they would the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Also whose to say they're not right? Spironolactone is like, the worst drug ever, and I can't wait to never need to take it again. : |<br /> <br /> It's perfectly rational for them to see those 'options' as abominable, but if it's the only option available to mundane humans who are not vampires, mages, or werewolves, and who are not kinfolk, then what are you going to do? Unfortunately they can't exactly go around performing rites for people without breaking the Litany.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979663#post979663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, again. Is every form of medicine tainted by the wyrm? Is all surgery?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Also? Gaia created mankind, not the Wyrm. Try again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enough medicine is tainted by the Wyrm that the Black Furies tend to abhor it. Black Furies will not go to a hospital for general treatment (they don't need to, they're werewolves) and they adamantly refuse to do so for labor and the birthing process. They will either use a kinfolk midwife, or they'll go to a birthing center run by kinfolk, or they'll run off to a place closest to the Wyld for it. It's not a stretch to believe they would foist herbal remedies on their kinfolk, and treat their injuries themselves. These are all pretty problematic except when you consider that they are werewolves, and spirits are actually real, so who's to say what &quot;natural remedies&quot; would and wouldn't work after awakening its spirit, especially on humans? A Black Fury Theurge would probably just as soon have their transgender kinfolk drink pregnant mare urine and eat flax seeds as they would any of those other things.<br /> <br /> Gaia created humans, but they were prey animals before the Wyrm in the form of a serpent convinced them to try hunting, and it was great! They loved it so much that they decided to start killing predators too, which is in defiance of Jungle Law, and the Red Talons have never forgiven them for committing the first murder.<br /> <br /> In that sense, if Gaia is our mother, the Wyrm is undoubtedly our father. Without the Wyrm we would all be prey animals hiding from the predators, and we would never have carved the niche for ourselves that we did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979697#post979697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Because they are [SIZE=14px]<b>fanatics!</b> [SIZE=12px]I thought we established this a few pages ago? They hate men, they want to kill men, a man walking up to them dressed like Chris Crocker and chanting about &quot;girl power&quot; is likely to piss them off, more than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another strawman. Black Furies do not hate men anymore than feminists do. They have male lovers, they have sons that mean the world to them. Men are a very important part of the tribe, they're just not 'part' of the tribe. It's actually two strawmen in one paragraph, a strawman for the black furies, and a strawman for the transgender people they are likely to meet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979697#post979697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - If that stuff was caused by unnatural phenomenon, then no. If, however, it was caused by the natural environment then it is simply nature taking its course. The forest burns down, but forests have burned down before and recovered naturally over time. A woman (or any female) dying in childbirth is a sign they weren't strong enough for proper breeding. A simple lack of endurance is not a sign of Wyrm taint. And as for planting a tree, I encourage you to look up how plants spread their seeds around.</div> </div> </div> </div>An animal (that's us) influencing their environment is not an unnatural phenomena. If we use our computers and our machines to do it for us, then it is of the Weaver, if it's seeping with corruption and pollution, it is of the Wyrm, but these are the methods, not the motivation or act. Wolves will prepare a site for a hunt in advance of their prey arriving, ants and other insects are obvious. Apes, whales, and countless others will also influence their environment to suit their needs, this is part of nature.<br /> <br /> Also, what? Women die in birthing 'accidents' all the time. There isn't some threshold set where if you're not STR0NG enough, you die. Most of the reasons for why maternal death rates have gone down is because modern medical process allows us to help prevent accidents. Which is also not unnatural. You have a very limited and ironically human notion of how nature works.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979710#post979710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Wait, I'm confused. Is a transwoman a woman who became a man, or a man who became a woman?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not encouraging when the person in the debate is uninformed to the point of not knowing the most foundational vocabulary to the subject at hand.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cisgender has its origin in the Latin-derived prefix cis-, meaning &quot;on this side of&quot;, which is an antonym for the Latin-derived prefix trans-, meaning &quot;across from&quot; or &quot;on the other side of&quot;. This usage can be seen in the cis\u2013trans distinction in chemistry, the cis\u2013trans or complementation test in genetics. . .&quot;<br /> <br /> That is to say that a ciswoman is one that was assigned female at birth and hasn't needed to transition either socially or physically. A Transwoman is a woman who was not assigned female at birth, and did have to transition, either socially or physically, or both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979710#post979710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - Except we've established that Werewolves do some pretty evil shit (from a human perspective) for the purpose of fighting the Wyrm. That's how they justify their actions, by saying it's for the greater good. But when it comes to letting outsiders into their ranks, I think that crosses a line. Even among human cultures, we've seen signs of xenophobia, jealously guarding their secrets because &quot;outsiders wouldn't understand.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sky high poverty, ostracism, suicide, and homicide rates feed wounds, banes, and ultimately serves the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979710#post979710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be willing to accept that in some packs, the Furies would tolerate their presence, but they would never accept them as a true woman. Oh, sure, they might put on airs for them in public, but all it takes is one bad mood for them to snap and take their pent up aggression out on the scapegoat. I imagine<b> &quot;What would you know!? You're not even a real woman!&quot;</b> to be a very common quote among such packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally feel that would be for the most part a minority, and if a Black Fury snapped and said that, her sisters would just stare at her in dumbstruck shock.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979733#post979733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently - according to some - cis Garou love the idea of pushing trans Garou into harano.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a more realistic result is said garou joining the Black Spiral dancers as the only means of acceptance and transition, before eventually deciding the entire garou nation needs to suffer the way they had to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-01-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:25:25-07:00","id":979762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979758#post979758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problematic terminology aside (&quot;male/female genetics/physiology&quot; implies that certain physiological and genetic traits are necessary qualities of certain genders,) it's more complicated even than that. In many cases, hormones and surgery are <i>not</i> used to &quot;normalize&quot; <i>anything</i>, because many trans people are perfectly comfortable with the physiologies and genetics they were born with, but still do not conform to the genders they were assigned at birth. Or are not comfortable but are unwilling or unable able to transition surgically or hormonally for any of a tremendous number of reasons.<br /> <br /> I am a woman. This is my body. Therefore, it is a woman's body, with or without any surgical or hormonal changes. To call my physiology or my genetics &quot;male&quot; is to invalidate my womanhood, whether intentionally or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>What then does that say about transwomen who do need to take hormones and physically transition, then? If body and genetics are not 'typically male' or 'typically female' how do we even have a discussion about those of us wired in such a way that 'not' physically transitioning causes constant mental, emotional, and physical discomfort? I am a woman, this is my body, therefor it's a woman's body has the implication that those of us where there is a very serious physical component to the condition are somehow problematic, in the same way TERFs who claim that the existence of transgender people implies there is some form of natural component to gender and that gender is not entirely socially constructed, which means that transgender individuals as a concept need to be ignored.<br /> <br /> I'm speaking as someone who consciously doesn't care what pronoun people use to refer to me, or what niche I occupy in society, and only started hormone replacement therapy because it was the only treatment that eased my depression and other stress-based symptoms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:27:41-07:00","id":979764,"title":"","content":"The easiest way to handle the terminology is &quot;assigned male/female at birth,&quot; which is the less-offensive way of saying &quot;used to he a man/woman.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:37:49-07:00","id":979765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979764#post979764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest way to handle the terminology is &quot;assigned male/female at birth,&quot; which is the less-offensive way of saying &quot;used to he a man/woman.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact I would say it is a great way to avoid saying &quot;used to be a man/woman&quot; because it doesn't imply a &quot;used to be&quot; anywhere. A trans woman who was assigned male at birth was never a man in the first place, although was possibly put in a position to pretend to be one for a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:38:43-07:00","id":979766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979760#post979760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a more realistic result isn't said garou joining the Black Spiral dancers as the only means of acceptance and transition, before eventually deciding the entire garou nation needs to suffer the way they had to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was being kind of snarky there, I admit it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:40:06-07:00","id":979769,"title":"","content":"Coming at the issue from a player's point of view, In my experience I'd say 9 1/2 times out of ten, when someone makes a character that isn't <i>mainstream</i> somehow (in this example it's trans, but sexuality, race and religion can be substituted), it's not because they want to get into an in-depth exploration this facet of society in a make believe world, it's because <i>they want to include things in their characters that they can relate to</i>.<br /> <br /> So every table has to decide if they're going to react to this sort of thing by toning down this one thing out of all the other things that go on in a game, or focusing on this one thing and making their table another example of transphobia/racism/homophobia/etc that someone needs to navigate. If YOUR reaction is an attempt to scramble to justify why this one thing needs to <i>suddenly</i> be focused on when it probably never game up as an issue before, you should take a good hard look at your motives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:41:26-07:00","id":979772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979762#post979762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What then does that say about transwomen who do need to take hormones and physically transition, then? If body and genetics are not 'typically male' or 'typically female' how do we even have a discussion about those of us wired in such a way that 'not' physically transitioning causes constant mental, emotional, and physical discomfort?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it poses a barrier to those discussions in any way. A trans person who experiences dysphoria and/or dysmorphia can and should be able to undergo any processes that help them alleviate those feelings. That doesn't make them any less their gender before undergoing those processes. I don't see a conflict between those points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979762#post979762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a woman, this is my body, therefor it's a woman's body has the implication that those of us where there is a very serious physical component to the condition are somehow problematic, in the same way TERFs who claim that the existence of transgender people implies there is some form of natural component to gender and that gender is not entirely socially constructed, which means that transgender individuals as a concept need to be ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Your body being a woman's body doesn't mean there is anything wrong with feeling uncomfortable with your body, nor that there is anything wrong with taking steps to make you feel more comfortable. Dysphoria and Dysmorphea not being a necessary component of transness doesn't mean it can't be a component of transness. It's quite a common component of it, in fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979762#post979762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm speaking as someone who consciously doesn't care what pronoun people use to refer to me, or what niche I occupy in society, and only started hormone replacement therapy because it was the only treatment that eased my depression and other stress-based symptoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing how this conflicts with the definition of trans I have been using. Not identifying with any gender is still covered under not identifying with the gender you were assigned at birth. If you weren't assigned a gender at birth, first of all props to your parents for letting you make that decision for yourself, and second of all, if you still consider yourself trans and/or still desire resources and support within trans communities, you are still welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-01-2016, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:42:08-07:00","id":979773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979762#post979762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What then does that say about transwomen who do need to take hormones and physically transition, then? If body and genetics are not 'typically male' or 'typically female' how do we even have a discussion about those of us wired in such a way that 'not' physically transitioning causes constant mental, emotional, and physical discomfort? I am a woman, this is my body, therefor it's a woman's body has the implication that those of us where there is a very serious physical component to the condition are somehow problematic, in the same way TERFs who claim that the existence of transgender people implies there is some form of natural component to gender and that gender is not entirely socially constructed, which means that transgender individuals as a concept need to be ignored.<br /> <br /> I'm speaking as someone who consciously doesn't care what pronoun people use to refer to me, or what niche I occupy in society, and only started hormone replacement therapy because it was the only treatment that eased my depression and other stress-based symptoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it implies there's anything problematic about transition. Accepting that a trans woman's body is in fact a woman's body and not a man's body actually reinforces the decision to transition or not, since it's your body thus your decision. No one else needs to be involved and it doesn't mean there is one correct way to be trans that everyone should follow.<br /> <br /> At least that's my reading of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:46:28-07:00","id":979776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979724#post979724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The language you're using here is not generally accepted within trans communities. A trans woman is a woman. To say that she &quot;was a man&quot; who &quot;became a woman&quot; implies that she was not a woman until she transitioned, which is not how gender works. Instead, we say that a trans woman is a woman who was assigned male at birth - her parents said &quot;this baby has a penis, so we will use he/him/his pronouns to refer to him and give him a masculine name.&quot; If that baby grows up and finds that those designations are at odds with their identity, they are trans. Alternatively, if that baby grew up feeling those designations suited their identity just fine, they are cis (which is Latin and literally means &quot;not trans&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand what you're saying, but it's not an ideology I was made accustomed to growing up. I was taught that gender was biological, rather than psychological. So please forgive me for not understanding properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:48:08-07:00","id":979777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979769#post979769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming at the issue from a player's point of view, In my experience I'd say 9 1/2 times out of ten, when someone makes a character that isn't <i>mainstream</i> somehow (in this example it's trans, but sexuality, race and religion can be substituted), it's not because they want to get into an in-depth exploration this facet of society in a make believe world, it's because <i>they want to include things in their characters that they can relate to</i>.<br /> <br /> So every table has to decide if they're going to react to this sort of thing by toning down this one thing out of all the other things that go on in a game, or focusing on this one thing and making their table another example of transphobia/racism/homophobia/etc that someone needs to navigate. If YOUR reaction is an attempt to scramble to justify why this one thing needs to <i>suddenly</i> be focused on when it probably never game up as an issue before, you should take a good hard look at your motives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I have trans characters because I can't safely be trans IRL, so I'd cock my head a little at a ST who decided that meant I had any interest in playing through a narrative where my allies all accuse me of being a Wyrm-tained horrific deceiver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:48:43-07:00","id":979778,"title":"","content":"Technically, sex is biological while gender is social.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:56:49-07:00","id":979783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979778#post979778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, sex is biological while gender is social.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically sex categories are a social construct as much as gender. There is no &quot;essential&quot; male or female biology, just anatomical features and organs we choose to label as male or female.<br /> <br /> Saying that it is a social construct does not mean it is not real. It means things like intersex infants being surgically altered to fit these constructed definitions of &quot;male&quot; or &quot;female.&quot; For one example. It means that trans people are acknowledged as members of the correct sex where surgery isn't necessarily a requirement any longer. So, good and bad. But to say &quot;sex is biological&quot; ignores a lot of discussion that's going on right now, never mind the lived realities of trans and intersex people.<br /> <br /> Here's a link: <a href=\"http://bennorton.com/gender-is-not-alone-the-social-construction-of-sex/\" target=\"_blank\">http://bennorton.com/gender-is-not-a...uction-of-sex/</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:58:52-07:00","id":979785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979776#post979776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand what you're saying, but it's not an ideology I was made accustomed to growing up. I was taught that gender was biological, rather than psychological. So please forgive me for not understanding properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. Not trying to chastise, just to inform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:22:41-07:00","id":979791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979772#post979772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how it poses a barrier to those discussions in any way. A trans person who experiences dysphoria and/or dysmorphia can and should be able to undergo any processes that help them alleviate those feelings. That doesn't make them any less their gender before undergoing those processes. I don't see a conflict between those points.<br /> <br /> <br /> How so? Your body being a woman's body doesn't mean there is anything wrong with feeling uncomfortable with your body, nor that there is anything wrong with taking steps to make you feel more comfortable. Dysphoria and Dysmorphea not being a necessary component of transness doesn't mean it can't be a component of transness. It's quite a common component of it, in fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not seeing how this conflicts with the definition of trans I have been using. Not identifying with any gender is still covered under not identifying with the gender you were assigned at birth. If you weren't assigned a gender at birth, first of all props to your parents for letting you make that decision for yourself, and second of all, if you still consider yourself trans and/or still desire resources and support within trans communities, you are still welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Problematic terminology aside (&quot;male/female genetics/physiology&quot; implies that certain physiological and genetic traits are necessary qualities of certain genders,) </div> </div> </div>To consider this in context, this was in response to someone saying 'female genetics/physiology', which you claim is problematic, because it suggests they are 'necessary', which I don't think is the case. I don't think female typical genetics or physiology as a definition precludes you being a woman in spite of those traits, and don' understand why defining them in that way is problematic or invalidating toward your gender identity. <br /> <br /> However, when you say it's problematic to use those definitions, then it becomes problematic for me to say &quot;I take estrogen because apparently my brain is wired in a typically female manner, testosterone, and the physical changes brought on by testosterone cause me discomfort.&quot; But using the above logic, it's inappropriate for me to put it that way because it might make someone who doesn't have those experiences feel invalidated in some way. For me it's really no different than an intersex condition, and I've gotten a lot of drama for voicing that sentiment, too. <br /> <br /> I'm at work as I right this, and running low on sleep, so if I'm missing your point or misrepresenting your argument I apologize, I'm doing my level best to understand here, but the argument that that it's wrong to refer to genetics or physiology as male or female sex wise is not one I've ever understood. Sex, like gender, can be a spectrum because of the number of parameters involved, but it's not going to be a very useful tool in science when you take something with a very high predictive rate and then scrap it entirely. you have no basis for measuring location on a spectrum without defining both sides.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:26:32-07:00","id":979794,"title":"","content":"No one is scrapping it, but understanding of it is evolving to better describe reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:38:14-07:00","id":979798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979776#post979776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> <br /> I understand what you're saying, but it's not an ideology I was made accustomed to growing up. I was taught that gender was biological, rather than psychological. So please forgive me for not understanding properly.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> Psychology is biological, especially if you're an atheist. Because there is no 'soul' your brain is responsible for your identity and consciousness. Your brain is a body part, like your liver or your heart, a very complex body part, but a product of your biology like everything else. Who you are as an individual has a lot to do with your neurological development. The reason why gender as a social construct is considered to be non-biological is because much of it is social, in other words women and men behave the way they do because society tells them that is what they are supposed to do, and then they get into the habit of doing that, and conditioned behaviors diehard. <br /> <br /> There is plenty of evidence to suggest that gender has a biological origin, identical twins are more likely to both be trans is one prevalent example. This does not mean that women are predisposed toward being less aggressive than men, or liking dresses. It means that a transgender person, often early on, will associate with women or men because 'that's what they are', and will pick up those behaviors because 'that's what women and men are supposed to do, right? I would like to fit in.&quot; <br /> <br /> As an example, when I was in elementary school I had a lot of issues where consciously I understood I was supposed to be a boy, but conditioning hadn't really taken hold yet. When asked to separate into lines of boy or girl, I would often find myself accidentally in the line for girls before running to the back of the boy's line and hoping no one saw me. There was one instance where we were asked to give presentations and at the end we were supposed to bow (for boys) or curtsy (for girls) and at the end of my presentation I automatically curtsied and tripped over myself trying to correct it halfway through the movement. There was another instance where I was kicked out of the boyscouts because I kept referring to everyone as she - even though I'd been reminded more than once where I was. I can remember very vividly forgetting that the same way you might forget you picked up an early shift at work. <br /> <br /> The thing is, in these instances I didn't consciously seek out these behaviors, I did not consciously 'want to be a girl'. Identity wise I was a girl, so when exposed to gender defining behaviors I would fuck it up and then feel very embarrassed due to my behavior. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979783#post979783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically sex categories are a social construct as much as gender. There is no &quot;essential&quot; male or female biology, just anatomical features and organs we choose to label as male or female.<br /> <br /> Saying that it is a social construct does not mean it is not real. It means things like intersex infants being surgically altered to fit these constructed definitions of &quot;male&quot; or &quot;female.&quot; For one example. It means that trans people are acknowledged as members of the correct sex where surgery isn't necessarily a requirement any longer. So, good and bad. But to say &quot;sex is biological&quot; ignores a lot of discussion that's going on right now, never mind the lived realities of trans and intersex people.<br /> <br /> Here's a link: <a href=\"http://bennorton.com/gender-is-not-alone-the-social-construction-of-sex/\" target=\"_blank\">http://bennorton.com/gender-is-not-a...uction-of-sex/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Sex categories exist because the entire point of science is to make accurate predictions. If I spot a woman on the street with overwhelming accuracy we can predict that her chromosomes are XX, and if we check that will be the case. There are outliers, because biology is not black and white, but this problem exists with countless theories and we don't throw those out either. Gender is not a construction of sex, but when it comes to interaction with social groups it's a guiding principle. The issue is when you assume someone's sex is outright determined by their chromosomes, or their primary sexual characteristics, when in reality the brain plays a much bigger role in what your identity will be like than any other body part. From there you gravitate toward members of the same sex because that's what society tells you to do, and the gender behaviors you pick up are theoretically a result of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:40:50-07:00","id":979800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979794#post979794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is scrapping it, but understanding of it is evolving to better describe reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please explain how telling people that it's problematic to suggest there is a female typical genetic/physiological boundary is anything but scrapping that instead of acknowledging that sex is a spectrum as much as gender is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:54:22-07:00","id":979807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979791#post979791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To consider this in context, this was in response to someone saying 'female genetics/physiology', which you claim is problematic, because it suggests they are 'necessary', which I don't think is the case. I don't think female typical genetics or physiology as a definition precludes you being a woman in spite of those traits, and don' understand why defining them in that way is problematic or invalidating toward your gender identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only speak for myself in this matter, but I personally find it invalidating because if my physiology is &quot;male&quot; or &quot;typically male&quot;, that implies that I'm less female than a woman with &quot;typically female&quot; physiology (I've never had tests done to analyze my genetics, so I won't speak to that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979791#post979791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, when you say it's problematic to use those definitions, then it becomes problematic for me to say &quot;I take estrogen because apparently my brain is wired in a typically female manner, testosterone, and the physical changes brought on by testosterone cause me discomfort.&quot; But using the above logic, it's inappropriate for me to put it that way because it might make someone who doesn't have those experiences feel invalidated in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's problematic of you to say. I mean, I would prefer you to phrase it differently, but there is nothing wrong with the sentiment, the problem is more of one with the limitations of our language related to sex. I don't tend to call people out on saying &quot;female/male anatomy&quot; or what have you, because I know they don't usually mean to say what that phrasing implies to me, and they don't really have a better term to use for it. So, to synthesize cause I kind of wandered there, I would certainly prefer that you not phrase it as &quot;apparently my brain is wired in a typically female matter&quot;, but there is nothing wrong with the sentiment that due to your brain chemistry, testosterone causes you discomfort and do you take estrogen to alleviate that, <i>per se</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979791#post979791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it's really no different than an intersex condition, and I've gotten a lot of drama for voicing that sentiment, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, intersex is exactly what the experience you describe sounds like to me, I certainly wouldn't give you any grief for saying so. But, it'a a sensitive issue and there's no consensus on the &quot;right terms&quot;. I'm sorry that's something you've had to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979791#post979791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm at work as I right this, and running low on sleep, so if I'm missing your point or misrepresenting your argument I apologize, I'm doing my level best to understand here, but the argument that that it's wrong to refer to genetics or physiology as male or female sex wise is not one I've ever understood.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no problem. I think we're having a good dialog and I hope I have not misrepresented your perspective either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979791#post979791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex, like gender, can be a spectrum because of the number of parameters involved, but it's not going to be a very useful tool in science when you take something with a very high predictive rate and then scrap it entirely. you have no basis for measuring location on a spectrum without defining both sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully agree with you there. I just want to push for terminology related to the sex spectrum that is not so bound up in the same language used to describe the gender spectrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-01-2016, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:54:32-07:00","id":979808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979798#post979798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex categories exist because the entire point of science is to make accurate predictions. If I spot a woman on the street with overwhelming accuracy we can predict that her chromosomes are XX, and if we check that will be the case. There are outliers, because biology is not black and white, but this problem exists with countless theories and we don't throw those out either. Gender is not a construction of sex, but when it comes to interaction with social groups it's a guiding principle. The issue is when you assume someone's sex is outright determined by their chromosomes, or their primary sexual characteristics, when in reality the brain plays a much bigger role in what your identity will be like than any other body part. From there you gravitate toward members of the same sex because that's what society tells you to do, and the gender behaviors you pick up are theoretically a result of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sex categories exist because people believe it is reasonable to take something fairly complex and simplify it down to a binary, and everyone who does not fit into that binary likely gets to suffer for it.<br /> <br /> Gender and sex is inextricably linked as social constructs. If you look up &quot;woman&quot; in the dictionary you will get something like &quot;an adult human female.&quot; It's practically circular, and leaves no room for intersex or trans people, as it suggests a trans woman would never be a woman because of the definition of &quot;female&quot; being &quot;of or denoting the sex that can bear offspring or produce eggs, distinguished biologically by the production of gametes (ova) that can be fertilized by male gametes.&quot; Admittedly, these are dictionary definitions which are of necessity very simplified and lacking in nuance, but this is about where arguing that sex categories are not social constructs takes us.<br /> <br /> No room for intersex people means surgical intervention as infants, and no room for trans people means massive amounts of gatekeeping and inaccessibility when it comes to trans-related medical care. For example, the fact that for decades in the US trans-related surgeries weren't covered by insurance at all, and even now it's not a guarantee (although it's much better than it was even ten years ago).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979800#post979800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please explain how telling people that it's problematic to suggest there is a female typical genetic/physiological boundary is anything but scrapping that instead of acknowledging that sex is a spectrum as much as gender is?</div> </div> </div> </div>It automatically excludes trans women from the definition of &quot;female,&quot; and a new definition would need to include trans women, including those who haven't transitioned, or who have only done certain things (like taking spironolactone and estrogen) but not other things (like electrolysis or surgery, for example). This doesn't deny that sex is a spectrum, but the binary sex model <i>does</i> deny that sex is a spectrum. And that's all it is - a model. It's not the best model, or the only possible model. It's not even the only model that's been used in human history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:57:18-07:00","id":979810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979777#post979777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. I have trans characters because I can't safely be trans IRL, so I'd cock my head a little at a ST who decided that meant I had any interest in playing through a narrative where my allies all accuse me of being a Wyrm-tained horrific deceiver.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a difference between universal resentment and rejection, and tailoring certain NPCs or encounters around the reality that people are going to stand in your way. One of these is oppressive and makes the player feel powerless to do anything, the other provides them a support network with which to confront these challenges, and overcome them in an environment that is safe and friendly.<br /> <br /> This makes the assumption that the ST is not an asshole and actually talks with players about their characters and what they're comfortable with in advance. I'm taking the time to respond to this because I'm interpreting it as an argument in favor of trivializing character traits. If the player isn't comfortable with it, leave them alone and let them have fun. I personally don't like playing characters where the traits exists solely for me to self-identify with the character, but I'm much more a narrativist than I am a simulationist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:59:53-07:00","id":979811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979807#post979807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully agree with you there. I just want to push for terminology related to the sex spectrum that is not so bound up in the same language used to describe the gender spectrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, this is a very short post without any real content - but Fucking This. +1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:08:36-07:00","id":979817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979808#post979808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex categories exist because people believe it is reasonable to take something fairly complex and simplify it down to a binary, and everyone who does not fit into that binary likely gets to suffer for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sex catagories exist because they are useful for making accurate predictions from a medical and scientific perspective. Simplifying it down into a binary is wrong as you've already pointed out. It's a spectrum, but again that spectrum has no meaning unless you define the extreme sides of it as 'one thing' and 'another thing'. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979808#post979808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gender and sex is inextricably linked as social constructs. If you look up &quot;woman&quot; in the dictionary you will get something like &quot;an adult human female.&quot; It's practically circular, and leaves no room for intersex or trans people, as it suggests a trans woman would never be a woman because of the definition of &quot;female&quot; being &quot;of or denoting the sex that can bear offspring or produce eggs, distinguished biologically by the production of gametes (ova) that can be fertilized by male gametes.&quot; Admittedly, these are dictionary definitions which are of necessity very simplified and lacking in nuance, but this is about where arguing that sex categories are not social constructs takes us.</div> </div> </div> </div>It leaves plenty of room for them if you switch from a sex binary system to a sex spectrum system where male and female are extreme examples. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979808#post979808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No room for intersex people means surgical intervention as infants, and no room for trans people means massive amounts of gatekeeping and inaccessibility when it comes to trans-related medical care. For example, the fact that for decades in the US trans-related surgeries weren't covered by insurance at all, and even now it's not a guarantee (although it's much better than it was even ten years ago).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're placing a lot of the blame for both of these things on one issue if you believe either of those things. Though I will admit that it plays a huge role in the reassignment of intersex infants. Gatekeeping on transrelated health care, particularly for women, has a lot more to do with misogyny than that, though. Trans people were full capable of getting government funding before the Reagan administration, when people like this happened: <a href=\"https://bitchmedia.org/post/the-long-history-of-transgender-exclusion-from-feminism\" target=\"_blank\">https://bitchmedia.org/post/the-long...-from-feminism</a><br /> <br /> Couple that with repeatedly being told that if I take Estrogen, I'll get cancer, while testosterone supplements are sold over the counter and are advertised on TV Infomercials as the solution to every problem a man might have. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979808#post979808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It automatically excludes trans women from the definition of &quot;female,&quot; and a new definition would need to include trans women, including those who haven't transitioned, or who have only done certain things (like taking spironolactone and estrogen) but not other things (like electrolysis or surgery, for example). This doesn't deny that sex is a spectrum, but the binary sex model <i>does</i> deny that sex is a spectrum. And that's all it is - a model. It's not the best model, or the only possible model. It's not even the only model that's been used in human history.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not going to establish a spectrum over binary by pronouncing exterminatus on the entire system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:15:32-07:00","id":979819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979817#post979817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're placing a lot of the blame for both of these things on one issue if you believe either of those things. Though I will admit that it plays a huge role in the reassignment of intersex infants. Gatekeeping on transrelated health care, particularly for women, has a lot more to do with misogyny than that, though. Trans people were full capable of getting government funding before the Reagan administration, when people like this happened: <a href=\"https://bitchmedia.org/post/the-long-history-of-transgender-exclusion-from-feminism\" target=\"_blank\">https://bitchmedia.org/post/the-long...-from-feminism</a></div> </div> </div> </div>1980 until 2016 is 36 years, hence decades. I didn't say it was never possible, but there was a point where it wasn't a thing.<br /> <br /> And I don't think you can really place most of the blame on misogyny, although a lot of it certainly has to do with transmisogyny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979817#post979817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not going to establish a spectrum over binary by pronouncing exterminatus on the entire system.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'm not pronouncing exterminatus on the entire system? I am saying that the entire system is a social construct. That's not eliminating it, not saying it's not real, not saying it's not based on real anatomy and internal organs. It says none of these things.<br /> <br /> But it's not that hard to avoid language that implicitly defines trans women out of womanhood, is it? Is it necessary to talk about &quot;biologically female&quot; or &quot;sex is biological, gender is cultural&quot; or the rather crude, &quot;sex is between your legs, gender is between your ears?&quot; All of these things support gendering trans bodies incorrectly, saying that a trans woman's body is really a male body, really a <i>man's</i> body, when there is no man involved because we're talking about a trans woman's body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-01-2016, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:41:02-07:00","id":979827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979817#post979817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex catagories exist because they are useful for making accurate predictions from a medical and scientific perspective. Simplifying it down into a binary is wrong as you've already pointed out. It's a spectrum, but again that spectrum has no meaning unless you define the extreme sides of it as 'one thing' and 'another thing'.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's useful, but we should make sure that the language we use to describe &quot;one thing&quot; and &quot;another thing&quot; doesn't implicitly invalidate trans people's genders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979817#post979817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It leaves plenty of room for them if you switch from a sex binary system to a sex spectrum system where male and female are extreme examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is male and female are, by usage, nearly interchangeable with the words that describe the extremes of the gender spectrum. Sex should be seen as a spectrum, and the extremes of that spectrum should be defined, but defining them as &quot;male&quot; and &quot;female&quot; is problematic because those concepts are too linked with the concept of manhood and womanhood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979817#post979817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not going to establish a spectrum over binary by pronouncing exterminatus on the entire system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the goal is not to reject the system, but to push for better language with which to describe the system. By rejecting &quot;male&quot; and &quot;female&quot; as descriptors of sex, we push people to find ways to communicate those concepts that are not hurtful to people who are one one extreme of the sex spectrum and the opposite extreme of the gender spectrum, and makes the distinction clearer for people who are not well-versed in sex and gender related issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-01-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:01:14-07:00","id":979838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979819#post979819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1980 until 2016 is 36 years, hence decades. I didn't say it was never possible, but there was a point where it wasn't a thing.<br /> <br /> And I don't think you can really place most of the blame on misogyny, although a lot of it certainly has to do with transmisogyny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument was that the language in place is the cause for gatekeeping and exclusion from health care for transgender people. Until the Reagan administration transgender people had access to those things. It would be erroneous to say gatekeeping didn't exist because that has existed to some extent in all of medicine depending on your doctor, the extent of your health insurance, and socio-economic factors. However when people talk about a transgender woman's inability to access healthcare, they are specifically referring to the difficulties that came out of the Reagan administration almost exclusively, and that had much to do with Trans Misogyny on the part of some radical feminists, and less to do with scientific language defining transwomen out of womanhood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979827#post979827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the goal is not to reject the system, but to push for better language with which to describe the system. By rejecting &quot;male&quot; and &quot;female&quot; as descriptors of sex, we push people to find ways to communicate those concepts that are not hurtful to people who are one one extreme of the sex spectrum and the opposite extreme of the gender spectrum, and makes the distinction clearer for people who are not well-versed in sex and gender related issues.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979819#post979819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's not that hard to avoid language that implicitly defines trans women out of womanhood, is it? Is it necessary to talk about &quot;biologically female&quot; or &quot;sex is biological, gender is cultural&quot; or the rather crude, &quot;sex is between your legs, gender is between your ears?&quot; All of these things support gendering trans bodies incorrectly, saying that a trans woman's body is really a male body, really a <i>man's</i> body, when there is no man involved because we're talking about a trans woman's body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there replacement language that can be pushed? I am presently unaware of an alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:15:00-07:00","id":979844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979838#post979838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there replacement language that can be pushed? I am presently unaware of an alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I am aware of either. I mean, I could make some up, but it's unlikely they'd gain any traction unless they were adopted by the medical community. And the medical community isn't likely to see any need to stop using male and female if people generally accept those terms.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, I guess it's not entirely true that I don't know of any other terms. I've heard XX and XY as gender-neutral terms describing sexual genetics, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-01-2016, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:19:30-07:00","id":979849,"title":"","content":"Might just be me but, it's hard to reject terms without newer terms to use. I don't mind being more accurate or even more polite if I have the language for it. If there is no alternative alternative then people won't see a reason to not accept those terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:28:01-07:00","id":979857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979838#post979838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your argument was that the language in place is the cause for gatekeeping and exclusion from health care for transgender people. Until the Reagan administration transgender people had access to those things. It would be erroneous to say gatekeeping didn't exist because that has existed to some extent in all of medicine depending on your doctor, the extent of your health insurance, and socio-economic factors. However when people talk about a transgender woman's inability to access healthcare, they are specifically referring to the difficulties that came out of the Reagan administration almost exclusively, and that had much to do with Trans Misogyny on the part of some radical feminists, and less to do with scientific language defining transwomen out of womanhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, no, that's a misunderstanding of what I wrote - or I wrote what I was trying to say very badly. Either works, probably the latter though.. It wasn't the language that did it, it was the attitude that trans women are really men, which radical feminists promote heavily, and which the language I was talking about crystallizes and in general supports.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there replacement language that can be pushed? I am presently unaware of an alternative. </div> </div> </div>Well, not referring to trans people as members of their sex assigned at birth tends to be a solution. Or not referring to &quot;biologically female&quot; or &quot;biologically male&quot; when it's just as easy to say cis man, trans man, cis woman, or trans woman as appropriate instead, if them being cis is a necessary distinction (such as distinguishing them from trans people).<br /> <br /> There are very few circumstances where it is necessary to refer to trans people in a manner that emphasizes their transness or the sex they were assigned at birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-01-2016, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:32:45-07:00","id":979858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979849#post979849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might just be me but, it's hard to reject terms without newer terms to use. I don't mind being more accurate or even more polite if I have the language for it. If there is no alternative alternative then people won't see a reason to not accept those terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coercively assigned male at birth, assigned male at birth, designated male at birth, female, trans female, woman, trans woman. Each of these should be use when the context is appropriate. If the sex assigned at birth matters (and most of the time it really doesn't matter at all) then there you go. Otherwise, it's just best to describe trans women as female and women. If talking specifically about trans women in a context that being trans matters then trans female or trans woman.<br /> <br /> Similar applies to trans men - coercively assigned female at birth, male, man, etc.<br /> <br /> And I emphasize again that the vast majority of the time, that when talking about a trans person, their assigned sex does not matter so much as their actual gender, and sticking to vocabulary consistent with that gender is the most appropriate decision.<br /> <br /> At least that's my understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:43:46-07:00","id":979861,"title":"","content":"I thought the subject was the 2 medical extremes of sex....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:49:52-07:00","id":979863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979857#post979857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, no, that's a misunderstanding of what I wrote - or I wrote what I was trying to say very badly. Either works, probably the latter though.. It wasn't the language that did it, it was the attitude that trans women are really men, which radical feminists promote heavily, and which the language I was talking about crystallizes and in general supports.<br /> <br /> Well, not referring to trans people as members of their sex assigned at birth tends to be a solution. Or not referring to &quot;biologically female&quot; or &quot;biologically male&quot; when it's just as easy to say cis man, trans man, cis woman, or trans woman as appropriate instead, if them being cis is a necessary distinction (such as distinguishing them from trans people).<br /> <br /> There are very few circumstances where it is necessary to refer to trans people in a manner that emphasizes their transness or the sex they were assigned at birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're both misunderstanding each other a bit here, and that's understandable because it's a very complicated issue. There's a reason why people specialize in these sorts of studies as a career, after all. <br /> <br /> So I don't have any issue with those terms you said above, the issue is that I am taking drugs to bring the rest of my body into line with how my brain is wired. Based on the fact that if I am not on the appropriate hormone I slip into a suicidal depression, I define myself as female - irrespective of any gender practices. I'm not opposed to makeup, or dresses, I typically go out in whatever I think looks good or makes me feel presentable. But - because I need to alter my body in order to ease my dysphoria, and those alterations bring it closer to what is traditionally female - do you see what I'm saying? If it's problematic to say one body type is more female than another, then there is no basis for me to be a transwoman, unless we're going to base it on how I interact with others in society, but what if I don't want to adhere to what society defines as 'female'? Of course I get self-conscious when my voice slips, or because I'm struggling with healthcare things and haven't been able to get surgery or electrolysis, but that's because other women don't need those things, and that puts me apart, which is something a social animal doesn't want. <br /> <br /> In the end the only thing I'm left with is that I am a woman, because the parts of me that matter, that govern my identity, consciousness, and living experience with the world around me, are wired in a way typical of females, regardless of what my visible sexual characteristics are, or my chromosomes. This is - in my opinion, based on my own research - likely because of hormones at the developmental stage where those sorts of distinctions began to form, with the net result that I identify with other humans who have similar characteristics to what my brain expects it should have, and that I need to take hormones and bring my body in line with what my brain is wired to accept.<br /> <br /> If we decide that it's problematic to label that as female, then I don't actually have a gender identity because there is no definition to sex at all, and most gender behaviors are entirely arbitrary and passed down throughout generations to people with similar characteristics, who are taught to keep to, and learn from, people with their characteristics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:50:58-07:00","id":979865,"title":"","content":"And since people insist on saying things like &quot;two medical extremes of sex&quot; I was trying to explain ways to talk about trans people that don't misgender them or their bodies (for example, finding ways to call trans women &quot;male&quot; or &quot;men&quot; or &quot;used to be men&quot; or &quot;really men&quot; etc). Which is to say it doesn't matter what the so-called &quot;medical extremes&quot; say when you're talking about people and their individual needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:57:47-07:00","id":979868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979863#post979863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we decide that it's problematic to label that as female, then I don't actually have a gender identity because there is no definition to sex at all, and most gender behaviors are entirely arbitrary and passed down throughout generations to people with similar characteristics, who are taught to keep to, and learn from, people with their characteristics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to trim down your post but this seemed like the essence of what you were getting at?<br /> <br /> Saying that as a trans woman you have a female body (as a woman is an adult human female) doesn't mean ignoring your needs. HRT, surgery, etc. are proven treatments that almost universally improve quality of life for trans people, and saying you're female doesn't also say &quot;you don't need those treatments.&quot; Nor does it say &quot;you already have a female body, so you're fine as you are.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not really problematic to label cis women as female but more to do so in a way that excludes trans women, or label trans women in a way that excludes them from being female.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-01-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:09:01-07:00","id":979877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979868#post979868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry to trim down your post but this seemed like the essence of what you were getting at?<br /> <br /> Saying that as a trans woman you have a female body (as a woman is an adult human female) doesn't mean ignoring your needs. HRT, surgery, etc. are proven treatments that almost universally improve quality of life for trans people, and saying you're female doesn't also say &quot;you don't need those treatments.&quot; Nor does it say &quot;you already have a female body, so you're fine as you are.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not really problematic to label cis women as female but more to do so in a way that excludes trans women, or label trans women in a way that excludes them from being female.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We're referring to biology, though. The person I was responding to specifically mentioned 'genetically male' and 'genetically female'. My argument is that it's possible to have one characteristic that is typically male or female without it ruling you. As an example, XY women, there are a few factors that can lead to this, one example leading to a lack of menstruation or developing secondary sexual characteristics until after they're placed on hormone therapy, as well, the gonads have to be removed because those are often cancerous. Although they have no eggs of their own, they still have all the relevant parts, they can menstruate, and they can get pregnant if an Ova is donated to them. It's still considered an 'anomaly' from the norm, because most women don't experience that hurdle.<br /> <br /> But if you declare that claiming certain reproductive parts as female is problematic, because not all female have them, then anomaly of <b>what?</b> Characteristic of <b>what?</b><br /> <br /> Likewise, if we decide that a brain wired to expect those things\u2014otherwise the body will tear itself apart out of stress\u2014is not due to having female neurology, because saying that neurology is problematic when there are women who don't experience gender dysphoria at all, ever, then wherein is the basis for someone being a woman at all? Gender theory? But gender is entirely arbitrary and depends on who you ask, so who is the arbiter, and if gender is purely subjective what value does it have in scientific discussions at all?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or for that matter, what value would it have as a method of identification, since what I mean when I say &quot;I'm female&quot; is going to be different (perhaps entirely so, especially in the case with people like Innocent earlier.) from what anyone else means when they say it? For that reason, I choose to identify by my perceived sex, not gender, and my overall perceived sex is female because of the parameters I mentioned in earlier posts. Certainly they're the ones that are most relevant, because I don't process my entire sense of self with what's between my legs, or with my chromosomes. It also influences how I approach gender behaviors at all, and how I learn from the people around me.<br /> <br /> So when it comes to identity, that seems like the most critical factor, is what I am saying. If we decide it's problematic to say that an XX chromosome is typical of females, or that the ability to carry young is typical of females, or that the brain being set up a certain way is typical of females, then it effectively leaves me with 'nothing' to identify with. In a sense, accomplishing the very thing you sought to correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-01-2016, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:18:30-07:00","id":979885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979877#post979877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We're referring to biology, though. The person I was responding to specifically mentioned 'genetically male' and 'genetically female'. My argument is that it's possible to have one characteristic that is typically male or female without it ruling you. As an example, XY women, there are a few factors that can lead to this, one example leading to a lack of menstruation or developing secondary sexual characteristics until after they're placed on hormone therapy, as well, the gonads have to be removed because those are often cancerous. Although they have no eggs of their own, they still have all the relevant parts, they can menstruate, and they can get pregnant if an Ova is donated to them. It's still considered an 'anomaly' from the norm, because most women don't experience that hurdle.<br /> <br /> But if you declare that claiming certain reproductive parts as female is problematic, because not all female have them, then anomaly of <b>what?</b> Characteristic of <b>what?</b><br /> <br /> Likewise, if we decide that a brain wired to expect those things\u2014otherwise the body will tear itself apart out of stress\u2014is not due to having female neurology, because saying that neurology is problematic when there are women who don't experience gender dysphoria at all, ever. Wherein is the basis for someone being a woman at all? Gender theory? But gender is entirely arbitrary and depends on who you ask, so who is the arbiter, and if gender is purely subjective what value does it have in scientific discussions at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reality is that whatever we call these things the need to transition still exists for many people, and choosing whether or not to refer to people as genetically female or male won't change that fact. No one reasonable is going to argue that a shift in language will negate the need to transition. The kind of people who would make that argument in all seriousness (I don't mean raising it as a concern like you are) are exactly the kind of people we shouldn't be listening to.<br /> <br /> Gender is a social construct, but that doesn't mean it's a purely subjective experience, or that it's not real. The majority of people have a subjective experience of gender, which includes an awareness of their own gender - being subjective doesn't make it wrong or false or nonexistent. It's still real. Not saying that being trans is a mental illness, but if we start discounting subjectivity as valid then mental illness becomes meaningless and millions of psychiatrists are out of a job. Subjectivity is a very important part of the human experience.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:23:38-07:00","id":979888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979849#post979849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might just be me but, it's hard to reject terms without newer terms to use. I don't mind being more accurate or even more polite if I have the language for it. If there is no alternative alternative then people won't see a reason to not accept those terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>If people don't reject the terms in common use, there's no impetus to create new terms. Also, &quot;finding a way to express myself without using terms that are harmful to you is hard&quot; is never a good reason to continue using harmful terms.<br /> <br /> Again, if you want me to make up a term, I will. I'd be surprised if it manages to spread beyond this conversation, let alone spread beyond these forums and then stick in the cultural consciousness. But we can try. In the mean time, XX and XY are gender-neutral ways to refer to chromosomes. Testosterone and Estrogen are gender-neutral ways to refer to hormones. Penis and vagina are gender-neutral ways to refer to genitals.<br /> <br /> Like, it's not as though vocabulary doesn't exist to describe features of sex. There are not yet terms that sum up common collections of them and aren't conflated with gender, but if we stop using gender-related terms to refer to sex and just use our expanded vocabularies, there becomes a reason for the people with the power to create new terms with traction to want to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:41:13-07:00","id":979894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979863#post979863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't have any issue with those terms you said above, the issue is that I am taking drugs to bring the rest of my body into line with how my brain is wired. Based on the fact that if I am not on the appropriate hormone I slip into a suicidal depression, I define myself as female - irrespective of any gender practices. I'm not opposed to makeup, or dresses, I typically go out in whatever I think looks good or makes me feel presentable. But - because I need to alter my body in order to ease my dysphoria, and those alterations bring it closer to what is traditionally female - do you see what I'm saying? If it's problematic to say one body type is more female than another, then there is no basis for me to be a transwoman,</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure there is. Do you identify with the gender you were assigned at birth? If not, you have a basis to identify yourself as trans. Do you prefer to be recognized as a woman? If so, you have a basis to identify yourself as a woman. Do you desire access to resources and support for transgender individuals? If so, you have a basis for access to resources and support for transgender individuals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979863#post979863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless we're going to base it on how I interact with others in society, but what if I don't want to adhere to what society defines as 'female'? Of course I get self-conscious when my voice slips, or because I'm struggling with healthcare things and haven't been able to get surgery or electrolysis, but that's because other women don't need those things, and that puts me apart, which is something a social animal doesn't want.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was the metric, I wouldn't qualify as female. Heck, I wear a beard a lot of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979863#post979863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end the only thing I'm left with is that I am a woman, because the parts of me that matter, that govern my identity, consciousness, and living experience with the world around me, are wired in a way typical of females, regardless of what my visible sexual characteristics are, or my chromosomes. This is - in my opinion, based on my own research - likely because of hormones at the developmental stage where those sorts of distinctions began to form, with the net result that I identify with other humans who have similar characteristics to what my brain expects it should have, and that I need to take hormones and bring my body in line with what my brain is wired to accept.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's absolutely a valid reason to identify as a trans woman, and none of it relies on using the word &quot;female&quot; to describe your sexual characteristics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979863#post979863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we decide that it's problematic to label that as female, then I don't actually have a gender identity because there is no definition to sex at all, and most gender behaviors are entirely arbitrary and passed down throughout generations to people with similar characteristics, who are taught to keep to, and learn from, people with their characteristics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, agender is a thing, along with a whole host of nonbinary gender terms, if you feel neither man or woman is an accurate description of your gender identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:04:32-07:00","id":979901,"title":"","content":"We are actually dealing with a similar issue with my fiance's younger sibling, who announced that he was a man despite having identified as a girl until last year (the younger sibling is XX and, according to their mother, was perfectly physiologically female). He (using the masculine gender pronoun out of respect for his right to choose) is developing his own masculine gender identity, but he is focusing on developing the most macho and misogynistic aspects of masculinity, which is making it hard for his relatives to take him seriously because he is becoming a caricature of a man rather than a 'real' man. <br /> <br /> It is odd contrasting his experience with the experience of the transwomen I have known. They have sacrificed male privilege because they wish to become what they see themselves as, which are women. He is trying to grab onto male privilege, and it is a bit disconcerting because he identifies with the worst parts of that privilege. <br /> <br /> While Black Furies may or may not accept the transwomen among their Kinfolk as 'women', I imagine that they would find transmen to be a betrayal of all of their beliefs. What do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:10:16-07:00","id":979905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979894#post979894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure there is. Do you identify with the gender you were assigned at birth? If not, you have a basis to identify yourself as trans. Do you prefer to be recognized as a woman? If so, you have a basis to identify yourself as a woman. Do you desire access to resources and support for transgender individuals? If so, you have a basis for access to resources and support for transgender individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't identify with the gender I was born at birth, but even if I didn't feel the need to transition I would not have felt it encapsulates what being a man means. Just as I don't feel like all of the behaviors associated with women define being a woman, even the ones I value. Being recognized as a woman is <b>meaningless</b> if we're using gender to define ourselves, because if I tell someone else I'm a woman, what I just communicated is what <i>they</i> understand women to be, not my position on the matter. Being transgender can no longer be defined by the pursuit of resources for transgender individuals, because a growing number of people identify as transgender with no desire to pursue those services or transition physically. Some don't alter anything about themselves except the pronoun they wish to be called. How is this helpful as a label when we have otherwise 'nothing' in common? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979894#post979894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that was the metric, I wouldn't qualify as female. Heck, I wear a beard a lot of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know enough about you to really argue the point, and it's not my place to pass judgment on you specifically as a person, no matter how much my Obrimos natures tells me I can. I don't actually have Prime :c. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979894#post979894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's absolutely a valid reason to identify as a trans woman, and none of it relies on using the word &quot;female&quot; to describe your sexual characteristics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it does? The entire basis for the assertion is that my brain\u2014the part of me that is even aware I exist\u2014is female typical.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979894#post979894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, agender is a thing, along with a whole host of nonbinary gender terms, if you feel neither man or woman is an accurate description of your gender identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that I 'do' feel I'm female, but my method of self-identification is problematic. If I base my identity on gender the way it's presented to me, with all of the problems I outlined above, then it's not even that I am agender, I am all the genders and none of the genders because there is no definitive example for which to base an argument, perspective, or feeling. It basically turns me into Schrodinger's Cat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:10:32-07:00","id":979906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979901#post979901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are actually dealing with a similar issue with my fiance's younger sibling, who announced that he was a man despite having identified as a girl until last year (the younger sibling is XX and, according to their mother, was perfectly physiologically female). He (using the masculine gender pronoun out of respect for his right to choose) is developing his own masculine gender identity, but he is focusing on developing the most macho and misogynistic aspects of masculinity, which is making it hard for his relatives to take him seriously because he is becoming a caricature of a man rather than a 'real' man. <br /> <br /> It is odd contrasting his experience with the experience of the transwomen I have known. They have sacrificed male privilege because they wish to become what they see themselves as, which are women. He is trying to grab onto male privilege, and it is a bit disconcerting because he identifies with the worst parts of that privilege. <br /> <br /> While Black Furies may or may not accept the transwomen among their Kinfolk as 'women', I imagine that they would find transmen to be a betrayal of all of their beliefs. What do you all think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when you don't have a ton of healthy examples of what masculinity means or looks like...<br /> <br /> But I can definitely see the Black Furies not being fans of trans men, or at the very least asking them to leave the Tribe, and that's before you factor in gross elders who might insist that they're still a woman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:15:32-07:00","id":979910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979901#post979901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are actually dealing with a similar issue with my fiance's younger sibling, who announced that he was a man despite having identified as a girl until last year (the younger sibling is XX and, according to their mother, was perfectly physiologically female). He (using the masculine gender pronoun out of respect for his right to choose) is developing his own masculine gender identity, but he is focusing on developing the most macho and misogynistic aspects of masculinity, which is making it hard for his relatives to take him seriously because he is becoming a caricature of a man rather than a 'real' man.<br /> <br /> It is odd contrasting his experience with the experience of the transwomen I have known. They have sacrificed male privilege because they wish to become what they see themselves as, which are women. He is trying to grab onto male privilege, and it is a bit disconcerting because he identifies with the worst parts of that privilege.<br /> <br /> While Black Furies may or may not accept the transwomen among their Kinfolk as 'women', I imagine that they would find transmen to be a betrayal of all of their beliefs. What do you all think?</div> </div> </div> </div>That really depends on how the person goes about it. If they're already in the tribe it's worth considering that some Black Furies are rumored to spontaneously become men because of the Wyld. If the transman takes on a spiritual/shamanistic perspective on it, then they might have a place in the tribe, especially as a 'gelding', if they don't have any interest in it, and wish to go about their lives, they would likely not be allowed in the sacred spaces or rituals, and would be better served in the Children of Gaia anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:36:43-07:00","id":979929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979910#post979910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That really depends on how the person goes about it. If they're already in the tribe it's worth considering that <b>some Black Furies are rumored to spontaneously become men because of the Wyld.</b> If the transman takes on a spiritual/shamanistic perspective on it, then they might have a place in the tribe, especially as a 'gelding', if they don't have any interest in it, and wish to go about their lives, they would likely not be allowed in the sacred spaces or rituals, and would be better served in the Children of Gaia anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's that? The Revised Tribebook?<br /> <br /> Not challenging, just curious where to look.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:09:30-07:00","id":979943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979905#post979905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't identify with the gender I was born at birth, but even if I didn't feel the need to transition I would not have felt it encapsulates what being a man means. Just as I don't feel like all of the behaviors associated with women define being a woman, even the ones I value. Being recognized as a woman is <b>meaningless</b> if we're using gender to define ourselves, because if I tell someone else I'm a woman, what I just communicated is what <i>they</i> understand women to be, not my position on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to desire to transition to be trans. You don't have to be a man or a woman to be trans. Trans is an extremely broad description that can be applied to people who occupy any position on the gender spectrum, as a way of expressing that their position on the gender spectrum is not the one their parents assigned them to at birth. And being recognized as a woman may be meaningless to you, but it sure as hell isn't to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979905#post979905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Being transgender can no longer be defined by the pursuit of resources for transgender individuals, because a growing number of people identify as transgender with no desire to pursue those services or transition physically.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how I define trans. If you do desire those resources, however, you should have the right to access to them, regardless of what definition consider yourself trans under.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979905#post979905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some don't alter anything about themselves except the pronoun they wish to be called. How is this helpful as a label when we have otherwise 'nothing' in common?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's helpful if it helps the person define their identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979905#post979905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know enough about you to really argue the point, and it's not my place to pass judgment on you specifically as a person, no matter how much my Obrimos natures tells me I can. I don't actually have Prime :c.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know as it matters anyway, we both seem to agree that gender expression is not the metric that defines gender identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979905#post979905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure it does? The entire basis for the assertion is that my brain\u2014the part of me that is even aware I exist\u2014is female typical.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is, none of what you described relies on the term &quot;female&quot;. You could say instead that your brain is typical of one extreme of the sex spectrum - the one that also typically has two X chromosomes, vaginas, and estrogen as a more predominant hormone than testosterone - without describing that position on the sex spectrum with a word also associated with a particular gender.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979905#post979905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that I 'do' feel I'm female, but my method of self-identification is problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that it is. I think the language you use to explain it is, but there is nothing inherently problematic with defining your own gender on the basis of your sexual features. As long as you don't define other people's genders that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979905#post979905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I base my identity on gender the way it's presented to me, with all of the problems I outlined above, then it's not even that I am agender, I am all the genders and none of the genders because there is no definitive example for which to base an argument, perspective, or feeling. It basically turns me into Schrodinger's Cat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I personally would describe that as genderfluid. That's also the term I would use to describe my own gender. I prefer she/her/hers pronouns over any gender neutral pronoun options and I describe myself as a woman because I trend feminine and &quot;genderfluid person&quot; is overly cumbersome. But I'm not going to tell you what terms to describe yourself with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:14:39-07:00","id":979944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979929#post979929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where's that? The Revised Tribebook?<br /> <br /> Not challenging, just curious where to look.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/TDVcp\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/TDVcp\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/TDVcp\" target=\"_blank\"> http://imgur.com/a/TDVcp </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All in all the notion is fairly terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:26:29-07:00","id":979953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979943#post979943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to desire to transition to be trans. You don't have to be a man or a woman to be trans. Trans is an extremely broad description that can be applied to people who occupy any position on the gender spectrum, as a way of expressing that their position on the gender spectrum is not the one their parents assigned them to at birth. And being recognized as a woman may be meaningless to you, but it sure as hell isn't to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's not how I define trans. If you do desire those resources, however, you should have the right to access to them, regardless of what definition consider yourself trans under.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's helpful if it helps the person define their identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know as it matters anyway, we both seem to agree that gender expression is not the metric that defines gender identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I'm saying is, none of what you described relies on the term &quot;female&quot;. You could say instead that your brain is typical of one extreme of the sex spectrum - the one that also typically has two X chromosomes, vaginas, and estrogen as a more predominant hormone than testosterone - without describing that position on the sex spectrum with a word also associated with a particular gender.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think that it is. I think the language you use to explain it is, but there is nothing inherently problematic with defining your own gender on the basis of your sexual features. As long as you don't define other people's genders that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, I personally would describe that as genderfluid. That's also the term I would use to describe my own gender. I prefer she/her/hers pronouns over any gender neutral pronoun options and I describe myself as a woman because I trend feminine and &quot;genderfluid person&quot; is overly cumbersome. But I'm not going to tell you what terms to describe yourself with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't really have a lot to add to this tangent at this point, beyond the realization that this entire conversation has made me feel like Wirt from Over the Garden Wall. Taking me further and further from where I want to be, <b>who,</b> I want to be.<br /> <br /> /rolls away dramatically.<br /> <br /> The world is a confusing place!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:36:58-07:00","id":979956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979944#post979944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/TDVcp\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/TDVcp\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/TDVcp\" target=\"_blank\"> http://imgur.com/a/TDVcp </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All in all the notion is fairly terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's pretty horrific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:40:57-07:00","id":979959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979953#post979953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really have a lot to add to this tangent at this point, beyond the realization that this entire conversation has made me feel like Wirt from Over the Garden Wall. Taking me further and further from where I want to be, <b>who,</b> I want to be.<br /> <br /> /rolls away dramatically.<br /> <br /> The world is a confusing place!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry. It was certainly not my intention to make you feel that way, and I apologize if I came across as trying to tell you who you should be at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:47:33-07:00","id":979961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979959#post979959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am sorry. It was certainly not my intention to make you feel that way, and I apologize if I came across as trying to tell you who you should be at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't. If you haven't seen the show the comedic tone might have been lost. Obviously you weren't passing it down as an edict or anything, but I work 12 hours today, and you've given me a lot to think about at a time when I'm already exhausted.<br /> <br /> Which is a good thing! The stuff to think about part, not the exhaustion. Obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:57:15-07:00","id":979969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=979961#post979961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You didn't. If you haven't seen the show the comedic tone might have been lost. Obviously you weren't passing it down as an edict or anything, but I work 12 hours today, and you've given me a lot to think about at a time when I'm already exhausted.<br /> <br /> Which is a good thing! The stuff to think about part, not the exhaustion. Obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's a relief. I have seen OtGW, but it's been a while, and the &quot;who I want to be&quot; part just made me worry I might have overstepped by saying your self-description of your gender sounds like something I would describe as genderfluid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:47:22-07:00","id":980389,"title":"","content":"I think the past few pages have highlighted important issues in the world of darkness<br /> <br /> 1- There is a massive transgender community here, both as general players and especially as the diehards on the forums. Many among this community attrach themselves to world of darkness because of it's strong attachment to narrative; It gives others the chance to rollplay anywhere along the gender spectrum (admitedly also as supernatural monster) and it has a strong appeal for this community for that reason. <br /> <br /> 2- World of darkness is a world like ours that sensationalizes every shitty aspect about our world. More divide, more hate, more corruption. <br /> <br /> 3- Building on points 1 and 2, some people don't want to deal with stuff that makes people uncomfortable. They just want to have fun. And that's totally fine and all, but...<br /> <br /> 4- maybe the trangender community feels more vulnerable or just has a really strong playerbase, but gender issues seems to become more progressive in the world of darkness... And from a literrary standpoint... That's a counterproductive technique. The world of darkness works on a princible device of identifing shitty things and sensationalizing them. IE the financial world is run by vampires, your job was made shitty to feed banes by an evil megacorp. the media is intentionally filling your head with shit to satisfy corperate interests, a great triatic evil, and a mage's paradigm. In the world of darkness, we're regressive, not progressive, and those guys that whine about 'the current generation' might as well be right. <br /> <b>It's really, really fucking weird when you make exceptions to this.</b> There was a portion of the book of the wyrm that explained Magadon pharmaceuticals and their evil branches, then had a bit about woman's health and how the 'feminist' research lead wasn't knowingly working for wyrm corp. Like what the fuck is anyone supposed to take away from that? Are we trying to say contraceptives, birth control and feminists are evil? Are we trying to say that an evil megacorp is being turned around by feminists? Why is something without a sinister secret agenda put in between &quot;miracle cures that're addictive make you sicker&quot; and &quot;abominable attempts at making new changing breeds &quot;. Are you not aware of how toxic such an anecdote is in a piece that otherwise works towards a literary theme? <br /> It's backwards, but if you put in stuff like &quot;Go transsexualism, get empowered&quot; amongst a setting of utter corruption and shit, well, you're kinda putting that empowering stuff in the pile of things you're finding abominable. You don't put good things in a setting about problems. Maybe people will confuse your meaning think you're trying to say that transexual empowerment is a problem just like fracking and warmongering. Black Furies excluding men was never supposed to be a good thing, it's like Talons being kill-humans or the Get being elitist, or the silver fangs relying on klaives,pure breed and ancestors to get them through a conversation. Having transgender black furies would need to open up the doors for all manner of other changes in context: like the Fianna could stop drinking themselves into depression or the bone gnawers could start catering for the lower-middle class.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T13:22:49-07:00","id":980399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980389#post980389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the past few pages have highlighted important issues in the world of darkness<br /> 4- maybe the trangender community feels more vulnerable or just has a really strong playerbase, but gender issues seems to become more progressive in the world of darkness... And from a literrary standpoint... That's a counterproductive technique. The world of darkness works on a princible device of identifing shitty things and sensationalizing them. IE the financial world is run by vampires, your job was made shitty to feed banes by an evil megacorp. the media is intentionally filling your head with shit to satisfy corperate interests, a great triatic evil, and a mage's paradigm. In the world of darkness, we're regressive, not progressive, and those guys that whine about 'the current generation' might as well be right.<br /> <b>It's really, really fucking weird when you make exceptions to this.</b> There was a portion of the book of the wyrm that explained Magadon pharmaceuticals and their evil branches, then had a bit about woman's health and how the 'feminist' research lead wasn't knowingly working for wyrm corp. Like what the fuck is anyone supposed to take away from that? Are we trying to say contraceptives, birth control and feminists are evil? Are we trying to say that an evil megacorp is being turned around by feminists? Why is something without a sinister secret agenda put in between &quot;miracle cures that're addictive make you sicker&quot; and &quot;abominable attempts at making new changing breeds &quot;. Are you not aware of how toxic such an anecdote is in a piece that otherwise works towards a literary theme?<br /> It's backwards, but if you put in stuff like &quot;Go transsexualism, get empowered&quot; amongst a setting of utter corruption and shit, well, you're kinda putting that empowering stuff in the pile of things you're finding abominable. You don't put good things in a setting about problems. Maybe people will confuse your meaning think you're trying to say that transexual empowerment is a problem just like fracking and warmongering. Black Furies excluding men was never supposed to be a good thing, it's like Talons being kill-humans or the Get being elitist, or the silver fangs relying on klaives,pure breed and ancestors to get them through a conversation. Having transgender black furies would need to open up the doors for all manner of other changes in context: like the Fianna could stop drinking themselves into depression or the bone gnawers could start catering for the lower-middle class.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's a thing, how can WoD reflect our world, if it is not allowed to? Stuff -needs- to progress, in order to match what our world is like today. Otherwise, it is stuck in 80s-90s and those decades do not reflect our world anymore, in pop culture or in general culture.<br /> <br /> As for the tribal examples you gave, all of those things have all ready happened in canon. There are Fianna who don't drink, Alberch earned the trust of his people outside klaives and purebreed, there are Red Talons who don't eat humans,etc. I understand that is how you see the setting, but in terms of the discussion, it does not reflect what has been written of the tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T13:40:51-07:00","id":980411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980389#post980389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the past few pages have highlighted important issues in the world of darkness<br /> <br /> 1- There is a massive transgender community here, both as general players and especially as the diehards on the forums. Many among this community attrach themselves to world of darkness because of it's strong attachment to narrative; It gives others the chance to rollplay anywhere along the gender spectrum (admitedly also as supernatural monster) and it has a strong appeal for this community for that reason.<br /> <br /> 2- World of darkness is a world like ours that sensationalizes every shitty aspect about our world. More divide, more hate, more corruption.<br /> <br /> 3- Building on points 1 and 2, some people don't want to deal with stuff that makes people uncomfortable. They just want to have fun. And that's totally fine and all, but...<br /> <br /> 4- maybe the trangender community feels more vulnerable or just has a really strong playerbase, but gender issues seems to become more progressive in the world of darkness... And from a literrary standpoint... That's a counterproductive technique. The world of darkness works on a princible device of identifing shitty things and sensationalizing them. IE the financial world is run by vampires, your job was made shitty to feed banes by an evil megacorp. the media is intentionally filling your head with shit to satisfy corperate interests, a great triatic evil, and a mage's paradigm. In the world of darkness, we're regressive, not progressive, and those guys that whine about 'the current generation' might as well be right.<br /> <b>It's really, really fucking weird when you make exceptions to this.</b> There was a portion of the book of the wyrm that explained Magadon pharmaceuticals and their evil branches, then had a bit about woman's health and how the 'feminist' research lead wasn't knowingly working for wyrm corp. Like what the fuck is anyone supposed to take away from that? Are we trying to say contraceptives, birth control and feminists are evil? Are we trying to say that an evil megacorp is being turned around by feminists? Why is something without a sinister secret agenda put in between &quot;miracle cures that're addictive make you sicker&quot; and &quot;abominable attempts at making new changing breeds &quot;. Are you not aware of how toxic such an anecdote is in a piece that otherwise works towards a literary theme?<br /> It's backwards, but if you put in stuff like &quot;Go transsexualism, get empowered&quot; amongst a setting of utter corruption and shit, well, you're kinda putting that empowering stuff in the pile of things you're finding abominable. You don't put good things in a setting about problems. Maybe people will confuse your meaning think you're trying to say that transexual empowerment is a problem just like fracking and warmongering. Black Furies excluding men was never supposed to be a good thing, it's like Talons being kill-humans or the Get being elitist, or the silver fangs relying on klaives,pure breed and ancestors to get them through a conversation. Having transgender black furies would need to open up the doors for all manner of other changes in context: like the Fianna could stop drinking themselves into depression or the bone gnawers could start catering for the lower-middle class.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I've already mentioned, I believe the proper path is to allow them to play those characters and make sure the threats they face are realistic without being insurmountable. The World of Darkness is dark, sure, but you have your pack, that's what they're there for. You have your sept if not your tribe, and while acceptance may not be a given, it should certainly be something you can work toward. I'm not sure how you think the WoD has no place for empowerment when everyone is literally playing superhuman monsters with complex personal struggles. Basically every splat just reinforces how meaningless normal humans are before you (unless you mess up, and they work together).<br /> <br /> Werewolf is a game about desperation, sure, but no one is going to read a book, watch a program, or play in a game where the entire scenario is utterly oppressive. The reason people play Werewolf is because there is hope, however dim. It's the same hope that exists at the end of Ragnarok (and if you actually read the sagas describe Ragnarok, that's a dark and terrifying future prospect).<br /> <br /> And it's that same hopeful conclusion to Ragnarok that is borrowed by the end of the Apocalypse End Times novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T13:44:18-07:00","id":980413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980399#post980399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Here's a thing, how can WoD reflect our world, if it is not allowed to? Stuff -needs- to progress, in order to match what our world is like today. Otherwise, it is stuck in 80s-90s and those decades do not reflect our world anymore, in pop culture or in general culture.<br /> <br /> As for the tribal examples you gave, all of those things have all ready happened in canon. There are Fianna who don't drink, Alberch earned the trust of his people outside klaives and purebreed, there are Red Talons who don't eat humans,etc. I understand that is how you see the setting, but in terms of the discussion, it does not reflect what has been written of the tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're forgetting that he refuses to read the Tribe Novels, because the writers are 'inconsistent'. He's not going to be aware of any of that. x:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T14:58:55-07:00","id":980437,"title":"","content":"Garou don't progress at the same rate as human society. Their principle weapon is thousands of years old and hasn't evolved (outside of glass walkers) while humanity built better and better weapons. Don't assume they'll be progressive because society is. Society isn't. Donald Trump is popular as part of a backlash against the PC crowd, and although <i>western society</i> is good to gays, trans people aren't in a great spot, especially outside the west. world of darkness more progressive than the real world is a no-no.<br /> And Solana, could you adress the argument there rather than make some poultry attack at credibility? I mean it's something you don't seem to understand, and i'm sorry that it's gone over your head, but please don't drag discussion down to that level. It's very simple: The black furies are criticised for being man-hating group, and if they stopped prioritising/excluding half the population, they'd possibly be a perfect tribe. Black furies are all too often the disagreeable and radical 'feminazi' stereotype you hear about. Now, under the logic that all tribes can be sumrised by flaws; if the black furies started to accept trans characters, then they'd suddenly be lumped in with the PC-to-the-Extreme I-Hate-Cis-White-Males kind of crowd. (which is also a weird departure to the literally binary view of Furys up till now)<br /> You do not want to transform black furies into a pro transgender group(Thematically, I think logistics has already been discussed well enough) unless you want to mock transgender activist, because as soon as you make the gender-disphoric guy into a Black Fury and send him in to kill the guy who wants to keep differently sexed bathrooms and have him murder a Silver fang for not using the right gender pronouns, you've made black furies into a parody. The black furies are criticised for focusing almost exclusively on 50% of the population: That one guy who focuses on less than 5%, rather than issues that effect a wider population, is going to be seen as worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 10-02-2016, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:02:52-07:00","id":980458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very simple: The black furies are criticised for being man-hating group, and if they stopped prioritising/excluding half the population, they'd possibly be a perfect tribe. Black furies are all too often the disagreeable and radical 'feminazi' stereotype you hear about. Now, under the logic that all tribes can be sumrised by flaws; if the black furies started to accept trans characters, then they'd suddenly be lumped in with the PC-to-the-Extreme I-Hate-Cis-White-Males kind of crowd. (which is also a weird departure to the literally binary view of Furys up till now)</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing, some Furies would go for that. But not all. The tribe, as written, has young upstarts and older traditionalists clashing. And these are the exact issues they argue about, because the tribe's goal is to protect women and the sacredness of it. But good luck trying to figure out -what- a woman is and what they are not, and that is where Furies end up infrighting.<br /> <br /> Another thing is, that Furies are a global tribe. Just because western society doesn't really have a place for transpeople, doesn't mean others are the same. The idea of a middle gender or a contrary is present in some.<br /> <br /> Infact, The Book of Auspices Theurge chapter outright states that some theurges seek to change their gender, because such an act can bring spiritual power to them to challenge the laws of nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not want to transform black furies into a pro transgender group(Thematically, I think logistics has already been discussed well enough) unless you want to mock transgender activist, because as soon as you make the gender-disphoric guy into a Black Fury and send him in to kill the guy who wants to keep differently sexed bathrooms and have him murder a Silver fang for not using the right gender pronouns, you've made black furies into a parody. The black furies are criticised for focusing almost exclusively on 50% of the population: That one guy who focuses on less than 5%, rather than issues that effect a wider population, is going to be seen as worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you know what would happen to that Fury? They would get punished severly and laughed at by the sept. Just because they were accepted, does not mean the Nation suddenly becomes a better place. Any intersex metis would feel annoyed at them, too. After all, the metis is hated for the same thing the Fury is supposed to be accepted with.<br /> <br /> Accepting trans people into Furies will not change the entire tribe, instead it can serve as a way to explore the whole idea of where the line of acceptance goes with each garou. Beatings and Elders misgendering would still ensue, but also rifts between different tribal factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:10:56-07:00","id":980462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and although <i>western society</i> is good to gays, trans people aren't in a great spot, especially outside the west. world of darkness more progressive than the real world is a no-no.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you think western society is &quot;good&quot; to the LQBT community says a lot for where you're coming from in this discussion. And the idea that the WoD has to be less progressive than the real world on every issue is just silly. You can have progression along with the world still going to shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean it's something you don't seem to understand, and i'm sorry that it's gone over your head, but please don't drag discussion down to that level.</div> </div> </div> </div>So 2 things. Being condescending never helps dialog. And &quot;drag discussion down to that level.&quot;? I feel like this thread has had one of the best conversations I've seen on here, especially dealing with such a sensitive subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's very simple: The black furies are criticised for being man-hating group, and if they stopped prioritising/excluding half the population, they'd possibly be a perfect tribe. Black furies are all too often the disagreeable and radical 'feminazi' stereotype you hear about.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is your point of view on them. I have never actually viewed the Black Furies this way. They aren't a &quot;man-hating group&quot;, though they almost certainly have members of the tribe that fit that description. Female empowerment does not equal man-hating. You do know that right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You do not want to transform black furies into a pro transgender group (Thematically, I think logistics has already been discussed well enough) unless you want to mock transgender activist, because as soon as you make the gender-disphoric guy into a Black Fury and send him in to kill the guy who wants to keep differently sexed bathrooms and have him murder a Silver fang for not using the right gender pronouns, you've made black furies into a parody.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who really thinks that is the conclusion to having the Furies accept a transgender member? That is so far beyond reasonable to me, that I don't really understand how you view Werewolf in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The black furies are criticised for focusing almost exclusively on 50% of the population: That one guy who focuses on less than 5%, rather than issues that effect a wider population, is going to be seen as worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being trans doesn't mean that the character is only going to focus on trans issues. It would be 1 aspect of the character, not the entirety of it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:22:21-07:00","id":980464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Text Wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the love of god please start using paragraphs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou don't progress at the same rate as human society. Their principle weapon is thousands of years old and hasn't evolved (outside of glass walkers).</div> </div> </div> </div>The second sentence isn't even coherent and has no context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't assume they'll be progressive because society is. Society isn't. Donald Trump is popular as part of a backlash against the PC crowd, and although <i>western society</i> is good to gays, trans people aren't in a great spot, especially outside the west. world of darkness more progressive than the real world is a no-no.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a few things - first of all don't assume that Donald Trump is good evidence for your argument - the guy is struggling to match/beat the least liked and most generally considered untrustworthy candidate in history. That does not speak well for him. Second, we're not talking about the World of Darkness, period. We're not talking about the Garou Nation, period. We're talking about a Tribe in the Garou Nation that is - at once - incredibly progressive and conservative. You seem to think Conservative means prejudiced against all the things you are prejudiced against, it doesn't. It means holding to old ideas. The Black Furies are conservative because their rites and procedures date back alllll the way to Ancient Greece. They are not based in conservative American values, they have no value for those as repeatedly stated in the Tribebook. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Solana, could you adress the argument there rather than make some poultry attack at credibility?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're really going to accuse me of an Ad Hominem attack after pages and pages of quoting every single &quot;paragraph&quot; you write with a reasoned response? That was a barb, and was directed at someone else as a joke, I wasn't even talking to you as a way of invalidating your argument. And, for the record, refusing to read those books is a relevant detail: it's evidence that you really have no idea what the person was talking about. So in this case, the Ad Hominem attack is valid because it's relevant to the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/SpgBkpb7xlU?t=447\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/SpgBkpb7xlU?t=447\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/SpgBkpb7xlU?t=447\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/SpgBkpb7xlU?t=447 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it's something you don't seem to understand, and i'm sorry that it's gone over your head, but please don't drag discussion down to that level. It's very simple:</div> </div> </div> </div>How has it gone over my head? On more than one occasion in this thread I've asked people not to insult others for the sake of insulting them. The joke I made is valid because your refusal to read the tribe novels means you won't know what they're even talking about. It's also relevant because you're arguing that your view is the correct one when by definition is <b>an incomplete view.</b><br /> <br /> I'm terribly sorry that this detail has gone over your head, but it's a very simple and crucial fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The black furies are criticised for being man-hating group, and if they stopped prioritising/excluding half the population, they'd possibly be a perfect tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you read the Tribe<b>book</b> you'd know that this is a stereotype they've fought for a long time to distance themselves from. They get female members constantly from other tribes believing these stereotypes, swaggering around the sept out to prove they're better than all the men, but that's not what being a Black Fury is about. Does that mean there is going to be some resistance in the tribe? Sure, but that's not your argument, your argument is that the entire Garou Nation <b>(nay, the world!)</b> will reject them, because it's the WoD and progressive things just don't happen.Werewolves don't discriminate based on sex except in fringe cases which are noteworthy only because of how rare they are. Werewolves will not judge your rank based on the color of your skin. They do care about Pure Breed, but this is an alien system that is not relatable to the racism you pointed out in America at this time. Werewolves are not conservative in the way you think they are. And they have much less cause to hate a group that many societies regarded as a natural part of life until Judeo-Christian religions got involved. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black furies are all too often the disagreeable and radical 'feminazi' stereotype you hear about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they're not, unless you think current feminists are all feminazis. If you read the Tribebook or the Tribenovel, you'd know that. Many of them are embittered toward men, because a lot of women suffer a lot of abuse at the hands of men, a lot of the times they end up protecting the helpless, a man is the aggressor, which lends itself to the same confirmation bias you might see in the police. Calling the police nazis because of confirmation bias is an extreme stretch. It's a bitterness I can relate to, because I suffered a lot of abuse from my father and brothers growing up, especially when I came out. That doesn't make me a nazi, and I don't 'hate all men' and want to kill them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, under the logic that all tribes can be sumrised by flaws; if the black furies started to accept trans characters, then they'd suddenly be lumped in with the PC-to-the-Extreme I-Hate-Cis-White-Males kind of crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean 'Summarized' or 'Surmised'? This is actually an important fucking distinction. You also misused that semi-colon. Look, I'm being a grammar and spelling <b>nazi</b>! Throwing nazi around lends credibility to our argument!<br /> <br /> That aside, what? I'll assume you meant summarized by their flaws, because that makes more grammatical sense than: &quot;Surmised by their flaws.&quot; <br /> <br /> How the hell do you reach that conclusion? Who's going to assume that? The rest of the Garou Nation which knows nothing about them because their sacred lands are secret as are their ancient rituals? What bearing does that have on the discussion at all? Are the Black Furies going to not do something because the others might think poorly of them? That would be the least Black Fury thing ever, and their tribal totem would <b>shun</b> the hell out of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not want to transform black furies into a pro transgender group(Thematically, I think logistics has already been discussed well enough) unless you want to mock transgender activist, because as soon as you make the gender-disphoric guy into a Black Fury and send him in to kill the guy who wants to keep differently sexed bathrooms and have him murder a Silver fang for not using the right gender pronouns, you've made black furies into a parody.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly I doubt you know the first thing about transgender activism, since you keep strawmaning them in this thread. Second, the Black Furies don't go around killing every person who upsets them. They solve the problem so that it goes away, they give the person they are helping the strength to fight back on their own. A Black Fury is not going to murder someone who has a view point but no influence on the system. She's not going to kill a politician with that kind of power until he proves that he is utterly irrevocably against human rights. A Black Fury might challenge someone to a duel over pronoun use (the actual Norse people did this all the time), but to argue that she will <b>kill</b> him is just drawing on your same strawman. <br /> <br /> You know who a Black Fury would kill? Some guy who rapes and then burns a transgender woman, before getting out of jail in three years off of manslaughter charges, because they just lost control of themselves once they learned that woman was trans. I invite you to look up Trans Panic as a legal defense. There are plenty of actual violent things the Black Furies could oppose that aren't petty murder over people with different ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980437#post980437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The black furies are criticised for focusing almost exclusively on 50% of the population: That one guy who focuses on less than 5%, rather than issues that effect a wider population, is going to be seen as worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>51%, if you want to go so far as to use specific numbers. <br /> <br /> And it's not like someone can champion multiple causes at one time, right? I mean it's not like Black Furies already do that by championing Gaia, and the environment, and children, and women, and homosexuals -<br /> <br /> Wait. Oh my god.<br /> <br /> They absolutely do! And it doesn't negatively impact them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:07:56-07:00","id":980543,"title":"","content":"I really don't get people who think Werewolf, of all the lines, should be one where there is no hope and everything at all times must be shit and dark. The entire point of the game is fighting to make a better world in a way that you can't really ignore or sidestep like you can in say, Mage, and without the tone of 'try and make it better, but you probably won't and you'll definitely die painful and alone' like Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:57:23-07:00","id":980614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980543#post980543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't get people who think Werewolf, of all the lines, should be one where there is no hope and everything at all times must be shit and dark. The entire point of the game is fighting to make a better world in a way that you can't really ignore or sidestep like you can in say, Mage, and without the tone of 'try and make it better, but you probably won't and you'll definitely die painful and alone' like Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf is kind of the game that has as many intrepentations as there are players. Not to mention, when the person started reading in the edition cycle matters a lot. If you started with 1st ed, then that is how you see a lot of things in the game by.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:23:10-07:00","id":980625,"title":"","content":"Even in first edition, a major component of the game was 'the world is shit. Try and make it less shit.' Like, that's the <i>core struggle</i> of the entire game, and has been since day one. The world is dying. Stand and fight and scream defiance into the dark to try and save it. Let me quote the 1st Ed core here.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Wyrm resides within them, just as it is found across Gaia; indeed, many of the Garou themselves have given up the struggle to join the enemy in treacherous alliance... The characters in Werewolf are expected to be heroes - they must care about what they have become and what they may soon be... They must defeat the monster within.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the <i>very first book</i>, the game has been about standing up, screaming that defiance, and fighting for a better world. The elements of the Garou nation that don't were traitors from the get-go, fallen fools in service wittingly or otherwise to the Enemy. You aren't meant to sit and go 'well it's all fucked so why bother'. You're meant to struggle against it and try and make it less fucked, if only by a single act of kindness or a single enemy killed at a time. Any interpretation of the game that rejects this as the core struggle (into which the personal struggle of balancing garou obligation with personal want, and the personal struggle with the Rage wyrm-seed burning in the breast) is a misinterpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T04:13:42-07:00","id":980696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980625#post980625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in first edition, a major component of the game was 'the world is shit. Try and make it less shit.' Like, that's the <i>core struggle</i> of the entire game, and has been since day one. The world is dying. Stand and fight and scream defiance into the dark to try and save it. Let me quote the 1st Ed core here.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Wyrm resides within them, just as it is found across Gaia; indeed, many of the Garou themselves have given up the struggle to join the enemy in treacherous alliance... The characters in Werewolf are expected to be heroes - they must care about what they have become and what they may soon be... They must defeat the monster within.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the <i>very first book</i>, the game has been about standing up, screaming that defiance, and fighting for a better world. The elements of the Garou nation that don't were traitors from the get-go, fallen fools in service wittingly or otherwise to the Enemy. You aren't meant to sit and go 'well it's all fucked so why bother'. You're meant to struggle against it and try and make it less fucked, if only by a single act of kindness or a single enemy killed at a time. Any interpretation of the game that rejects this as the core struggle (into which the personal struggle of balancing garou obligation with personal want, and the personal struggle with the Rage wyrm-seed burning in the breast) is a misinterpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>(empahsis mine)<br /> <br /> Well, that is good to hear about the 1st ed.<br /> <br /> Though, I think the issue we are discussing here isn't as much about the PCs as it is about the rest of the Nation and how they act. Let me look at what 1st, 2nd, Larp and GURPS say about the Furies and the issues brought up here, so we can get a clearer view on the canon involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b> Werewolf the Apocalypse 1st edition, p.110</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Black Furies are composed almost entirely of female garou, though there are a few male metis members of the tribe, resulting from from a Fury's illict mating with a Garou of another tribe. Other than these metis, they give away any male child to other tribes. </i><br /> <br /> <b>GURPS</b><br /> -Same as the 1st. ed-<br /> <br /> <b>Apocalypse (as far as I know the earliest LARP book), p.44</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>The Black Furies exist as a counterpoint to somewhat male-dominated garou society.<br /> --<br /> They believe that their Goddess, Artemis (luna in another guise), wants them to remain apart from men. The only men in their tribe are those of the infertile metis breed.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf Players Guide, p.49</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Black Furies do not allow male homid or lupus to serve in their tribe. However, they no longer euthanize male children. They usually send any male Garou to the Children of Gaia.<br /> --<br /> Male metis are allowed to stay with the tribe, thoigh they can never advance far within the tribal structure and are usually relegated to a support position. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf the Apocalypse 2nd. ed, p.92</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Furies claim that Luna, in her aspect as Artemis the Huntress, created their tribe of she-wolves and appointed them to be protectors of the Wyld, defenders of women, and punishers of men. They uphold these duties with grim determination.<br /> <br /> Other tribes look askance at the Furies, who give away or kill their male children. Many outside the tribe see the Furies as man-haters, but the truth is more complex. Although the tribe tolerates male metis, the Furies have a definite gender bias; they believe that women share a deeper bond with Gaia than any man can know, and see themselves as aspects of the Goddess incarnate. In her name, they Rage against any insult to women, nature or the Goddess. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf the Dark Ages, p.62- 64</b><br /> <br /> <i>Although some Furies prefer to gently influence their mortal wards, often spreading the gospel of the Virgin Mary, a growing number believe that the only way to keep the Patriarch's grasping talons away is bloodshed.<br /> --<br /> Determined to maintain the all-female tribal membership, the Furies have traditionally killed any male children<br /> born to them (although male children born to Kin were<br /> allowed to survive). Now an argument divides the Furies, as<br /> some of their number denounce the practice as wasteful,<br /> foolish and cruel. This growing minority allow their male<br /> children to live, so that they may one day be able to pass on<br /> the blood of the Furies to their daughters. The Furies intend<br /> to carefully watch these male children and their descendants. Elders of both the Children of Gaia and the Silent<br /> <br /> Striders have agreed to take in any of the male cubs who<br /> show signs of undergoing the Change.<br /> One of the few exceptions to this law is that of the<br /> metis. From time to time, a Fury breaks the first tenet ofthe<br /> Litany and births a male metis cub. Althought some elders<br /> charge that a deformed body must house a deformed spirit,<br /> the Furies as often as not decide that punishing a child for a<br /> mother's sin is poor precedent. Once in while, line<br /> blurs even further, and male cubs that ordinally have<br /> been killed are allowed to survive. The reasoning varies from<br /> situation to situation (and, after all, it happens very<br /> rarely), but usually it's decided t ma e metis, raised at<br /> the sept by necessity, has a tter c ance of growing up<br /> receptive to the Mother. No Black Fury sept has ever lost a<br /> metis to the Patriarch...<br /> --<br /> The Black Furies believe that breeding is a sacred duty<br /> and gift, and carefully choose the fathers of their children.<br /> Some among the more extreme Furies breed only with<br /> wolves, thus avoiding contact with narrow-minded human<br /> men. Others carefully maintain small dynasties of Kinfolk,<br /> to improve the chance of their children being Garou.There<br /> is a small minority of Black Furies who look for a truly loving<br /> relationship, but most Furies feel that their role is as a</i><br /> warrior, not a wife.<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Ages: Werewolf, p.56</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>The Black Furies are fierce defenders of the Wyld and vengeful protectors of women everywhere.<br /> --<br /> According to other legends, Gaia herself formed the Furies. They are all female so that each one might know the value of the lives she bears.<br /> --<br /> The Furies protect women wherever they are victimized. They take female cubs from other tribes, ones who have been mistreated by their brothers and fathers. They sometimes allow human women who have escaped desperate lives to live with Fury kinfolk. They have little respect, however, for women who refuse to take the freedom that is offered to them. While their totem, Pegasus, requires her followers to aid helpless women wherever they can be found, even pegasus has no desire to help those who will not help themselves.<br /> The Most inviolate law of the Black Furies is that of the tribe's gender. Throught history, many Black Furies have ceremonially sacrificed male children in order to preserve the tribe as it is. A growing number of Furies, however, argue that this practise is wasteful and foolish. </i><br /> <br /> Okay, so what I gather from all of these core snippets, is that pretty much only the 2nd ed really pushes the man-hating feminazi stereotype. The 1st ed actually focuses much more on the mysticism of the Furies than their gender bias and in fact does not even mention killing male cubs at all.<br /> <br /> Generally, though, all texts are very clear on that the tribe is split over the matter and aren't all man hating.<br /> <br /> If anyone wants me to, I can go through the first tribebook to see what opinions are found there.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:01:26-07:00","id":980717,"title":"","content":"A few pro trans writters have had their say in some of the later books. <br /> It always sticks out like a sore thumb. <br /> <br /> What the world of darkness emphasized in the 90's <br /> Apathy<br /> Hate<br /> Sexism<br /> Racism<br /> domestic violence<br /> Sex offences<br /> Drug use<br /> Organised crime<br /> Wealth dichotomy <br /> Islamophobia<br /> nihlism<br /> Consumerism <br /> Pollution<br /> Corporate greed<br /> Corperate malpractice<br /> Unsafe consumable products<br /> Police Corruption and brutality<br /> The machines taking over<br /> The decline of faith, belief and spirituality<br /> Faith being misused <br /> Satanism<br /> neocolonialism <br /> Hostile Buyouts <br /> Theft, or the practice of violently wrecking somone's shit and claiming it as your own, as seen in Diablorie, Nodes, Caerns<br /> <br /> I think it's clear that they were trying to make a consistent statement here. Everything they focused on was bad. I'm sorry, I'm a university literature student, even trying to be objective says it's clear that this was deliberate. It makes you more aware of issues. <br /> <br /> What the world of darkness has emphasized more recently<br /> Apathy<br /> Hate<br /> domestic violence<br /> Sex offences<br /> Drug use<br /> Organised crime<br /> Wealth dichotomy <br /> nihilism<br /> Pro-Islam tolerance<br /> strong Independent women<br /> Transgenderism <br /> Consumerism <br /> Pollution<br /> Corporate greed<br /> Corperate malpractice<br /> Unsafe consumable products<br /> Police Corruption and brutality<br /> The decline of faith, belief and spirituality<br /> Faith being misused <br /> neocolonialism <br /> Hostile Buyouts <br /> Theft, or the practice of violently wrecking somone's shit and claiming it as your own, as seen in Diablorie, Nodes, Caerns<br /> <br /> Do you understand how fucking weird it is? Here you've got a shitlist, and one of the writers, willfully ignorant of the pattern (and often logistical problems), decides to put loved ones on the firing range with all the targets? It's confusing, because if you're entirely neutral, you'll end up thinking &quot;Is there something terribly wrong with strong independent women?&quot; Even if you're not been poisoned by literature or media studies, you'll still take it in unconsciously like that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:22:27-07:00","id":980729,"title":"","content":"First, I object to your description of being 'poisoned by literature or media studies'.<br /> <br /> Second, you are confusing the subjects. It is not in debate that the World of Darkness has evolved. What is in debate is how Black Furies view transgender persons, and over the last few posts, the nature of the setting (specific to Werewolf) as not being purely about 'the world sucks, suck it up' but about 'the world sucks, fight back'. That being the goal, the presence of strong female characters, transgendered characters, and characters of diverse cultural, racial, and religious backgrounds in the setting does not set them up as a target on the firing line - it sets them up as precious icons of hope and strength in a complicated and often dark world. Do you think that including anything in the setting 'puts it on the firing range'?<br /> <br /> Third, the World of Darkness setting still makes points about misogyny, sexism, racism and islamophobia. Part of how it does that now is by including contrasting viewpoints and characters who are strong women (and their allies), muslims, etc. You treat it as having been done away with - the reality is it still present, but now subject to a more nuanced position and critique than 'look at these things we say are bad, but are also inadvertantly including in our work'. The inclusion of transgendered characters ties in with this and by the general purpose of heightening awareness of and critiquing real issues.<br /> <br /> Tell me, do you think the setting did not contain a message of tolerance for those of other racial and religious backgrounds in its earlier incarnations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:42:20-07:00","id":980738,"title":"","content":"The black furies are supposed to represent radical nazi feminists just as they represent bastions of female empowerment. But the Black Furies do it a step further than other tribes. A female garou is equal to any other male in any other tribe, Black furies are Ironically, the most problematically sexist tribe. (yes, that includes the Get. They'll give you a hard time, but will ultimately respect you more for for going through it. Furies ban nearly half the pop) If we include Trans people into the Furies, then just as much as we're empowering trans people, we'll be putting them on a pedastool and then have it corrupted by those angry SJWs who hate on anyone who doesn't like safe spaces or use correct pronouns . Do you really want that? Because that's what you're asking for.<br /> I am totally fine with that if you ignore my other problems, but the problem is here is that nobody's going to write this in as a consistent thing that keeps in context with the world of darkness, because the people who really want this are often those angry SJWs who aren't going to treat trans people and their strongest supporters as anything other than paragons. The world doesn't work like that and neither does the world of darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 10-03-2016, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:52:05-07:00","id":980744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980738#post980738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The black furies are supposed to represent radical nazi feminists just as they represent bastions of female empowerment. But the Black Furies do it a step further than other tribes. A female garou is equal to any other male in any other tribe, Black furies are Ironically, the most problematically sexist tribe. (yes, that includes the Get. They'll give you a hard time, but will ultimately respect you more for for going through it. Furies ban nearly half the pop) If we include Trans people into the Furies, then just as much as we're empowering trans people, we'll be putting them on a pedastool and then have it corrupted by those angry SJWs who hate on anyone who doesn't like safe spaces or use correct pronouns . Do you really want that? Because that's what you're asking for.<br /> <br /> I am totally fine with that if you ignore my other problems, but the problem is here is that nobody's going to write this in as a consistent thing that keeps in context with the world of darkness, because the people who really want this are often those angry SJWs who aren't going to treat trans people and their strongest supporters as anything other than paragons. The world doesn't work like that and neither does the world of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 'radical nazi feminist' reading of the Black Furies is a possible one, and there is a faction within them that is emblematic of extreme seperatist feminists. That does not make them the be all and end all of the tribe, just as the presence of radical and seperatist feminists does not make feminism as a movement nothing but radical seperatists.<br /> <br /> Including transwomen in the women tribe is not putting them on a pedestal. It is instead putting them on even footing with ciswomen. If I were to say that the leadership of the Furies or their greatest heroes should be made into transwomen, I would be putting them on a pedestal.<br /> <br /> I want it. Does that make me an angry SJW? Do I strike you as not recognizing that transpeople can be just as deeply flawed as anyone else, because they are just the same as anyone else?<br /> <br /> Further, why should we permit concern over 'angry SJWs who hate on anyone who doesn't like safe spaces or use correct pronouns' (a nebulous group and a pretty basic strawman at that) to prevent a logical exploration of transpeople's place in the Black Furies and a more inclusive atmosphere for transgender gamers?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:08:11-07:00","id":980754,"title":"","content":"Because that's the current patern of things. Read the DAV20 section on Ahrimanes. You have to read between the lines on what's wrong with them, because otherwise they're a too-perfect bunch of mary sues. Not everyone reads between the lines. It's not universal, there are examples of Trans people portrayed as people rather than idols (A certain Tzmisce comes to mind) but it happens all too often that a writer has an agenda to portray LGBT ludicrously positive while everyone else gets a realistic portrayal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 10-03-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:13:31-07:00","id":980757,"title":"","content":"I recall us debating about the Ahrimanes. You didn't convince me of the issue then, and I remain unconvinced. Can you point to more evidence of the claimed pattern?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:17:56-07:00","id":980760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980614#post980614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf is kind of the game that has as many intrepentations as there are players. Not to mention, when the person started reading in the edition cycle matters a lot. If you started with 1st ed, then that is how you see a lot of things in the game by.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. It may have something to do with the Rokea and Mokole changing rather substantially between presentation in editions, though, since those Fera brought me into this game. So now, when I see someone opining for the &quot;old days&quot;, I just think that they don't like doing proper research, or accepting it, because a lot of those early books had considerable flaws that, in modern times, could have been remedied with a brief internet search.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:23:28-07:00","id":980762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980754#post980754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's the current patern of things. Read the DAV20 section on Ahrimanes. You have to read between the lines on what's wrong with them, because otherwise they're a too-perfect bunch of mary sues. Not everyone reads between the lines. It's not universal, there are examples of Trans people portrayed as people rather than idols (A certain Tzmisce comes to mind) but it happens all too often that a writer has an agenda to portray LGBT ludicrously positive while everyone else gets a realistic portrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because of the massive cultural weight of people seeing &quot;trans&quot; anything other than fats and thinking of Dr. Frank N. Furter or some other, similar presentation. It takes a lot of work to undo that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-03-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:54:34-07:00","id":980839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980757#post980757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall us debating about the Ahrimanes. You didn't convince me of the issue then, and I remain unconvinced. Can you point to more evidence of the claimed pattern?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I wouldn't convince you of the issue then. You and I go into these arguments for entirely different purposes. You go in to defend your point of view, I try to inform others and inform myself through the clash of ideas. I literally changed my outlook from that whole Ahrimane debacle, from &quot;they don't fit, and are there for wish fullfillment&quot; to &quot;they were designed not to fit, to be an example of an anachronistic, radical, feminst crusade that will die out when the vampires get older/further move into vampiric society, the embracing men issue comes up, or they piss off the wrong prince's patriarchy. They were likely . Ahrimanes to me went from 'silly and anachronistic' To 'Doomed and interesting' very quickly, and I liked that. The problem here is that I had to debate the flaws of the ahrimanes online because they weren't immediately apparent in the book. Because, y'know, we can't have overt criticism of a gender movement (that said, I do wonder who wrote that bloodline and their agenda for it) <br /> A further point where there is difference: I present multiple arguments. I'm looking at Black furies and transgender from both thematic reasoning and a logistical one. I mean, the most likely scenario of a transgender person joining the black furies is as follows. <br /> <br /> The character petitions pegasus to join the tribe<br /> High chance of Pegasus rejecting the person (probably politely) on the basis that they have a working pair of balls. <br /> If we assume the character changed their physical body and had surgery or magic, chances are that pegasus might get outraged that a person would willingly &quot;geld&quot; themselves in that way, for to him it was done by a despised individual. Of course, there's another chance that pegasus feels honoured by this action, and a smaller chance where he even makes it a requirement to join (either through consentual surgery/rituals or a great spiritual quest to change). Anyhow. Lets assume the possible chance that pegasus gives the go ahead. <br /> -Black furies murder eachother, preferably you, over your right to be in the tribe. <br /> -You will forever be barred from any good roles/secret services because a significant portion of the tribe don't trust/like you.<br /> - You will forever have people question your right to be in the furies, from claiths to elders. <br /> - anyone who backs you will probably be in the blast radius of whatever hate you get. <br /> Honestly, you're better off in the Get of Fenrir or the shadow lords than you are in a black fury sept. Any person that really wants to be treated better for being a transexual should join the children of Gaia or the Glass Walkers. <br /> - The first guy who gets into the black furies will likely be treated so badly, probably killed, that it wont be attempted again until the <i>entire</i> tribe changes. <br /> - It massively disrupts tribal unity. The Black Furies will be weaker as a result. <br /> <br /> (of course, you may note I'm changing the subject from examples because I don't wanna re-read through loads of books to find page numbers. I can give you Ahrimanes, should you choose to accept it, the odd magadon section on Women's medicine in book of the Wyrm, mentioned earier. I could also point out to other super-progressive stuff that doesn't fit, Like DAv20's picture of a gangrel being a black woman with an early arming sword and a european-colonial era pirate outfit, symbolic of a liberty so great that it'd only make sense with <i>Temporis</i>. But actually quote harvesting, no thanks.) <br /> <br /> Transgender is totaly fine (even though i personally have reason to believe that the wolf/warrior/survival cult nature of the garou would make such a thing less pronounced)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:55:28-07:00","id":980840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980754#post980754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's the current patern of things. Read the DAV20 section on Ahrimanes. You have to read between the lines on what's wrong with them, because otherwise they're a too-perfect bunch of mary sues. Not everyone reads between the lines. It's not universal, there are examples of Trans people portrayed as people rather than idols (A certain Tzmisce comes to mind) but it happens all too often that a writer has an agenda to portray LGBT ludicrously positive while everyone else gets a realistic portrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna have to stop you right there if you're trying to convince me that Sascha &quot;rip off my penis and throw it&quot; Vykos is good or unbiased trans representation. Fuck right off with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:13:45-07:00","id":980859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980840#post980840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm gonna have to stop you right there if you're trying to convince me that Sascha &quot;rip off my penis and throw it&quot; Vykos is good or unbiased trans representation. Fuck right off with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't read too much into it, but I don't think an evil transvestite is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> We used to have this show, Little Britain. The jokes were crude, vugar, outrageously homophobic, racist and sexist. Yet one of the main characters was gay in real life, and he went super overboard to mocking stereotypes of the LGBT spectrum. It was funny at the time, but looking back on it, it's incredibly vulgar and not funny. It wasn't just mocking the gays, it was mocking the stereotypes of gays, which it exaggerates to the point of not being true. When I looked at Dr Frank .N Furter, I saw a character who made me uncomfortable, but he was also a bombastically unrealistic stereotype of transvestites and it was easy to recognize that. If Vykos throws his penis at the enemy, we're not making fun of transvestites, we're making fun of irrational fear of transvestites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:22:35-07:00","id":980866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980738#post980738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The black furies are supposed to represent radical nazi feminists just as they represent bastions of female empowerment.<br /> But the Black Furies do it a step further than other tribes. A female garou is equal to any other male in any other tribe, Black furies are Ironically, the most problematically sexist tribe. (yes, that includes the Get. They'll give you a hard time, but will ultimately respect you more for for going through it. Furies ban nearly half the pop) If we include Trans people into the Furies, then just as much as we're empowering trans people, we'll be putting them on a pedastool and then have it corrupted by those angry SJWs who hate on anyone who doesn't like safe spaces or use correct pronouns . Do you really want that? Because that's what you're asking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, from the things I quoted from the corebooks, I'd say someone got a bee in the bonnet about Furies and radicalism in 2nd ed, given how stark the difference between it an 1st ed's writing was.<br /> <br /> But no, I highly doubt that Furies including transwomen would put them on a pedestal over other tribes. This is basically Silver Fangs or Fianna allowing metis into their tribe levels of social fixing, they are women so they can join, but it is a point of contention and I doubt the transwoman would have fun times. No one here is saying that Furies will 100% embrace the concept, if anything it would be a very difficult one for many to swallow.<br /> <br /> As for the SJW point, as Ioomer said, they honestly are not the group we should be focusing on here. Aside from WtA being WAY too filled with stuff they'd dislike, Trans does not equal SJW.<br /> <br /> And besides, all of this boils to a question, if a transperson wanted to play themselves in WoD, could they?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:31:13-07:00","id":980873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980839#post980839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course I wouldn't convince you of the issue then. You and I go into these arguments for entirely different purposes. You go in to defend your point of view, I try to inform others and inform myself through the clash of ideas. I literally changed my outlook from that whole Ahrimane debacle, from &quot;they don't fit, and are there for wish fullfillment&quot; to &quot;they were designed not to fit, to be an example of an anachronistic, radical, feminst crusade that will die out when the vampires get older/further move into vampiric society, the embracing men issue comes up, or they piss off the wrong prince's patriarchy. They were likely . Ahrimanes to me went from 'silly and anachronistic' To 'Doomed and interesting' very quickly, and I liked that. The problem here is that I had to debate the flaws of the ahrimanes online because they weren't immediately apparent in the book. Because, y'know, we can't have overt criticism of a gender movement (that said, I do wonder who wrote that bloodline and their agenda for it)<br /> A further point where there is difference: I present multiple arguments. I'm looking at Black furies and transgender from both thematic reasoning and a logistical one. I mean, the most likely scenario of a transgender person joining the black furies is as follows.<br /> <br /> The character petitions pegasus to join the tribe<br /> High chance of Pegasus rejecting the person (probably politely) on the basis that they have a working pair of balls.<br /> If we assume the character changed their physical body and had surgery or magic, chances are that pegasus might get outraged that a person would willingly &quot;geld&quot; themselves in that way, for to him it was done by a despised individual. Of course, there's another chance that pegasus feels honoured by this action, and a smaller chance where he even makes it a requirement to join (either through consentual surgery/rituals or a great spiritual quest to change). Anyhow. Lets assume the possible chance that pegasus gives the go ahead.<br /> -Black furies murder eachother, preferably you, over your right to be in the tribe.<br /> -You will forever be barred from any good roles/secret services because a significant portion of the tribe don't trust/like you.<br /> - You will forever have people question your right to be in the furies, from claiths to elders.<br /> - anyone who backs you will probably be in the blast radius of whatever hate you get.<br /> Honestly, you're better off in the Get of Fenrir or the shadow lords than you are in a black fury sept. Any person that really wants to be treated better for being a transexual should join the children of Gaia or the Glass Walkers.<br /> - The first guy who gets into the black furies will likely be treated so badly, probably killed, that it wont be attempted again until the <i>entire</i> tribe changes.<br /> - It massively disrupts tribal unity. The Black Furies will be weaker as a result.<br /> <br /> (of course, you may note I'm changing the subject from examples because I don't wanna re-read through loads of books to find page numbers. I can give you Ahrimanes, should you choose to accept it, the odd magadon section on Women's medicine in book of the Wyrm, mentioned earier. I could also point out to other super-progressive stuff that doesn't fit, Like DAv20's picture of a gangrel being a black woman with an early arming sword and a european-colonial era pirate outfit, symbolic of a liberty so great that it'd only make sense with <i>Temporis</i>. But actually quote harvesting, no thanks.)<br /> <br /> Transgender is totaly fine (even though i personally have reason to believe that the wolf/warrior/survival cult nature of the garou would make such a thing less pronounced)</div> </div> </div> </div>I enter into debates because I find the subject matter interesting. It so happens that I disagreed with you over the possible origins of the all-female aspect of the bloodline, because the specific history that would lend itself to that aspect is an area of some interest to me. Do not presume to ascribe to me a motive.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk thematic and logistical reasons, the simplest reason to permit it in-universe was already given. The Wyrm feeds on despair. Encouraging despair thus encourages the Wyrm. The Black Furies oppose the Wyrm, and have a mythic basis to permit transwomen. Thus, there is both a basis for admission and an argument to be made that the only acceptable course of action is to accept transwomen, whether the TERF segment of the tribe likes it or not. There is no actual basis in their practice or myth to prohibit transwomen; there is instead basis both pragmatic and spiritual to permit them. As for out-of-universe, I don't think I need to explain why it is preferable to admit than not, but if you like I can.<br /> <br /> I also have trouble taking you seriously when, talking about transwomen, you go full into 'the first guy who gets into the black furies...' They aren't guys. They are gals. There are also already male black furies, and quite a few.<br /> <br /> I reject the argument around Magadon and around the DV:20 Gangrel picture. I have no issue with it being of a black woman, and inclusion of entirely plausible characters (yes, shockingly, there were people of colour in medieval europe!) in the art does not constitute a pattern of, and I quote, ' an agenda to portray LGBT ludicrously positive while everyone else gets a realistic portrayal.' I do object to the problems with the outfit, but that's as a history nerd. On Magadon, I fail to see how the inclusion of an unknowing dupe running the women's health division constitutes part of a pattern of, and I again quote, ' an agenda to portray LGBT ludicrously positive while everyone else gets a realistic portrayal. ' Given that it sits in a setting alongside many strong feminists who are <i>not</i> fooled by Pentex, it also cannot be said to be an attempt to represent all feminism as naive, blinkered, etc, if you were intending on advancing that argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:52:26-07:00","id":980883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980859#post980859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't read too much into it, but I don't think an evil transvestite is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> We used to have this show, Little Britain. The jokes were crude, vugar, outrageously homophobic, racist and sexist. Yet one of the main characters was gay in real life, and he went super overboard to mocking stereotypes of the LGBT spectrum. It was funny at the time, but looking back on it, it's incredibly vulgar and not funny. It wasn't just mocking the gays, it was mocking the stereotypes of gays, which it exaggerates to the point of not being true. When I looked at Dr Frank .N Furter, I saw a character who made me uncomfortable, but he was also a bombastically unrealistic stereotype of transvestites and it was easy to recognize that. If Vykos throws his penis at the enemy, we're not making fun of transvestites, we're making fun of irrational fear of transvestites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've gotten into enough fights with people whose only contact with anyone who doesn't conform to common notions of gender is that particular inhuman flesh monster. Folks can't realize parody if they don't know what's being parodied, to say nothing of whether or not those things (in this case, people like me and those I love) need to be parodied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:53:42-07:00","id":980886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980873#post980873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I enter into debates because I find the subject matter interesting. It so happens that I disagreed with you over the possible origins of the all-female aspect of the bloodline, because the specific history that would lend itself to that aspect is an area of some interest to me. Do not presume to ascribe to me a motive.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk thematic and logistical reasons, the simplest reason to permit it in-universe was already given. The Wyrm feeds on despair. Encouraging despair thus encourages the Wyrm. The Black Furies oppose the Wyrm, and have a mythic basis to permit transwomen. Thus, there is both a basis for admission and an argument to be made that the only acceptable course of action is to accept transwomen, whether the TERF segment of the tribe likes it or not. There is no actual basis in their practice or myth to prohibit transwomen; there is instead basis both pragmatic and spiritual to permit them. As for out-of-universe, I don't think I need to explain why it is preferable to admit than not, but if you like I can.<br /> <br /> I also have trouble taking you seriously when, talking about transwomen, you go full into 'the first guy who gets into the black furies...' They aren't guys. They are gals. There are also already male black furies, and quite a few.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wish I could like this twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:31:05-07:00","id":980906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980717#post980717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few pro trans writters have had their say in some of the later books.<br /> It always sticks out like a sore thumb.<br /> <br /> What the world of darkness emphasized in the 90's<br /> Apathy<br /> Hate<br /> Sexism<br /> Racism<br /> domestic violence<br /> Sex offences<br /> Drug use<br /> Organised crime<br /> Wealth dichotomy<br /> Islamophobia<br /> nihlism<br /> Consumerism<br /> Pollution<br /> Corporate greed<br /> Corperate malpractice<br /> Unsafe consumable products<br /> Police Corruption and brutality<br /> The machines taking over<br /> The decline of faith, belief and spirituality<br /> Faith being misused<br /> Satanism<br /> neocolonialism<br /> Hostile Buyouts<br /> Theft, or the practice of violently wrecking somone's shit and claiming it as your own, as seen in Diablorie, Nodes, Caerns<br /> <br /> I think it's clear that they were trying to make a consistent statement here. Everything they focused on was bad. I'm sorry, I'm a university literature student, even trying to be objective says it's clear that this was deliberate. It makes you more aware of issues.<br /> <br /> What the world of darkness has emphasized more recently<br /> Apathy<br /> Hate<br /> domestic violence<br /> Sex offences<br /> Drug use<br /> Organised crime<br /> Wealth dichotomy<br /> nihilism<br /> Pro-Islam tolerance<br /> strong Independent women<br /> Transgenderism<br /> Consumerism<br /> Pollution<br /> Corporate greed<br /> Corperate malpractice<br /> Unsafe consumable products<br /> Police Corruption and brutality<br /> The decline of faith, belief and spirituality<br /> Faith being misused<br /> neocolonialism<br /> Hostile Buyouts<br /> Theft, or the practice of violently wrecking somone's shit and claiming it as your own, as seen in Diablorie, Nodes, Caerns</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I refuse to accept that you are a university literature student until presented with evidence. If you are you're a very terrible one.<br /> <br /> Also it wasn't just transgender writers, there are plenty of cismale and cisfemale writers that pushed transgender issues forward as well. They're all over the place in the CoD. I know they exist because I know them personally.<br /> <br /> Also the phenomena that is transgender people is not an 'ism'. See, subtly tossing out that you're a literature student so &quot;I know my stuff here&quot; is a) an argument from authority and b) leaves us incredulous, because you routinely don't use paragraphs, formatting, you misspell more words than anyone else in this discussion, and your grammar is almost always wrong. These are all things we would expect a student of literature to have mastered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980717#post980717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you understand how fucking weird it is? Here you've got a shitlist, and one of the writers, willfully ignorant of the pattern (and often logistical problems), decides to put loved ones on the firing range with all the targets? It's confusing, because if you're entirely neutral, you'll end up thinking &quot;Is there something terribly wrong with strong independent women?&quot; Even if you're not been poisoned by literature or media studies, you'll still take it in unconsciously like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What 'pattern'? The one you've created in your head? What do you mean by 'throwing loved ones on the firing range'? At no point has the World of Darkness ever suggested that strong independent women are inherently antagonistic in some way, and the group you're specifically blaming it on would never write that.<br /> <br /> Poisoned by Literature or Media studies, huh? I thought you were a student of Literature at university? You may not understand this, but that's akin to saying you major <b>in literature</b>. In the same way that telling someone you're studying to become a doctor of medicine is a declaration of specialty. So, what? You've made it your life's ambition to constantly poison yourself, or just read all the literature that's being produced and cry wolf as progressive values slowly seep into modern culture because progressivism over time pretty much always wins out?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I'm missing what you're saying here, because if I'm not, then your mind is a hive of non sequitors and that's just truly frightening to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-03-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:35:23-07:00","id":980908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980738#post980738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The black furies are supposed to represent radical nazi feminists just as they represent bastions of female empowerment. But the Black Furies do it a step further than other tribes. A female garou is equal to any other male in any other tribe, Black furies are Ironically, the most problematically sexist tribe. (yes, that includes the Get. They'll give you a hard time, but will ultimately respect you more for for going through it. Furies ban nearly half the pop) If we include Trans people into the Furies, then just as much as we're empowering trans people, we'll be putting them on a pedastool and then have it corrupted by those angry SJWs who hate on anyone who doesn't like safe spaces or use correct pronouns . Do you really want that? Because that's what you're asking for.<br /> I am totally fine with that if you ignore my other problems, but the problem is here is that nobody's going to write this in as a consistent thing that keeps in context with the world of darkness, because the people who really want this are often those angry SJWs who aren't going to treat trans people and their strongest supporters as anything other than paragons. The world doesn't work like that and neither does the world of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is a &quot;pedastool&quot; a chair you use to climb up on that cross?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:53:50-07:00","id":980921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980738#post980738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The black furies are supposed to represent <b>radical nazi feminists</b> just as they represent bastions of female empowerment. But the Black Furies do it a step further than other tribes. A female garou is equal to any other male in any other tribe, Black furies are Ironically, the most problematically sexist tribe. (yes, that includes the Get. They'll give you a hard time, but will ultimately respect you more for for going through it. Furies ban nearly half the pop) If we include Trans people into the Furies, then just as much as we're empowering trans people, we'll be putting them on a pedastool and then have it<b> corrupted by those angry SJWs</b> who hate on anyone who doesn't like <b>safe spaces</b> or use correct pronouns . Do you really want that? Because that's what you're asking for.<br /> I am totally fine with that if you ignore my other problems, but the problem is here is that nobody's going to write this in as a consistent thing that keeps in context with the world of darkness, because the people who really want this are often those<b> angry SJWs </b>who aren't going to treat trans people and their strongest supporters as anything other than paragons. The world doesn't work like that and neither does the world of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Your comments are so loaded with coded dog whistles I could summon a pack of anti-feminist Garou with them. They come pre-armed with fedoras and cheap whiskey.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, you're dancing around the point - that transwomen are women. You reveal your ignorance later on:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we assume the character changed their physical body and had surgery or magic, chances are that pegasus might get outraged that a person would willingly &quot;geld&quot; themselves in that way, for to him it was done by a despised individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pegasus is a her now.<br /> Further, Pegasus stands up for those who fight to change their circumstances. If a personal ritual gelding isn't doing that, I clearly don't know what is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any person that really wants to be treated better for being a transexual</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof, ooof.<br /> <br /> &quot;Transexual&quot; people, or in better parlance &quot;transgender&quot; people, do not wish to be treated &quot;better,&quot; and this is exceptionally revealing on your part. You think that we want pedestals and accolades and regard.<br /> <br /> What we <i>want</i> is to get over a personal disability and be acknowledged for who and what we actually are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The first <b>guy </b>who gets into the black furies will likely be treated so badly,</div> </div> </div> </div>Guy.<br /> <br /> Are we supposed to treat you seriously when you delegitimize them, demean them, and refuse to acknowledge the validity of their existence?<br /> <br /> That's the real argument here. You don't really care about the Black Furies - you just don't like the idea that people can be transgender, and you'll fuck any expression of it that you can find.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980908#post980908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is a &quot;pedastool&quot; a chair you use to climb up on that cross?</div> </div> </div> </div>Brutal <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reject the argument around Magadon and around the DV:20 Gangrel picture. I have no issue with it being of a black woman, and inclusion of entirely plausible characters (yes, shockingly, there were people of colour in medieval europe!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, there were Chinese people as far as Britain in Roman times - and a pattern of female gladiators, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-03-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:01:36-07:00","id":980924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980839#post980839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course I wouldn't convince you of the issue then. You and I go into these arguments for entirely different purposes. You go in to defend your point of view, I try to inform others and inform myself through the clash of ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>How noble of you, except you tried to pull the same nonsense in this thread. You don't care about the clash of ideas, if you did you might actually respond to anything any of us have said, instead of just repeating your claims over and over and over again, basing this on some golden era where the books were 'more consistent' without actually demonstrating how they are more consistent or appealing to anyone but yourself. For someone who revels in the clash of ideas you've certainly... opposed reading the tribenovels because they're going to be counter to what you think the game is.<br /> <br /> /pads off to get some nails and a &quot;pedastool&quot; for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980839#post980839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I literally changed my outlook from that whole Ahrimane debacle, from &quot;they don't fit, and are there for wish fullfillment&quot; to &quot;they were designed not to fit, to be an example of an anachronistic, radical, feminst crusade that will die out when the vampires get older/further move into vampiric society, the embracing men issue comes up, or they piss off the wrong prince's patriarchy. They were likely . Ahrimanes to me went from 'silly and anachronistic' To 'Doomed and interesting' very quickly, and I liked that. The problem here is that I had to debate the flaws of the ahrimanes online because they weren't immediately apparent in the book. Because, y'know, we can't have overt criticism of a gender movement (that said, I do wonder who wrote that bloodline and their agenda for it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except you didn't actually change your position on <i>them</i> you changed your position on including them <i>in the setting</i>. I don't even need to go back and find that thread to see how your entire understanding of the subject is based on a strawman, you're fairly transparent about it at least. <br /> <br /> You can criticize any movement, but if all you have are strawmen and a gross refusal to defend what is the foundation of your beliefs and misunderstandings, then you're going to piss off 'any' group that you're trying to persuade. We've got enough shit to deal with, we don't need some MRA type telling us how injecting more of our own very real issues into a game is somehow ruining a game set in a world where those issues must also exist. <br /> <br /> A further point where there is difference: I present multiple arguments. I'm looking at Black furies and transgender from both thematic reasoning and a logistical one. I mean, the most likely scenario of a transgender person joining the black furies is as follows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980839#post980839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character petitions pegasus to join the tribe<br /> High chance of Pegasus rejecting the person (probably politely) on the basis that they have a working pair of balls.<br /> If we assume the character changed their physical body and had surgery or magic, chances are that pegasus might get outraged that a person would willingly &quot;geld&quot; themselves in that way, for to him it was done by a despised individual. Of course, there's another chance that pegasus feels honoured by this action, and a smaller chance where he even makes it a requirement to join (either through consentual surgery/rituals or a great spiritual quest to change). Anyhow. Lets assume the possible chance that pegasus gives the go ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pegasus is a her, now, and identifies as 'she' 'her', etc. It's also her name. Her name is Pegasus, not pegasus. <br /> <br /> First of all, anyone on HRT is chemically sterile, and have all of the practical effects of 'being gelded'. <br /> <br /> Second of all, why would she be insulted by that? Countless ancient cultures had individuals like the Galloi would would willfully sever their male parts from themselves in order to live as women. Pegasus destroyed Bellerophon because he tried to control her, it's explicitly stated in the book. It's not because she has penis envy. Saying that Pegasus would be enraged completely denies the culture that she came out of. As a student of Literature, you should already know all of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980839#post980839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Black furies murder eachother, preferably you, over your right to be in the tribe.<br /> -You will forever be barred from any good roles/secret services because a significant portion of the tribe don't trust/like you.<br /> - You will forever have people question your right to be in the furies, from claiths to elders.<br /> - anyone who backs you will probably be in the blast radius of whatever hate you get.<br /> Honestly, you're better off in the Get of Fenrir or the shadow lords than you are in a black fury sept. Any person that really wants to be treated better for being a transexual should join the children of Gaia or the Glass Walkers.<br /> - The first guy who gets into the black furies will likely be treated so badly, probably killed, that it wont be attempted again until the <i>entire</i> tribe changes.<br /> - It massively disrupts tribal unity. The Black Furies will be weaker as a result.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone questions your place in the tribe and they are beneath you, then you are honorbound to duel them. Please understand that duels do not = murder, or require a death. For the love of god please figure out how the basic social structure of this supernatural race works. <br /> <br /> The first 'guy'? You're sure all about that clash of ideas, the way you just ignore everything presented to you without comment and then just reassert your flawed arguments. Also yeah, every time a minority pressed for progress in <i>anything</i>, one person died and they all dispersed, until decades later when shit got better on its own. Are you absolutely insane?<br /> <br /> Actually they'd be stronger as a result of including more members in their group. Your same argument could be used to argue that freeing black slaves was a bad decision because AMERICAN UNITY IS DESTROYED, WE ARE NOW A WEAKER NATION. Do you just not understand how messed up your reasoning is throughout this entire thread?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980839#post980839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(of course, you may note I'm changing the subject from examples because I don't wanna re-read through loads of books to find page numbers. I can give you Ahrimanes, should you choose to accept it, the odd magadon section on Women's medicine in book of the Wyrm, mentioned earier. I could also point out to other super-progressive stuff that doesn't fit, Like DAv20's picture of a gangrel being a black woman with an early arming sword and a european-colonial era pirate outfit, symbolic of a liberty so great that it'd only make sense with <i>Temporis</i>. But actually quote harvesting, no thanks.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you just not aware that there were black pirates who were not also slaves? It would help if you pointed out how <i>any</i> of these things failed to make sense, instead of just asserting that they don't, because it clashes with your delicate sensibility of how the World of Darkness works, which so far seems to be whatever suits your angry MRA mindset.<br /> <br /> Look, I can generalize and assign labels in a reductionary fashion too!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:07:30-07:00","id":980930,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980696#post980696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so what I gather from all of these core snippets, is that pretty much only the 2nd ed really pushes the man-hating feminazi stereotype. The 1st ed actually focuses much more on the mysticism of the Furies than their gender bias and in fact does not even mention killing male cubs at all.<br /> <br /> Generally, though, all texts are very clear on that the tribe is split over the matter and aren't all man hating.<br /> <br /> If anyone wants me to, I can go through the first tribebook to see what opinions are found there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish you people would stop doing all your posts at night while I sleep. :c<br /> <br /> Anyway. Going through the first tribebook and the revised tribebook would probably have been ideal, because the tribebooks separate a lot of fact from myth. My understanding of both isn't just that the male cubs were murdered for being male, but offered up in their then incredibly bloody rituals. It makes no implication that they relished doing this, only that males can never join the tribe, they desperately need to bolster their tribe's numbers, and every child is a mouth to feed. So, here's a bloody offering to the spirits, hope for a girl next time. I have no doubts in my mind that most Black Fury mothers were devastated by this, and that quite a few hid their child away from the tribe's elders.<br /> <br /> The point I'm getting at here is that the sacrifice of male children is not indicative of Man Hatred, it's indicative of a tribe that needs females to practically reproduce itself, would not take women of other tribes at the time, and had limited resources with which to feed its young. Eventually the Black Furies stopped prohibiting females of other tribes, they stopped sacrificing their boys, etc. This won out as the pristine sacredness of their lands and rites took a back seat to the continued survival of the tribe, and not having to murder half of your children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-03-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:16:31-07:00","id":980936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980924#post980924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you just not aware that there were black pirates who were not also slaves?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the benefit of doubting idiot Innocent Flower:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Caesar_(pirate)\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Caesar_(pirate)\" target=\"_blank\"> Black Caesar (pirate) - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Caesar_(pirate)\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Caesar_(pirate) </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:33:30-07:00","id":980944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980930#post980930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I wish you people would stop doing all your posts at night while I sleep. :c<br /> <br /> Anyway. Going through the first tribebook and the revised tribebook would probably have been ideal, because the tribebooks separate a lot of fact from myth. My understanding of both isn't just that the male cubs were murdered for being male, but offered up in their then incredibly bloody rituals. It makes no implication that they relished doing this, only that males can never join the tribe, they desperately need to bolster their tribe's numbers, and every child is a mouth to feed. So, here's a bloody offering to the spirits, hope for a girl next time. I have no doubts in my mind that most Black Fury mothers were devastated by this, and that quite a few hid their child away from the tribe's elders.<br /> <br /> The point I'm getting at here is that the sacrifice of male children is not indicative of Man Hatred, it's indicative of a tribe that needs females to practically reproduce itself, would not take women of other tribes at the time, and had limited resources with which to feed its young. Eventually the Black Furies stopped prohibiting females of other tribes, they stopped sacrificing their boys, etc. This won out as the pristine sacredness of their lands and rites took a back seat to the continued survival of the tribe, and not having to murder half of your children.</div> </div> </div> </div>I focused on the cores, as they are used as summaries for most players what the tribes are. Tribebooks tend to be more something you buy if you REALLY are interested. Plus, the Dark Ages were added because I wanted to see the comparison between Furies on the ropes vs Furies when they had free reign. Personally, Werewolf the Dark Ages discusses the matter better.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I personally think some Furies did go into the 'kill males' stuff, given the older books note that Furies took to Impegrium with zeal. But, as you say, the issue of mating and the issue of basic concept of motherhood overtook that viewpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:37:19-07:00","id":980947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980936#post980936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the benefit of doubting idiot Innocent Flower:</div> </div> </div> </div>While I disagree with pretty much every point he/she has made, calling them an idiot isn't terribly helpful to forum discussions.<br /> <br /> It's funny, somewhere around page 8 or so of this thread I had commented on how impressed I was that this topic was being handled so well. These last few pages though, are about what I was expecting (and feared) when I started reading it initially.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, even though the thread has wandered some from the initial topic and most of the points I would have made have been thoroughly discussed, my opinion is:<br /> I do see a transgender Garou running into issues and prejudice in general in the Garou Nation. But I don't see any reason why their story should somehow be an impossible one. If Pegasus accepts them (and there is lore reason why she would), then she (the Garou) is a Fury. It's pretty straight forward. Some elders may or may not like it, but that doesn't really matter in the long run as their Totem has spoken. They are likely to face hardships above and beyond the rank and file Garou, but similar can be said of any PC character.<br /> <br /> Also, if the Furies/Pegasus accept male Metis (and we know they do), there is no reason they couldn't accept a transgender female Garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:54:34-07:00","id":980958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980944#post980944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I focused on the cores, as they are used as summaries for most players what the tribes are. Tribebooks tend to be more something you buy if you REALLY are interested. Plus, the Dark Ages were added because I wanted to see the comparison between Furies on the ropes vs Furies when they had free reign. Personally, Werewolf the Dark Ages discusses the matter better.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I personally think some Furies did go into the 'kill males' stuff, given the older books note that Furies took to Impegrium with zeal. But, as you say, the issue of mating and the issue of basic concept of motherhood overtook that viewpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I'm not arguing that there are no Black Furies that think enslaving men is a good idea or whatever. But the conversation in this thread has been general. It's similar to talking about Islamic Terrorists in a way that generalizes all people who are Islamic. Language is important because we might understand what we meant to say, but anyone who hears us is going to interpret it through their reading comprehension skills and the tact with which you wrote it.<br /> <br /> And as mentioned I wasn't convinced that sacrificing male children was motivated out of hatred rather than survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:00:57-07:00","id":980961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980947#post980947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I disagree with pretty much every point he/she has made, calling them an idiot isn't terribly helpful to forum discussions.<br /> <br /> It's funny, somewhere around page 8 or so of this thread I had commented on how impressed I was that this topic was being handled so well. These last few pages though, are about what I was expecting (and feared) when I started reading it initially.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, even though the thread has wandered some from the initial topic and most of the points I would have made have been thoroughly discussed, my opinion is:<br /> I do see a transgender Garou running into issues and prejudice in general in the Garou Nation. But I don't see any reason why their story should somehow be an impossible one. If Pegasus accepts them (and there is lore reason why she would), then she (the Garou) is a Fury. It's pretty straight forward. Some elders may or may not like it, but that doesn't really matter in the long run as their Totem has spoken. They are likely to face hardships above and beyond the rank and file Garou, but similar can be said of any PC character.<br /> <br /> Also, if the Furies/Pegasus accept male Metis (and we know they do), there is no reason they couldn't accept a transgender female Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my defense it gets very frustrating debating with a person who arrogantly asserts that their interpretation is the only interpretation of the books, and then routinely ignores your criticisms in order to reiterate hostile points of view that have had a direct impact on my life while the speaker puts on airs of being some sort of noble rational. I do my best to keep civil but a lot of the things Flower.Innocent says are just so subtly disgusting that the only reaction I can put forward is disgust. If he were any less subtle about it I would just flag the posts and move on. There are people who read this thread and remain undecided, and it feels wrong to just let his thoughts lie without challenge because that could have an effect on what people take away from it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot to point out how much worse it is when said person asserts their interpretation as being the only one, whilst also refusing to read all of the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:02:58-07:00","id":980964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980866#post980866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And besides, all of this boils to a question, if a transperson wanted to play themselves in WoD, could they?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the answer to this question isn't &quot;yes&quot; unless every transperson is rounded up and killed in WoD. This seems to be more about if these trans player characters get niches where other characters don't turn it into a hardship. That has its advantages, but maybe that issue can add to the story? That may be less of departure from every life than it would be for others , but then WoD splats are generally supernatural badasses cut off from mainstream society. That doesn't stop their own splat from harassing them, but they've still got their pack, coterie, cabal or whatever. The chances are that the other players won't be interested in playing transphobes with a real trans person, especially across the table, and that would mean that their player characters have the trans player character's back as much as the next.<br /> <br /> As for the thread title, I should think that Pegasus would have a rather cut and dry opinion (&quot;They're women&quot;,&quot;They're not women&quot;,&quot;<i>She</i> was a woman, but <i>this</i> is a deluded or lying man&quot; etc.) and the Black Furies would follow it with zeal. Real historical taboos in Greece would hardly stop them and the tribe could well have acknowledged the concept since before we have any hint as to what their human neighbours thought, so what evidence is there either way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:06:36-07:00","id":980967,"title":"","content":"I'm getting close to the point where I just want to say every single Black Fury is trans and leave it at that. That makes as much sense or more than any of the counter-arguments in this thread and has the benefit of making me feel happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:09:53-07:00","id":980971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980967#post980967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting close to the point where I just want to say every single Black Fury is trans and leave it at that. That makes as much sense or more than any of the counter-arguments in this thread and has the benefit of making me feel happy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hist, you'll vindicate all the TERFs who somehow figured out we plan on replacing all ciswomen as sleeper agents for a patriarchy that is phasing out &quot;actual women&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:11:57-07:00","id":980972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980971#post980971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hist, you'll vindicate all the TERFs who somehow figured out we plan on replacing all ciswomen as sleeper agents for a patriarchy that is phasing out &amp;quot;actual women&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>...wait, have we not gone public with that yet?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:12:18-07:00","id":980973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980964#post980964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The chances are that the other players won't be interested in playing transphobes with a real trans person, especially across the table, and that would mean that their player characters have the trans player character's back as much as the next.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does go into the same issue as metis, though. In general, I'd say it is good to discuss things like that before the game to make sure who is ok with what.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:02:14-07:00","id":981005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980961#post980961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my defense ....</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I completely understand the reaction (especially after a few pages of arguing some seemingly basic truths). Just pointing out that actually posting such is generally unhelpful. It wasn't you anyways, that flat out called the person an idiot. I think your posts were more quippy (and amusing) than bluntly insulting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:28:58-07:00","id":981022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980936#post980936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the benefit of doubting idiot Innocent Flower:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Caesar_(pirate)\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Caesar_(pirate)</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sword. somewhere between the 10th and 13th century.<br /> Outfit. 17th or 18th century.<br /> Gangrel is probably young given how little she's paled.<br /> Also, Female and black, Leading a ship (which is presumably european) Now, that's not impossible (good job for finding that historical annecdote, you devil) But it's improbable, and then we mix it in with the fact that, well, this game was made for a setting between 10th and 13th centuries (though it'd does do fine later on) and, well, wouldn't it be great if we actually captured the typical gangrel rather than something both atypical and improbable. The adventure theme is obvious, but I don't think gangrel apreciate cosy cargo ships as a rule, even if they are from the future.<br /> <br /> Now, as to the complaints who maintain some semblence of dignity in their posts (seriously Jachra. Why the devolution?) I guess I'm being unusually stuborn for the following reasons.<br /> Firstly, Many of you seem very motivated to be progressive. I realise I'm in a thread about being progressive, and I'm well aware that numerical advantage/disadvantage can change the psychology of a person. I'm also very aware that all of us pick and choose parts of the books that we like when we make points. The books disagree, so that's natural. I guess (read a bit later on in this post)<br /> <br /> When I said 'The black furies will be on a pedastool' I didn't mean 'The black furies will suddenly be the best and most noble tribe ever'. I mean 'the Black furies will be closer to being <i>fixed</i>'<br /> My logic goes as following: If each tribe (and as a rule, every single breed of fera, bar maybe the corax) got along well and everyone didn't have some terrible flaw, the wyrm would've been easily crushed. Have you seen all the gifts these folks have, even in more conservative editions? If everyone shared and got along and understood eachother, Gaia would win. So, pedastool is probably the wrong word, but the closer a tribe gets to fixing it's core issues the closer we get to a glorious victory, and that's fine if you're playing an apocalypse game, but I think we can all agree that the world still has a lot of problems, and many of us want to play games post-metaplot ending the world. Every single breed or tribe has a crux. Corax don't shut up. Ratkin are insane. Nagah kill good changers that know too much. Shadow lords are fierce darwinists, Furies are hung up about gender. That's their Issue. Pretend for a moment that Black Furies are actually all men and their entire mythology is about fatherhood. Maybe Minotaur is now their patron or something. Now ask for them to accept Trans. Yes, you can argue it's different, because the actual Furies are supporting the underdog gender (Despite they being the Fierce, Savage, Murder machines of those underdogs) but the point is that Gender is their focus and their crux. They could accept trans, but they're certain to be <i>the</i> most hostile tribe available for them. Their origins for their gender-based discrimination is irrelevent; a vocal minority of them them really don't like men, and some of them is enough. It sounds great on paper; to be so successfully transgender that the women-only tribe will accept you, but reality will be sadly much harsher. Every other tribe is completely fine with having a transgender Garou.<br /> <br /> Secondly... I haven't read 2nd edition. I jumped on the boat and the overwhelming majority of the things i've read have been either Revised or 20th anniversary. The notion that I'm getting all my ideas from second edition baffles me. World of darkness still seems like a dark place, and since I've gathered that from only Revised or 20th... Well, I do wonder how dark 2nd is. I'm only 21. The World of darkness is <i>older</i> than me. But even V20 gives us a description of Gothic-punk and gives us the shitty world of darkness I've been pointing at, and W20 still does the same even after the seventh sign, and that's not even going into the W20 book of the wyrm, which downright parodies real corperations into worse, more insidious and more rediculous ones. Hell, If you've played bloodlines, you might note the GTA-style silly brand names of parody. They're all drinking <i>Demon Seed </i>for one. Gothic or not, The world is <i>Punk</i>, but the problem with <i>Punk</i> is that it tends to clash with itself. World of darkness is not Warhammer 40k style grimdark, but it's certainly supposed to be darker than reality.<br /> <br /> So, I do sincerely apologise. I have a problem with writing so I often spread my points too far out or don't convey them well, don't realize it, and then wonder what they're not getting about them, so I repeat some or add more. I actually use forums to practice writing somewhat, so that doesn't help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 10-03-2016, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:20:26-07:00","id":981065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as to the complaints who maintain some semblence of dignity in their posts (seriously Jachra. Why the devolution?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You called transwomen men. That's not a devolution on my part, unless you mean I devolved by falling to your admittedly extremely low level, around the same height as my feet I'd wager. Treat others with respect and you shall be respected in turn, pal.<br /> <br /> Maybe a few Black Furies are TERFs. Somehow I doubt it - their totem certainly wouldn't tolerate it, having transitioned herself. That's really all that can be said to your arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:32:26-07:00","id":981072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Female and black, Leading a ship (which is presumably european) Now, that's not impossible (good job for finding that historical annecdote, you devil) But it's improbable, and then we mix it in with the fact that, well, this game was made for a setting between 10th and 13th centuries (though it'd does do fine later on) and, well, wouldn't it be great if we actually captured the typical gangrel rather than something both atypical and improbable. The adventure theme is obvious, but I don't think gangrel apreciate cosy cargo ships as a rule, even if they are from the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>The typical Gangrel is going to be an atypical human being. A cargo ship in that era is <i>not</i> cozy. They're cold, drafty, etc etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as to the complaints who maintain some semblence of dignity in their posts (seriously Jachra. Why the devolution?) I guess I'm being unusually stuborn for the following reasons.<br /> Firstly, Many of you seem very motivated to be progressive. I realise I'm in a thread about being progressive, and I'm well aware that numerical advantage/disadvantage can change the psychology of a person. I'm also very aware that all of us pick and choose parts of the books that we like when we make points. The books disagree, so that's natural. I guess (read a bit later on in this post)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am progressive and I hold progressive values. My motivation for this thread was to better understand the spirituality of the Black Furies, and I feel that I have. My progressive values have no bearing on how I'm going to interpret a group. I have already given you countless reasons why I believe that transgender women fit into the Black Furies, but to do you a service I will repeat them.<ul><li>Pegasus was a masculine spirit that was emasculated and became female. This is problematic by my standards, but I have no problem accepting it because that was the mindset at the time. To castrate someone was to unman them, and to unman them was to effectively make them women. This is not at all true for humans, but it could be for spirits, and Pegasus seems reasonably secure in her femininity, even if it's not the sort that human men would accept. Either way, effectively the Black Fury tribal totem <b>is transgender</b>.</li> <li>Pegasus charges the Black Furies, above all else, with protecting the helpless and teaching the weak to defend themselves. Transsexual people are a population of people that are terribly at risk, even more so than ciswomen, doubly so if that transwoman is of color. And yet, in spite of this, they stay true to themselves. They reject the authority and persecution of a society that is for the most part dominated by male influence. The existence of Trans Misogyny is an entire thing that we don't really have time to get into, but I strongly suggest you research it sometime. There is plenty of evidence that transwomen are often singled out over transmen because &quot;A woman wanting to be a man is natural and endearing.&quot; but &quot;A man wanting to be a woman is perverse and regressive.&quot; A transgender woman who is herself in spite of all these hurdles cannot possibly be 'Weak' by Pegasus's definition, but they are often helpless in the face of poverty, discrimination at work and when buying/renting a home, murder and family abuse. This doesn't mean they will be accepted into the tribe, but it does mean that Black Furies are duty bound by Pegasus herself to protect these people. Ergo, it's unlikely that TERFs are going to be the norm. Black Furies will likely have protected a transwoman at some point and given the opportunity to form a personal connection with some. This necessarily prohibits animosity. It's why the best method to get conservative white people to support gay rights is to <b>actually have gay men and women speak with them in a personal context</b>.</li> <li>The culture at the time of Ancient Greece was one in which men became women and had children (see Tiresias) by Hera, or were transformed likewise by Artemis. There is Venus Castina ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus_Castina\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus_Castina</a> ) who transformed a whole group of men into women. That's the wikipedia article, you can find more information on it if you look. In other words men were becoming women all the time, and to Pegasus's Brood this would not at all be unusual. This was at a time when your choices were limited to self castration, which in the eyes of the Greeks or the Romans, was enough to transform you into a woman, in much the same way that the Northen Europeans often use crossdressing as a vehicle of transformation. The very rich could drink urine from a pregnant mare for the hormones laced in it, and I suspect there is plenty of ritual tie ins for a Tribal Totem who is an equine there. People in the north would chew on flax seeds, which as it turns out carry an amount of estrogen as well. Any Historically Accurate interpretation of the Black Furies is going to treat them like a mystery cult from that time period. Men could become women and join said mystery cults in that time period, ergo transwomen should be able to join the Furies.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I said 'The black furies will be on a pedastool' I didn't mean 'The black furies will suddenly be the best and most noble tribe ever'. I mean 'the Black furies will be closer to being <i>fixed</i>'</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Black Furies are not intolerant, they simply believe that some magic is for women and not men. Not inviting men into their tribe unless they are sterile metis does not make them intolerant or bigoted. Magic so far does not seem to exist in this world, so there's no real reason to segregate the sexes over anything. If magic did exist, and that magic were spiritual and shamanistic to the extent that werewolf is, then I'd be every bit on board with the Black Furies about how it's important for there to be a tribe of women doing female magic. You could argue that a tribe of men doing men's magic should be a thing, too, and indeed in some books it is hinted that some of their male cubs 'may' be looking for a patron to form just such a tribe.<br /> <br /> That is, the ones who don't just assume that's the Get of Fenris.<br /> <br /> Arguably the bigger threat to their tribe is how much they <i>hate</i> the Weaver, and willfully throw themselves into Wyld energies, a practice which has spawned a fucking metamorphic plague that threatens to erase your memories and all that you are. Imagine that for a moment. Imagine that you are a woman, that you are happy to be a woman, have found meaning and identity in the rites of the Black Furies. Now let's assume that the comment about some women even becoming men is true. Imagine that your body starts to change - but not all of your memories have yet. You get to be conscious as over the course of weeks or months you slowly become a man, falling outside of the circle you used to belong to, and find increasingly more and more of your memories are just rewritten. Isn't that fucking horrible?<br /> <br /> I reckon that's a much bigger threat to the Black Furies than accepting transwomen into their ranks, or their position that men should go to another tribe for their rituals and identity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My logic goes as following: If each tribe (and as a rule, every single breed of fera, bar maybe the corax) got along well and everyone didn't have some terrible flaw, the wyrm would've been easily crushed. Have you seen all the gifts these folks have, even in more conservative editions? If everyone shared and got along and understood eachother, Gaia would win. So, pedastool is probably the wrong word, but the closer a tribe gets to fixing it's core issues the closer we get to a glorious victory, and that's fine if you're playing an apocalypse game,</div> </div> </div> </div>Except as I pointed out above, most of us don't think the Black Furies are overwhelmingly anti-male, or even generally anti-male. A Black Fury who goes around killing men and being a bully who oppresses people is not going to go up in rank when Pegasus's brood refuse to acknowledge her any longer. Those sorts of elements tend to be on the fringe, like the Neo-Nationalist Get of Fenris who hate people who aren't white. It simply isn't the norm.<br /> <br /> What <i>is</i> pressing is that the Black Furies love the Wyld too much, and would if left to their own devices empower the Wyld to a point where it's as much a threat to the world as the Weaver or the Wyrm, because as it turns out the Triad was meant to keep balance <b>together</b>. The Black Furies have lost sight of this and they're paying for it. Everyone seems to forget that killing the Wyrm is not the perfect victory, the world will be pretty well fucked if there is no Wyrm. The ideal picturesque victory is one in which the Wyrm is cleansed of its madness and the Weaver is put in its place. The Black Furies do not see it that way. Many of them literally believe that the Wyld is perfect and can do no wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I think we can all agree that the world still has a lot of problems, and many of us want to play games post-metaplot ending the world. Every single breed or tribe has a crux. Corax don't shut up. Ratkin are insane. Nagah kill good changers that know too much. Shadow lords are fierce darwinists, Furies are hung up about gender. That's their Issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until you show how not accepting men into their tribe has somehow doomed them more than they already are, saying it over and over again does not an effective argument make. You are just repeating yourself. I have gone out of my way to cite examples in the book for why men are special and important to them, just not in their rituals and not on in their sacred glades. More evidence? The Black Furies can empathize with the Red Talons but what the Red Talons do consistently <b>disturbs them</b>. They are not man haters as a general tribe. They do not have a thing where they go out and kill men. Their mates are men, their sons are men. The issue with Black Furies is that their sacred places are running out, their magic isn't progressing as fast as it could, and the Wyld. <br /> <br /> Moreover, transwomen aren't men, would you please provide proof that they would consider it otherwise? If you can't then please stop repeating yourself and accept that you have no argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretend for a moment that Black Furies are actually all men and their entire mythology is about fatherhood. Maybe Minotaur is now their patron or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Minotaur is a product of masculine abuse of women, just so you know. Both in his conception and after his murder. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now ask for them to accept Trans. Yes, you can argue it's different, because the actual Furies are supporting the underdog gender (Despite they being the Fierce, Savage, Murder machines of those underdogs) but the point is that Gender is their focus and their crux.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please to explain why the Children of Minotaur would have any problem with accepting Transmen? I mean, if they're stereotypical MRA types they surely will, but men are not typically MRA types. Most men are quite well aware of the levels of privilege they enjoy in the world, and openly laugh at the notion that there needs to be a Masculine school of thought to correct the imbalance. I'm not sure why you think this hypothetical would be at all different given identical cultural roots and mysticism. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could accept trans, but they're certain to be <i>the</i> most hostile tribe available for them. Their origins for their gender-based discrimination is irrelevent; a vocal minority of them them really don't like men, and some of them is enough. It sounds great on paper; to be so successfully transgender that the women-only tribe will accept you, but reality will be sadly much harsher. Every other tribe is completely fine with having a transgender Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Get of Fenris would be the most hostile tribe to Transgender women as written, because the Get of Fenris aren't written with a focus on Jotuns and the hunter gatherer peoples that came before cities began to form in the North. The culture the writers derive their traits from has a word for transgender women, it's called Ergi, or 'Soft Man', accusing someone of this meant they were either cast out of a community or else honor bound to challenge the person who levied the insult. Accusations of being Ergi were serious business. Because of this, the Get of Fenris is going to be the most hostile tribe. Shadow Lords would probably be fine with your switching sex for the sake of a political marriage, but they're not going to be okay with you doing it for your own ends, especially if that decision interferes with their plan for your life. They also dominate a region where anti-gay/trans sentiments are peaked. The only reason why the Silver Fangs don't fall into this trap is because their shamanistic culture includes stories of crossdressing or otherwise transgender shamans. The belief in that region is that, on a whim, the spirits can rip your spirit apart and put it back together in such a way as to make you more useful to them. In light of this, the cubs are likely to taunt you, the elders are likely to treat you with some measure of fear and respect. it would still be viewed as a tragic sacrifice for the sake of the people, not as something to take pride in, and not necessarily 'really' female.<br /> <br /> You've still yet to validate your position that the Black Furies would abuse women who are less fortunate than they. By the way, Transwomen still aren't men. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly... I haven't read 2nd edition. I jumped on the boat and the overwhelming majority of the things i've read have been either Revised or 20th anniversary. The notion that I'm getting all my ideas from second edition baffles me. World of darkness still seems like a dark place, and since I've gathered that from only Revised or 20th... Well, I do wonder how dark 2nd is. I'm only 21. The World of darkness is <i>older</i> than me. But even V20 gives us a description of Gothic-punk and gives us the shitty world of darkness I've been pointing at, and W20 still does the same even after the seventh sign, and that's not even going into the W20 book of the wyrm, which downright parodies real corperations into worse, more insidious and more rediculous ones. Hell, If you've played bloodlines, you might note the GTA-style silly brand names of parody. They're all drinking <i>Demon Seed </i>for one. Gothic or not, The world is <i>Punk</i>, but the problem with <i>Punk</i> is that it tends to clash with itself. World of darkness is not Warhammer 40k style grimdark, but it's certainly supposed to be darker than reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've already been confronted on why this doesn't really have any bearing on the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I do sincerely apologise. I have a problem with writing so I often spread my points too far out or don't convey them well, don't realise it, and then wonder what they're not getting about them, so I repeat some or add more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your problem isn't your writing, or your grammar, or anything else.<ul><li>You will construct an argument from a place of incomplete knowledge that suits a preconceived narrative.</li> <li>You will deride others by saying that it's fine if they disagree, but if they do, they're wrong per the books.</li> <li>You routinely ignore the arguments of others and then just repeat yourself. Saying you're not a great writer is meaningless when the cause isn't that you're bad at arguing, it's that your arguments are bad.</li> <li>When confronted, you will assume the other person is only holding their position because they're progressive, without considering that maybe they hold it because the best arguments suggest it.</li> <li>You refuse to read all of the books but at the same time insist they cleave to your interpretation, except you also admit that's not the case when you give your reason for not reading them: The writers are inconsistent (because they don't cleave to my interpretation). You did this when you cited your resistance to novels, you did it a second time when you showed how things have changed over time in the books, and why you disagree with that. That's not poor argument skills, that's refuting your own argument.</li> </ul>As a writer I really don't appreciate you calling my author's integrity into question over a disagreement, when you don't even know me. I care much more about painting a compelling picture with words that helps the players grow or learn something over the course of the story. If all I wanted was to push my own progressive narrative then I would not have made this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:37:10-07:00","id":981074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I said 'The black furies will be on a pedastool' I didn't mean 'The black furies will suddenly be the best and most noble tribe ever'. I mean 'the Black furies will be closer to being <i>fixed</i>'<br /> My logic goes as following: If each tribe (and as a rule, every single breed of fera, bar maybe the corax) got along well and everyone didn't have some terrible flaw, the wyrm would've been easily crushed. Have you seen all the gifts these folks have, even in more conservative editions? If everyone shared and got along and understood eachother, Gaia would win. So, pedastool is probably the wrong word, but the closer a tribe gets to fixing it's core issues the closer we get to a glorious victory, and that's fine if you're playing an apocalypse game, but I think we can all agree that the world still has a lot of problems, and many of us want to play games post-metaplot ending the world. Every single breed or tribe has a crux. Corax don't shut up. Ratkin are insane. Nagah kill good changers that know too much. Shadow lords are fierce darwinists, Furies are hung up about gender. That's their Issue. Pretend for a moment that Black Furies are actually all men and their entire mythology is about fatherhood. Maybe Minotaur is now their patron or something. Now ask for them to accept Trans. Yes, you can argue it's different, because the actual Furies are supporting the underdog gender (Despite they being the Fierce, Savage, Murder machines of those underdogs) but the point is that Gender is their focus and their crux. They could accept trans, but they're certain to be <i>the</i> most hostile tribe available for them. Their origins for their gender-based discrimination is irrelevent; a vocal minority of them them really don't like men, and some of them is enough. It sounds great on paper; to be so successfully transgender that the women-only tribe will accept you, but reality will be sadly much harsher. Every other tribe is completely fine with having a transgender Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, though, it would not be fixing them. Like I said in a previous post, it is the same kind of social fix as the Silver Fangs or Fianna allowing metis. Technically, it is an improvement. In reality, it is still going to be a hard road ahead for the trans Fury. And that is okay, it creates good play. I myself have played Metis Fangs, and it has been far more interesting than many of my garou from more allowing tribes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:50:57-07:00","id":981078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They could accept trans, but they're certain to be <i>the</i> most hostile tribe available for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I actually think they would be in the top 3 for being accepting, right along with the Bone Gnawers, followed closely by the Glasswalkers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Their origins for their gender-based discrimination is irrelevent;</div> </div> </div> </div>On this we certainly disagree, since it directly relates to if/how they (and Pegasus) would accept a transgender female.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a vocal minority of them them really don't like men, and some of them is enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you think a vocal minority not liking men will be enough to overturn the tribal Totem's decision? I think that vocal minority would be enough to give the character a hard time. But that's about it. They are going to have the acceptance (begrudging or not) of most of the tribe. And the support of some of the rest of the tribe. She will also have the support of her pack and pack totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It sounds great on paper; to be so successfully transgender that the women-only tribe will accept you, but reality will be sadly much harsher. Every other tribe is completely fine with having a transgender Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div> The character's story very well may be a hard one. That's fine. Nobody is saying that this particular Garou's life is going to be easy. Just that it is a perfectly viable storyline.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:56:31-07:00","id":981079,"title":"","content":"Not accepting men into the tribe severely cripples reproductive capability. Kinfolk births outnumber garou 10 to 1, but kinfolk-kinfolk offspring are 10 times less likely to breed true than Garou-kinfolk offspring. Therefor, in most tribes, assuming monogamy among males, the ratio of kinfolk born garou to garou-kinfolk born humans is roughly 1:1.<br /> <br /> However, if you eliminate male garou; you're in a pickle. Males can put their seed into a lot of people with little consequence, or they can repeatedly impregnate the same kinfolk. Female garou, on the other hand, can't afford to reproduce like that. A female Garou is out of action for nine months every childbirth, which is objectively a problem if you're running a numbers game. It's significantly easier on female lupus, who take three months (but require the right season) and i suspect black furies have a decent lupus ratio for this reason alone, but we also need to factor in:<br /> The bred true children that are given away, on account of being male (not a massive problem for the nation, since they'll find other tribes, but not great for the Furies)<br /> The effect that this decreased birth rate has over time. The majority of the tribe will come from kinfolk or adoptions from other tribes. All things considered, the Furies are most certainly one of the smallest tribes because they lack male garou.<br /> <br /> This, I believe, is a massive flaw, Arguably moreso than being too close to the wyld or hating the weaver. Please consider this when you allow transexuals into the Black Furies. They'd both be invaluable for breeding and yet to breed in the manner of man somewhat denies that you've changed sex. (yes, I'm aware that being a Transexual doesn't mean sexual orientation has changed, but I believe the point still stands, especially with the emphasis on maiden/mother/crone)<br /> Also. Has this been mentioned yet here? I was under the assumption that it'd be a big thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 10-03-2016, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:08:44-07:00","id":981085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981079#post981079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not accepting men into the tribe severely cripples reproductive capability. Kinfolk births outnumber garou 10 to 1, but kinfolk-kinfolk offspring are 10 times less likely to breed true than Garou-kinfolk offspring. Therefor, in most tribes, assuming monogamy, the ratio of kinfolk born garou to garou-kinfolk born humans is roughly 1:1.<br /> <br /> However, if you eliminate male garou, you're in a pickle. Males can put their seed into a lot of people with little consequence, or they can repeatedly impregnate the same kinfolk. Female garou, on the other hand, can't afford to reproduce like that. A female Garou is out of action for nine months every childbirth, which is objectively a problem if you're running a numbers game. It's significantly easier on female lupus, who take three months (but require the right season) and i suspect black furies have a decent lupus ratio for this reason alone, but we also need to factor in:<br /> The bred true children that are given away, on account of being male (not a massive problem for the nation, since they'll find other tribes, but not great for the Furies)<br /> The effect that this decreased birth rate has over time. The majority of the tribe will come from kinfolk or adoptions from other tribes. All things considered, the Furies are most certainly one of the smallest tribes because they lack male garou.<br /> <br /> This, I believe, is a massive flaw, Arguably moreso than being too close to the wyld or hating the weaver. Please consider this when you allow transexuals into the Black Furies. They'd both be invaluable for breeding and yet to breed in the manner of man somewhat denies that you've changed sex. (yes, I'm aware that being a Transexual doesn't mean sexual orientation has changed, but I believe the point still stands)<br /> Also. Has this been mentioned yet here? I was under the assumption that it'd be a big thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be a significant hurdle except they addressed this by accepting women who were born of other tribes. It's going to be a factor in how many of them have Pure Breed, but the Black Furies in general no longer put that on the same 'pedastool' as they used to. Is a Black Fury child with high breeding going to be cherished? Undoubtedly, the same way their lupus are cherished. But the Tribe has already recognized this numbers issue and addressed it by taking women from literally anywhere.<br /> <br /> In other words, the circumstance you believe to be their biggest flaw was <i>already addressed by them ages ago.</i><br /> <br /> Also admitting Transwomen into the tribe would not have 'solved this problem', because Transwomen are not men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:11:32-07:00","id":981087,"title":"","content":"Adopting from other tribes doesn't give the numbers that Garou sperm would give. It's a help, but it's not a significant one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:20:23-07:00","id":981092,"title":"","content":"Garou sperms does not give anything, it is the fact of procreation with a Garou that results in a higher probability of producing a Garou child. Anyway, statistically speaking, the Black Furies are making the right choice for reproduction. A single male Kinfolk with Pure Breed 5 could be shared between five Black Fury Garou. With a 35% chance at producing a Garou child, the Black Furies could produce 7 Garou children and 13 Kinfolk children if each of them had four children. In addition, the Pure Breed 5 male Kinfolk could breed with fifty female Kinfolk and, if each produced four children, he would sire a minimum of twelve Garou children and 188 Garou Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:34:32-07:00","id":981098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981092#post981092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou sperms does not give anything, it is the fact of procreation with a Garou that results in a higher probability of producing a Garou child. Anyway, statistically speaking, the Black Furies are making the right choice for reproduction. A single male Kinfolk with Pure Breed 5 could be shared between five Black Fury Garou. With a 35% chance at producing a Garou child, the Black Furies could produce 7 Garou children and 13 Kinfolk children if each of them had four children. In addition, the Pure Breed 5 male Kinfolk could breed with fifty female Kinfolk and, if each produced four children, he would sire a minimum of twelve Garou children and 188 Garou Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a bit funny how he uses Monogamous relationships as an example but then mentions that male garou are reproductively superior because they can impregnate 'all the bitches' (literally). Ironically, the thing he claims as a weakness for their numbers could theoretically 'hurt' their numbers if the population boost from including male garou doesn't out weigh the number of women who come to them specifically because of its tribal identity (which we have to assume is kind of all of them, or else what's the point?).<br /> <br /> Once men are included, the tribe loses its identity and women from other tribes stop entering it as the rites and traditions get watered down over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:40:13-07:00","id":981100,"title":"","content":"What source is that from? Somehow, it strikes odd with something else I read about black furies having caring husbands. <br /> Anyhow. That's still far less practical than Five male Garou of variable pure breed having sex with Five kinfolk of variable purebreed. More than four children is very reasonable for kinfolk, though very in the way for female furies, some of whom will be rather uncomfortable with the idea of being part of a breeding program. It seems Antithetical to an anti-sex-oppression group. <br /> Let's not even go into male Garou who sleep around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:46:56-07:00","id":981103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981098#post981098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's a bit funny how he uses Monogamous relationships as an example but then mentions that male garou are reproductively superior because they can impregnate 'all the bitches' (literally). Ironically, the thing he claims as a weakness for their numbers could theoretically 'hurt' their numbers if the population boost from including male garou doesn't out weigh the number of women who come to them specifically because of its tribal identity (which we have to assume is kind of all of them, or else what's the point?).<br /> <br /> Once men are included, the tribe loses its identity and women from other tribes stop entering it as the rites and traditions get watered down over time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, you've misread, possibly deliberately. A single Male garou and a single female kinfolk constitutes as monogomy. However, the breeding here is still better than a female garou and a male kinfolk. The Female kinfolk does not need to fight. She can have a child whenever the last one pops out and her body recovers. A female garou, however, won't give up the fight to bear children (maybe with an exception or too) She's needed on the frontlines, and can't be pregnant for that. Meanwhile, a male Garou can leave his pregnant kinfolk at home, the whole process taking a minimum of a minute of his time to execute. He isn't slutting around, but he can still put more children into the world and do his duty as a warrior of gaia.<br /> <br /> You can factor Polygamy into account after, but the numbers here are enough. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> once men are included, the tribe loses its identity and women from other tribes stop entering it as the rites and traditions get watered down over time. </div> </div> </div> Which is basically a rationale for those who identify as women, yet have working penises, shouldn't be entering the tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:16:47-07:00","id":981120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=980947#post980947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I disagree with pretty much every point he/she has made, calling them an idiot isn't terribly helpful to forum discussions.<br /> <br /> It's funny, somewhere around page 8 or so of this thread I had commented on how impressed I was that this topic was being handled so well. These last few pages though, are about what I was expecting (and feared) when I started reading it initially.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't make it much farther than 10, give-or-take, before abandoning thread. I'm surprised you feel like it's only started in the last few pages. The fact that personal attack posts rival most of the book-quoting posts in 'Likes' kind of keyed me in that a decent number of the folks still following are more interested in an echo chamber than game-based debate.<br /> <br /> Still, I enjoyed the people who choose to leave at a similar point and sent me my first private messages (Yay!) to continue the civil brainstorming aspect of what was otherwise a very thought-provoking question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:50:49-07:00","id":981138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981103#post981103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you've misread, possibly deliberately. A single Male garou and a single female kinfolk constitutes as monogomy. However, the breeding here is still better than a female garou and a male kinfolk. The Female kinfolk does not need to fight. She can have a child whenever the last one pops out and her body recovers. A female garou, however, won't give up the fight to bear children (maybe with an exception or too) She's needed on the frontlines, and can't be pregnant for that. Meanwhile, a male Garou can leave his pregnant kinfolk at home, the whole process taking a minimum of a minute of his time to execute. He isn't slutting around, but he can still put more children into the world and do his duty as a warrior of gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>This presents the problem that you are assuming female kinfolk 'do' that, but they demonstrably don't in the novels. It's also problematic because, really, if all the garou cared about was making more soldiers they would just bump together and breed a metis army like the Black Spiral Dancers. Reproduction in the Garou Nation is more complicated than that, and there are Black Furies who balance constantly having children and going into battle whenever they're not incapacitatingly pregnant - which is only at the very end, anyway.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say those are the norm either, but if I were a Black Fury it's what I'd do. Probably more out of a desire to have all the kids rather than the imperative that I must industrialize my tribe's reproduction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981103#post981103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can factor Polygamy into account after, but the numbers here are enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in fact you do. You do so when you specifically said a Purebreed 5 male Garou is more useful than women because he can go around impregnating countless females, instead of just being impregnated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981103#post981103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is basically a rationale for those who identify as women, yet have working penises, shouldn't be entering the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>TERFs had their hayday in the 80s, that's almost 30 years ago. The women who are against transgender women in their bathrooms are also conservative often Christian white women who would not join the Black Furies anyway. Conversely - the young women who are likely to change and search for a tribe, are often third wave intersectional feminists who <i>will</i> accept trans women in their tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-03-2016, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:52:59-07:00","id":981143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981120#post981120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I didn't make it much farther than 10, give-or-take, before abandoning thread. I'm surprised you feel like it's only started in the last few pages. The fact that personal attack posts rival most of the book-quoting posts in 'Likes' kind of keyed me in that a decent number of the folks still following are more interested in an echo chamber than game-based debate.<br /> <br /> Still, I enjoyed the people who choose to leave at a similar point and sent me my first private messages (Yay!) to continue the civil brainstorming aspect of what was otherwise a very thought-provoking question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what your position is, but if you want to talk with me about it I'm open to responding to any criticism of my conclusions here, or in Private Message where you don't need to worry about being intimidated by the number of people who liked what I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:36:57-07:00","id":981165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981022#post981022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gangrel is probably young given how little she's paled.<br /> Also, Female and black, Leading a ship (which is presumably european) Now, that's not impossible (good job for finding that historical annecdote, you devil) But it's improbable, and then we mix it in with the fact that, well, this game was made for a setting between 10th and 13th centuries (though it'd does do fine later on) and, well, wouldn't it be great if we actually captured the typical gangrel rather than something both atypical and improbable. The adventure theme is obvious, but I don't think gangrel apreciate cosy cargo ships as a rule, even if they are from the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. There is a problem with the outfit being from the wrong time period. It is not a problem with the character concept, which I am not so convinced is 'improbable' when there are multiple seafaring Gangrel given, some from the same (or even earlier) time periods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, as to the complaints who maintain some semblence of dignity in their posts (seriously Jachra. Why the devolution?) I guess I'm being unusually stuborn for the following reasons.<br /> Firstly, Many of you seem very motivated to be progressive. I realise I'm in a thread about being progressive, and I'm well aware that numerical advantage/disadvantage can change the psychology of a person. I'm also very aware that all of us pick and choose parts of the books that we like when we make points. The books disagree, so that's natural. I guess (read a bit later on in this post) </div> </div> </div>Yes, many of us are progressive. Often this comes as the result of studying the issues in question, looking at the relative merits of each position, and deciding that the position usually described as 'progressive' is more morally, intellectually, and emotionally satisfying or meritorious.<br /> <br /> The books do not disagree with the notion that there can be transwomen Furies, either explicitly or by implication. I invite you to provide evidence, including page numbers, if you believe they directly touch on the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I said 'The black furies will be on a pedastool' I didn't mean 'The black furies will suddenly be the best and most noble tribe ever'. I mean 'the Black furies will be closer to being <i>fixed</i>' </div> </div> </div>No, this wouldn't 'fix' the Furies. What it would do is simply recognize that they have <i>no actual reason</i> to oppose the induction of transwomen, and multiple reasons in favour of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My logic goes as following: If each tribe (and as a rule, every single breed of fera, bar maybe the corax) got along well and everyone didn't have some terrible flaw, the wyrm would've been easily crushed. Have you seen all the gifts these folks have, even in more conservative editions? If everyone shared and got along and understood eachother, Gaia would win. So, pedastool is probably the wrong word, but the closer a tribe gets to fixing it's core issues the closer we get to a glorious victory, and that's fine if you're playing an apocalypse game, but I think we can all agree that the world still has a lot of problems, and many of us want to play games post-metaplot ending the world. Every single breed or tribe has a crux. Corax don't shut up. Ratkin are insane. Nagah kill good changers that know too much. Shadow lords are fierce darwinists, Furies are hung up about gender. That's their Issue. </div> </div> </div>Furies are actually hung up on <i>imbalanced power dynamics and the abuse of power directed against women</i>, not about gender in and of itself. Given the potential for such systemic imbalances to feed the Wyrm, it's actually an understandable area of concern, especially when they don't see other tribes focusing on it.<br /> <br /> The flaw of the Furies is not that they do not accept men. It is that they hew too close to the Wyld, rage too hard against the Weaver (especially when it isn't needed) and forget that they are servants of Gaia first and foremost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pretend for a moment that Black Furies are actually all men and their entire mythology is about fatherhood. Maybe Minotaur is now their patron or something. Now ask for them to accept Trans. Yes, you can argue it's different, because the actual Furies are supporting the underdog gender (Despite they being the Fierce, Savage, Murder machines of those underdogs) but the point is that Gender is their focus and their crux. They could accept trans, but they're certain to be <i>the</i> most hostile tribe available for them. Their origins for their gender-based discrimination is irrelevent; a vocal minority of them them really don't like men, and some of them is enough. It sounds great on paper; to be so successfully transgender that the women-only tribe will accept you, but reality will be sadly much harsher. Every other tribe is completely fine with having a transgender Garou. </div> </div> </div>I would welcome a counterpart of all-male garou looking to address the specific issues that affect men, and seeking to practice Secret Men's Business. There were, and are, mystery traditions and sacred religions that impart secrets on only one of the genders, including men. Perhaps it isn't your intent, but I picture them working very closely with the Furies to address the male side of the power imbalance, just as those mystery traditions and religions have men and women work closely together while being initiated into different secrets.<br /> <br /> Further, I fail to see why a tribe of men would not accept transmen. I particularly fail to see why in your hypothetical 'swap the gender of the Furies', given that the Furies are dominant in a region (Greece and the Balkans) where there is a long, long history of transmen.<br /> <br /> I also fail to see why the vocal minority are going to be the ones who rule the roost when Pegasus and Artemis lend support to the idea, and when it's perfectly acceptable for any other member of the tribe to literally throat that minority if they won't shut up about it. If Peggy Stone-Chaser doesn't like the transladies in the tribe because by golly when she was in college Germaine Greer was all the rage, she might want to keep her mouth shut unless she wants to be challenged to a duel and throated by another Fury more faithful to their totem and to the moon.<br /> <br /> [quote[Secondly... I haven't read 2nd edition. I jumped on the boat and the overwhelming majority of the things i've read have been either Revised or 20th anniversary. The notion that I'm getting all my ideas from second edition baffles me. World of darkness still seems like a dark place, and since I've gathered that from only Revised or 20th... Well, I do wonder how dark 2nd is. I'm only 21. The World of darkness is <i>older</i> than me. But even V20 gives us a description of Gothic-punk and gives us the shitty world of darkness I've been pointing at, and W20 still does the same even after the seventh sign, and that's not even going into the W20 book of the wyrm, which downright parodies real corperations into worse, more insidious and more rediculous ones. Hell, If you've played bloodlines, you might note the GTA-style silly brand names of parody. They're all drinking <i>Demon Seed </i>for one. Gothic or not, The world is <i>Punk</i>, but the problem with <i>Punk</i> is that it tends to clash with itself. World of darkness is not Warhammer 40k style grimdark, but it's certainly supposed to be darker than reality.<br /> <br /> So, I do sincerely apologise. I have a problem with writing so I often spread my points too far out or don't convey them well, don't realize it, and then wonder what they're not getting about them, so I repeat some or add more. I actually use forums to practice writing somewhat, so that doesn't help. [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> That's strange, because the only edition that could actually lend any kind of support to your argument is actually 2nd Ed. If you're getting it from W20, I suggest you read it again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981079#post981079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not accepting men into the tribe severely cripples reproductive capability. Kinfolk births outnumber garou 10 to 1, but kinfolk-kinfolk offspring are 10 times less likely to breed true than Garou-kinfolk offspring. Therefor, in most tribes, assuming monogamy among males, the ratio of kinfolk born garou to garou-kinfolk born humans is roughly 1:1.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nice, but it has no bearing at all on whether or not there can be transwomen in the Furies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, if you eliminate male garou; you're in a pickle. Males can put their seed into a lot of people with little consequence, or they can repeatedly impregnate the same kinfolk. Female garou, on the other hand, can't afford to reproduce like that. A female Garou is out of action for nine months every childbirth, which is objectively a problem if you're running a numbers game. It's significantly easier on female lupus, who take three months (but require the right season) and i suspect black furies have a decent lupus ratio for this reason alone, but we also need to factor in:<br /> The bred true children that are given away, on account of being male (not a massive problem for the nation, since they'll find other tribes, but not great for the Furies)<br /> The effect that this decreased birth rate has over time. The majority of the tribe will come from kinfolk or adoptions from other tribes. All things considered, the Furies are most certainly one of the smallest tribes because they lack male garou. </div> </div> </div>Also nice, but not relevant to permitting transwomen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This, I believe, is a massive flaw, Arguably moreso than being too close to the wyld or hating the weaver. Please consider this when you allow transexuals into the Black Furies. They'd both be invaluable for breeding and yet to breed in the manner of man somewhat denies that you've changed sex. (yes, I'm aware that being a Transexual doesn't mean sexual orientation has changed, but I believe the point still stands, especially with the emphasis on maiden/mother/crone)<br /> Also. Has this been mentioned yet here? I was under the assumption that it'd be a big thing. </div> </div> </div>Many transwomen, especially those who have chosen to undergo castration (obviously) or heavy HRT, are infertile. So no, they aren't 'invaluable for breeding', nor does 'breed in the manner of man' going to 'deny that they've changed sex'. The issue is gender, not biological sex, by the way. The two are distinct. As for your invocation of the maiden/mother/crone, there is a place for sterile Garou in that mixture, and among the Furies it is automatically into Crone - which you may recognize as a position of some respect in that tribe.<br /> <br /> Further, if we accept your argument that there is a number crisis among the Furies (which I do not necessarily do, as the Furies are something like 7% of all published Garou, placing them in the middle of the Garou population spectrum), then it follows that the Tribe cannot afford to turn away any Garou accepted by Pegasus, whether cis or trans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981087#post981087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adopting from other tribes doesn't give the numbers that Garou sperm would give. It's a help, but it's not a significant one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please provide a source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981100#post981100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What source is that from? Somehow, it strikes odd with something else I read about black furies having caring husbands.<br /> Anyhow. That's still far less practical than Five male Garou of variable pure breed having sex with Five kinfolk of variable purebreed. More than four children is very reasonable for kinfolk, though very in the way for female furies, some of whom will be rather uncomfortable with the idea of being part of a breeding program. It seems Antithetical to an anti-sex-oppression group.<br /> Let's not even go into male Garou who sleep around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when was practicality the primary concern of the Furies in matters of totemic ideology? They don't get to go 'Oh Pegasus, you're so impossible!', they get to go 'Yes Pegasus okay we will do that'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981103#post981103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you've misread, possibly deliberately. A single Male garou and a single female kinfolk constitutes as monogomy. However, the breeding here is still better than a female garou and a male kinfolk. The Female kinfolk does not need to fight. She can have a child whenever the last one pops out and her body recovers. A female garou, however, won't give up the fight to bear children (maybe with an exception or too) She's needed on the frontlines, and can't be pregnant for that. Meanwhile, a male Garou can leave his pregnant kinfolk at home, the whole process taking a minimum of a minute of his time to execute. He isn't slutting around, but he can still put more children into the world and do his duty as a warrior of gaia.<br /> <br /> You can factor Polygamy into account after, but the numbers here are enough.<br /> <br /> Which is basically a rationale for those who identify as women, yet have working penises, shouldn't be entering the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem obsessed with the question of Garou reproduction, which is not what is under debate. What is under debate is the position of transwomen in the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> Is the definition of a man 'possesses a working penis'? Is the a woman defined as 'does not possess a working penis'? I personally like to think my masculinity hinges on more than my dick working. If it did, and it ever stopped, I might be in for some real trouble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981072#post981072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get of Fenris would be the most hostile tribe to Transgender women as written, because the Get of Fenris aren't written with a focus on Jotuns and the hunter gatherer peoples that came before cities began to form in the North. The culture the writers derive their traits from has a word for transgender women, it's called Ergi, or 'Soft Man', accusing someone of this meant they were either cast out of a community or else honor bound to challenge the person who levied the insult. Accusations of being Ergi were serious business. Because of this, the Get of Fenris is going to be the most hostile tribe. Shadow Lords would probably be fine with your switching sex for the sake of a political marriage, but they're not going to be okay with you doing it for your own ends, especially if that decision interferes with their plan for your life. They also dominate a region where anti-gay/trans sentiments are peaked. The only reason why the Silver Fangs don't fall into this trap is because their shamanistic culture includes stories of crossdressing or otherwise transgender shamans. The belief in that region is that, on a whim, the spirits can rip your spirit apart and put it back together in such a way as to make you more useful to them. In light of this, the cubs are likely to taunt you, the elders are likely to treat you with some measure of fear and respect. it would still be viewed as a tragic sacrifice for the sake of the people, not as something to take pride in, and not necessarily 'really' female.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this come up fairly often, and I always have to disagree with it. There's not much of a case to be made for Ergi being a term for a transwoman or for applying to transwomen at all. It is purely a manly insult, and it casts aspersions on masculinity. There was no actual obligation to fight them over it, nor did it result in those so accused being cast out so much as carrying a social stigma - and that stigma dealt with manliness. The outcast status attaches to a different matter, which is fighting duels over honour, and it comes from refusing to do so or failing to turn up (and not always - it's complex), with the reason for being cast out being cowardice more than being ergi. Given that we see related terms being used to describe 'getting old' because it made men less virile and physically powerful, there's more at play too, and we also see a few people who seem quite happy being described by the terms crop up in the sagas.<br /> <br /> While it is likely more than a few of the Norse would have found transwomen pretty strange, if they just shrug and go 'yes, I am unmanly. That might be because I am not a man', that's the end of it unless the accuser happens to be an absolute dickhead and keeps pushing. In which case you can, if you like, kick the shit out of him for being a dickhead. It's not a perfect system, but it's not as simple as 'ergi = trans'. A lot of the stuff out there about that comes from modern Asatru and heathenry practitioners applying what they assume to be universal and traditional, but which actually stems from modern Western thinking, back onto the term.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I practice a form of reconstructivist sei\u00f0r so I am, by definition, ergi. But if it was good enough for Old One Eye, it's good enough for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:59:38-07:00","id":981184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981165#post981165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see this come up fairly often, and I always have to disagree with it. There's not much of a case to be made for Ergi being a term for a transwoman or for applying to transwomen at all. It is purely a manly insult, and it casts aspersions on masculinity. There was no actual obligation to fight them over it, nor did it result in those so accused being cast out so much as carrying a social stigma - and that stigma dealt with manliness. The outcast status attaches to a different matter, which is fighting duels over honour, and it comes from refusing to do so or failing to turn up (and not always - it's complex), with the reason for being cast out being cowardice more than being ergi. Given that we see related terms being used to describe 'getting old' because it made men less virile and physically powerful, there's more at play too, and we also see a few people who seem quite happy being described by the terms crop up in the sagas.<br /> <br /> While it is likely more than a few of the Norse would have found transwomen pretty strange, if they just shrug and go 'yes, I am unmanly. That might be because I am not a man', that's the end of it unless the accuser happens to be an absolute dickhead and keeps pushing. In which case you can, if you like, kick the shit out of him for being a dickhead. It's not a perfect system, but it's not as simple as 'ergi = trans'. A lot of the stuff out there about that comes from modern Asatru and heathenry practitioners applying what they assume to be universal and traditional, but which actually stems from modern Western thinking, back onto the term.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I practice a form of reconstructivist sei\u00f0r so I am, by definition, ergi. But if it was good enough for Old One Eye, it's good enough for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was well aware that Ergi is not actually a term for transgender, which is why I tried to point out that the literal meaning would be closer to a 'soft' or unmanly man, and is part of where the expression 'you've gone soft' comes from. Irregardless it's evidence that feminine behaviors are somehow something to be ashamed of, and because of this, some Get of Fenris might be the opinion that a transwoman is some sort of low testosterone beta male, who only 'wants to be a female because they need testosterone supplements' or something. <br /> <br /> I'm certainly glad writings I've experienced where they talk about the ramifications of the insult were wrong. If you have more resources on that I'd love to read them, because I always like hearing that my ancestors weren't as belligerent as I thought they were. <br /> <br /> As for reconstructionism, my only real knowledge of Northern European reconstructionism stems from books written by Raven Kaldera, whom you may or may not have heard of. If you've got some other good books to read, I wouldn't mind hearing them. I do like to read quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:28:19-07:00","id":981209,"title":"","content":"I mostly roll with Wodening's <i>Germanic Magic</i> and <i>Chanting Around the High Seat</i>, which are anglo-saxon but provide a basis for seidr I feel is more usable than Kvelduf or Kaldera's work. As for the ramifications, it comes mostly from an understanding of their laws and legal culture, so my suggestion there would be William Ian Miller's work on the subject (his bibliographies are also full of helpful suggestions that I personally haven't read) along with a reading of the gragas and the gotalag. Unfortunately it's one of those areas where there's not a great deal of clarity, so even with those we may come to disagree on it again, but the usual rule is that for an insult, it's the insulted party who demands blood and not the insulter.<br /> <br /> So in our case, if Bjorn Dickheadsson hurls out 'argi' at a transwoman, he can't follow it up with 'come fight me!' and have it be legally binding that she do so. She can, as she's still legally a man there in all likelihood (and if not, she can't but her male kinsmen can and probably would), and if she doesn't show up after then comes the exile, but likewise for him (though it isn't quite so clear cut, as quite often men would refuse duels on the grounds their opponent was beneath them and then simply say 'try and run me out of town for it and I will kill everyone you send', which is admittedly something of a failing on the part of any legal system.) None of this goes towards extrajudicial killings, which I suspect were probably as much an issue as they are now for people without a patron watching their backs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 10-03-2016, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T01:44:01-07:00","id":981350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=981165#post981165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I practice a form of reconstructivist sei\u00f0r so I am, by definition, ergi. But if it was good enough for Old One Eye, it's good enough for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>As if Old One Eye didn't want to be his mother's daughter.<br /> *projecting*<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T10:28:47-07:00","id":1442279,"title":"","content":"I would think that opinions may vary depending on the sept and the individual Black Furies. I actually think it would be on brand for the Black Furies to be allies to transgender individuals. I also think it could be a really interesting story for a trans man Black Fury character (born female) to try to figure out to deal with his identity and what it means for his tribal affiliation. It is a delicate subject though so I would hesitate to focus much on that as a storyteller. <br /> As for my own selfish interest, I think the Garou are awesome, so I would rather not see them acting like transphobic dickbags. <br /> We're also dealing with the fact that a lot has changed, both in game and out of game, in the last 20 years. The Black Furies of 1993 would not be the same Black Furies of 2021. Perhaps they are now accepting a few male members so long as they champion feminist causes and are accepted by Pegasus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26415-cultofjimmy","name":"CultofJimmy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T18:16:41-07:00","id":1442449,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jesus, this was long I will not read </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>everything. </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But I saw a lot of shitty takes from people who appear strangely uncomfortable with the trans subject being portrayed in any way. Nice to see a lot of very reasonable posts too. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think more important than the tribe, is the totem, if pegasus accepts a trans woman, who is anyone to say otherwise? the literal totem that validates your tribe is accepting someone, do you think you know more than it? And I do think Pegasus could accept trans women, absolutely. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I've asked myself this same question for another reasons that is related to it. I'm doing something for storyteller vault, it's a changeling book about totems (yes, changeling can adopt totems too) and I wrote this part about how some of the already well established totems view changelings, and this is what I wrote about Pegasus:</span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pegasus accepts changelings of all genders. Since changelings reincarnate in new bodies, many of them already experienced being a woman, and those who didn\u2019t eventually will, so they are all welcome under its wings with the exception of the arcadian sidhe, who stole the bodies of innocent people, refusing the changeling way. Pegasus values changelings a lot, considering them children of the wyld. It tries to help changelings by the mere fact that they are endangered in this world of banality, but also to get their help in return.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Boon: Followers gain the winged merit for free while they remain loyal to Pegasus. </span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ban: Followers must help preserve caerns, freeholds and nature in general. They may not be allies with the arcadian sidhe.</span></span></i><br /> <br /> Considering Pegasus already accepts male metis, and the also the existence of some offcial characters, such as tiresias, named after the myth of the man who changed his sex. There was also another metis whose name I forgot, but his sex changed depending on which form he was, and as crinos he was a hemaphrodite.<br /> <br /> (Im not conflating being trans with hemaprhoditism, or genre with sex, merely pointing there is a lot of examples of non-cis, non-female or non usual black furies, which some probably could include a trans woman too, or even a trans man, why not? It could be a female born metis who transitioned )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 04-02-2021, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T00:15:45-07:00","id":1442467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442449#post1442449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think more important than the tribe, is the totem, if pegasus accepts a trans woman, who is anyone to say otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, anyone who doesn't like it.<br /> As it was pointed out, iirc by the Elder Theurge Wendigo in the last instalment of the tribe novel series. Spirits have their own agendas, what they do, say or information they relay, might be influenced by what they are. One doesn't become Elder by blindly following what spirits say.<br /> And, personally, I agree with that. Sure, garou are in one part devoted followers of their totems. And, although I think devotion to their pack totem is far more important in their everyday life than their tribal totem, or the caern spirits W20 elevated to sept totems, their tribal totems clearly have some influence over the garou. But, they are also living thinking beings, who are headstrong and form their own decisions, likes and dislikes.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;the tribal totem could just be responsible for who enters the tribe and who doesn't&quot; is an easy and cheap way out of the conversation and the drama and conflict. And, as I pointed out, the tribal totem's acceptance is important for completing the Rite of Passage and gain entry into the tribe, but it is the local garou who decide who undergoes the Rite in the first place. If you aren't admitted to the Rite of Passage, your case never makes it to the tribal totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442449#post1442449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the literal totem that validates your tribe is accepting someone, do you think you know more than it?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They admit garou who later turn Ronin, because the can't handle the garou life, or even worse, traitors, BSD and what not. So, just like any other parent, Totems know squat. They act as if they know and hope for the best.<br /> <br /> In the end it comes down to this: Do you want to play werewolf as a game where your fate is governed by powerful beings, removed from the world - or is it about warriors who pledge themselves to a cause willingly (well, maybe indoctrinated, but by their peers not literal godlike beings). Because, if spirits, Celestina and Incarnae level, really maneuver in the world like that, they are basically Antedeluvians, and the game is basically furry vampire. And, that is not what I want.<br /> <br /> So, I think the discussion should be have had on the level of the actual black furies garou. What their totem accepts is a factor, sure, but shifting all the responsibility to the Totem is dishonourable and weak, within the game. Because it is avoiding the discussion.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> And that is the whole problem with the authors deciding on the matter and making absolute statements in the books. I really praised Black Fury revised TB for it's sidebars and story seeds where the ST/Players were left to decide things and play the game like they wanted.<br /> The same should have been done for the Black Furies and the Transgender question. Describing that there are options, like no transgender at all, transgenders who are now female are okay, but those who turn into man have to leave the tribe behind, to all transgenders are okay. The same considerations for other non-classical gender roles. Then present that the practice might be uniform in the whole tribe, or different from one Black Fury lead sept to another, and that Pegasus is okay with that, too. Ultimately leaving the discussion and decision with the players.<br /> Sure, some people might not come to the same decision that the authors would have liked, but that is okay. The game books are supposed to be a service to the players, not a vehicle to push one's own political views, or that of the editors or that of a company, or that one thinks is most acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 04-03-2021, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T05:16:25-07:00","id":1442485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442467#post1442467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, as I pointed out,...</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be better to assume that people in this necroed thread haven't necessarily read a completely unrelated sounding topic where this was last discussed ad nauseam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end it comes down to this: Do you want to play werewolf as a game where your fate is governed by powerful beings, removed from the world - or is it about warriors who pledge themselves to a cause willingly (well, maybe indoctrinated, but by their peers not literal godlike beings). </div> </div> </div>One of the Tribal Totems clarifying their position on what they consider appropriate bodies for applicants to the Tribe to have is not the hyperbolic strawman you're making it out to be. Also all the stuff I pointed out last time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that is the whole problem with the authors deciding on the matter and making absolute statements in the books. </div> </div> </div>This is not an absolute. Sometimes writers need to make a stand, and sometimes it's best to leave things open.<br /> <br /> I think it's fair to say that when it comes to things that touch on civil rights, minority representation and depiction, and such it's generally a better idea to take a stand on the side of affirmation.<br /> <br /> No cis-folks are hurt because the next round of WtA writers decide to retcon things so that Pegasus has always been totally cool with trans Garou in general and the Black Furies have easily adapted to the shifting norms around gender in modern times as they have going back to antiquity (please see so much of the rest of this thread regarding the cultural and mythological sources of the Black Furies and why they should have a long tradition of being open about this stuff).<br /> <br /> Plenty of trans-folks are hurt when their identities are treated like academic minutae for gamers to debate about, while game lore and RPG &quot;art&quot; is treated as far more sacrosanct than the real lives it reflects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same considerations for other non-classical gender roles. </div> </div> </div>To reiterate given this thread? There's a large difference between actual classical gender roles, and modern heteronormative gender roles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The game books are supposed to be a service to the players, not a vehicle to push one's own political views, or that of the editors or that of a company, or that one thinks is most acceptable. </div> </div> </div>Gaming books are absolutely supposed to push political views. It's part of the service to the target audience of players.<br /> <br /> I will never cease to be amazed that even if people might want to debate that as a generality, that they wouldn't accept it as true about the WoD; a series of games that has always pushed a strong political message.<br /> <br /> Any debate about the Black Furies and trans characters isn't about pushing politics or not The Black Furies are a political statement by the writers already. The debate is about how to refine that statement in the light of changing cultural norms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T10:56:18-07:00","id":1442508,"title":"","content":"Glad to see that this thread returned on the very next day after the International Transgender Day of Visibility /s <br /> <br /> We\u2019ve been over this in circles time and time again but I\u2019ll go over the basics of my stance again and offer my support for those who have returned to these trenches like Heavy Arms.<br /> <br /> There is a valid argument to be made that thematic stories could be told using the Black Furies about Trans-Woman fighting to be recognized in the face of TERF-y attitudes (Trans Exclusionary Radical Feminists), which the tribe of Pegasus could serve as a useful allegory for given its connection with the feminist movement and that this is a continuing battle.<br /> <br /> That said, what matters for more is the safety and enjoyment of the players at your table. Trans people have to fight constantly to have their identities not be attacked and are embroiled in battles in several states across this country (USA), today, to have their rights not be infringed on account of who they are. If a Trans player wants to play a Trans character in a game about ecological activist werewolves and not have to deal with the shit they deal with day-to-day in that game that\u2019s their right and as an ST you have an obligation to respect their wishes if you wish to run a game at that table. Some people may want to have that fight and if so then great, run that game. It\u2019s the same reason you would acknowledge the wishes of an American indigenous person who wants to play a Pure Tribe but doesn\u2019t want to deal with settler racism in their fantasy game or a British/Irish person who wants to play a gaelic bard but doesn\u2019t want to have to deal with the legacy of The Troubles, etc.<br /> <br /> My opinion on what White Wolf should do is have a side column addressing this and offer suggestions on how to talk about this with your players and various ways to play, with such things being present, somewhat present, or not at all present.<br /> <br /> My take on what default should be is that trans woman should be accepted by Pegasus but conservative camps disagree and want to stop this somehow. Again though; this would only come up in my games, assuming I had a Trans player at my table (which I usually do in my group) after I\u2019ve spoken with them about if they\u2019d be comfortable with such plot elements in our story.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re all here to have fun. Respect people\u2019s boundaries and talk to your fellow players. Session 0 is good. Lines/Veils are good. Trans rights are human rights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T11:46:18-07:00","id":1442510,"title":"","content":"Transgnerism isn\u2019t a new concept, trans individuals have existed for 10\u2019000s of years, and are documented in many different cultures.<br /> <br /> The Furies are older then TERFs<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lhamana\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/We-Wa%2C_a_Zuni_berdache%2C_weaving_-_NARA_-_523796_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-We-Wa%2C_a_Zuni_berdache%2C_weaving_-_NARA_-_523796_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lhamana\" target=\"_blank\"> Lhamana - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lhamana\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lhamana </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 04-03-2021, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T12:16:24-07:00","id":1442516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442485#post1442485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the Tribal Totems clarifying their position on what they consider appropriate bodies for applicants to the Tribe to have is not the hyperbolic strawman you're making it out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is an exaggeration to some degree. Still I find a detailed list of what is okay and what is not okay beneath a Totem.<br /> Fenris wants strength. What this means practically is for the garou to decide. There is no minimum of physical traits issued by Fenris, neither a list of Phobias or other Flaws that are a total no go for the Rite of Passage.<br /> Same should go with Pegasus. The entry requirement is to be female or show some vaguely defined characteristics, like present for example in Male Metis of Black Fury heritage. It is for the garou to decide if any given transgender person is applicable or not. Same for people who identify as non-binary or one of the several other possibilities. There is a dating website I have an account at, that lists 11 possible entries for gender, besides male and female, one of them being 'not applicable' - still only natural people may have an account, so no companies with no genders or so.<br /> <br /> In the end, gender, is just one personality trait, for better choice of words, that defines a person and therefore whether or not the person should be a Black Fury. But it is for the Black Furies to decide whom they accept to be part of their community and whom they deem fits into the guidelines Pegasus has given, vague as they may be. What the rules state is that Pegasus could veto the admission into the tribe. But, if Pegasus does this or not is up to the ST in any specific case and should be depending on what the Players want as elements in the game.<br /> <br /> Also, Pegasus can decide differently on a case-to-case basis. Possibly one MtF transgender person meets the overall requirements to be a Black Fury, while another doesn't. Meaning that even if official rulebooks, novels, comics depict such a character it doesn't mean that any such a character must be allowed in any game if there is someone feeling uncomfortable with it in any given game. But talking about this Out-of-charakter when starting a game seems to be the best way to go here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442485#post1442485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To reiterate given this thread? There's a large difference between actual classical gender roles, and modern heteronormative gender roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm no native English speaker, therefore I'm not totally sure what the miss understanding here is. I, guess I should have written &quot;same consideration for all who do not identify as plain female/male&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442508#post1442508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Trans player wants to play a Trans character in a game about ecological activist werewolves and not have to deal with the shit they deal with day-to-day in that game that\u2019s their right and as an ST you have an obligation to respect their wishes if you wish to run a game at that table. Some people may want to have that fight and if so then great, run that game. It\u2019s the same reason you would acknowledge the wishes of an American indigenous person who wants to play a Pure Tribe but doesn\u2019t want to deal with settler racism in their fantasy game or a British/Irish person who wants to play a gaelic bard but doesn\u2019t want to have to deal with the legacy of The Troubles, etc.<br /> <br /> My opinion on what White Wolf should do is have a side column addressing this and offer suggestions on how to talk about this with your players and various ways to play, with such things being present, somewhat present, or not at all present.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind this.<br /> <br /> Being on the same page about the game one what's to play with others is critical. That's part of the problem I have with retcons or massive changes to the Setting in general - but that's another topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T14:15:45-07:00","id":1442533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=978479#post978479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Born the wrong sex&quot; is a very limiting definition for transgender, and does not apply to a lot of transgender peoples' experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is perhaps the first issue. What does the Garou Nation and the single tribes think it means being transgender? As far as I know, there is no official answer, so you can make up your own. Personally, I see the Garou as looking at stuff in black and white in a world that is mostly shades of grey. After all, they hope to defeat the Wyrm and don't even realise that they will shatter the balance of the triad even more by eliminating one of the three.<br /> <br /> If being transgender among Garou comes down to not accepting the gender they are born as, or change it, we have a parallel in the Rite of Renunciation. A Garou is born under an auspice, and those who undergo the rite to change it are looked at with suspicion (the text has an example of the reasoning behind it &quot;who is the Garou, after all, to decide he knows better than Luna?&quot;). In the same way, a change in the gender that one was born might look as questioning Gaia's wisdom. <br /> Also, as somebody pointed out, the Garou are a dying breed and mating to create the next generation of Gaia's warriors is paramount. Garou who would voluntarily compromise their ability to sire or bear children would very likely not be looked at too kindly.<br /> <br /> Black Fury or not, with the reasons I have given above I find it kind of hard to find a good rationale for Garou being accepting of transgenders among themselves and their kinfolk, even if they might have a rather different approach when it comes to normal people. Again, this is how I see it but even so it does not exclude the possibility that groups or individuals might have other opinions.<br /> <br /> That said, the WoD ia a child of its time, and it might not have kept up to date too well with the world nowadays.<br /> I do understand the inclusivity/representation issue, to some extent. I am only a pasty white guy approaching middle age, so I hope you will excuse me if I show ignorance or naivety on these matters, but I often find that fiction (literature, games, movies) already present metaphors that allow to explore social/political issues if we want to, in a subtle way that I actually find more effective than the &quot;in your face&quot; approach.<br /> And if those issues don't matter, what do you get by bringing them to the table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","name":"Nigredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T14:41:09-07:00","id":1442539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442516#post1442516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it is an exaggeration to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>That degree is such that if you actually believed it WtA wouldn't be for you by your own standards already because of how Falcon, Griffon, and Pegasus already dictate things about members of their Tribes and thus turn WtA into furry vampire by exercising such active control over the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still I find a detailed list of what is okay and what is not okay beneath a Totem. </div> </div> </div>You might want to remember that last time around? I was the one arguing that Pegasus even bothering to care about gender was a silly idea from an in-character/universe building perspective and the gender exclusivity with caveats of the Tribe as it exists in print wasn't in keeping with what a Totem should be concerned about.<br /> <br /> Pegasus, by the books, became the Totem of the Black Furies after the Tribe grew beyond a small group dedicated to the actual Greek mythological Furies, as caring about not accepting being subservient to men (the Furies that didn't want to submit to patriarchy, Pegasus out of anger at being mutilated at a man's hands). Pegasus, who was born with a functional penis and all, shouldn't care at all about what's between your legs, but your dedication towards smashing the patriarchy (and in WtA terms The Patriarch aspect of the Weaver). The Black Furies might have started as an all female group and grown into a matriarchal society, and wish to continue being a matriarchal society as long as patriarchy remains as powerful as it is, but matriarchal societies are not inherently single sex or single gender societies. And the BFs developing in a cultural context that doesn't support that idea in the slightest (again, see lots of stuff in this thread already).<br /> <br /> And oh, look, a position from Pegasus about what Pegasus wants that's far more in line with Fenris: a more vague and general attitude that can be interpreted multiple ways. Not what the books have now which is a list of what is and isn't OK by Pegasus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What the rules state is that Pegasus could veto the admission into the tribe. </div> </div> </div>The RAW state Pegasus automatically vetos admissions into the Tribe. It's not up to the STs and players anyway outside of house rues:<br /> <br /> &quot;Pegasus, their tribal totem, will not accept male Garou. The sole exception is the male metis:&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Pegasus can decide differently on a case-to-case basis. </div> </div> </div>Could, but as noted, doesn't. Also I thought you didn't want the Totems to be so directly active in the day-to-day of their Tribes so the game didn't become furry VtM.<br /> <br /> And of course, the standard of, &quot;shows a passion for fighting the patriarchy&quot; is plenty of a principle to decide if a trans Garou is appropriate to bring to Pegasus for consideration without any sort of weird &quot;this trans persons is really a woman, and this one isn't&quot; judgements from Pegasus (via the ST, making any trans players highly likely to be uncomfortable with the proceedings).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm no native English speaker, therefore I'm not totally sure what the miss understanding here is. I, guess I should have written &quot;same consideration for all who do not identify as plain female/male&quot;. </div> </div> </div>A bit of a play on words on my part: &quot;classical&quot; can refer to both &quot;traditional&quot; as well as specific historical periods such as classical era of Greek history (the period between the fall of the Athenian tyrants and Greece being conquered by Alexander).<br /> <br /> The point is that &quot;classical&quot; refers to a specific time and place, where heteronormative refers to the current dominant gender binary in Western culture.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T14:51:57-07:00","id":1442540,"title":"","content":"Like I\u2019m know thinking of a Transmale Black Fury, he would not be liked in his birth tribe. I see the three Pure tribes as being open to certain types of cultural third genders, and them even having special rituals position rather Garou or Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T15:22:30-07:00","id":1442546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442539#post1442539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could, but as noted, doesn't. Also I thought you didn't want the Totems to be so directly active in the day-to-day of their Tribes so the game didn't become furry VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is right, I don't. I would, in any case, have the totem Incarnae have intermediates to make it's will known.<br /> <br /> Is there any case known that any attempt to introduce a garou into a tribe against tribal policy was ever attempted? In Fiction, Novels, official character bios?<br /> Seems like blasphemy to me, if the garou were to try to even bring a garou into the tribe, while they believe the Totem actually enforced the rules they adhere to. Maybe it doesn't and it is simply the garou that enforce the rules, because they believe they don't have a choice in the matter...<br /> <br /> Well, your are quoting correctly, that it has been stated that Pegasus will not accept male garou. My veto thought stemmed from the &quot;Rite of Passage&quot; and that any totem could veto any garou introduced into their tribe - I wasn't recalling the explicit statement about Pegasus. But, they don't seem to picky. Stargazer TB 1st was all about a garou who rose to Get Adren, iirc, before discovering he was a reincarnate Stargazer and chose to get re-educated. This of course stems from the idea that there are to few Stargazer births for the souls to reincarnate. Re-Incarnation doesn't play too big a role for most tribes belief system though, and Past Live was turned into Ancestors. But, my point, Fenris didn't mind a Stargazer soul in his tribe, and the garou couldn't have known, but saw someone who was strong and on the biological side had Get ancestry, supposedly.<br /> <br /> But leaving the transgender question aside for a moment. What would happen if some Black Furies would start a Rite of Passage for a boy garou. Adhering to all the other traditions laid out in the Black Fury Tribe Book?<br /> a) Would Pegasus be aware when the Rite starts and therefore send visions to other Black Furies to end this Rite?<br /> b) Would Pegasus materialise and strike down the cub? The Rite Master? All in attendance?<br /> c) Would the Rite end and the cub simply become an Rank 1 Ronin, with no XP cost reduction on tribal gifts? And his tribal membership not recognised by any spirit?<br /> d) Would one argue, the difficulty for the Rite itself would rise to infinite, so that the Ritemaster can't score any success? What about spending Willpower for one auto success?<br /> <br /> I would probably go with a) or c), for I don't like the spirit's as god-like entities directly interfere with the garou. And, while a) shows some involvement, it is still the other Black Furies free will decision to act upon the vision, or not, if simply the info &quot;they are trying to bring a male into the tribe&quot; is conveyed, without any clear instruction on what to do with the info...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T15:26:23-07:00","id":1442547,"title":"","content":"Aren\u2019t male M\u00e9tis accepted into the Black furies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T16:15:19-07:00","id":1442551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442546#post1442546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is right, I don't. I would, in any case, have the totem Incarnae have intermediates to make it's will known.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still how VtM works. Arikel doesn't send orders to freshly Embraced Toreador to tell them what to do. The Antedeluvian subtly influences that 4th and 5th gens that are active, who use their massive world influence to push Princes and Archons around, who then pass it on to locals, who then dump on the lowly newbies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any case known that any attempt to introduce a garou into a tribe against tribal policy was ever attempted? </div> </div> </div>Evan-Heals-the-Past is the only real prominent example, but the Wendigo don't have anything like the three Tribes with strict definable restrictions on membership from their Totems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it doesn't and it is simply the garou that enforce the rules, because they believe they don't have a choice in the matter... </div> </div> </div>Trying to cast doubt or muddy the waters on something that the books are clear about doesn't help this discussion. There isn't a &quot;maybe&quot; about Pegasus's general position. The book tells us what it is, it isn't simply the Garou enforcing a rule they believe in but their Totem doesn't actually care about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, my point, Fenris didn't mind a Stargazer soul in his tribe, and the garou couldn't have known, but saw someone who was strong and on the biological side had Get ancestry, supposedly. </div> </div> </div>And this ignores something I'll keep banging on about<b></b>: not all Tribes are written equally in this regard. Specially the Black Furies, Silver Fangs, and Red Talons have overt restrictions that are not subject to interpretation. A cis-man Garou isn't getting into the Furies, a Purebreed 0-2 isn't getting into the Fangs, and a Homid isn't getting into the Talons. Period. Unless the Totems change their minds, or the writers retcon things.<br /> <br /> The Fenris-Gazer thing works because neither Tribe has these sorts of considerations to deal with. Fenris and Chimera are basically cool with whoever tries to get in and trust their Tribes to make initiation such that it screens for those that wouldn't fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would happen if some Black Furies would start a Rite of Passage for a boy garou. Adhering to all the other traditions laid out in the Black Fury Tribe Book? </div> </div> </div>e) The Rite automatically fails, as the books have noted any Rite can if the Rite would violate the will of the spirits that empower it (though more of an issue for Punishment Rites). The Ritemaster probably takes a Renown hit, and the Cub is still a Cub and has to try again with a different Tribe. <br /> <br /> A and B are never indicated as something the Totems would bother doing in this case.<br /> C is also overboard as no Cub would be made Ronin over a single failed Rite of Passage. Some Garou have to take a few swings at it according to the books, so there's no reason to assume something like this.<br /> D isn't supported as how Rites without a chance of success are handled.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T18:16:25-07:00","id":1442665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442547#post1442547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren\u2019t male M\u00e9tis accepted into the Black furies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not with that accent mark, they aren't.<br /> <br /> (It's supposed to be pronounced like the Titaness Metis, which is read mee-teez, not may-tee.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T03:49:02-07:00","id":1442699,"title":"","content":"Well then, I think I'm in favour of some clarification like this:<br /> Pegasus' opposition to homid/lupus males in the tribe is just as much the consensus opinion of the Garou as it is divine doctrine. The status of MtF-transgenders cubs to join is discussed among the garou with various opinions going around. Over the course of history Pegasus allowed some MtF-transgender garou into the tribe while not allowing others for reasons not obvious to the tribe. FtM-transgenders are not permitted to join the tribe, but might exist in the tribe when they joined before their transition. Usually there is some social pressure to leave Black Fury communities or even the tribe. So, these garou are either adopted into another tribe or live in mixed-tribal septs or wandering packs with fewer contact to their tribe than usual. Agender, genderfluid, genderqueer, enby and other non-cis people might or might not be able to join the tribe, with the Garou of any given Black Fury sept deciding if they want to educate any such applicant as a Black Fury and Pegasus not providing any reason when allowing or not allowing such an applicant into the tribe after the Rite of Passage. In general, the Black Fury attribute some cultural significance to being female, so any such applicant usually identifies as at least partly female or is biologically female, while perhaps identifying as genderless. A biologically male agender might for most Black Furies be to far a stretch to be accepted as applicant to join the tribe.<br /> <br /> Sidebar: It is by design, that Pegasus doesn't explain himself to his people. Maybe one applicant just doesn't feel right to the Totem, while another does. Tribal Totems also admit to their tribes garou who later turn traitors, get corrupted, even become BSD. So, the Totem isn't all-knowing. It is for the players and Storytellers to discuss and decide how and to what extend the topic of non-cis characters shall be present in their game. This goes for NPCs as well as for PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 04-05-2021, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T05:34:22-07:00","id":1442705,"title":"","content":"There's still an essential problem that's not addressed (because for whatever reason you want to put this on STs and groups instead of the game taking a stand):<br /> <br /> You're actively putting making things fun for trans players below making things fun for people that think trans people exist for them to have debates about the validity of their identifies. You can plaster &quot;trans rights and human rights&quot; all over all your writing and your posts and etc. But slogans are hollow if you don't actually work towards the message. There are transphobes in the WoD because the WoD is our world but darker. That doesn't mean the WoD has to put anything in the books that makes transphobia valid in any way. The WoD and WtA do not need to engage with or lead credence to the idea that there's a good faith debate about trans identities being valid.<br /> <br /> I have yet to see a single compelling reason the default of the game shouldn't be: &quot;Pegasus cares about smashing the patriarchy, and any Garou that dedicates themselves to that cause is welcome,&quot; so trans and enby folks and all stripes have a Tribe that speaks to the broad group of people that have been oppressed by patriarchy and toxic masculinity. They can sit down, stat up a radical modern intersectional feminist Black Fury, and fight the literal spirit of patriarchy. Because this is, at its core, a fun game and it should be living up to its political positions (such as affirming the identities of trans folks and making the game welcoming and fun for them).<br /> <br /> The sidebars are how you discuss the complexity and history of feminism and gender non-conformity, discuss what level of internal conflict within the Black Furies the players want on screen as the Tribe reflects modern feminism including struggles over accepting trans identities and allyship with the LGBTQ+ communities. If the group wants to explore transphobic views within the Garou Nation and the Black Furies, the sidebar is where you give advice on how. Sidebars aren't for trying to weasel word your way out of refusing to affirm trans rights in your game design.<br /> <br /> For all you said about not turning WtA into VtM, stop trying to turn Pegasus into Malkav. Pegasus does not need to be complicated. Pegasus does not need a whole paragraph to dance around a bunch of different identities to address what Pegasus does and doesn't accept into the Tribe. As I have repeatedly pointed out we can make Pegasus very direct, very straightforward, and more like the majority of the Totems. Making them (Pegasus, canonically, uses they as of W20, not he, because Pegasus sees themself as agender at this point) all about smashing the patriarchy solves all the problems, and leaves plenty of room for people that want to explore real world contentious topics in more depth free to do so.<br /> <br /> So for the sake of this conversation going somewhere good, please, why?<br /> <br /> Why is this, &quot;Pegasus became the patron of the Black Furies due to their mutual mistreatment by a male dominated world. As the Tribe grew, Pegasus has come to accept all that desire in their hearts to tear down patriarchy so no sex or gender rules over another. The Furies over their long history, have sometimes found themselves at odds with Pegasus as culture and tradition can clash with idealism, but with so many enemies unity in the name of practicality usually keeps the Tribe together.&quot; in any way less preferable to the paragraph you posted?<br /> <br /> What does it fail to accomplish of what we want out of WtA and the Black Furies? It's a nice short elevator pitch that's easy to get. It doesn't rely on Pegasus being too much like an Antedelvuian. The relationship between Totem and Tribe is complicated and not always in sync. The Black Furies are still the defenders of women, children, and Wyld spaces; but all of the things pointed out earlier in this thread about their cultural connections to non-conformity and trans identities can be worked in smoothly. The idea of internal conflict over such topics is setup without being forced into the core of the Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T11:16:02-07:00","id":1442748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals?p=1442705#post1442705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Pegasus cares about smashing the patriarchy, and any Garou that dedicates themselves to that cause is welcome&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if there is any additional wording, explaining that cis-man can't just join with a lip service to smashing the patriarchy, because the Black Furies will evaluate any applicant, than it is fine by me.<br /> <br /> In any case the mentality of the garou in question should decide if suitable for any given tribe, and gender-identity is only a part of what makes a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}